\s1 Solomon’s Prayer for Wisdom
\r (1 Kings 3:1–15; Psalm 45:1–17; Psalm 72:1–20)
\p \v 1 \rb Now Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֥ה\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֖יד\rb* \rb established himself securely|וַיִּתְחַזֵּ֛ק\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb his kingdom|מַלְכוּת֑וֹ\rb*, \rb and the LORD|וַיהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb his God|אֱלֹהָיו֙\rb* \rb was with him|עִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and highly|לְמָֽעְלָה׃\rb* \rb exalted him|וַֽיְגַדְּלֵ֖הוּ\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb Then Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֣ה\rb* \rb spoke|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֡ל\rb*, \rb to the commanders|לְשָׂרֵי֩\rb* \rb of thousands|הָאֲלָפִ֨ים\rb* \rb and of hundreds|וְהַמֵּא֜וֹת\rb*, \rb to the judges|וְלַשֹּֽׁפְטִ֗ים\rb*, \rb and to every|וּלְכֹ֛ל\rb* \rb leader|נָשִׂ֥יא\rb* \rb in all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*— \rb the heads|רָאשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb of the families|הָאָבֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb And Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹה֙\rb* \rb and the whole|וְכָל־\rb* \rb assembly|הַקָּהָ֣ל\rb*\rb |עִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּלְכ֗וּ\rb* \rb to the high place|לַבָּמָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb at Gibeon|בְּגִבְע֑וֹן\rb* \rb because|כִּי־\rb* \rb it was|הָיָ֗ה\rb* \rb the location of|שָׁ֣ם\rb* \rb God’s|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb Tent|אֹ֤הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵד֙\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb* \rb the servant|עֶֽבֶד־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb had made|עָשָׂ֛ה\rb* \rb in the wilderness|בַּמִּדְבָּֽר׃\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb Now|אֲבָ֗ל\rb* \rb David|דָוִיד֙\rb* \rb had brought|הֶעֱלָ֤ה\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֤וֹן\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb from Kiriath-jearim|יְעָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb to the place|דָּוִ֑יד\rb* \rb he had prepared|בַּֽהֵכִ֥ין\rb* \rb for it|ל֖וֹ\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֧י\rb* \rb he had pitched|נָֽטָה־\rb* \rb a tent|אֹ֖הֶל\rb* \rb for it|ל֛וֹ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb But the bronze|הַנְּחֹ֗שֶׁת\rb* \rb altar|וּמִזְבַּ֣ח\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb made by|עָשָׂה֙\rb* \rb Bezalel|בְּצַלְאֵל֙\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Uri|אוּרִ֣י\rb*, \rb the son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Hur|ח֔וּר\rb*, \rb was in Gibeon|שָׂ֕ם\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb*\f + \fr 1:5 \ft LXX, Vulgate, and some Hebrew manuscripts \fqa was there before\ft ; MT \fqa he placed before\f* \rb the tabernacle|מִשְׁכַּ֣ן\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*. \rb So Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֖ה\rb* \rb and the assembly|וְהַקָּהָֽל׃\rb* \rb inquired of Him there|וַיִּדְרְשֵׁ֥הוּ\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֨ה\rb* \rb offered sacrifices|וַיַּעַל֩\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֜ם\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the bronze|הַנְּחֹ֙שֶׁת֙\rb* \rb altar|מִזְבַּ֤ח\rb* \rb at the Tent|לְאֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵ֑ד\rb*, \rb where|עָלָ֛יו\rb* \rb he offered|וַיַּ֧עַל\rb* \rb a thousand|אָֽלֶף׃\rb* \rb burnt offerings|עֹל֖וֹת\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb That|הַה֔וּא\rb* \rb night|בַּלַּ֣יְלָה\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb appeared|נִרְאָ֥ה\rb* \rb to Solomon|לִשְׁלֹמֹ֑ה\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |ל֔וֹ\rb*, “\rb Ask|שְׁאַ֖ל\rb*\rb |מָ֥ה\rb*, \rb and I will give it|אֶתֶּן־\rb* \rb to you|לָֽךְ׃\rb*!”
\p \v 8 \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹה֙\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to God|לֵֽאלֹהִ֔ים\rb*: “\rb You|אַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb have shown|עָשִׂ֛יתָ\rb* \rb much|גָּד֑וֹל\rb* \rb loving devotion|חֶ֣סֶד\rb*\f + \fr 1:8 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa chesed \ft are translated here and in most cases throughout the Scriptures as \fqa loving devotion\ft ; the range of meaning includes \fqa love\ft , \fqa goodness\ft , \fqa kindness\ft , \fqa faithfulness\ft , and \fqa mercy\ft , as well as \fqa loyalty to a covenant\ft .\f* \rb to|עִם־\rb* \rb my father|אָבִ֖י\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֥יד\rb*, \rb and You have made me king|וְהִמְלַכְתַּ֖נִי\rb* \rb in his place|תַּחְתָּֽיו׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb Now|עַתָּה֙\rb*, \rb O LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*, \rb let Your promise|דְּבָ֣רְךָ֔\rb* \rb to|עִ֖ם\rb* \rb my father|אָבִ֑י\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֣יד\rb* \rb be fulfilled|יֵֽאָמֵן֙\rb*. \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb You|אַתָּה֙\rb* \rb have made me king|הִמְלַכְתַּ֔נִי\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb a people|עַ֕ם\rb* \rb as numerous|רַ֖ב\rb* \rb as the dust|כַּעֲפַ֥ר\rb* \rb of the earth|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb Now|עַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb grant|תֶּן־\rb* \rb me|לִ֔י\rb* \rb wisdom|חָכְמָ֤ה\rb* \rb and knowledge|וּמַדָּע֙\rb*, \rb so that I may lead|וְאֵֽצְאָ֛ה\rb*\rb |לִפְנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |וְאָב֑וֹאָה\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb people|הָֽעָם־\rb*.\f + \fr 1:10 \ft Literally \fqa so that I may go out before this people and come in\f* \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb who|מִ֣י\rb* \rb is able to govern|יִשְׁפֹּ֔ט\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb great|הַגָּדֽוֹל׃ס\rb* \rb people of Yours|עַמְּךָ֥\rb*?”
\p \v 11 \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֣ים׀\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר־\rb* \rb to Solomon|לִשְׁלֹמֹ֡ה\rb*, “\rb Since|יַ֣עַן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb this|זֹ֜את\rb* \rb was|הָיְתָ֨ה\rb* \rb in|עִם־\rb* \rb your heart|לְבָבֶ֗ךָ\rb* \rb instead of|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb requesting|שָׁ֠אַלְתָּ\rb* \rb riches|עֹ֣שֶׁר\rb* \rb or wealth|נְכָסִ֤ים\rb* \rb or honor for yourself|וְכָבוֹד֙\rb* \rb or|וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb death|נֶ֣פֶשׁ\rb* \rb for your enemies|שֹׂנְאֶ֔יךָ\rb* — \rb and since you have not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb even|וְגַם־\rb* \rb requested|שָׁאָ֑לְתָּ\rb* \rb long|רַבִּ֖ים\rb* \rb life|יָמִ֥ים\rb* \rb but have asked|וַתִּֽשְׁאַל־\rb* \rb for wisdom|חָכְמָ֣ה\rb* \rb and knowledge|וּמַדָּ֔ע\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb to govern|תִּשְׁפּוֹט֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My people|עַמִּ֔י\rb* \rb over|עָלָֽיו׃\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I have made you king|הִמְלַכְתִּ֖יךָ\rb* — \v 12 \rb therefore wisdom|הַֽחָכְמָ֥ה\rb* \rb and knowledge|וְהַמַּדָּ֖ע\rb* \rb have been granted|נָת֣וּן\rb* \rb to you|לָ֑ךְ\rb*. \rb And I will also give|אֶתֶּן־\rb* \rb you|לָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb riches|וְעֹ֨שֶׁר\rb* \rb and wealth|וּנְכָסִ֤ים\rb* \rb and honor|וְכָבוֹד֙\rb* \rb unlike|לֹא־\rb*\rb |כֵ֗ן\rb* \rb anything|אֲשֶׁ֣ר׀\rb*\rb |הָ֣יָה\rb* \rb given to the kings|לַמְּלָכִים֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb before you|לְפָנֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb or|יִֽהְיֶה־\rb*\rb |כֵּֽן׃\rb*\rb |לֹ֥א\rb* \rb after you|וְאַחֲרֶ֖יךָ\rb*.”
\p \v 13 \rb So Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֜ה\rb* \rb went|וַיָּבֹ֨א\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|יְר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb from the high place|לַבָּמָ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb in Gibeon|בְּגִבְעוֹן֙\rb*, \rb from before|מִלִּפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the Tent|אֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵ֑ד\rb*, \rb and he reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֖ךְ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃פ\rb*.
\s1 Solomon’s Riches
\r (1 Kings 10:26–29)
\p \v 14 \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹה֮\rb* \rb accumulated|וַיֶּאֱסֹ֣ף\rb*\rb |רֶ֣כֶב\rb*\rb |וּפָרָשִׁים֒\rb*\f + \fr 1:14 \ft Literally \fqa Solomon accumulated chariots and horses; he had\f*\rb |וַֽיְהִי־\rb*\rb |ל֗וֹ\rb* \rb 1,400|אֶ֤לֶף\rb*\rb |וְאַרְבַּע־\rb*\rb |מֵאוֹת֙\rb* \rb chariots|רֶ֔כֶב\rb* \rb and 12,000|וּשְׁנֵים־\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֶ֖לֶף\rb* \rb horses|פָּרָשִׁ֑ים\rb*,\f + \fr 1:14 \ft Or \fqa horsemen \ft or \fqa charioteers\f* \rb which he stationed|וַיַּנִּיחֵם֙\rb* \rb in the chariot|הָרֶ֔כֶב\rb* \rb cities|בְּעָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb and also with|וְעִם־\rb* \rb him|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירֽוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb The king|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb made|וַיִּתֵּ֨ן\rb* \rb silver|הַכֶּ֧סֶף\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and gold|הַזָּהָ֛ב\rb* \rb as common in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \rb as stones|כָּאֲבָנִ֑ים\rb*, \rb and|וְאֵ֣ת\rb*\rb |נָתַ֛ן\rb* \rb cedar|הָאֲרָזִ֗ים\rb* \rb as abundant|לָרֹֽב׃\rb* \rb as sycamore|כַּשִּׁקְמִ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb in the foothills|בַּשְּׁפֵלָ֖ה\rb*.\f + \fr 1:15 \ft Hebrew \fqa Shephelah \ft or \fqa lowlands\ft ; that is, the western foothills of Judea\f*
\p \v 16 \rb Solomon’s|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |לִשְׁלֹמֹ֖ה\rb* \rb horses|הַסּוּסִ֛ים\rb* \rb were imported|וּמוֹצָ֧א\rb* \rb from Egypt|מִמִּצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb and Kue|וּמִקְוֵ֕א\rb*;\f + \fr 1:16 \ft Probably an area in Cilicia, a province in the southeast of Asia Minor\f* \rb the royal|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb merchants|סֹחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb purchased them|יִקְח֖וּ\rb*\rb |בִּמְחִֽיר׃\rb* \rb from Kue|מִקְוֵ֥א\rb*. \v 17 \rb A chariot|מֶרְכָּבָה֙\rb* \rb could be imported|וַֽ֠יַּעֲלוּ\rb*\rb |וַיּוֹצִ֨יאוּ\rb* \rb from Egypt|מִמִּצְרַ֤יִם\rb* \rb for six|בְּשֵׁ֣שׁ\rb* \rb hundred shekels|מֵא֣וֹת\rb* \rb of silver|כֶּ֔סֶף\rb*,\f + \fr 1:17 \fqa 600 shekels \ft is approximately 15.1 pounds or 6.8 kilograms of silver.\f* \rb and a horse|וְס֖וּס\rb* \rb for a hundred|וּמֵאָ֑ה\rb* \rb and fifty|בַּחֲמִשִּׁ֣ים\rb*.\f + \fr 1:17 \fqa 150 shekels \ft is approximately 3.8 pounds or 1.7 kilograms of silver.\f* \rb Likewise|וְ֠כֵן\rb*, \rb they|בְּיָדָ֥ם\rb* \rb exported them|יוֹצִֽיאוּ׃\rb* \rb to all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the kings|מַלְכֵ֧י\rb* \rb of the Hittites|הַֽחִתִּ֛ים\rb* \rb and to the kings|וּמַלְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Aram|אֲרָ֖ם\rb*.
\c 2
\s1 Preparations for the Temple
\r (1 Kings 5:1–6)
\p \v 1 \rb Now Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֗ה\rb* \rb purposed|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to build|לִבְנ֥וֹת\rb* \rb a house|בַּ֙יִת֙\rb* \rb for the Name|לְשֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and a royal|לְמַלְכוּתֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb palace for himself|וּבַ֖יִת\rb*. \v 2 \rb So he conscripted|וַיִּסְפֹּ֨ר\rb*\rb |שְׁלֹמֹ֜ה\rb* \rb 70,000|שִׁבְעִ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֶ֙לֶף֙\rb*\rb |אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb porters|סַבָּ֔ל\rb*, \rb 80,000|וּשְׁמוֹנִ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֶ֛לֶף\rb*\rb |אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb stonecutters|חֹצֵ֣ב\rb* \rb in the mountains|בָּהָ֑ר\rb*, \rb and 3,600|שְׁלֹ֥שֶׁת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִ֖ים\rb*\rb |וְשֵׁ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵאֽוֹת׃פ\rb* \rb supervisors|וּמְנַצְּחִ֣ים\rb*\rb |עֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb Then Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֔ה\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֣ח\rb* \rb word to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Hiram|חוּרָ֥ם\rb*\f + \fr 2:3 \ft Hebrew \fqa Huram\ft , a variant of \fqa Hiram\ft ; also in verses 11 and 12\f* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Tyre|צֹ֖ר\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*:
\pmo “\rb Do for me as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb you did|עָשִׂ֙יתָ֙\rb* \rb for|עִם־\rb* \rb my father|אָבִ֔י\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֣יד\rb* \rb when you sent|וַתִּֽשְׁלַֽח־\rb* \rb him|ל֣וֹ\rb* \rb cedars|אֲרָזִ֔ים\rb* \rb to build|לִבְנֽוֹת־\rb* \rb himself|ל֥וֹ\rb* \rb a house|בַ֖יִת\rb* \rb to live|לָשֶׁ֥בֶת\rb* \rb in|בּֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb Behold|הִנֵּה֩\rb*,\rb |אֲנִ֨י\rb* \rb I am about to build|בֽוֹנֶה־\rb* \rb a house|בַּ֜יִת\rb* \rb for the Name|לְשֵׁ֣ם׀\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb my God|אֱלֹהָ֗י\rb* \rb to dedicate|לְהַקְדִּ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb to Him|ל֡וֹ\rb* \rb for burning|לְהַקְטִ֣יר\rb* \rb fragrant|סַמִּים֩\rb* \rb incense|קְטֹֽרֶת־\rb* \rb before Him|לְפָנָ֣יו\rb*, \rb for displaying the showbread|וּמַעֲרֶ֨כֶת\rb* \rb continuously|תָּמִ֤יד\rb*, \rb and for making burnt offerings|וְעֹלוֹת֙\rb* \rb every morning|לַבֹּ֣קֶר\rb* \rb and evening|וְלָעֶ֔רֶב\rb* \rb as well as on the Sabbaths|לַשַּׁבָּתוֹת֙\rb*, \rb New Moons|וְלֶ֣חֳדָשִׁ֔ים\rb*, \rb and appointed feasts|וּֽלְמוֹעֲדֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֑ינוּ\rb*. \rb This|זֹ֥את\rb* \rb is ordained for|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel forever|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*\rb |לְעוֹלָ֖ם\rb*.
\b 
\pmo \v 5 \rb The house|וְהַבַּ֛יִת\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am building|בוֹנֶ֖ה\rb* \rb will be great|גָּד֑וֹל\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb is greater|גָד֥וֹל\rb* \rb than all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb gods|הָאֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb But who|וּמִ֤י\rb* \rb is able|יַעֲצָר־\rb*\rb |כֹּ֙חַ֙\rb* \rb to build|לִבְנֽוֹת־\rb* \rb a house|בַ֔יִת\rb* \rb for Him|ל֣וֹ\rb*, \rb since|כִּ֧י\rb* \rb the heavens|הַשָּׁמַ֛יִם\rb*, \rb even the highest heavens|וּשְׁמֵ֥י\rb*\rb |הַשָּׁמַ֖יִם\rb*, \rb cannot|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb contain Him|יְכַלְכְּלֻ֑הוּ\rb*? \rb Who then|וּמִ֤י\rb* \rb am I|אֲנִי֙\rb*, \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I should build|אֶבְנֶה־\rb* \rb a house|בַ֔יִת\rb* \rb for Him|לּ֣וֹ\rb*, \rb except as a place|כִּ֖י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb to burn sacrifices|לְהַקְטִ֥יר\rb* \rb before Him|לְפָנָֽיו׃\rb*?
\b 
\pmo \v 7 \rb Send|שְֽׁלַֽח־\rb* \rb me|לִ֣י\rb*, \rb therefore|וְעַתָּ֡ה\rb*, \rb a craftsman|אִישׁ־\rb*\rb |חָכָ֡ם\rb* \rb skilled|וְיֹדֵ֖עַ\rb* \rb in engraving|לְפַתֵּ֣חַ\rb*\rb |פִּתּוּחִ֑ים\rb* \rb to work|לַעֲשׂוֹת֩\rb* \rb with gold|בַּזָּהָ֨ב\rb* \rb and silver|וּבַכֶּ֜סֶף\rb*, \rb with bronze|וּבַנְּחֹ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb and iron|וּבַבַּרְזֶ֗ל\rb*, \rb and with purple|וּבָֽאַרְגְּוָן֙\rb*, \rb crimson|וְכַרְמִ֣יל\rb*, \rb and blue yarn|וּתְכֵ֔לֶת\rb*. \rb He will work with|עִם־\rb* \rb my craftsmen|הַֽחֲכָמִ֗ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb*\rb |עִמִּי֙\rb* \rb in Judah|בִּֽיהוּדָ֣ה\rb* \rb and Jerusalem|וּבִֽירוּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb*, \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb my father|אָבִֽי׃\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֥יד\rb* \rb provided|הֵכִ֖ין\rb*.
\b 
\pmo \v 8 \rb Send me|וּֽשְׁלַֽח־\rb* \rb also|לִי֩\rb* \rb cedar|אֲרָזִ֜ים\rb*, \rb cypress|בְּרוֹשִׁ֣ים\rb*,\f + \fr 2:8 \ft Or \fqa pine \ft or \fqa juniper \ft or \fqa fir\f* \rb and algum|וְאַלְגּוּמִּים֮\rb*\f + \fr 2:8 \fqa Algum \ft is probably a variant of \fqa almug\ft ; see 1 Kings 10:11.\f* \rb logs|עֲצֵ֨י\rb* \rb from Lebanon|מֵֽהַלְּבָנוֹן֒\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb know|יָדַ֔עְתִּי\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb your servants|עֲבָדֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb have skill|יֽוֹדְעִ֔ים\rb* \rb to cut|לִכְר֖וֹת\rb* \rb timber|עֲצֵ֣י\rb* \rb there|לְבָנ֑וֹן\rb*. \rb And indeed|וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb*, \rb my servants|עֲבָדַ֖י\rb* \rb will work with|עִם־\rb* \rb yours|עֲבָדֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \v 9 \rb to prepare|וּלְהָכִ֥ין\rb* \rb for me|לִ֛י\rb* \rb timber|עֵצִ֖ים\rb* \rb in abundance|לָרֹ֑ב\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the temple|הַבַּ֛יִת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am building|בוֹנֶ֖ה\rb* \rb will be great|גָּד֥וֹל\rb* \rb and wonderful|וְהַפְלֵֽא׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb |וְהִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb I will pay|נָתַתִּי֩\rb* \rb your servants|לַעֲבָדֶ֗יךָ\rb*, \rb the woodcutters|לַֽחֹטְבִ֣ים׀\rb*\rb |לְֽכֹרְתֵ֣י׀\rb*\rb |הָעֵצִ֡ים\rb*, \rb 20,000|עֶשְׂרִ֣ים\rb*\rb |אֶ֔לֶף\rb* \rb cors|כֹּרִים֙\rb* \rb of ground|מַכּ֜וֹת\rb* \rb wheat|חִטִּ֨ים׀\rb*,\f + \fr 2:10 \fqa 20,000 cors \ft is approximately 124,800 bushels or 4.4 million liters (probably about 3,800 tons or 3,400 metric tons of wheat).\f* \rb 20,000|עֶשְׂרִ֣ים\rb*\rb |אָ֑לֶף\rb* \rb cors|כֹּרִ֖ים\rb* \rb of barley|וּשְׂעֹרִ֕ים\rb*,\f + \fr 2:10 \fqa 20,000 cors \ft is approximately 124,800 bushels or 4.4 million liters (probably about 2,910 tons or 2,700 metric tons of barley).\f* \rb 20,000|עֶשְׂרִ֣ים\rb*\rb |אֶ֔לֶף\rb* \rb baths|בַּתִּים֙\rb* \rb of wine|וְיַ֗יִן\rb*,\f + \fr 2:10 \fqa 20,000 baths \ft is approximately 116,000 gallons or 440,000 liters of wine.\f* \rb and 20,000|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |אָֽלֶף׃פ\rb* \rb baths|בַּתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb of olive oil|וְשֶׁ֕מֶן\rb*.\f + \fr 2:10 \ft Or \fqa 20,000 baths of oil\ft ; that is, approximately 116,000 gallons or 440,000 liters\f*”
\s1 Hiram’s Reply to Solomon
\r (1 Kings 5:7–12)
\p \v 11 \rb Then|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb Hiram|חוּרָ֤ם\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Tyre|צֹר֙\rb* \rb wrote a letter|בִּכְתָ֔ב\rb* \rb in reply|וַיִּשְׁלַ֖ח\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֑ה\rb*:
\pmo “\rb Because the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb loves|בְּאַהֲבַ֤ת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb His people|עַמּ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb He has set you|נְתָנְךָ֥\rb* \rb over them|עֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb as king|מֶֽלֶךְ׃\rb*.”
\pmo \v 12 \rb And Hiram|חוּרָם֒\rb* \rb added|וַיֹּאמֶר֮\rb*:
\pmo “\rb Blessed be|בָּר֤וּךְ\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb made|עָשָׂ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the heavens|הַשָּׁמַ֖יִם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the earth|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*! \rb He|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb has given|נָתַן֩\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb David|לְדָוִ֨יד\rb* \rb a wise|חָכָ֗ם\rb*\rb |יוֹדֵ֙עַ֙\rb* \rb son|בֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb with insight|שֵׂ֣כֶל\rb* \rb and understanding|וּבִינָ֔ה\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb will build|יִבְנֶה־\rb* \rb a temple|בַּ֙יִת֙\rb* \rb for the LORD|לַיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and a royal|לְמַלְכוּתֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb palace for himself|וּבַ֖יִת\rb*.
\b 
\pmo \v 13 \rb So now I|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb am sending you|שָׁלַ֧חְתִּי\rb* \rb Huram-abi|לְחוּרָ֥ם\rb*,\rb |אָבִֽי׃\rb* \rb a skillful|חָכָ֛ם\rb* \rb man|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb endowed|יוֹדֵ֥עַ\rb* \rb with creativity|בִּינָ֖ה\rb*.\f + \fr 2:13 \ft Or \fqa understanding\f* \v 14 \rb He is the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of a woman|אִשָּׁ֞ה\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the daughters|בְּנ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of Dan|דָּ֗ן\rb*, \rb and his father|וְאָבִ֣יו\rb* \rb is a man|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb of Tyre|צֹרִ֡י\rb*. \rb He is skilled|יוֹדֵ֡עַ\rb* \rb in work|לַעֲשׂ֣וֹת\rb* \rb with gold|בַּזָּֽהָב־\rb* \rb and silver|וּ֠בַכֶּסֶף\rb*, \rb bronze|בַּנְּחֹ֨שֶׁת\rb* \rb and iron|בַּבַּרְזֶ֜ל\rb*, \rb stone|בָּאֲבָנִ֣ים\rb* \rb and wood|וּבָעֵצִ֗ים\rb*, \rb purple|בָּאַרְגָּמָ֤ן\rb*, \rb blue|בַּתְּכֵ֙לֶת֙\rb*, \rb and crimson yarn|וּבַכַּרְמִ֔יל\rb*, \rb and fine linen|וּבַבּ֣וּץ\rb*. \rb He is experienced in every kind|כָּל־\rb* \rb of engraving|וּלְפַתֵּ֙חַ֙\rb*\rb |פִּתּ֔וּחַ\rb* \rb and can execute|וְלַחְשֹׁ֖ב\rb* \rb any|כָּל־\rb* \rb design|מַחֲשָׁ֑בֶת\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb is given|יִנָּֽתֶן־\rb* \rb him|לוֹ֙\rb*. \rb He will work with|עִם־\rb* \rb your craftsmen|חֲכָמֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb and with those|וְֽחַכְמֵ֔י\rb* \rb of my lord|אֲדֹנִ֖י\rb*, \rb your father|אָבִֽיךָ׃\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֥יד\rb*.
\b 
\pmo \v 15 \rb Now|וְ֠עַתָּה\rb* \rb let my lord|אֲדֹנִ֔י\rb* \rb send|יִשְׁלַ֖ח\rb* \rb to his servants|לַעֲבָדָֽיו׃\rb* \rb the wheat|הַחִטִּ֨ים\rb*, \rb barley|וְהַשְּׂעֹרִ֜ים\rb*, \rb olive oil|הַשֶּׁ֤מֶן\rb*, \rb and wine|וְהַיַּ֙יִן֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he promised|אָמַ֣ר\rb*. \v 16 \rb We|וַ֠אֲנַחְנוּ\rb* \rb will cut|נִכְרֹ֨ת\rb* \rb logs|עֵצִ֤ים\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb Lebanon|הַלְּבָנוֹן֙\rb*, \rb as many|כְּכָל־\rb* \rb as you need|צָרְכֶּ֔ךָ\rb*, \rb and we will float them|וּנְבִיאֵ֥ם\rb* \rb to you|לְךָ֛\rb* \rb as rafts|רַפְסֹד֖וֹת\rb* \rb by|עַל־\rb* \rb sea|יָ֣ם\rb* \rb down to Joppa|יָפ֑וֹ\rb*. \rb Then you|וְאַתָּ֛ה\rb* \rb can take them up|תַּעֲלֶ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃פ\rb*.”
\p \v 17 \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֗ה\rb* \rb numbered|וַיִּסְפֹּ֣ר\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the foreign|הַגֵּירִים֙\rb* \rb men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֤ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb following|אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb the census|הַסְּפָ֔ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |סְפָרָ֖ם\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֑יו\rb* \rb David had conducted|דָּוִ֣יד\rb*, \rb and there were found to be|וַיִּמָּצְא֗וּ\rb* \rb 153,600 in all|מֵאָ֤ה\rb*\rb |וַחֲמִשִּׁים֙\rb*\rb |אֶ֔לֶף\rb*\rb |וּשְׁלֹ֥שֶׁת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִ֖ים\rb*\rb |וְשֵׁ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵאֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 18 \rb Solomon made|וַיַּ֨עַשׂ\rb*\rb |מֵהֶ֜ם\rb* \rb 70,000 of them|שִׁבְעִ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֶ֙לֶף֙\rb* \rb porters|סַבָּ֔ל\rb*, \rb 80,000|וּשְׁמֹנִ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֶ֖לֶף\rb* \rb stonecutters|חֹצֵ֣ב\rb* \rb in the mountains|בָּהָ֑ר\rb*, \rb and 3,600|וּשְׁלֹ֤שֶׁת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִים֙\rb*\rb |וְשֵׁ֣שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵא֔וֹת\rb* \rb supervisors|מְנַצְּחִ֖ים\rb*\rb |לְהַעֲבִ֥יד\rb*\rb |הָעָֽם׃\rb*.\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\c 3
\s1 Temple Construction Begins
\r (1 Kings 6:1–4)
\p \v 1 \rb Then Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֗ה\rb* \rb began|וַיָּ֣חֶל\rb* \rb to build|לִבְנ֤וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּיר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb on Mount|בְּהַר֙\rb* \rb Moriah|הַמּ֣וֹרִיָּ֔ה\rb*, \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD had appeared|נִרְאָ֖ה\rb*\f + \fr 3:1 \ft See LXX; Hebrew \fqa where He had appeared\f* \rb to his father|אָבִ֑יהוּ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb David|לְדָוִ֣יד\rb*. \rb This was the place that|בִּמְק֣וֹם\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֔יד\rb* \rb had prepared|הֵכִין֙\rb* \rb on the threshing floor|בְּגֹ֖רֶן\rb* \rb of Ornan|אָרְנָ֥ן\rb*\f + \fr 3:1 \fqa Ornan \ft is a variant of \fqa Araunah\ft ; see 2 Samuel 24:16.\f* \rb the Jebusite|הַיְבוּסִֽי׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb Solomon began|וַ֠יָּחֶל\rb* \rb construction|לִבְנ֞וֹת\rb* \rb on the second day|בַּשֵּׁנִ֔י\rb* \rb of the second|הַשֵּׁנִי֙\rb* \rb month|בַּחֹ֤דֶשׁ\rb* \rb in the fourth|אַרְבַּ֖ע\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַ֥ת\rb* \rb of his reign|לְמַלְכוּתֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb |וְאֵ֙לֶּה֙\rb* \rb The foundation|הוּסַ֣ד\rb* \rb that Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֔ה\rb* \rb laid|לִבְנ֖וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb for the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb* \rb was sixty|שִׁשִּׁ֔ים\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּ֞וֹת\rb* \rb long|הָאֹ֡רֶךְ\rb* \rb and twenty|עֶשְׂרִֽים׃\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּ֥וֹת\rb* \rb wide|וְרֹ֖חַב\rb*,\f + \fr 3:3 \ft The foundation was approximately 90 feet long and 30 feet wide (27.4 meters long and 9.1 meters wide).\f* \rb according to the old|הָרִֽאשׁוֹנָה֙\rb* \rb standard|בַּמִּדָּ֤ה\rb*\rb |אַמּ֣וֹת\rb*.\f + \fr 3:3 \ft The old standard of measurement was a cubit equal to 18 inches or 45.7 centimeters. The new standard, a cubit of approximately 21 inches or 53.3 centimeters (the long cubit) is the basic unit of length throughout Ezekiel 40 to 48.\f* \v 4 \rb The portico|וְהָאוּלָ֡ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb at|עַל־\rb* \rb the front|פְּנֵ֨י\rb*,\rb |הָאֹ֜רֶךְ\rb* \rb extending across|עַל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֤י\rb* \rb the width|רֹֽחַב־\rb* \rb of the temple|הַבַּ֙יִת֙\rb*, \rb was twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֔ים\rb* \rb cubits long|אַמּ֣וֹת\rb*\f + \fr 3:4 \fqa 20 cubits \ft is approximately 30 feet or 9.1 meters; also in verses 8, 11, and 13.\f* \rb and|מֵאָ֣ה\rb* \rb twenty cubits|וְעֶשְׂרִ֑ים\rb* \rb high|וְהַגֹּ֖בַהּ\rb*.\f + \fr 3:4 \ft Some LXX and Syriac manuscripts; Hebrew \fqa 120 cubits high \ft (approximately 180 feet or 54.9 meters)\f* \rb He overlaid|וַיְצַפֵּ֥הוּ\rb* \rb the inside|מִפְּנִ֖ימָה\rb* \rb with pure|טָהֽוֹר׃\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֥ב\rb*.
\s1 The Temple’s Interior
\r (1 Kings 6:14–22)
\p \v 5 \rb |וְאֵ֣ת׀\rb* \rb He paneled|חִפָּה֙\rb* \rb the main|הַגָּד֗וֹל\rb* \rb room|הַבַּ֣יִת\rb* \rb with|עֵ֣ץ\rb* \rb cypress|בְּרוֹשִׁ֔ים\rb*,\f + \fr 3:5 \ft Or \fqa pine \ft or \fqa juniper \ft or \fqa fir\f* \rb which he overlaid|וַיְחַפֵּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb with fine|ט֑וֹב\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֣ב\rb* \rb and decorated|וַיַּ֧עַל\rb*\rb |עָלָ֛יו\rb* \rb with palm trees|תִּמֹרִ֖ים\rb* \rb and chains|וְשַׁרְשְׁרֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb He adorned|וַיְצַ֧ף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the temple|הַבַּ֛יִת\rb* \rb with precious|יְקָרָ֖ה\rb* \rb stones|אֶ֥בֶן\rb* \rb for beauty|לְתִפְאָ֑רֶת\rb*, \rb and its gold|וְהַזָּהָ֖ב\rb* \rb was|זְהַ֥ב\rb* \rb from Parvaim|פַּרְוָֽיִם׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb He overlaid|וַיְחַ֨ף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb its|הַבַּ֜יִת\rb* \rb beams|הַקֹּר֧וֹת\rb*, \rb thresholds|הַסִּפִּ֛ים\rb*, \rb walls|וְקִֽירוֹתָ֥יו\rb*, \rb and doors|וְדַלְתוֹתָ֖יו\rb* \rb with gold|זָהָ֑ב\rb*, \rb and he carved|וּפִתַּ֥ח\rb* \rb cherubim|כְּרוּבִ֖ים\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the walls|הַקִּירֽוֹת׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb Then he made|וַיַּ֙עַשׂ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Most Holy|קֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*\rb |הַקֳּדָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb Place|בֵּֽית־\rb*;\f + \fr 3:8 \ft Or \fqa the Holy of Holies\ft ; also in verse 10\f* \rb its length|אָרְכּ֞וֹ\rb* \rb corresponded to|עַל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֤י\rb* \rb the width|רֹֽחַב־\rb* \rb of the temple|הַבַּ֙יִת֙\rb*— \rb twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֔ים\rb* \rb cubits long|אַמּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb and twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֑ים\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb wide|וְרָחְבּ֖וֹ\rb*. \rb And he overlaid the inside|וַיְחַפֵּ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb with six|שֵׁ֥שׁ\rb* \rb hundred|מֵאֽוֹת׃\rb* \rb talents|לְכִכָּרִ֖ים\rb* \rb of fine|ט֔וֹב\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֣ב\rb*.\f + \fr 3:8 \fqa 600 talents \ft is approximately 22.6 tons or 20.5 metric tons of gold.\f* \v 9 \rb The weight|וּמִשְׁקָ֛ל\rb* \rb of the nails|לְמִסְמְר֥וֹת\rb* \rb was fifty|חֲמִשִּׁ֣ים\rb* \rb shekels|לִשְׁקָלִ֖ים\rb* \rb of gold|זָהָ֑ב\rb*.\f + \fr 3:9 \fqa 50 shekels \ft is approximately 1.26 pounds or 569.8 grams of gold.\f* \rb He also overlaid|חִפָּ֥ה\rb* \rb the upper rooms|וְהָעֲלִיּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb with gold|זָהָֽב׃\rb*.
\s1 The Cherubim
\r (1 Kings 6:23–30)
\p \v 10 \rb In the Most Holy|קֹ֤דֶשׁ\rb*\rb |הַקֳּדָשִׁים֙\rb* \rb Place|בְּבֵֽית־\rb* \rb he made|וַיַּ֜עַשׂ\rb* \rb two|שְׁנַ֔יִם\rb* \rb cherubim|כְּרוּבִ֣ים\rb* \rb of sculptured|צַעֲצֻעִ֑ים\rb* \rb work|מַעֲשֵׂ֖ה\rb*, \rb and he overlaid|וַיְצַפּ֥וּ\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb with gold|זָהָֽב׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb The total|אָרְכָּ֖ם\rb* \rb wingspan|וְכַנְפֵי֙\rb* \rb of the cherubim|הַכְּרוּבִ֔ים\rb* \rb was twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֑ים\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּ֣וֹת\rb*. \rb One wing|כְּנַ֨ף\rb* \rb of the first cherub|הָאֶחָ֜ד\rb* \rb was five|חָמֵ֗שׁ\rb* \rb cubits long|לְאַמּ֣וֹת\rb*\f + \fr 3:11 \fqa 5 cubits \ft is approximately 7.5 feet or 2.3 meters; also in verse 15.\f* \rb and touched|מַגַּ֙עַת֙\rb* \rb the wall|לְקִ֣יר\rb* \rb of the temple|הַבַּ֔יִת\rb*, \rb and its other|הָאַחֶ֙רֶת֙\rb* \rb wing|וְהַכָּנָ֤ף\rb* \rb was five|חָמֵ֔שׁ\rb* \rb cubits long|אַמּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb and touched|מַגִּ֕יעַ\rb* \rb the wing|לִכְנַ֖ף\rb* \rb of the other|הָאַחֵֽר׃\rb* \rb cherub|הַכְּר֥וּב\rb*. \v 12 \rb The wing|וּכְנַ֨ף\rb* \rb of the second|הָאֶחָד֙\rb* \rb cherub|הַכְּר֤וּב\rb* \rb also measured five|חָמֵ֔שׁ\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb and touched|מַגִּ֖יעַ\rb* \rb the wall|לְקִ֣יר\rb* \rb of the temple|הַבָּ֑יִת\rb*, \rb while its other|הָאַחֶ֙רֶת֙\rb* \rb wing|וְהַכָּנָ֤ף\rb* \rb measured five|חָמֵ֔שׁ\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb and touched|דְּבֵקָ֕ה\rb* \rb the wing|לִכְנַ֖ף\rb* \rb of the first|הָאַחֵֽר׃\rb* \rb cherub|הַכְּר֥וּב\rb*. \v 13 \rb So the total wingspan|כַּנְפֵי֙\rb*\rb |פֹּֽרְשִׂ֖ים\rb* \rb of these|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb cherubim|הַכְּרוּבִ֣ים\rb* \rb was twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֑ים\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּ֣וֹת\rb*. \rb They|וְהֵ֛ם\rb* \rb stood|עֹמְדִ֥ים\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb their feet|רַגְלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*, \rb facing|וּפְנֵיהֶ֥ם\rb* \rb the main room|לַבָּֽיִת׃ס\rb*.
\s1 The Veil and Pillars
\r (1 Kings 7:13–22)
\p \v 14 \rb He made|וַיַּ֙עַשׂ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the veil|הַפָּרֹ֔כֶת\rb* \rb of blue|תְּכֵ֥לֶת\rb*, \rb purple|וְאַרְגָּמָ֖ן\rb*, \rb and crimson yarn|וְכַרְמִ֣יל\rb* \rb and fine linen|וּב֑וּץ\rb*, \rb with cherubim|כְּרוּבִֽים׃ס\rb* \rb woven|וַיַּ֥עַל\rb* \rb into it|עָלָ֖יו\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb In front|לִפְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of the temple|הַבַּ֙יִת֙\rb* \rb he made|וַיַּ֜עַשׂ\rb* \rb two|שְׁנַ֔יִם\rb* \rb pillars|עַמּוּדִ֣ים\rb*, \rb which together were thirty-five|שְׁלֹשִׁ֥ים\rb*\rb |וְחָמֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּ֕וֹת\rb* \rb high|אֹ֑רֶךְ\rb*,\f + \fr 3:15 \fqa 35 cubits \ft is approximately 52.5 feet or 16 meters.\f* \rb each with a capital|וְהַצֶּ֥פֶת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb top|רֹאשׁ֖וֹ\rb* \rb measuring five|חָמֵֽשׁ׃ס\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּ֥וֹת\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb He made|וַיַּ֤עַשׂ\rb* \rb interwoven|בַּדְּבִ֔יר\rb* \rb chains|שַׁרְשְׁרוֹת֙\rb*\f + \fr 3:16 \ft Or \fqa He made chains in the inner sanctuary\f* \rb and put them|וַיִּתֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb top|רֹ֣אשׁ\rb* \rb of the pillars|הָעַמֻּדִ֑ים\rb*. \rb He made|וַיַּ֤עַשׂ\rb* \rb a hundred|מֵאָ֔ה\rb* \rb pomegranates|רִמּוֹנִים֙\rb* \rb and fastened them|וַיִּתֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb into the chainwork|בַּֽשַּׁרְשְׁרֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb Then he set up|וַיָּ֤קֶם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the pillars|הָֽעַמּוּדִים֙\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb front|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the temple|הַהֵיכָ֔ל\rb*, \rb one|אֶחָ֥ד\rb* \rb on the south|מִיָּמִ֖ין\rb* \rb and one|וְאֶחָ֣ד\rb* \rb on the north|מֵֽהַשְּׂמֹ֑אול\rb*. \rb The pillar on the south|הַיְמִינִי\rb* \rb he named|וַיִּקְרָ֤א\rb*\rb |שֵׁם־\rb* \rb Jachin|יָכִ֔ין\rb*,\f + \fr 3:17 \fqa Jachin \ft probably means \fqa He establishes\ft .\f* \rb and the pillar on the north|הַשְּׂמָאלִ֖י\rb* \rb he named|וְשֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb Boaz|בֹּֽעַז׃ס\rb*.\f + \fr 3:17 \fqa Boaz \ft probably means \fqa in Him is strength\ft .\f*
\c 4
\s1 The Bronze Altar and Molten Sea
\r (1 Kings 7:23–26)
\p \v 1 \rb He made|וַיַּ֙עַשׂ֙\rb* \rb a bronze|נְחֹ֔שֶׁת\rb* \rb altar|מִזְבַּ֣ח\rb* \rb twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֤ים\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּה֙\rb* \rb long|אָרְכּ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb twenty|וְעֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּ֖ה\rb* \rb wide|רָחְבּ֑וֹ\rb*, \rb and ten|וְעֶ֥שֶׂר\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb high|קוֹמָתֽוֹ׃ס\rb*.\f + \fr 4:1 \ft The altar was approximately 30 feet in length and width and 15 feet high (9.1 meters in length and width and 4.6 meters high).\f*
\p \v 2 \rb He also made|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Sea|הַיָּ֖ם\rb* \rb of cast metal|מוּצָ֑ק\rb*. \rb It was circular in shape|עָג֣וֹל׀\rb*\rb |סָבִ֗יב\rb*, \rb measuring ten|עֶ֣שֶׂר\rb* \rb cubits|בָּֽ֠אַמָּה\rb* \rb from rim|מִשְּׂפָת֨וֹ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb rim|שְׂפָת֜וֹ\rb*, \rb five|וְחָמֵ֤שׁ\rb* \rb cubits|בָּֽאַמָּה֙\rb* \rb in height|קֽוֹמָת֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and thirty|שְׁלֹשִׁ֣ים\rb* \rb cubits|בָּֽאַמָּ֔ה\rb* \rb in circumference|וְקָו֙\rb*\rb |יָסֹ֥ב\rb*\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb*\rb |סָבִֽיב׃\rb*.\f + \fr 4:2 \ft The Sea was approximately 15 feet from rim to rim, 7.5 feet in height, and 45 feet in circumference (4.6 meters from rim to rim, 2.3 meters in height, and 13.7 meters in circumference).\f* \v 3 \rb Below the rim|תַּ֨חַת\rb*, \rb figures|וּדְמ֣וּת\rb* \rb of oxen|בְּקָרִים֩\rb* \rb encircled|סָבִ֤יב׀\rb*\rb |סָבִיב֙\rb*\rb |סוֹבְבִ֣ים\rb* \rb it|אֹת֔וֹ\rb*, \rb ten|עֶ֚שֶׂר\rb* \rb per cubit|בָּֽאַמָּ֔ה\rb* \rb all the way|מַקִּיפִ֥ים\rb* \rb around|סָבִ֑יב\rb* \rb the Sea|הַיָּ֖ם\rb*,\rb |הַבָּקָ֔ר\rb* \rb cast|יְצוּקִ֖ים\rb* \rb in two|שְׁנַ֤יִם\rb* \rb rows|טוּרִים֙\rb* \rb as a part of the Sea|בְּמֻֽצַקְתּֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb The Sea stood|עוֹמֵ֞ד\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb twelve|שְׁנֵ֧ים\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֣ר\rb* \rb oxen|בָּקָ֗ר\rb*, \rb three|שְׁלֹשָׁ֣ה\rb* \rb facing|פֹנִ֣ים׀\rb* \rb north|צָפ֡וֹנָה\rb*, \rb three|וּשְׁלוֹשָׁה֩\rb* \rb facing|פֹנִ֨ים׀\rb* \rb west|יָ֜מָּה\rb*, \rb three|וּשְׁלֹשָׁ֣ה׀\rb* \rb facing|פֹּנִ֣ים\rb* \rb south|נֶ֗גְבָּה\rb*, \rb and three|וּשְׁלֹשָׁה֙\rb* \rb facing|פֹּנִ֣ים\rb* \rb east|מִזְרָ֔חָה\rb*. \rb The Sea|וְהַיָּ֥ם\rb* \rb rested on them|עֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |מִלְמָ֑עְלָה\rb*, \rb with all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb their hindquarters|אֲחֹרֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb toward the center|בָּֽיְתָה׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb It was a handbreadth|טֶ֔פַח\rb* \rb thick|וְעָבְי֣וֹ\rb*,\f + \fr 4:5 \fqa A handbreadth \ft is approximately 2.9 inches or 7.4 centimeters.\f* \rb and its rim|וּשְׂפָתוֹ֙\rb* \rb was fashioned|כְּמַעֲשֵׂ֣ה\rb* \rb like the brim|שְׂפַת־\rb* \rb of a cup|כּ֔וֹס\rb*, \rb like a lily|שֽׁוֹשַׁנָּ֑ה\rb*\rb |מַחֲזִ֣יק\rb* \rb blossom|פֶּ֖רַח\rb*. \rb It could hold|יָכִֽיל׃ס\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb thousand|אֲלָפִ֖ים\rb* \rb baths|בַּתִּ֔ים\rb*.\f + \fr 4:5 \fqa 3,000 baths \ft is approximately 17,400 gallons or 66,000 liters.\f*
\s1 The Ten Basins, Lampstands, and Tables
\r (1 Kings 7:38–39)
\p \v 6 \rb He also made|וַיַּ֣עַשׂ\rb* \rb ten|עֲשָׂרָה֒\rb* \rb basins|כִּיּוֹרִים֮\rb* \rb for washing|לְרָחְצָ֣ה\rb* \rb and placed|וַ֠יִּתֵּן\rb* \rb five|חֲמִשָּׁ֨ה\rb* \rb on the south side|מִיָּמִ֜ין\rb* \rb and five|וַחֲמִשָּׁ֤ה\rb* \rb on the north|מִשְּׂמֹאול֙\rb*. \rb The parts|מַעֲשֵׂ֥ה\rb* \rb of the burnt offering|הָעוֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb were rinsed|יָדִ֣יחוּ\rb* \rb in them|בָ֑ם\rb*, \rb but the priests used|לַכֹּהֲנִ֖ים\rb* \rb the Sea|וְהַיָּ֕ם\rb* \rb for washing|לְרָחְצָ֥ה\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb He made|וַ֠יַּעַשׂ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb ten|עֶ֖שֶׂר\rb* \rb gold|הַזָּהָ֛ב\rb* \rb lampstands|מְנֹר֧וֹת\rb* \rb according to their specifications|כְּמִשְׁפָּטָ֑ם\rb* \rb and placed them|וַיִּתֵּן֙\rb* \rb in the temple|בַּֽהֵיכָ֔ל\rb*, \rb five|חָמֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb on the south side|מִיָּמִ֖ין\rb* \rb and five|וְחָמֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb on the north|מִשְּׂמֹֽאול׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb Additionally, he made|וַיַּ֣עַשׂ\rb* \rb ten|עֲשָׂרָה֒\rb* \rb tables|שֻׁלְחָנוֹת֮\rb* \rb and placed them|וַיַּנַּח֙\rb* \rb in the temple|בַּֽהֵיכָ֔ל\rb*, \rb five|חֲמִשָּׁ֥ה\rb* \rb on the south side|מִיָּמִ֖ין\rb* \rb and five|וַחֲמִשָּׁ֣ה\rb* \rb on the north|מִשְּׂמֹ֑אול\rb*. \rb He also made|וַיַּ֛עַשׂ\rb* \rb a hundred|מֵאָֽה׃\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֖ב\rb* \rb bowls|מִזְרְקֵ֥י\rb*.
\s1 The Courts
\p \v 9 \rb He made|וַיַּ֙עַשׂ֙\rb* \rb the courtyard|חֲצַ֣ר\rb* \rb of the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֔ים\rb* \rb and the large|הַגְּדוֹלָ֑ה\rb* \rb court|וְהָעֲזָרָ֖ה\rb* \rb with its doors|וּדְלָת֧וֹת\rb*\rb |לָעֲזָרָ֛ה\rb*, \rb and he overlaid|צִפָּ֥ה\rb* \rb the doors|וְדַלְתוֹתֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb with bronze|נְחֹֽשֶׁת׃\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb He put|נָתַ֞ן\rb* \rb the Sea|הַיָּ֗ם\rb* \rb on the south|הַיְמָנִ֛ית\rb* \rb side|מִכֶּ֧תֶף\rb*, \rb at the southeast corner|קֵ֖דְמָה\rb*\rb |מִמּ֥וּל\rb*\rb |נֶֽגְבָּה׃\rb*.
\s1 Completion of the Bronze Works
\r (1 Kings 7:40–47)
\p \v 11 \rb Additionally, Huram|חוּרָ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb made|וַיַּ֣עַשׂ\rb* \rb the pots|הַ֨סִּיר֔וֹת\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb shovels|הַיָּעִ֖ים\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and sprinkling bowls|הַמִּזְרָק֑וֹתס\rb*.
\p \rb So Huram|חִירָם\rb* \rb finished|וַיְכַ֣ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the work|הַמְּלָאכָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he had undertaken|עָשָׂ֛ה\rb* \rb for King|לַמֶּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֖ה\rb* \rb in the house|בְּבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \v 12 \rb the two|שְׁנַ֔יִם\rb* \rb pillars|עַמּוּדִ֣ים\rb*;
\li1 \rb the two|שְׁתָּ֑יִם\rb* \rb bowl-shaped|וְהַגֻּלּ֧וֹת\rb* \rb capitals|וְהַכֹּתָר֛וֹת\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb atop|רֹ֥אשׁ\rb* \rb the pillars|הָעַמּוּדִ֖ים\rb*;
\li1 \rb the two|שְׁתַּ֔יִם\rb* \rb sets of network|וְהַשְּׂבָכ֣וֹת\rb* \rb covering|לְכַסּ֗וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb both|שְׁתֵּי֙\rb* \rb bowls|גֻּלּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the capitals|הַכֹּֽתָר֔וֹת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb atop|רֹ֥אשׁ\rb* \rb the pillars|הָֽעַמּוּדִֽים׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 13 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the four|אַרְבַּ֥ע\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֖וֹת\rb* \rb pomegranates|הָֽרִמּוֹנִ֛ים\rb* \rb for the two|לִשְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb sets of network|הַשְּׂבָכ֑וֹת\rb* \rb (two|שְׁנַ֨יִם\rb* \rb rows|טוּרִ֤ים\rb* \rb of pomegranates|רִמּוֹנִים֙\rb* \rb for each|הָאֶחָ֔ת\rb* \rb network|לַשְּׂבָכָ֣ה\rb* \rb covering|לְכַסּ֗וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb both|שְׁתֵּי֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb the bowl-shaped|גֻּלּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb capitals|הַכֹּֽתָר֔וֹת\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb atop|פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the pillars)|הָעַמּוּדִֽים׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 14 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the stands|הַמְּכֹנ֖וֹת\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֑ה\rb*;
\li1 \rb the basins|הַכִּיֹּר֥וֹת\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֖ה\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the stands|הַמְּכֹנֽוֹת׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 15 \rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |אֶחָ֑ד\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the Sea|הַיָּ֖ם\rb*;
\li1 \rb the twelve|שְׁנֵים־\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֖ר\rb* \rb oxen|הַבָּקָ֥ר\rb* \rb underneath the Sea|תַּחְתָּֽיו׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 16 \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the pots|הַ֠סִּירוֹת\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb shovels|הַיָּעִ֤ים\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb meat forks|הַמִּזְלָגוֹת֙\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the other articles|כְּלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*.
\p \rb All these objects that Huram-abi|חוּרָ֥ם\rb*\rb |אָבִ֛יו\rb* \rb made|עָשָׂ֞ה\rb* \rb for King|לַמֶּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֖ה\rb* \rb for the house|לְבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb were of polished|מָרֽוּק׃\rb* \rb bronze|נְחֹ֖שֶׁת\rb*. \v 17 \rb The king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*\rb |בַּעֲבִ֖י\rb* \rb had them cast|יְצָקָ֣ם\rb* \rb in clay molds|הָאֲדָמָ֑ה\rb* \rb in the plain|בְּכִכַּ֤ר\rb* \rb of the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּן֙\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb Succoth|סֻכּ֖וֹת\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֥ין\rb* \rb and Zeredah|צְרֵדָֽתָה׃\rb*.\f + \fr 4:17 \fqa Zeredah \ft is a variant of \fqa Zarethan\ft ; see 1 Kings 7:46.\f* \v 18 \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֛ה\rb* \rb made|וַיַּ֧עַשׂ\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb articles|הַכֵּלִ֥ים\rb* \rb in such great abundance|לָרֹ֣ב\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb that|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb the weight|מִשְׁקַ֥ל\rb* \rb of the bronze|הַנְּחֹֽשֶׁת׃פ\rb* \rb could not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb be determined|נֶחְקַ֖ר\rb*.
\s1 Completion of the Gold Furnishings
\r (1 Kings 7:48–51)
\p \v 19 \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb also made|וַיַּ֣עַשׂ\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the furnishings|הַכֵּלִ֔ים\rb* \rb for|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb the golden|הַזָּהָ֔ב\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb altar|מִזְבַּ֣ח\rb*;
\li1 \rb the tables|הַשֻּׁלְחָנ֔וֹת\rb* \rb on which was placed|וַעֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb the Bread|לֶ֥חֶם\rb* \rb of the Presence|הַפָּנִֽים׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 20 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the lampstands|הַמְּנֹר֞וֹת\rb* \rb of pure|סָגֽוּר׃\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֥ב\rb* \rb and their lamps|וְנֵרֹתֵיהֶ֗ם\rb*, \rb to burn|לְבַעֲרָ֧ם\rb* \rb in front|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the inner sanctuary|הַדְּבִ֖יר\rb* \rb as prescribed|כַּמִּשְׁפָּ֛ט\rb*;
\li1 \v 21 \rb the flowers|וְהַפֶּ֧רַח\rb*, \rb lamps|וְהַנֵּר֛וֹת\rb*,\rb |ה֖וּא\rb* \rb and tongs|וְהַמֶּלְקַחַ֖יִם\rb* \rb of gold|זָהָ֑ב\rb*— \rb of purest|מִכְל֥וֹת\rb* \rb gold|זָהָֽב׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 22 \rb the wick trimmers|וְהַֽמְזַמְּר֧וֹת\rb*, \rb sprinkling bowls|וְהַמִּזְרָק֛וֹת\rb*, \rb ladles|וְהַכַּפּ֥וֹת\rb*, \rb and censers|וְהַמַּחְתּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb of pure|סָג֑וּר\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֣ב\rb*;
\li1 \rb and the gold|זָהָֽב׃\rb* \rb doors|וּפֶ֣תַח\rb* \rb of the temple|הַ֠בַּיִת\rb*: \rb the inner|הַפְּנִימִיּ֜וֹת\rb* \rb doors|דַּלְתוֹתָ֨יו\rb* \rb to the Most Holy Place|לְקֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*\rb |הַקֳּדָשִׁ֗ים\rb*\f + \fr 4:22 \ft Or \fqa the Holy of Holies\f* \rb as well as the doors|וְדַלְתֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the main hall|הַבַּ֛יִת\rb*\rb |לַהֵיכָ֖ל\rb*.
\c 5
\s1 The Ark Enters the Temple
\r (1 Kings 8:1–11)
\p \v 1 \rb So all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the work|הַמְּלָאכָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֖ה\rb* \rb had performed|עָשָׂ֥ה\rb* \rb for the house|לְבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑הס\rb* \rb was completed|וַתִּשְׁלַם֙\rb*.
\p \rb Then Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb brought in the items|וַיָּבֵ֨א\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֗יו\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֣יד\rb* \rb had dedicated|קָדְשֵׁ֣י׀\rb*— \rb the silver|הַכֶּ֤סֶף\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the gold|הַזָּהָב֙\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the furnishings|הַכֵּלִ֔ים\rb*— \rb and he placed them|נָתַ֕ן\rb* \rb in the treasuries|בְּאֹצְר֖וֹת\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִֽים׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb At that time|אָז֩\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb assembled|יַקְהֵ֨יל\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb the elders|זִקְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb*—\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the tribal|הַמַּטּ֜וֹת\rb* \rb heads|רָאשֵׁ֨י\rb* \rb and family leaders|הָאָב֛וֹת\rb*\rb |נְשִׂיאֵ֧י\rb*\rb |לִבְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* — \rb to bring up|לְֽהַעֲל֞וֹת\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֧וֹן\rb* \rb of the covenant|בְּרִית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הִ֥יא\rb* \rb from Zion|צִיּֽוֹן׃\rb*, \rb the City|מֵעִ֥יר\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֖יד\rb*. \v 3 \rb So all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the men|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb came together|וַיִּקָּהֲל֧וּ\rb* \rb to the king|הַמֶּ֛לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb at the feast|בֶּחָ֑ג\rb* \rb in the seventh|הַשְּׁבִעִֽי׃\rb* \rb month|הַחֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb*.\f + \fr 5:3 \ft That is, the Feast of Tabernacles (or Booths or Shelters); see Leviticus 23:33–36.\f*
\p \v 4 \rb When all|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb the elders|זִקְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb had arrived|וַיָּבֹ֕אוּ\rb*, \rb the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took up|וַיִּשְׂא֥וּ\rb* \rb the ark|הָאָרֽוֹן׃\rb*, \v 5 \rb and they brought up|וַיַּעֲל֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ark|הָאָרוֹן֙\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the Tent|אֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵ֔ד\rb* \rb with|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb its|בָּאֹ֑הֶל\rb* \rb sacred|הַקֹּ֖דֶשׁ\rb* \rb furnishings|כְּלֵ֥י\rb*. \rb The Levitical|הַלְוִיִּֽם׃\rb* \rb priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֖ים\rb* \rb carried them up|הֶעֱל֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֔ם\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb There, before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the ark|הָאָר֑וֹן\rb*, \rb King|וְהַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֗ה\rb* \rb and the whole|וְכָל־\rb* \rb congregation|עֲדַ֧ת\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb who had assembled|הַנּוֹעָדִ֥ים\rb* \rb with him|עָלָ֖יו\rb* \rb sacrificed|מְזַבְּחִים֙\rb* \rb so many|מֵרֹֽב׃\rb* \rb sheep|צֹ֣אן\rb* \rb and oxen|וּבָקָ֔ר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb they could not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb be counted|יִסָּפְר֛וּ\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb or numbered|יִמָּנ֖וּ\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb Then the priests|הַ֠כֹּהֲנִים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb brought|וַיָּבִ֣יאוּ\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֨וֹן\rb* \rb of the covenant|בְּרִית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb its place|מְקוֹמ֛וֹ\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb the inner sanctuary|דְּבִ֥יר\rb* \rb of the temple|הַבַּ֖יִת\rb*,\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the Most Holy Place|קֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*\rb |הַקְּדָשִׁ֑ים\rb*,\f + \fr 5:7 \ft Or \fqa the Holy of Holies\f*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb beneath|תַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb the wings|כַּנְפֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the cherubim|הַכְּרוּבִֽים׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb For|וַיִּהְי֤וּ\rb* \rb the cherubim|הַכְּרוּבִים֙\rb* \rb spread|פֹּרְשִׂ֣ים\rb* \rb their wings|כְּנָפַ֔יִם\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the place|מְק֖וֹם\rb* \rb of the ark|הָאָר֑וֹן\rb*\rb |הַכְּרוּבִ֛ים\rb* \rb and overshadowed|וַיְכַסּ֧וּ\rb*\rb |מִלְמָֽעְלָה׃\rb* \rb the ark|הָאָר֥וֹן\rb* \rb and|וְעַל־\rb* \rb its poles|בַּדָּ֖יו\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb The poles|הַבַּדִּים֒\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb the ark|הָאָרוֹן֙\rb* \rb extended far enough|וַֽיַּאֲרִיכוּ֮\rb* \rb that their|הַבַּדִּ֤ים\rb* \rb ends|רָאשֵׁ֨י\rb* \rb were visible|וַיֵּרָאוּ֩\rb* \rb from|עַל־\rb* \rb in front|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the inner sanctuary|הַדְּבִ֔יר\rb*,\f + \fr 5:9 \ft Some Hebrew manuscripts and LXX \fqa The poles extended far enough that their ends were visible from the Holy Place in front of the inner sanctuary\ft ; see 1 Kings 8:8.\f* \rb but not|וְלֹ֥א\rb*\rb |יֵרָא֖וּ\rb* \rb from outside the Holy Place|הַח֑וּצָה\rb*;\f + \fr 5:9 \ft Literally \fqa not from outside\f* \rb and they are|וַֽיְהִי־\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֔ם\rb* \rb to|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb There was nothing|אֵ֚ין\rb* \rb in the ark|בָּֽאָר֔וֹן\rb* \rb except|רַ֚ק\rb* \rb the two|שְׁנֵ֣י\rb* \rb tablets|הַלֻּח֔וֹת\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb had placed in it|נָתַ֥ן\rb* \rb at Horeb|בְּחֹרֵ֑ב\rb*,\f + \fr 5:10 \ft That is, Mount Sinai, or possibly a mountain in the range containing Mount Sinai\f* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb had made a covenant|כָּרַ֤ת\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb after they had come out|בְּצֵאתָ֖ם\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִמִּצְרָֽיִם׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb Now|כִּ֠י\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֤ים\rb* \rb who were present|הַֽנִּמְצְאִים֙\rb* \rb had consecrated themselves|הִתְקַדָּ֔שׁוּ\rb* \rb regardless of|אֵ֖ין\rb*\rb |לִשְׁמ֥וֹר\rb* \rb their divisions|לְמַחְלְקֽוֹת׃\rb*. \rb And when|וַיְהִ֕י\rb* \rb the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֖ים\rb* \rb came out|בְּצֵ֥את\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb the Holy Place|הַקֹּ֑דֶשׁ\rb*, \v 12 \rb all|לְכֻלָּ֡ם\rb* \rb the Levitical|וְהַלְוִיִּ֣ם\rb* \rb singers|הַמְשֹׁרֲרִ֣ים\rb* — \rb Asaph|לְאָסָ֡ף\rb*, \rb Heman|לְהֵימָ֣ן\rb*, \rb Jeduthun|לִֽ֠ידֻתוּן\rb*, \rb and their sons|וְלִבְנֵיהֶ֨ם\rb* \rb and relatives|וְלַאֲחֵיהֶ֜ם\rb* — \rb stood|עֹמְדִ֖ים\rb* \rb on the east side|מִזְרָ֣ח\rb* \rb of the altar|לַמִּזְבֵּ֑חַ\rb*, \rb dressed|מְלֻבָּשִׁ֣ים\rb* \rb in fine linen|בּ֗וּץ\rb* \rb and playing cymbals|בִּמְצִלְתַּ֙יִם֙\rb*, \rb harps|וּבִנְבָלִ֣ים\rb*, \rb and lyres|וְכִנֹּר֔וֹת\rb*, \rb accompanied by|וְעִמָּהֶ֤ם\rb* \rb 120|לְמֵאָ֣ה\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִ֔ים\rb* \rb priests|כֹּֽהֲנִים֙\rb* \rb sounding|מַחְצְרִרִים\rb* \rb trumpets|בַּחֲצֹֽצְרֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb |וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb The trumpeters|לַמַּחֲצֹצְרִים\rb* \rb and singers|וְלַמְשֹֽׁרֲרִ֜ים\rb*\rb |לְהַשְׁמִ֣יעַ\rb* \rb joined together|כְ֠אֶחָד\rb* \rb to praise|לְהַלֵּ֣ל\rb* \rb and thank|וּלְהֹדוֹת֮\rb* \rb the LORD|לַיהוָה֒\rb* \rb with one|אֶחָ֗ד\rb* \rb voice|קוֹל־\rb*. \rb They lifted up|וּכְהָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb their voices|ק֠וֹל\rb*, \rb accompanied by trumpets|בַּחֲצֹצְר֨וֹת\rb*, \rb cymbals|וּבִמְצִלְתַּ֜יִם\rb*, \rb and musical|הַשִּׁ֗יר\rb* \rb instruments|וּבִכְלֵ֣י\rb*, \rb in praise|וּבְהַלֵּ֤ל\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָה֙\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb He is good|ט֔וֹב\rb*;\rb |כִּ֥י\rb*
\q2 \rb His loving devotion endures forever|חַסְדּ֑וֹ\rb*\rb |לְעוֹלָ֖ם\rb*.”
\p \rb And the temple|וְהַבַּ֛יִת\rb*, \rb the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*, \rb was filled|מָלֵ֥א\rb* \rb with a cloud|עָנָ֖ן\rb* \v 14 \rb so that the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֛ים\rb* \rb could|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb not|יָֽכְל֧וּ\rb* \rb stand there|לַעֲמ֥וֹד\rb* \rb to minister|לְשָׁרֵ֖ת\rb* \rb because|מִפְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the cloud|הֶעָנָ֑ן\rb*. \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the glory|כְבוֹד־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb filled|מָלֵ֥א\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִֽים׃פ\rb*.
\c 6
\s1 Solomon Blesses the LORD
\r (1 Kings 8:12–21)
\p \v 1 \rb Then|אָ֖ז\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֑ה\rb* \rb declared|אָמַ֣ר\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb The LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb has said|אָמַ֔ר\rb* \rb that He would dwell|לִשְׁכּ֖וֹן\rb*
\q2 \rb in the thick cloud|בָּעֲרָפֶֽל׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 2 \rb But I|וַֽאֲנִ֛י\rb* \rb have built|בָּנִ֥יתִי\rb* \rb You|לָ֑ךְ\rb* \rb an exalted|זְבֻ֖ל\rb* \rb house|בֵית־\rb*,
\q2 \rb a place|וּמָכ֥וֹן\rb* \rb for You to dwell|לְשִׁבְתְּךָ֖\rb* \rb forever|עוֹלָמִֽים׃\rb*.”
\p \v 3 \rb And as the whole|וְכָל־\rb* \rb assembly|קְהַ֥ל\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb stood there|עוֹמֵֽד׃\rb*, \rb the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |פָּנָ֔יו\rb* \rb turned around|וַיַּסֵּ֤ב\rb* \rb and blessed|וַיְבָ֕רֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb them all|כָּל־\rb*\rb |קְהַ֣ל\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \v 4 \rb and said|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*:
\pmo “\rb Blessed be|בָּר֤וּךְ\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb has fulfilled|מִלֵּ֖א\rb* \rb with His own hand|וּבְיָדָ֥יו\rb* \rb what He spoke|דִּבֶּ֣ר\rb* \rb with His mouth|בְּפִ֔יו\rb* \rb to|אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb my father|אָבִ֑י\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֣יד\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 5 ‘\rb Since|מִן־\rb* \rb the day|הַיּ֗וֹם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb I brought|הוֹצֵ֣אתִי\rb* \rb My people|עַמִּי֮\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb out of the land|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַיִם֒\rb*, \rb I have not|לֹא־\rb* \rb chosen|בָחַ֣רְתִּֽי\rb* \rb a city|בְעִ֗יר\rb* \rb from any|מִכֹּל֙\rb* \rb tribe|שִׁבְטֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb in which to build|לִבְנ֣וֹת\rb* \rb a house|בַּ֔יִת\rb* \rb so that My Name|שְׁמִ֖י\rb* \rb would be|לִהְי֥וֹת\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֑ם\rb*, \rb nor|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb have I chosen|בָחַ֣רְתִּֽי\rb* \rb anyone|בְאִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb to be|לִהְי֥וֹת\rb* \rb ruler|נָגִ֖יד\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb My people|עַמִּ֥י\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb But now I have chosen|וָאֶבְחַר֙\rb* \rb Jerusalem|בִּיר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb for My Name|שְׁמִ֖י\rb* \rb to be|לִהְי֥וֹת\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֑ם\rb*, \rb and I have chosen|וָאֶבְחַ֣ר\rb* \rb David|בְּדָוִ֔יד\rb* \rb to be|לִהְי֖וֹת\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb My people|עַמִּ֥י\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.’
\pmo \v 7 \rb Now it was|וַיְהִ֕י\rb* \rb in|עִם־\rb* \rb the heart|לְבַ֖ב\rb* \rb of my father|אָבִ֑י\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֣יד\rb* \rb to build|לִבְנ֣וֹת\rb* \rb a house|בַּ֔יִת\rb* \rb for the Name|לְשֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb But the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb my father|אָבִ֔י\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֣יד\rb*, ‘\rb Since|יַ֗עַן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb it was|הָיָה֙\rb* \rb in|עִם־\rb* \rb your heart|לְבָ֣בְךָ֔\rb* \rb to build|לִבְנ֥וֹת\rb* \rb a house|בַּ֖יִת\rb* \rb for My Name|לִשְׁמִ֑י\rb*, \rb you have done well|הֱ‍ֽטִיב֔וֹתָ\rb* \rb to have this|כִּ֥י\rb*\rb |הָיָ֖ה\rb* \rb in|עִם־\rb* \rb your heart|לְבָבֶֽךָ׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb Nevertheless|רַ֣ק\rb*, \rb you|אַתָּ֔ה\rb* \rb are not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb the one to build it|תִבְנֶ֖ה\rb*\rb |הַבָּ֑יִת\rb*; \rb but|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb your son|בִנְךָ֙\rb*, \rb your own offspring|הַיּוֹצֵ֣א\rb*\rb |מֵֽחֲלָצֶ֔יךָ\rb*\rb |הֽוּא־\rb*, \rb will build|יִבְנֶ֥ה\rb* \rb the house|הַבַּ֖יִת\rb* \rb for My Name|לִשְׁמִֽי׃\rb*.’
\pmo \v 10 \rb Now the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb has fulfilled|וַיָּ֣קֶם\rb* \rb the word|דְּבָר֖וֹ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb He spoke|דִּבֵּ֑ר\rb*. \rb I have succeeded|וָאָק֡וּם\rb*\rb |תַּחַת֩\rb* \rb my father|אָבִ֜י\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֨יד\rb*, \rb and I sit|וָאֵשֵׁ֣ב׀\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the throne|כִּסֵּ֣א\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb*, \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb promised|דִּבֶּ֣ר\rb*. \rb I have built|וָאֶבְנֶ֣ה\rb* \rb the house|הַבַּ֔יִת\rb* \rb for the Name|לְשֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb And there I have placed|וָאָשִׂ֥ים\rb*\rb |שָׁם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ark|הָ֣אָר֔וֹן\rb*, \rb which contains|שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb the covenant|בְּרִ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb He made|כָּרַ֖ת\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb the children|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.”
\s1 Solomon’s Prayer of Dedication
\r (1 Kings 8:22–53)
\p \v 12 \rb Then Solomon stood|וַֽיַּעֲמֹ֗ד\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵי֙\rb* \rb the altar|מִזְבַּ֣ח\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb in front of|נֶ֖גֶד\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb assembly|קְהַ֣ל\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb and spread out|וַיִּפְרֹ֖שׂ\rb* \rb his hands|כַּפָּֽיו׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb Now|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֜ה\rb* \rb had made|עָשָׂ֨ה\rb* \rb a bronze|נְחֹ֗שֶׁת\rb* \rb platform|כִּיּ֣וֹר\rb* \rb five|חָמֵ֨שׁ\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּ֜וֹת\rb* \rb long|אָרְכּ֗וֹ\rb*, \rb five|וְחָמֵ֤שׁ\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּוֹת֙\rb* \rb wide|רָחְבּ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and three|שָׁל֖וֹשׁ\rb* \rb cubits|וְאַמּ֥וֹת\rb* \rb high|קוֹמָת֑וֹ\rb*\f + \fr 6:13 \ft The platform was approximately 7.5 feet in length and width, and 4.5 feet high (2.3 meters in length and width, and 1.4 meters high).\f* \rb and had placed it|וַֽיִּתְּנֵהוּ֮\rb* \rb in the middle|בְּת֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb of the courtyard|הָעֲזָרָה֒\rb*. \rb He stood|וַיַּעֲמֹ֣ד\rb* \rb on it|עָלָ֗יו\rb*, \rb knelt down|וַיִּבְרַ֤ךְ\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |בִּרְכָּיו֙\rb* \rb before|נֶ֚גֶד\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb assembly|קְהַ֣ל\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb spread out|וַיִּפְרֹ֥שׂ\rb* \rb his hands|כַּפָּ֖יו\rb* \rb toward heaven|הַשָּׁמָֽיְמָה׃\rb*, \v 14 \rb and said|וַיֹּאמַ֗ר\rb*:
