\c 7
\s1 Fire from Heaven
\r (Psalm 136:1–26)
\p \v 1 \rb When Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹה֙\rb* \rb had finished|וּכְכַלּ֤וֹת\rb* \rb praying|לְהִתְפַּלֵּ֔ל\rb*, \rb fire|וְהָאֵ֗שׁ\rb* \rb came down|יָֽרְדָה֙\rb* \rb from heaven|מֵֽהַשָּׁמַ֔יִם\rb* \rb and consumed|וַתֹּ֥אכַל\rb* \rb the burnt offering|הָעֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb and the sacrifices|וְהַזְּבָחִ֑ים\rb*, \rb and the glory|וּכְב֥וֹד\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb filled|מָלֵ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the temple|הַבָּֽיִת׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb The priests|הַכֹּ֣הֲנִ֔ים\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb were unable|יָֽכְלוּ֙\rb* \rb to enter|לָב֖וֹא\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the glory|כְבוֹד־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had filled|מָלֵ֥א\rb* \rb it|בֵּ֥ית\rb*\rb |יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb When all|וְכֹ֣ל׀\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb saw|רֹאִים֙\rb* \rb the fire|הָאֵ֔שׁ\rb* \rb coming down|בְּרֶ֣דֶת\rb* \rb and the glory|וּכְב֥וֹד\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb above|עַל־\rb* \rb the temple|הַבָּ֑יִת\rb*, \rb they bowed down|וַיִּכְרְעוּ֩\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the pavement|הָרִֽצְפָה֙\rb* \rb with their faces|אַפַּ֨יִם\rb* \rb to the ground|אַ֤רְצָה\rb*, \rb and they worshiped|וַיִּֽשְׁתַּֽחֲו֔וּ\rb* \rb and gave thanks|וְהוֹד֤וֹת\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָה֙\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb He is good|ט֔וֹב\rb*;
\q2 \rb |כִּ֥י\rb* \rb His loving devotion|חַסְדּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb endures forever|לְעוֹלָ֖ם\rb*.”
\s1 Sacrifices of Dedication
\r (1 Kings 8:62–66)
\p \v 4 \rb Then the king|וְהַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֑ם\rb* \rb offered|זֹבְחִ֥ים\rb* \rb sacrifices|זֶ֖בַח\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*. \v 5 \rb And King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹה֮\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb offered|וַיִּזְבַּ֞ח\rb* \rb a sacrifice|זֶ֣בַח\rb* \rb of 22,000|עֶשְׂרִ֤ים\rb*\rb |וּשְׁנַ֙יִם֙\rb*\rb |אֶ֔לֶף\rb* \rb oxen|הַבָּקָ֗ר\rb* \rb and 120,000|מֵאָ֥ה\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אָ֑לֶף\rb* \rb sheep|וְצֹ֕אן\rb*. \rb So the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָֽם׃\rb* \rb dedicated|וַֽיַּחְנְכוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of God|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb The priests|וְהַכֹּהֲנִ֞ים\rb* \rb stood|עֹמְדִ֗ים\rb* \rb at|עַל־\rb* \rb their posts|מִשְׁמְרוֹתָ֣ם\rb*, \rb as did the Levites|וְהַלְוִיִּ֞ם\rb* \rb with the musical|שִׁ֤יר\rb* \rb instruments|בִּכְלֵי־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֣יד\rb* \rb had made|עָשָׂ֜ה\rb* \rb for giving thanks|לְהֹד֤וֹת\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָה֙\rb* \rb and with which David|דָּוִ֖יד\rb* \rb had offered praise, saying|בְּהַלֵּ֥ל\rb*, “\rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb His loving devotion|חַסְדּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb endures forever|לְעוֹלָ֣ם\rb*.”\rb |בְּיָדָ֑ם\rb* \rb Across from the Levites|נֶגְדָּ֔ם\rb*, \rb the priests|וְהַכֹּהֲנִים֙\rb* \rb sounded trumpets|מַחֲצֹצְרִים\rb*, \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb were standing|עֹמְדִֽים׃ס\rb*.
