\p \v 8 \rb So at that|הַהִ֜יא\rb* \rb time|בָּעֵ֨ת\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֣ל\rb* \rb with him|עִמּ֔וֹ\rb*— \rb a very|מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb great|גָּד֣וֹל\rb* \rb assembly of people|קָהָ֖ל\rb*\rb |מִלְּב֥וֹא\rb* \rb from Lebo-hamath|חֲמָ֖ת\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the Brook|נַ֥חַל\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*— \rb kept|וַיַּ֣עַשׂ\rb* \rb the feast|הֶ֠חָג\rb*\f + \fr 7:8 \ft That is, the Feast of Tabernacles (or Booths or Shelters); see Leviticus 23:33–36.\f* \rb for seven|שִׁבְעַ֤ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִים֙\rb*. \v 9 \rb On the eighth|הַשְּׁמִינִ֖י\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb they held|וַֽיַּעֲשׂ֛וּ\rb* \rb a solemn assembly|עֲצָ֑רֶת\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb the dedication|חֲנֻכַּ֣ת\rb* \rb of the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֗חַ\rb*\rb |עָשׂוּ֙\rb* \rb had lasted seven|שִׁבְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֔ים\rb*, \rb and the feast|וְהֶחָ֖ג\rb* \rb seven|שִׁבְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb days more|יָמִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb On the twenty-third|עֶשְׂרִ֤ים\rb*\rb |וּשְׁלֹשָׁה֙\rb* \rb day|וּבְי֨וֹם\rb* \rb of the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֔י\rb* \rb month|לַחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb Solomon sent the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb away|שִׁלַּ֥ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to their homes|לְאָהֳלֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb joyful|שְׂמֵחִים֙\rb* \rb and glad|וְט֣וֹבֵי\rb* \rb of heart|לֵ֔ב\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb the good things|הַטּוֹבָ֗ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb had done|עָשָׂ֤ה\rb* \rb for David|לְדָוִ֣יד\rb*, \rb for Solomon|וְלִשְׁלֹמֹ֔ה\rb*, \rb and for His people|עַמּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb Israel|וּלְיִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*.
\s1 The LORD’s Response to Solomon
\r (1 Kings 9:1–9)
\p \v 11 \rb When Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had finished|וַיְכַ֧ל\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the royal|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֨ת\rb* \rb palace|בֵּ֣ית\rb*, \rb successfully|הִצְלִֽיחַ׃פ\rb* \rb carrying out|הַבָּ֜א\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that was in|עַל־\rb* \rb his|שְׁלֹמֹ֗ה\rb* \rb heart|לֵ֣ב\rb* \rb to do|לַעֲשׂ֧וֹת\rb* \rb for the house|בְּבֵית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb and for his own palace|וּבְבֵית֖וֹ\rb*, \v 12 \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb appeared|וַיֵּרָ֧א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb him|שְׁלֹמֹ֖ה\rb* \rb at night|בַּלָּ֑יְלָה\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to him|ל֗וֹ\rb*:
\pmo “\rb I have heard|שָׁמַ֙עְתִּי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your prayer|תְּפִלָּתֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb and have chosen|וּבָחַ֜רְתִּי\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֛ה\rb* \rb place|בַּמָּק֥וֹם\rb* \rb for Myself|לִ֖י\rb* \rb as a house|לְבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb of sacrifice|זָֽבַח׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb If|הֵ֣ן\rb* \rb I close|אֶֽעֱצֹ֤ר\rb* \rb the sky|הַשָּׁמַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb so there is|יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb no|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb rain|מָטָ֔ר\rb*, \rb or if|וְהֵן־\rb* \rb I command|אֲצַוֶּ֥ה\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb the locust|חָגָ֖ב\rb* \rb to devour|לֶאֱכ֣וֹל\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*, \rb or if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb I send|אֲשַׁלַּ֥ח\rb* \rb a plague|דֶּ֖בֶר\rb* \rb among My people|בְּעַמִּֽי׃\rb*, \v 14 \rb and if My people|עַמִּ֜י\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb are called|נִֽקְרָא־\rb* \rb by|עֲלֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb My name|שְׁמִ֣י\rb* \rb humble themselves|וְיִכָּנְע֨וּ\rb* \rb and pray|וְיִֽתְפַּֽלְלוּ֙\rb* \rb and seek|וִֽיבַקְשׁ֣וּ\rb* \rb My face|פָנַ֔י\rb* \rb and turn|וְיָשֻׁ֖בוּ\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb their wicked|הָרָעִ֑ים\rb* \rb ways|מִדַּרְכֵיהֶ֣ם\rb*, \rb then I|וַאֲנִי֙\rb* \rb will hear|אֶשְׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb from heaven|הַשָּׁמַ֔יִם\rb*, \rb forgive|וְאֶסְלַח֙\rb* \rb their sin|לְחַטָּאתָ֔ם\rb*, \rb and heal|וְאֶרְפָּ֖א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their land|אַרְצָֽם׃\rb*.
\pmo \v 15 \rb Now|עַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb My eyes|עֵינַי֙\rb* \rb will be|יִהְי֣וּ\rb* \rb open|פְתֻח֔וֹת\rb* \rb and My ears|וְאָזְנַ֖י\rb* \rb attentive|קַשֻּׁב֑וֹת\rb* \rb to the prayers offered|לִתְפִלַּ֖ת\rb* \rb in this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb place|הַמָּק֥וֹם\rb*. \v 16 \rb |וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb For I have now chosen|בָּחַ֤רְתִּי\rb* \rb and consecrated|וְהִקְדַּ֙שְׁתִּי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb temple|הַבַּ֣יִת\rb* \rb so that My Name|שְׁמִ֥י\rb* \rb may be|לִהְיוֹת־\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb forever|עַד־\rb*\rb |עוֹלָ֑ם\rb*. \rb My eyes|עֵינַ֧י\rb* \rb and My heart|וְלִבִּ֛י\rb* \rb will be|וְהָי֨וּ\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb for all time|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִֽים׃\rb*.
\pmo \v 17 \rb And as for you|וְאַתָּ֞ה\rb*, \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb you walk|תֵּלֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb before Me|לְפָנַ֗י\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb your father|אָבִ֔יךָ\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֣יד\rb* \rb walked|הָלַךְ֙\rb*, \rb doing|וְלַעֲשׂ֕וֹת\rb* \rb all|כְּכֹ֖ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I have commanded you|צִוִּיתִ֑יךָ\rb*, \rb and if you keep|תִּשְׁמֽוֹר׃\rb* \rb My statutes|וְחֻקַּ֥י\rb* \rb and ordinances|וּמִשְׁפָּטַ֖י\rb*, \v 18 \rb then I will establish|וַהֲקִ֣ימוֹתִ֔י\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb your royal|מַלְכוּתֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb throne|כִּסֵּ֣א\rb*, \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I covenanted|כָּרַ֗תִּי\rb* \rb with your father|אָבִ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb David|לְדָוִ֤יד\rb* \rb when I said|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, ‘\rb You will never|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb fail|יִכָּרֵ֤ת\rb* \rb to have a man|אִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb to rule|מוֹשֵׁ֖ל\rb* \rb over Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.’
\pmo \v 19 \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֔ם\rb* \rb turn away|תְּשׁוּב֣וּן\rb* \rb and forsake|וַעֲזַבְתֶּם֙\rb* \rb the statutes|חֻקּוֹתַ֣י\rb* \rb and commandments|וּמִצְוֺתַ֔י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I have set|נָתַ֖תִּי\rb* \rb before you|לִפְנֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb and if you go off|וַהֲלַכְתֶּ֗ם\rb* \rb to serve|וַעֲבַדְתֶּם֙\rb* \rb and worship|וְהִשְׁתַּחֲוִיתֶ֖ם\rb* \rb other|אֲחֵרִ֔ים\rb* \rb gods|אֱלֹהִ֣ים\rb*, \v 20 \rb then I will uproot Israel|וּנְתַשְׁתִּ֗ים\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֤ל\rb* \rb the soil|אַדְמָתִי֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I have given|נָתַ֣תִּי\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb and I will banish|אַשְׁלִ֖יךְ\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb My presence|פָּנָ֑י\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb temple|הַבַּ֤יִת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I have sanctified|הִקְדַּ֣שְׁתִּי\rb* \rb for My Name|לִשְׁמִ֔י\rb*. \rb I will make it|וְאֶתְּנֶ֛נּוּ\rb* \rb an object of scorn|לְמָשָׁ֥ל\rb* \rb and ridicule|וְלִשְׁנִינָ֖ה\rb* \rb among all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the peoples|הָעַמִּֽים׃\rb*.
\pmo \v 21 \rb And when this|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb temple|וְהַבַּ֤יִת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb has become|הָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb a heap of rubble|עֶלְי֔וֹן\rb*,\f + \fr 7:21 \ft Some LXX manuscripts, Syriac, and Arabic; Hebrew \fqa And though this temple is now exalted\ft ; see also 1 Kings 9:8.\f* \rb all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb who pass|עֹבֵ֥ר\rb* \rb by it|עָלָ֖יו\rb* \rb will be appalled|יִשֹּׁ֑ם\rb* \rb and say|וְאָמַ֗ר\rb*, ‘\rb Why|בַּמֶּ֨ה\rb* \rb has the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb done|עָשָׂ֤ה\rb* \rb such a thing|כָּ֔כָה\rb* \rb to this|הַזֹּ֖את\rb* \rb land|לָאָ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb and to this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb temple|וְלַבַּ֥יִת\rb*?’ \v 22 \rb And others will answer|וְאָמְר֗וּ\rb*, ‘\rb Because|עַל֩\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb they have forsaken|עָֽזְב֜וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה׀\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of their fathers|אֲבֹתֵיהֶ֗ם\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb brought them|הוֹצִיאָם֮\rb* \rb out of the land|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַיִם֒\rb*, \rb and have embraced|וַֽיַּחֲזִ֙יקוּ֙\rb* \rb other|אֲחֵרִ֔ים\rb* \rb gods|בֵּאלֹהִ֣ים\rb*, \rb worshiping|וַיִּשְׁתַּחֲו֥וּ\rb* \rb and serving them|וַיַּֽעַבְד֑וּם\rb*— \rb because of|עַל־\rb* \rb this|כֵּן֙\rb*, \rb He has brought|הֵבִ֣יא\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּֽאת׃פ\rb* \rb disaster|הָרָעָ֖ה\rb* \rb upon them|עֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*.’”\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb*
\c 8
\s1 Solomon’s Additional Achievements
\r (1 Kings 9:10–28)
\p \v 1 \rb Now|וַיְהִ֞י\rb* \rb at the end|מִקֵּ֣ץ׀\rb* \rb of the twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֣ים\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֗ה\rb* \rb during which|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had built|בָּנָ֧ה\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb his own palace|בֵּיתֽוֹ׃\rb*, \v 2 \rb Solomon|לִשְׁלֹמֹ֔ה\rb* \rb rebuilt|בָּנָ֥ה\rb* \rb the cities|וְהֶעָרִ֗ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb Hiram|חוּרָם֙\rb*\f + \fr 8:2 \ft Hebrew \fqa Huram\ft , a variant of \fqa Hiram\ft ; also in verse 18\f* \rb had given|נָתַ֤ן\rb* \rb him|שְׁלֹמֹ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb and settled|וַיּ֥וֹשֶׁב\rb* \rb Israelites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb Then Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹה֙\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּ֤לֶךְ\rb*\rb |חֲמָ֣ת\rb* \rb to Hamath-zobah|צוֹבָ֔ה\rb* \rb and captured|וַיֶּחֱזַ֖ק\rb* \rb it|עָלֶֽיהָ׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb He built|וַיִּ֥בֶן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Tadmor|תַּדְמֹ֖ר\rb* \rb in the wilderness|בַּמִּדְבָּ֑ר\rb*, \rb in addition|וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb to all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the store|הַֽמִּסְכְּנ֔וֹת\rb* \rb cities|עָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he had built|בָּנָ֖ה\rb* \rb in Hamath|בַּחֲמָֽת׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb He rebuilt|וַיִּ֜בֶן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Upper|הָֽעֶלְי֔וֹן\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |בֵּ֥ית\rb*\rb |חוֹרוֹן֙\rb* \rb and Lower|הַתַּחְתּ֑וֹן\rb* \rb Beth-horon|חוֹר֖וֹן\rb* \rb as fortified|מָצ֔וֹר\rb* \rb cities|עָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb with walls|חוֹמ֖וֹת\rb*, \rb gates|דְּלָתַ֥יִם\rb*, \rb and bars|וּבְרִֽיחַ׃\rb*, \v 6 \rb as well as|וְאֶֽת־\rb* \rb Baalath|בַּעֲלָ֗ת\rb*,\rb |וְאֵ֨ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the store|הַֽמִּסְכְּנוֹת֙\rb* \rb cities|עָרֵ֤י\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb belonged to|הָי֣וּ\rb* \rb Solomon|לִשְׁלֹמֹ֔ה\rb*, \rb and|וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the cities|עָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb for his chariots|הָרֶ֔כֶב\rb* \rb and|וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb horses|הַפָּרָשִׁ֑ים\rb*\f + \fr 8:6 \ft Or \fqa horsemen \ft or \fqa charioteers\f* —\rb |וְאֵ֣ת׀\rb*\rb |עָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb whatever|כָּל־\rb*\rb |חֵ֣שֶׁק\rb* \rb he|שְׁלֹמֹ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb desired|חָשַׁק֙\rb* \rb to build|לִבְנ֤וֹת\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירֽוּשָׁלִַ֙ם֙\rb*, \rb Lebanon|וּבַלְּבָנ֔וֹן\rb*, \rb and throughout|וּבְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of his dominion|מֶמְשַׁלְתּֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb As for all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָ֠עָם\rb* \rb who remained|הַנּוֹתָ֨ר\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb the Hittites|הַחִתִּ֜י\rb*, \rb Amorites|וְהָאֱמֹרִ֤י\rb*, \rb Perizzites|וְהַפְּרִזִּי֙\rb*, \rb Hivites|וְהַחִוִּ֣י\rb*, \rb and Jebusites|וְהַיְבוּסִ֔י\rb* (\rb these people|אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb were not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb Israelites|מִיִּשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*\rb |הֵֽמָּה׃\rb*) — \v 8 \rb |מִן־\rb* \rb their descendants|בְּנֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb remained|נוֹתְר֤וּ\rb* \rb in the land|בָּאָ֔רֶץ\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵיהֶם֙\rb*, \rb those whom|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb had not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb destroyed|כִלּ֖וּם\rb* — \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹה֙\rb* \rb conscripted these people|וַיַּעֲלֵ֤ם\rb* \rb to be forced laborers|לְמַ֔ס\rb*, \rb as they are to|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb this|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb day|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb But|וּמִן־\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֛ה\rb* \rb did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb consign|נָתַ֧ן\rb*\rb |בְּנֵי֙\rb* \rb any of the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb to slave|לַעֲבָדִ֖ים\rb* \rb labor|לִמְלַאכְתּ֑וֹ\rb*, \rb because|כִּי־\rb* \rb they were|הֵ֜מָּה\rb* \rb his men|אַנְשֵׁ֤י\rb* \rb of war|מִלְחָמָה֙\rb*, \rb the leaders of|וְשָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb his captains|שָׁלִישָׁ֔יו\rb*, \rb and the commanders|וְשָׂרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of his chariots|רִכְבּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb and cavalry|וּפָרָשָֽׁיו׃פ\rb*. \v 10 \rb They|וְאֵ֨לֶּה\rb* \rb were also the chief|שָׂרֵ֤י\rb* \rb officers|הַנְּצִיבִים\rb* \rb for King|לַמֶּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֖ה\rb*: \rb 250|חֲמִשִּׁ֣ים\rb*\rb |וּמָאתָ֑יִם\rb* \rb supervisors|הָרֹדִ֖ים\rb*\rb |בָּעָֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹה֙\rb* \rb brought|הֶעֱלָ֤ה\rb* \rb the daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֗ה\rb* \rb up from the City|מֵעִ֣יר\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֔יד\rb* \rb to the palace|לַבַּ֖יִת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he had built|בָּֽנָה־\rb* \rb for her|לָ֑הּ\rb*. \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb he said|אָמַ֗ר\rb*, “\rb My wife|אִשָּׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לִי֙\rb* \rb must not|לֹא־\rb* \rb live|תֵשֵׁ֨ב\rb* \rb in the house|בְּבֵית֙\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֣יד\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb because|כִּי־\rb* \rb the places|הֵ֔מָּה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֥וֹן\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃פ\rb* \rb has entered|בָּֽאָ֥ה\rb* \rb are holy|קֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*.”
\p \v 12 \rb At that time|אָ֣ז\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֛ה\rb* \rb offered|הֶעֱלָ֧ה\rb* \rb burnt offerings|עֹל֖וֹת\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb on|עַ֚ל\rb* \rb the altar|מִזְבַּ֣ח\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he had built|בָּנָ֖ה\rb* \rb in front|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the portico|הָאוּלָֽם׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb He observed the daily|י֣וֹם\rb*\rb |בְּי֗וֹם\rb* \rb requirement|וּבִדְבַר־\rb* \rb for offerings|לְהַעֲלוֹת֙\rb* \rb according to the commandment|כְּמִצְוַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb for Sabbaths|לַשַּׁבָּתוֹת֙\rb*, \rb New Moons|וְלֶ֣חֳדָשִׁ֔ים\rb*, \rb and the three|שָׁל֥וֹשׁ\rb*\rb |פְּעָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb annual|בַּשָּׁנָ֑ה\rb* \rb appointed feasts|וְלַמּ֣וֹעֲד֔וֹת\rb* — \rb the Feast|בְּחַ֧ג\rb* \rb of Unleavened Bread|הַמַּצּ֛וֹת\rb*,\f + \fr 8:13 \ft That is, the seven-day period after the Passover during which no leaven may be eaten; see Exodus 12:14–20.\f* \rb the Feast|וּבְחַ֥ג\rb* \rb of Weeks|הַשָּׁבֻע֖וֹת\rb*,\f + \fr 8:13 \ft That is, Shavuot, the late spring feast of pilgrimage to Jerusalem; it is also known as \fqa the Feast of Harvest\ft (see Exodus 23:16) or \fqa the Feast of Pentecost\ft (see Acts 2:1).\f* \rb and the Feast|וּבְחַ֥ג\rb* \rb of Tabernacles|הַסֻּכּֽוֹת׃\rb*.\f + \fr 8:13 \ft That is, Sukkot, the autumn feast of pilgrimage to Jerusalem; also translated as \fqa the Feast of Booths \ft or \fqa the Feast of Shelters \ft and originally called \fqa the Feast of Ingathering\ft (see Exodus 23:16 and Exodus 34:22).\f*
\p \v 14 \rb In keeping with the ordinances|כְּמִשְׁפַּ֣ט\rb* \rb of his father|אָ֠בִיו\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb David|דָּֽוִיד־\rb*, \rb Solomon appointed|וַיַּעֲמֵ֣ד\rb* \rb the divisions|מַחְלְק֨וֹת\rb* \rb of the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֜ים\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb their service|עֲבֹדָתָ֗ם\rb*, \rb and the Levites|וְהַלְוִיִּ֣ם\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb their duties|מִ֠שְׁמְרוֹתָם\rb* \rb to offer praise|לְהַלֵּ֨ל\rb* \rb and to minister|וּלְשָׁרֵ֜ת\rb* \rb before|נֶ֤גֶד\rb* \rb the priests|הַכֹּֽהֲנִים֙\rb* \rb according to the daily|י֣וֹם\rb*\rb |בְּיוֹמ֔וֹ\rb* \rb requirement|לִדְבַר־\rb*. \rb He also appointed gatekeepers|וְהַשּׁוֹעֲרִ֥ים\rb* \rb by their divisions|בְּמַחְלְקוֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb at each gate|לְשַׁ֣עַר\rb*\rb |וָשָׁ֑עַר\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb this|כֵ֔ן\rb* \rb had been the command|מִצְוַ֖ת\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֥יד\rb*, \rb the man|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb They did not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb turn aside|סָרוּ֩\rb* \rb from the king’s|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb command|מִצְוַ֨ת\rb* \rb regarding|עַל־\rb* \rb the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֧ים\rb* \rb or the Levites|וְהַלְוִיִּ֛ם\rb* \rb in any|לְכָל־\rb* \rb matter|דָּבָ֖ר\rb*, \rb including that of the treasuries|וְלָאֹצָרֽוֹת׃\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb Thus all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the work|מְלֶ֣אכֶת\rb* \rb of Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֔ה\rb* \rb was carried out|וַתִּכֹּן֙\rb*, \rb from|עַד־\rb* \rb the day|הַיּ֛וֹם\rb* \rb the foundation was laid|מוּסַ֥ד\rb* \rb for the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb until|וְעַד־\rb* \rb it was finished|כְּלֹת֑וֹ\rb*. \rb So the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb* \rb was completed|שָׁלֵ֖ם\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb Then|אָז֩\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֜ה\rb* \rb went|הָלַ֨ךְ\rb*\rb |לְעֶצְיֽוֹן־\rb* \rb to Ezion-geber|גֶּ֧בֶר\rb* \rb and to|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb Eloth|אֵיל֛וֹת\rb*\f + \fr 8:17 \fqa Eloth \ft is a variant of \fqa Elath\ft ; see LXX, 2 Kings 14:22, and 2 Kings 16:6.\f* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the coast|שְׂפַ֥ת\rb*\rb |הַיָּ֖ם\rb*\rb |בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Edom|אֱדֽוֹם׃\rb*.\f + \fr 8:17 \ft That is, along the shore of the Red Sea in the land of Edom\f* \v 18 \rb So Hiram|חוּרָ֨ם\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּֽשְׁלַֽח־\rb* \rb him|לוֹ֩\rb* \rb ships|אוֹנִיּוֹת\rb* \rb captained by|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb his servants|עֲבָדָ֜יו\rb*, \rb along with crews|וַעֲבָדִים֮\rb* \rb of experienced sailors|י֣וֹדְעֵי\rb*\rb |יָם֒\rb*. \rb They went|וַיָּבֹ֜אוּ\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb Solomon’s|שְׁלֹמֹה֙\rb* \rb servants|עַבְדֵ֤י\rb* \rb to Ophir|אוֹפִ֔ירָה\rb* \rb and acquired|וַיִּקְח֣וּ\rb* \rb from there|מִשָּׁ֔ם\rb* \rb 450|אַרְבַּע־\rb*\rb |מֵא֥וֹת\rb*\rb |וַחֲמִשִּׁ֖ים\rb* \rb talents|כִּכַּ֣ר\rb* \rb of gold|זָהָ֑ב\rb*,\f + \fr 8:18 \fqa 450 talents \ft is approximately 17 tons or 15.4 metric tons of gold.\f* \rb which they delivered|וַיָּבִ֖יאוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹֽה׃פ\rb*.
\c 9
\s1 The Queen of Sheba
\r (1 Kings 10:1–13)
\p \v 1 \rb Now when the queen|וּמַֽלְכַּת־\rb* \rb of Sheba|שְׁבָ֗א\rb* \rb heard|שָֽׁמְעָה֮\rb* \rb about|אֶת־\rb* \rb the fame|שֵׁ֣מַע\rb* \rb of Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹה֒\rb*, \rb she came|וַתָּב֣וֹא\rb* \rb to test|לְנַסּוֹת֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb him|שְׁלֹמֹ֨ה\rb* \rb with difficult questions|בְחִיד֜וֹת\rb*. \rb She arrived in Jerusalem|בִּירֽוּשָׁלִַ֗ם\rb* \rb with a very|מְאֹ֡ד\rb* \rb large|כָּבֵ֣ד\rb* \rb caravan|בְּחַ֣יִל\rb*— \rb with camels|וּ֠גְמַלִּים\rb* \rb bearing|נֹשְׂאִ֨ים\rb* \rb spices|בְּשָׂמִ֧ים\rb*, \rb gold|וְזָהָ֛ב\rb* \rb in abundance|לָרֹ֖ב\rb*, \rb and precious|יְקָרָ֑ה\rb* \rb stones|וְאֶ֣בֶן\rb*.
\p \rb And she came|וַתָּבוֹא֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֔ה\rb* \rb and spoke|וַתְּדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb with him|עִמּ֔וֹ\rb*\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb about all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb was|הָיָ֖ה\rb* \rb on|עִם־\rb* \rb her mind|לְבָבָֽהּ׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb And Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb answered|וַיַּגֶּד־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb her questions|דְּבָרֶ֑יהָ\rb*; \rb nothing|וְלֹֽא־\rb*\rb |דָּבָר֙\rb* \rb was too difficult|נֶעְלַ֤ם\rb* \rb for him|מִשְּׁלֹמֹ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb*\rb |לֹ֦א\rb* \rb to explain|הִגִּ֖יד\rb*\rb |לָֽהּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb When the queen|מַֽלְכַּת־\rb* \rb of Sheba|שְׁבָ֔א\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb saw|וַתֵּ֙רֶא֙\rb* \rb the wisdom|חָכְמַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֑ה\rb*, \rb the palace|וְהַבַּ֖יִת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he had built|בָּנָֽה׃\rb*, \v 4 \rb the food|וּמַאֲכַ֣ל\rb* \rb at his table|שֻׁלְחָנ֡וֹ\rb*, \rb the seating|וּמוֹשַׁ֣ב\rb* \rb of his servants|עֲבָדָיו֩\rb*, \rb the service|וּמַעֲמַ֨ד\rb* \rb and attire|וּמַלְבּֽוּשֵׁיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb of his attendants|מְשָׁרְתָ֜יו\rb*, \rb the attire|וּמַלְבּ֣וּשֵׁיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb of his cupbearers|וּמַשְׁקָיו֙\rb*, \rb and the burnt offerings|וַעֲלִיָּת֔וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he presented|יַעֲלֶ֖ה\rb*\f + \fr 9:4 \ft LXX and Syriac (see also 1 Kings 10:5); Hebrew \fqa and his stairway by which he went up\f* \rb at the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*,\rb |וְלֹא־\rb*\rb |הָ֥יָה\rb*\rb |ע֛וֹד\rb* \rb it took her breath away|רֽוּחַ׃\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb She said|וַתֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*, “\rb The report|הַדָּבָ֔ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I heard|שָׁמַ֖עְתִּי\rb* \rb in my own country|בְּאַרְצִ֑י\rb* \rb about|עַל־\rb* \rb your words|דְּבָרֶ֖יךָ\rb*\f + \fr 9:5 \ft Or \fqa your achievements\f* \rb and|וְעַל־\rb* \rb wisdom|חָכְמָתֶֽךָ׃\rb* \rb is true|אֱמֶת֙\rb*. \v 6 \rb But I did not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb believe|הֶאֱמַ֣נְתִּי\rb* \rb the reports|לְדִבְרֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb until|עַ֤ד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I came|בָּ֙אתִי֙\rb* \rb and saw|וַתִּרְאֶ֣ינָה\rb* \rb with my own eyes|עֵינַ֔י\rb*. \rb Indeed|וְהִנֵּה֙\rb*, \rb not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb half|חֲצִ֖י\rb* \rb of the greatness|מַרְבִּ֣ית\rb* \rb of your wisdom|חָכְמָתֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb was told|הֻגַּד־\rb* \rb to me|לִ֔י\rb*. \rb You have far exceeded|יָסַ֕פְתָּ\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb the report|הַשְּׁמוּעָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I heard|שָׁמָֽעְתִּי׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb How blessed|אַשְׁרֵ֣י\rb* \rb are your men|אֲנָשֶׁ֔יךָ\rb*! \rb How blessed|וְאַשְׁרֵ֖י\rb* \rb are these|אֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb servants of yours|עֲבָדֶ֣יךָ\rb* \rb who stand|הָעֹמְדִ֤ים\rb* \rb continually|תָּמִ֔יד\rb* \rb before you|לְפָנֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb and hear|וְשֹׁמְעִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your wisdom|חָכְמָתֶֽךָ׃\rb*! \v 8 \rb Blessed|בָּר֔וּךְ\rb* \rb be|יְהִ֨י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר׀\rb* \rb has delighted|חָפֵ֣ץ\rb* \rb in you|בְּךָ֗\rb* \rb to set you|לְתִתְּךָ֤\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb His throne|כִּסְאוֹ֙\rb* \rb to be king|לְמֶ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb for the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֑יךָ\rb*. \rb Because your God|אֱלֹהֶ֤יךָ\rb* \rb loved|בְּאַהֲבַ֨ת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb enough to establish them|לְהַעֲמִיד֣וֹ\rb* \rb forever|לְעוֹלָ֔ם\rb*, \rb He has made you|וַיִּתֶּנְךָ֤\rb* \rb king|לְמֶ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb over them|עֲלֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb to carry out|לַעֲשׂ֖וֹת\rb* \rb justice|מִשְׁפָּ֥ט\rb* \rb and righteousness|וּצְדָקָֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 9 \rb Then she gave|וַתִּתֵּ֨ן\rb* \rb the king|לַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb 120|מֵאָ֥ה\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִ֣ים׀\rb* \rb talents|כִּכַּ֣ר\rb* \rb of gold|זָהָ֗ב\rb*,\f + \fr 9:9 \fqa 120 talents \ft is approximately 4.52 tons or 4.1 metric tons of gold.\f* \rb a great quantity of|לָרֹ֥ב\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֖ד\rb* \rb spices|וּבְשָׂמִ֛ים\rb*, \rb and precious|יְקָרָ֑ה\rb* \rb stones|וְאֶ֣בֶן\rb*. \rb There had never been|הָיָה֙\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb such|הַה֔וּא\rb* \rb spices|כַּבֹּ֣שֶׂם\rb* \rb as those|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the queen|מַֽלְכַּת־\rb* \rb of Sheba|שְׁבָ֖א\rb* \rb gave|נָתְנָ֥ה\rb* \rb to King|לַמֶּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 10 (\rb The servants|עַבְדֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Hiram|חִירָם\rb* \rb and|וְעַבְדֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֔ה\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb brought|הֵבִ֥יאוּ\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֖ב\rb* \rb from Ophir|מֵאוֹפִ֑יר\rb* \rb also|וְגַם־\rb* \rb brought|הֵבִ֛יאוּ\rb* \rb algum|אַלְגּוּמִּ֖ים\rb*\f + \fr 9:10 \fqa Algum \ft is probably a variant of \fqa almug\ft ; also in verse 11; see 1 Kings 10:11.\f* \rb wood|עֲצֵ֥י\rb* \rb and precious|יְקָרָֽה׃\rb* \rb stones|וְאֶ֥בֶן\rb*. \v 11 \rb The king|הַ֠מֶּלֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb made|וַיַּ֣עַשׂ\rb* \rb the algum|הָֽאַלְגּוּמִּ֜ים\rb* \rb wood|עֲצֵ֨י\rb* \rb into steps|מְסִלּ֤וֹת\rb*\f + \fr 9:11 \ft Or \fqa gateways\f* \rb for the house|לְבֵית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb and for the king’s|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb palace|וּלְבֵ֣ית\rb*, \rb and into lyres|וְכִנֹּר֥וֹת\rb* \rb and harps|וּנְבָלִ֖ים\rb* \rb for the singers|לַשָּׁרִ֑ים\rb*. \rb Never|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb before|לְפָנִ֖ים\rb* \rb had anything like them|כָהֵ֛ם\rb* \rb been seen|נִרְא֥וּ\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb*.)
\p \v 12 \rb King|וְהַמֶּ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֜ה\rb* \rb gave|נָתַ֣ן\rb* \rb the queen|לְמַֽלְכַּת־\rb* \rb of Sheba|שְׁבָ֗א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb she desired|חֶפְצָהּ֙\rb* — \rb whatever|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb she asked|שָׁאָ֔לָה\rb* — \rb far more than|מִלְּבַ֖ד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb she had brought|הֵבִ֣יאָה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb*. \rb Then she|הִ֥יא\rb* \rb left|וַֽתַּהֲפֹ֛ךְ\rb* \rb and returned|וַתֵּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb to her own country|לְאַרְצָ֖הּ\rb*, \rb along with her servants|וַעֲבָדֶֽיהָ׃פ\rb*.
\s1 Solomon’s Wealth and Splendor
\r (1 Kings 10:14–29)
\p \v 13 \rb The weight|מִשְׁקַ֣ל\rb* \rb of gold|הַזָּהָ֔ב\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb came|בָּ֥א\rb* \rb to Solomon|לִשְׁלֹמֹ֖ה\rb* \rb each year|בְּשָׁנָ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶחָ֑ת\rb* \rb was|וַיְהִי֙\rb* \rb 666|שֵׁ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵא֛וֹת\rb*\rb |וְשִׁשִּׁ֥ים\rb*\rb |וָשֵׁ֖שׁ\rb* \rb talents|כִּכְּרֵ֥י\rb*\rb |זָהָֽב׃\rb*,\f + \fr 9:13 \fqa 666 talents \ft is approximately 25.1 tons or 22.8 metric tons of gold.\f* \v 14 \rb not including|לְבַ֞ד\rb* \rb the revenue|מְבִיאִ֑ים\rb* \rb from the merchants|מֵאַנְשֵׁ֧י\rb*\rb |הַתָּרִ֛ים\rb* \rb and traders|וְהַסֹּחֲרִ֖ים\rb*. \rb And all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the Arabian|עֲרַב֙\rb* \rb kings|מַלְכֵ֤י\rb* \rb and governors|וּפַח֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb also brought|מְבִיאִ֛ים\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֥ב\rb* \rb and silver|וָכֶ֖סֶף\rb* \rb to Solomon|לִשְׁלֹמֹֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb King|הַמֶּ֧לֶךְ\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֛ה\rb* \rb made|וַיַּ֨עַשׂ\rb* \rb two hundred|מָאתַ֥יִם\rb* \rb large shields|צִנָּ֖ה\rb* \rb of hammered|שָׁח֑וּט\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֣ב\rb*; \rb six|שֵׁ֤שׁ\rb* \rb hundred shekels|מֵאוֹת֙\rb* \rb of hammered|שָׁח֔וּט\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֣ב\rb*\f + \fr 9:15 \fqa 600 shekels \ft is approximately 15.1 pounds or 6.8 kilograms of gold.\f* \rb went|יַעֲלֶ֖ה\rb* \rb into|עַל־\rb* \rb each|הָאֶחָֽת׃\rb* \rb shield|הַצִּנָּ֥ה\rb*. \v 16 \rb He also made three|וּשְׁלֹשׁ־\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֤וֹת\rb* \rb small shields|מָֽגִנִּים֙\rb* \rb of hammered|שָׁח֔וּט\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֣ב\rb*; \rb three|שְׁלֹ֤שׁ\rb* \rb hundred shekels|מֵאוֹת֙\rb* \rb of gold|זָהָ֔ב\rb*\f + \fr 9:16 \fqa 300 shekels \ft is approximately 7.5 pounds or 3.4 kilograms of gold.\f* \rb went|יַעֲלֶ֖ה\rb* \rb into|עַל־\rb* \rb each|הָאֶחָ֑ת\rb* \rb shield|הַמָּגֵ֣ן\rb*. \rb And the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb put them|וַיִּתְּנֵ֣ם\rb* \rb in the House|בְּבֵ֖ית\rb* \rb of the Forest|יַ֥עַר\rb* \rb of Lebanon|הַלְּבָנֽוֹן׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb Additionally, the king|הַמֶּ֛לֶךְ\rb* \rb made|וַיַּ֧עַשׂ\rb* \rb a great|גָּד֑וֹל\rb* \rb throne|כִּסֵּא־\rb* \rb of ivory|שֵׁ֖ן\rb* \rb and overlaid it|וַיְצַפֵּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb with pure|טָהֽוֹר׃\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֥ב\rb*. \v 18 \rb The throne|לַ֠כִּסֵּא\rb* \rb had six|וְשֵׁ֣שׁ\rb* \rb steps|מַעֲל֣וֹת\rb*, \rb and a footstool|וְכֶ֨בֶשׁ\rb* \rb of gold|בַּזָּהָ֤ב\rb*\rb |לַכִּסֵּא֙\rb* \rb was attached to it|מָאֳחָזִ֔ים\rb*. \rb There were armrests|וְיָד֛וֹת\rb* \rb on both sides|מִזֶּ֥ה\rb*\rb |וּמִזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb of|עַל־\rb* \rb the seat|מְק֣וֹם\rb*\rb |הַשָּׁ֑בֶת\rb*,\rb |וּשְׁנַ֣יִם\rb* \rb with a lion|אֲרָי֔וֹת\rb* \rb standing|עֹמְדִ֖ים\rb* \rb beside|אֵ֥צֶל\rb* \rb each armrest|הַיָּדֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb Twelve|וּשְׁנֵ֧ים\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֣ר\rb* \rb lions|אֲרָי֗וֹת\rb* \rb stood|עֹמְדִ֥ים\rb*\rb |שָׁ֛ם\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the six|שֵׁ֥שׁ\rb* \rb steps|הַֽמַּעֲל֖וֹת\rb*, \rb one at either end|מִזֶּ֣ה\rb* \rb of each step|וּמִזֶּ֑ה\rb*. \rb Nothing|לֹא־\rb* \rb like this|כֵ֖ן\rb* \rb had ever been made|נַעֲשָׂ֥ה\rb* \rb for any|לְכָל־\rb* \rb kingdom|מַמְלָכָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb All|וְ֠כֹל\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb Solomon’s|שְׁלֹמֹה֙\rb* \rb drinking|מַשְׁקֵ֨ה\rb* \rb cups|כְּלֵ֞י\rb* \rb were gold|זָהָ֔ב\rb*, \rb and all|וְכֹ֗ל\rb* \rb the utensils|כְּלֵ֛י\rb* \rb of the House|בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb of the Forest|יַ֥עַר\rb* \rb of Lebanon|הַלְּבָנ֖וֹן\rb* \rb were pure|סָג֑וּר\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֣ב\rb*. \rb There was no|אֵ֣ין\rb* \rb silver|כֶּ֗סֶף\rb*, \rb because it was accounted|נֶחְשָׁ֛ב\rb* \rb as nothing|לִמְאֽוּמָה׃\rb* \rb in the days|בִּימֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֖ה\rb*. \v 21 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the king had|לַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb the ships|אֳנִיּ֤וֹת\rb* \rb of Tarshish|תַּרְשִׁ֔ישׁ\rb*\f + \fr 9:21 \ft Or \fqa a fleet of trading ships\ft ; twice in this verse\f* \rb that went|הֹלְכ֣וֹת\rb* \rb with|עִ֖ם\rb* \rb Hiram’s|חוּרָ֑ם\rb*\f + \fr 9:21 \ft Hebrew \fqa Huram’s\ft , a variant of \fqa Hiram’s\f* \rb servants|עַבְדֵ֣י\rb*, \rb and once|אַחַת֩\rb* \rb every three|לְשָׁל֨וֹשׁ\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִ֜ים\rb* \rb the ships|אֳנִיּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of Tarshish|תַּרְשִׁ֗ישׁ\rb* \rb would arrive|תָּב֣וֹאנָה׀\rb* \rb bearing|נֹֽשְׂאוֹת֙\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֣ב\rb*, \rb silver|וָכֶ֔סֶף\rb*, \rb ivory|שֶׁנְהַבִּ֥ים\rb*, \rb apes|וְקוֹפִ֖ים\rb*, \rb and peacocks|וְתוּכִּיִּֽים׃פ\rb*.\f + \fr 9:21 \ft Or \fqa baboons\f*
\p \v 22 \rb So King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֔ה\rb* \rb surpassed|וַיִּגְדַּל֙\rb* \rb all|מִכֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb the kings|מַלְכֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the earth|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb in riches|לְעֹ֖שֶׁר\rb* \rb and wisdom|וְחָכְמָֽה׃\rb*. \v 23 \rb All|וְכֹל֙\rb* \rb the kings|מַלְכֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the earth|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb sought|מְבַקְשִׁ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb an audience|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb with Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֑ה\rb* \rb to hear|לִשְׁמֹ֙עַ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the wisdom|חָכְמָת֔וֹ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb had put|נָתַ֥ן\rb* \rb in his heart|בְּלִבּֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 24 \rb |דְּבַר־\rb* \rb Year|שָׁנָ֖ה\rb* \rb after year|בְּשָׁנָֽה׃פ\rb*, \rb each|וְהֵ֣ם\rb* \rb visitor|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb would bring|מְבִיאִ֣ים\rb* \rb his tribute|מִנְחָת֡וֹ\rb*: \rb articles|כְּלֵ֣י\rb* \rb of silver|כֶסֶף֩\rb*\rb |וּכְלֵ֨י\rb* \rb and gold|זָהָ֤ב\rb*, \rb clothing|וּשְׂלָמוֹת֙\rb*, \rb weapons|נֵ֣שֶׁק\rb*, \rb spices|וּבְשָׂמִ֔ים\rb*, \rb horses|סוּסִ֖ים\rb*, \rb and mules|וּפְרָדִ֑ים\rb*.
\p \v 25 \rb Solomon|לִשְׁלֹמֹ֜ה\rb* \rb had|וַיְהִ֨י\rb* \rb 4,000|אַרְבַּעַת֩\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִ֨ים\rb* \rb stalls|אֻֽרְי֤וֹת\rb* \rb for horses|סוּסִים֙\rb* \rb and chariots|וּמַרְכָּב֔וֹת\rb*, \rb and 12,000|וּשְׁנֵים־\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֶ֖לֶף\rb* \rb horses|פָּרָשִׁ֑ים\rb*,\f + \fr 9:25 \ft Or \fqa horsemen \ft or \fqa charioteers\f* \rb which he stationed|וַיַּנִּיחֵם֙\rb* \rb in the chariot|הָרֶ֔כֶב\rb* \rb cities|בְּעָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb and also with|וְעִם־\rb* \rb him|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*. \v 26 \rb |וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb He reigned|מוֹשֵׁ֖ל\rb* \rb over all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the kings|הַמְּלָכִ֑ים\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the Euphrates|הַנָּהָר֙\rb*\f + \fr 9:26 \ft Hebrew \fqa the River\f* \rb to|וְעַד־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb*, \rb as|וְעַ֖ד\rb* \rb far as the border|גְּב֥וּל\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*. \v 27 \rb The king|הַמֶּ֧לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb made|וַיִּתֵּ֨ן\rb* \rb silver|הַכֶּ֛סֶף\rb* \rb as common in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \rb as stones|כָּאֲבָנִ֑ים\rb*,\rb |וְאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb and|נָתַ֛ן\rb* \rb cedar|הָאֲרָזִ֗ים\rb* \rb as abundant|לָרֹֽב׃\rb* \rb as sycamore|כַּשִּׁקְמִ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb in the foothills|בַּשְּׁפֵלָ֖ה\rb*.\f + \fr 9:27 \ft Hebrew \fqa Shephelah \ft or \fqa lowlands\ft ; that is, the western foothills of Judea\f* \v 28 \rb Solomon’s|לִשְׁלֹמֹ֖ה\rb* \rb horses|סוּסִ֧ים\rb* \rb were imported|וּמוֹצִיאִ֨ים\rb* \rb from Egypt|מִמִּצְרַ֛יִם\rb* \rb and from all|וּמִכָּל־\rb* \rb the lands|הָאֲרָצֽוֹת׃\rb*.
\s1 The Death of Solomon
\r (1 Kings 11:41–43)
\p \v 29 \rb As for the rest|וּשְׁאָר֙\rb* \rb of the acts|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֔ה\rb*, \rb from beginning|הָרִאשֹׁנִ֖ים\rb* \rb to end|וְהָאֲחֲרוֹנִ֑ים\rb*, \rb are they|הֵ֣ם\rb* \rb not|הֲלֹא־\rb* \rb written|כְּתוּבִ֗ים\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the Records|דִּבְרֵי֙\rb* \rb of Nathan|נָתָ֣ן\rb* \rb the Prophet|הַנָּבִ֔יא\rb*, \rb in|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the Prophecy|נְבוּאַ֞ת\rb* \rb of Ahijah|אֲחִיָּ֣ה\rb* \rb the Shilonite|הַשִּֽׁילוֹנִ֗י\rb*, \rb and in the Visions|וּבַחֲזוֹת֙\rb* \rb of Iddo|יֶעְדִּי\rb* \rb the Seer|הַחֹזֶ֔ה\rb* \rb concerning|עַל־\rb* \rb Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֖ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Nebat|נְבָֽט׃\rb*? \v 30 \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֧ה\rb* \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֨ךְ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִֽירוּשָׁלִַ֛ם\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb forty|אַרְבָּעִ֥ים\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָֽה׃\rb*. \v 31 \rb And Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹה֙\rb* \rb rested|וַיִּשְׁכַּ֤ב\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb his fathers|אֲבֹתָ֔יו\rb* \rb and was buried|וַֽיִּקְבְּרֻ֔הוּ\rb* \rb in the city|בְּעִ֖יר\rb* \rb of his father|אָבִ֑יו\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֣יד\rb*. \rb And his son|בְּנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Rehoboam|רְחַבְעָ֥ם\rb* \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֛ךְ\rb* \rb in his place|תַּחְתָּֽיו׃פ\rb*.
\c 10
\s1 Rebellion against Rehoboam
\r (1 Kings 12:1–15)
\p \v 1 \rb Then Rehoboam|רְחַבְעָ֖ם\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb to Shechem|שְׁכֶ֑מָה\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb had gone|בָּ֥אוּ\rb* \rb there|שְׁכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb to make him king|לְהַמְלִ֥יךְ\rb*\rb |אֹתֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb |וַיְהִ֞י\rb* \rb When Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֤ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Nebat|נְבָט֙\rb* \rb heard about this|כִּשְׁמֹ֨עַ\rb*, \rb he|יָרָבְעָ֖ם\rb* \rb returned|וַיָּ֥שָׁב\rb* \rb from Egypt|מִמִּצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*,\rb |וְה֣וּא\rb*\rb |בְמִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he had fled|בָּרַ֔ח\rb* \rb from King|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֣ה\rb*\rb |מִפְּנֵ֖י\rb*. \v 3 \rb So they sent for|וַֽיִּשְׁלְחוּ֙\rb* \rb Jeroboam|וַיִּקְרְאוּ־\rb*, \rb and he|יָרָבְעָ֖ם\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֥א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Rehoboam|רְחַבְעָ֖ם\rb* \rb and said|וַֽיְדַבְּר֔וּ\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 4 “\rb Your father|אָבִ֖יךָ\rb* \rb put a heavy|הִקְשָׁ֣ה\rb* \rb yoke|עֻלֵּ֑נוּ\rb* \rb on us|אֶת־\rb*. \rb But now|וְעַתָּ֡ה\rb* \rb you must lighten|הָקֵל֩\rb* \rb the burden|הַקָּשָׁ֗ה\rb* \rb of your father’s|אָבִ֜יךָ\rb* \rb service|מֵעֲבֹדַ֨ת\rb* \rb and the heavy|הַכָּבֵ֛ד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb yoke|וּמֵעֻלּ֧וֹ\rb* \rb he put|נָתַ֥ן\rb* \rb on us|עָלֵ֖ינוּ\rb*, \rb and we will serve you|וְנַֽעַבְדֶֽךָּ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 5 \rb Rehoboam answered|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Come back|וְשׁ֣וּבוּ\rb* \rb to me|אֵלָ֑י\rb*\rb |אֲלֵהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb in|ע֛וֹד\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֖ים\rb*.” \rb So the people|הָעָֽם׃ס\rb* \rb departed|וַיֵּ֖לֶךְ\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb Then King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Rehoboam|רְחַבְעָ֗ם\rb* \rb consulted|וַיִּוָּעַ֞ץ\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb the elders|הַזְּקֵנִים֙\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |הָי֣וּ\rb* \rb had served|עֹֽמְדִ֗ים\rb*\rb |לִפְנֵי֙\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֔יו\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֣ה\rb* \rb during|בִּֽהְיֹת֥וֹ\rb* \rb his lifetime|חַ֖י\rb*. “\rb How|אֵ֚יךְ\rb* \rb do you|אַתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb advise me|נֽוֹעָצִ֔ים\rb* \rb to respond|לְהָשִׁ֥יב\rb*\rb |דָּבָֽר׃\rb* \rb to these|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb people|לָֽעָם־\rb*?” \rb he asked|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb They replied|וַיְדַבְּר֨וּ\rb*, “\rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb you will be|תִּֽהְיֶ֨ה\rb* \rb kind|לְט֜וֹב\rb* \rb to these|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb people|לְהָעָ֤ם\rb* \rb and please them|וּרְצִיתָ֔ם\rb* \rb by speaking|וְדִבַּרְתָּ֥\rb* \rb kind|טוֹבִ֑ים\rb* \rb words|דְּבָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb to them|אֲלֵהֶ֖ם\rb*, \rb they will be|וְהָי֥וּ\rb* \rb your|לְךָ֛\rb* \rb servants|עֲבָדִ֖ים\rb* \rb forever|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִֽים׃\rb*.”
\p \v 8 \rb But Rehoboam rejected|וַֽיַּעֲזֹ֛ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the advice|עֲצַ֥ת\rb* \rb of the elders|הַזְּקֵנִ֖ים\rb*; \rb instead, he consulted|וַיִּוָּעַ֗ץ\rb* \rb the young men|הַיְלָדִים֙\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb had grown up|גָּדְל֣וּ\rb* \rb with him|אִתּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and served|הָעֹמְדִ֖ים\rb* \rb him|לְפָנָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb He asked|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb them|אֲלֵהֶ֗ם\rb*, “\rb What|מָ֚ה\rb* \rb message|דָּבָ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb do you|אַתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb advise|נֽוֹעָצִ֔ים\rb* \rb that we send back|וְנָשִׁ֥יב\rb* \rb to these|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb people|הָעָ֣ם\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb have spoken|דִּבְּר֤וּ\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַי֙\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, ‘\rb Lighten|הָקֵל֙\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb the yoke|הָעֹ֔ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb your father|אָבִ֖יךָ\rb* \rb put|נָתַ֥ן\rb* \rb on us|עָלֵֽינוּ׃\rb*’ ?”
\p \v 10 \rb The young men|הַיְלָדִים֙\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb had grown up|גָּדְל֣וּ\rb*\rb |אִתּוֹ֮\rb* \rb with him|אִתּ֗וֹ\rb* \rb replied|וַיְדַבְּר֣וּ\rb*, “\rb This is how|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb you should answer|לֵאמֹר֒\rb*\rb |תֹאמַ֡ר\rb* \rb these people|לָעָם֩\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb said|דִּבְּר֨וּ\rb* \rb to you|אֵלֶ֜יךָ\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* ‘\rb Your father|אָבִ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb made our yoke|עֻלֵּ֔נוּ\rb* \rb heavy|הִכְבִּ֣יד\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb but you|וְאַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb must make it lighter|הָקֵ֣ל\rb*\rb |מֵעָלֵ֑ינוּ\rb*.’ \rb This is what|כֹּ֚ה\rb* \rb you should tell|תֹּאמַ֣ר\rb* \rb them|אֲלֵהֶ֔ם\rb*: ‘\rb My little finger|קָֽטָנִּ֥י\rb* \rb is thicker|עָבָ֖ה\rb* \rb than my father’s|אָבִֽי׃\rb* \rb waist|מִמָּתְנֵ֥י\rb*! \v 11 \rb Whereas|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb my father|אָבִי֙\rb* \rb burdened|הֶעְמִ֤יס\rb* \rb you with a heavy|כָּבֵ֔ד\rb* \rb yoke|עֹ֣ל\rb*, \rb I|וַאֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb will add|אֹסִ֣יף\rb*\rb |עַֽל־\rb* \rb to|עֲלֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb your yoke|עֻלְּכֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb Whereas my father|אָבִ֗י\rb* \rb scourged|יִסַּ֤ר\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶם֙\rb* \rb with whips|בַּשּׁוֹטִ֔ים\rb*, \rb I will scourge you|וַאֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb with scorpions|בָּֽעֲקְרַבִּֽים׃ס\rb*.’”
\p \v 12 \rb After three|הַשְּׁלִשִׁ֑י\rb* \rb days|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb*, \rb Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֧ם\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֛ם\rb* \rb returned|וַיָּבֹ֨א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Rehoboam|רְחַבְעָ֖ם\rb*, \rb since|כַּאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb*\rb |דִּבֶּ֤ר\rb* \rb had said|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, “\rb Come back|שׁ֥וּבוּ\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֖י\rb* \rb on the third|הַשְּׁלִשִֽׁי׃\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb*.” \v 13 \rb And the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb answered them|וַיַּעֲנֵ֥ם\rb* \rb harshly|קָשָׁ֑ה\rb*. \rb King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Rehoboam|רְחַבְעָ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb rejected|וַֽיַּעֲזֹב֙\rb* \rb the advice|עֲצַ֥ת\rb* \rb of the elders|הַזְּקֵנִֽים׃\rb* \v 14 \rb and spoke|וַיְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb to them|אֲלֵהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb as the young men|הַיְלָדִים֙\rb* \rb had advised|כַּעֲצַ֤ת\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, “\rb Whereas my father made your yoke|עֻלְּכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb heavy|אַכְבִּיד֙\rb*,\f + \fr 10:14 \ft LXX and many Hebrew manuscripts (see also 1 Kings 12:14); MT \fqa Whereas I made your yoke heavy\f*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb I|וַאֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb will add|אֹסִ֣יף\rb* \rb to your yoke|עָלָ֑יו\rb*. \rb Whereas my father|אָבִ֗י\rb* \rb scourged|יִסַּ֤ר\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶם֙\rb* \rb with whips|בַּשּׁוֹטִ֔ים\rb*, \rb I will scourge you|וַאֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb with scorpions|בָּעֲקְרַבִּֽים׃\rb*.”
\p \v 15 \rb So the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb did not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb listen|שָׁמַ֥ע\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֑ם\rb*, \rb and indeed|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb this turn of events|נְסִבָּה֙\rb* \rb was|הָיְתָ֤ה\rb* \rb from|מֵעִ֣ם\rb* \rb God|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*, \rb in order that|לְמַעַן֩\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb might fulfill|הָקִ֨ים\rb* \rb the word|דְּבָר֗וֹ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb He had spoken|דִּבֶּר֙\rb* \rb through|בְּיַד֙\rb* \rb Ahijah|אֲחִיָּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb the Shilonite|הַשִּֽׁלוֹנִ֔י\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֖ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Nebat|נְבָֽט׃\rb*.
\s1 The Kingdom Divided
\r (1 Kings 12:16–19)
\p \v 16 \rb When all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb Israel saw|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb that|כִּ֠י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּלֶךְ֮\rb*\rb |לָהֶם֒\rb* \rb had refused|לֹא־\rb* \rb to listen|שָׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb to them|הָעָ֣ם\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb they answered|וַיָּשִׁ֣יבוּ\rb*\f + \fr 10:16 \ft Syriac, Vulgate, and many Hebrew manuscripts; MT \fqa And all Israel, since the king had refused to listen to them, answered\ft .\f* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ׀\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֡ר\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb What|מַה־\rb* \rb portion|חֵ֨לֶק\rb* \rb do we have|לָּנוּ֩\rb* \rb in David|בְּדָוִ֜יד\rb*,
\q2 \rb and what|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb inheritance|נַחֲלָ֣ה\rb* \rb in the son|בְּבֶן־\rb* \rb of Jesse|יִשַׁ֗י\rb*?
\q1 \rb |אִ֤ישׁ\rb* \rb To your tents|לְאֹהָלֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*, \rb O Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*!
\q2 \rb Look|רְאֵ֥ה\rb* \rb now|בֵיתְךָ֖\rb* \rb to your own house|עַתָּ֕ה\rb*, \rb O David|דָּוִ֑יד\rb*!”
\p \rb So all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb home|לְאֹהָלָֽיו׃ס\rb*, \v 17 \rb but Rehoboam|רְחַבְעָֽם׃\rb* \rb still reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֥ךְ\rb* \rb over|עֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb the Israelites|וּבְנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb living|הַיֹּֽשְׁבִ֖ים\rb* \rb in the cities|בְּעָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb Then King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Rehoboam|רְחַבְעָ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb sent out|וַיִּשְׁלַ֞ח\rb* \rb Hadoram|הֲדֹרָם֙\rb*,\f + \fr 10:18 \fqa Hadoram \ft is a variant of \fqa Adoram \ft and \fqa Adoniram\ft ; see 2 Samuel 20:24 and 1 Kings 4:6.\f* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb was in charge|עַל־\rb* \rb of the forced labor|הַמַּ֔ס\rb*, \rb but the Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb stoned|וַיִּרְגְּמוּ־\rb* \rb him|ב֧וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶ֖בֶן\rb* \rb to death|וַיָּמֹ֑ת\rb*. \rb And King|וְהַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Rehoboam|רְחַבְעָ֗ם\rb* \rb mounted|לַֽעֲל֣וֹת\rb* \rb his chariot|בַּמֶּרְכָּבָ֔ה\rb* \rb in haste|הִתְאַמֵּץ֙\rb* \rb and escaped|לָנ֖וּס\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃ס\rb*. \v 19 \rb So to|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb this|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb day|הַזֶּֽה׃ס\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb has been in rebellion|וַיִּפְשְׁע֤וּ\rb* \rb against the house|בְּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֔יד\rb*.
\c 11
\s1 Shemaiah’s Prophecy
\r (1 Kings 12:20–24)
\p \v 1 \rb When Rehoboam|רְחַבְעָם֮\rb* \rb arrived|וַיָּבֹ֣א\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַם֒\rb*, \rb he mobilized|וַיַּקְהֵל֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֨ית\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֜ה\rb* \rb and Benjamin|וּבִנְיָמִ֗ן\rb* — \rb 180,000|מֵאָ֨ה\rb*\rb |וּשְׁמוֹנִ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֶ֛לֶף\rb* \rb chosen|בָּח֖וּר\rb*\rb |עֹשֵׂ֣ה\rb* \rb warriors|מִלְחָמָ֑ה\rb* — \rb to fight|לְהִלָּחֵם֙\rb* \rb against|עִם־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb and restore|לְהָשִׁ֥יב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the kingdom|הַמַּמְלָכָ֖ה\rb* \rb to Rehoboam|לִרְחַבְעָֽם׃פ\rb*. \v 2 \rb But the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִי֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Shemaiah|שְׁמַֽעְיָ֥הוּ\rb* \rb the man|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*: \v 3 “\rb Tell|אֱמֹ֕ר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb Rehoboam|רְחַבְעָ֥ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֖ה\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb and|וְאֶל֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb in Judah|בִּיהוּדָ֥ה\rb* \rb and Benjamin|וּבִנְיָמִ֖ן\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 4 \rb that this is what|כֹּ֣ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֡ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר\rb*: ‘\rb You are not|לֹא־\rb* \rb to go up|תַעֲלוּ֩\rb*\rb |וְלֹא־\rb* \rb and fight|תִלָּ֨חֲמ֜וּ\rb* \rb against|עִם־\rb* \rb your brothers|אֲחֵיכֶ֗ם\rb*. \rb Each|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of you must return|שׁ֚וּבוּ\rb* \rb home|לְבֵית֔וֹ\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֧י\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֣ר\rb* \rb is|נִהְיָ֖ה\rb* \rb My doing|מֵֽאִתִּ֛י\rb*.’”
\p \rb So they listened|וַֽיִּשְׁמְעוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to the words|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and turned back|וַיָּשֻׁ֖בוּ\rb* \rb from going|מִלֶּ֥כֶת\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָֽם׃פ\rb*.
\s1 Rehoboam Fortifies Judah
\p \v 5 \rb Rehoboam|רְחַבְעָ֖ם\rb* \rb lived|וַיֵּ֥שֶׁב\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb*, \rb and he built up|וַיִּ֧בֶן\rb* \rb cities|עָרִ֛ים\rb* \rb for defense|לְמָצ֖וֹר\rb* \rb in Judah|בִּיהוּדָֽה׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb He built up|וַיִּ֧בֶן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb Bethlehem|לֶ֛חֶם\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Etam|עֵיטָ֖ם\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Tekoa|תְּקֽוֹעַ׃\rb*, \v 7 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb Beth-zur|צ֥וּר\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Soco|שׂוֹכ֖וֹ\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Adullam|עֲדֻלָּֽם׃\rb*, \v 8 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Gath|גַּ֥ת\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Mareshah|מָרֵשָׁ֖ה\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Ziph|זִֽיף׃\rb*, \v 9 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Adoraim|אֲדוֹרַ֥יִם\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Lachish|לָכִ֖ישׁ\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Azekah|עֲזֵקָֽה׃\rb*, \v 10 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Zorah|צָרְעָה֙\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Aijalon|אַיָּל֔וֹן\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Hebron|חֶבְר֔וֹן\rb*,\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the fortified|מְצֻרֽוֹת׃\rb* \rb cities|עָרֵ֖י\rb* \rb in Judah|בִּיהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb and Benjamin|וּבְבִנְיָמִ֑ן\rb*. \v 11 \rb He strengthened|וַיְחַזֵּ֖ק\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their fortifications|הַמְּצֻר֑וֹת\rb* \rb and put|וַיִּתֵּ֤ן\rb* \rb officers|נְגִידִ֔ים\rb* \rb in them|בָּהֶם֙\rb*, \rb with supplies|וְאֹצְר֥וֹת\rb* \rb of food|מַאֲכָ֖ל\rb*, \rb oil|וְשֶׁ֥מֶן\rb*, \rb and wine|וָיָֽיִן׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb He also put shields|צִנּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb and spears|וּרְמָחִ֔ים\rb* \rb in all|וּבְכָל־\rb*\rb |עִ֤יר\rb* \rb the cities|וָעִיר֙\rb* \rb and strengthened them|וַֽיְחַזְּקֵ֖ם\rb* \rb greatly|לְהַרְבֵּ֣ה\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֑ד\rb*. \rb So Judah|יְהוּדָ֥ה\rb* \rb and Benjamin|וּבִנְיָמִֽן׃ס\rb* \rb belonged|וַיְהִי־\rb* \rb to him|ל֖וֹ\rb*.
\s1 Jeroboam Forsakes the Priests and Levites
\p \v 13 \rb Moreover, the priests|וְהַכֹּהֲנִים֙\rb* \rb and Levites|וְהַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb* \rb from|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb their districts|גְּבוּלָֽם׃\rb* \rb throughout|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb stood|הִֽתְיַצְּב֥וּ\rb* \rb with Rehoboam|עָלָ֖יו\rb*. \v 14 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb left|עָזְב֣וּ\rb* \rb their pasturelands|מִגְרְשֵׁיהֶם֙\rb* \rb and their possessions|וַאֲחֻזָּתָ֔ם\rb* \rb and went|וַיֵּלְכ֥וּ\rb* \rb to Judah|לִיהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb and Jerusalem|וְלִֽירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb Jeroboam|יָֽרָבְעָם֙\rb* \rb and his sons|וּבָנָ֔יו\rb* \rb had rejected them|הִזְנִיחָ֤ם\rb* \rb as priests|מִכַּהֵ֖ן\rb* \rb of the LORD|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb And Jeroboam appointed|וַיַּֽעֲמֶד־\rb* \rb his own|לוֹ֙\rb* \rb priests|כֹּֽהֲנִ֔ים\rb* \rb for the high places|לַבָּמ֖וֹת\rb* \rb and for the goat demons|וְלַשְּׂעִירִ֑ים\rb* \rb and calf idols|וְלָעֲגָלִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he had made|עָשָֽׂה׃\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb Those from every|מִכֹּל֙\rb* \rb tribe|שִׁבְטֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb who had set|הַנֹּֽתְנִים֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their hearts|לְבָבָ֔ם\rb* \rb to seek|לְבַקֵּ֕שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb their|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb*\rb |וְאַחֲרֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb followed the Levites|בָּ֚אוּ\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|יְר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb to sacrifice|לִזְבּ֕וֹחַ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of their fathers|אֲבוֹתֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb So they strengthened|וַֽיְחַזְּקוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the kingdom|מַלְכ֣וּת\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb and supported|וַֽיְאַמְּצ֛וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Rehoboam|רְחַבְעָ֥ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֖ה\rb* \rb for three|שָׁל֑וֹשׁ\rb* \rb years|לְשָׁנִ֣ים\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb they walked|הָֽלְכ֗וּ\rb* \rb for three|שָׁלֽוֹשׁ׃\rb* \rb years|לְשָׁנִ֥ים\rb* \rb in the way|בְּדֶ֧רֶךְ\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֛יד\rb* \rb and Solomon|וּשְׁלֹמֹ֖ה\rb*.
\s1 Rehoboam’s Family
\p \v 18 \rb And Rehoboam|רְחַבְעָם֙\rb* \rb married|וַיִּֽקַּֽח־\rb*\rb |ל֤וֹ\rb*\rb |אִשָּׁ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Mahalath|מָ֣חֲלַ֔ת\rb*, \rb who was the daughter|בֶּן\rb* \rb of David’s|דָּוִ֑יד\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb Jerimoth|יְרִימ֖וֹת\rb* \rb and of Abihail|אֲבִיהַ֕יִל\rb*, \rb the daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Jesse’s|יִשָֽׁי׃\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb Eliab|אֱלִיאָ֖ב\rb*. \v 19 \rb She bore|וַתֵּ֥לֶד\rb* \rb sons|בָּנִ֑ים\rb* \rb to him|ל֖וֹ\rb*:\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Jeush|יְע֥וּשׁ\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Shemariah|שְׁמַרְיָ֖ה\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Zaham|זָֽהַם׃\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb After her|וְאַחֲרֶ֣יהָ\rb*, \rb he married|לָקַ֔ח\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb Maacah|מַעֲכָ֖ה\rb* \rb daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Absalom|אַבְשָׁל֑וֹם\rb*, \rb and she bore|וַתֵּ֣לֶד\rb* \rb to him|ל֗וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Abijah|אֲבִיָּה֙\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Attai|עַתַּ֔י\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Ziza|זִיזָ֖א\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Shelomith|שְׁלֹמִֽית׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb Rehoboam|רְחַבְעָ֜ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb loved|וַיֶּאֱהַ֨ב\rb* \rb Maacah|מַעֲכָ֣ה\rb* \rb daughter|בַת־\rb* \rb of Absalom|אַבְשָׁל֗וֹם\rb* \rb more than all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb his wives|נָשָׁיו֙\rb* \rb and concubines|וּפִ֣ילַגְשָׁ֔יו\rb*.\rb |כִּ֠י\rb* \rb In all, he had|נָשָׂ֔א\rb* \rb eighteen|שְׁמוֹנֶֽה־\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵה֙\rb* \rb wives|נָשִׁ֤ים\rb* \rb and sixty|שִׁשִּׁ֑ים\rb* \rb concubines|וּפִֽילַגְשִׁ֖ים\rb*, \rb and he was the father|וַיּ֗וֹלֶד\rb* \rb of twenty-eight|עֶשְׂרִ֧ים\rb*\rb |וּשְׁמוֹנָ֛ה\rb* \rb sons|בָּנִ֖ים\rb* \rb and sixty|וְשִׁשִּׁ֥ים\rb* \rb daughters|בָּנֽוֹת׃\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb Rehoboam|רְחַבְעָ֛ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb appointed|וַיַּֽעֲמֵ֨ד\rb* \rb Abijah|אֲבִיָּ֥ה\rb* \rb son|בֶֽן־\rb* \rb of Maacah|מַעֲכָ֖ה\rb* \rb as chief|לָרֹ֧אשׁ\rb* \rb prince|לְנָגִ֣יד\rb* \rb among his brothers|בְּאֶחָ֑יו\rb*,\rb |כִּ֖י\rb* \rb intending to make him king|לְהַמְלִיכֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 23 \rb Rehoboam also acted wisely|וַיָּבֶן֩\rb* \rb by dispersing|וַיִּפְרֹ֨ץ\rb* \rb some of his sons|בָּנָ֜יו\rb* \rb throughout|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb the districts|אַרְצ֧וֹת\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֣ה\rb* \rb and Benjamin|וּבִנְיָמִ֗ן\rb*,\rb |לְכֹל֙\rb* \rb and to all|לְֽכָל־\rb* \rb the fortified|הַמְּצֻר֔וֹת\rb* \rb cities|עָרֵ֣י\rb*. \rb He gave|וַיִּתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb abundant|לָרֹ֑ב\rb* \rb provisions|הַמָּז֖וֹן\rb* \rb and sought|וַיִּשְׁאַ֖ל\rb* \rb many|הֲמ֥וֹן\rb* \rb wives for them|נָשִֽׁים׃\rb*.
\c 12
\s1 Shishak Raids Jerusalem
\r (1 Kings 14:25–28)
\p \v 1 \rb |וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb After Rehoboam had established|כְּהָכִ֞ין\rb* \rb his|רְחַבְעָם֙\rb* \rb sovereignty|מַלְכ֤וּת\rb* \rb and royal power|וּכְחֶזְקָת֔וֹ\rb*, \rb he and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*\f + \fr 12:1 \ft That is, Judah; in 2 Chronicles, Judah is occasionally called Israel, as representative of the true Israel.\f* \rb with him|עִמּֽוֹ׃פ\rb* \rb forsook|עָזַ֖ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Law|תּוֹרַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*. \v 2 \rb |וַיְהִ֞י\rb* \rb In the fifth|הַֽחֲמִישִׁית֙\rb* \rb year|בַּשָּׁנָ֤ה\rb* \rb of Rehoboam’s|רְחַבְעָ֔ם\rb* \rb reign|לַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb they had been unfaithful|מָעֲל֖וּ\rb* \rb to the LORD|בַּיהוָֽה׃\rb*, \rb Shishak|שִׁישַׁ֥ק\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb attacked|עָלָ֛ה\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \v 3 \rb with 1,200|בְּאֶ֤לֶף\rb*\rb |וּמָאתַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb chariots|רֶ֔כֶב\rb*, \rb 60,000|וּבְשִׁשִּׁ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֶ֖לֶף\rb* \rb horsemen|פָּרָשִׁ֑ים\rb*,\f + \fr 12:3 \ft Or \fqa charioteers\f* \rb and countless|וְאֵ֣ין\rb*\rb |מִסְפָּ֗ר\rb* \rb troops|לָעָ֞ם\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb came|בָּ֤אוּ\rb* \rb with him|עִמּוֹ֙\rb* \rb out of Egypt|מִמִּצְרַ֔יִם\rb*— \rb Libyans|לוּבִ֥ים\rb*, \rb Sukkites|סֻכִּיִּ֖ים\rb*, \rb and Cushites|וְכוּשִֽׁים׃\rb*.\f + \fr 12:3 \ft That is, people from the upper Nile region\f* \v 4 \rb He captured|וַיִּלְכֹּ֛ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the fortified|הַמְּצֻר֖וֹת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb cities|עָרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Judah|לִֽיהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb and came|וַיָּבֹ֖א\rb* \rb as far as|עַד־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb Then Shemaiah|וּֽשְׁמַֽעְיָ֤ה\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִיא֙\rb* \rb came|בָּ֣א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Rehoboam|רְחַבְעָ֔ם\rb* \rb and the leaders|וְשָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb had gathered|נֶאֶסְפ֥וּ\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \rb because of|מִפְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Shishak|שִׁישָׁ֑ק\rb*, \rb and he said to|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֜ם\rb*, “\rb This is what|כֹּה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר\rb*: ‘\rb You|אַתֶּם֙\rb* \rb have forsaken Me|עֲזַבְתֶּ֣ם\rb*;\rb |אֹתִ֔י\rb* \rb therefore|וְאַף־\rb*, \rb I|אֲנִ֛י\rb* \rb have forsaken|עָזַ֥בְתִּי\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb into the hand|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb of Shishak|שִׁישָֽׁק׃\rb*.’”
\p \v 6 \rb So the leaders|שָׂרֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb and the king|וְהַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb humbled themselves|וַיִּכָּנְע֥וּ\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּאמְר֖וּ\rb*, “\rb The LORD is|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb righteous|צַדִּ֥יק׀\rb*.”
\p \v 7 \rb When the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb saw|וּבִרְא֤וֹת\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb they had humbled themselves|נִכְנָ֔עוּ\rb*, \rb the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb came|הָיָה֩\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Shemaiah|שְׁמַֽעְיָ֧ה׀\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֛ר\rb*, “\rb They have humbled themselves|נִכְנְע֖וּ\rb*; \rb I will not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb destroy them|אַשְׁחִיתֵ֑ם\rb*, \rb but will soon grant|וְנָתַתִּ֨י\rb*\rb |כִּמְעַט֙\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֤ם\rb* \rb deliverance|לִפְלֵיטָ֔ה\rb*. \rb My wrath|חֲמָתִ֛י\rb* \rb will not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb be poured out|תִתַּ֧ךְ\rb* \rb on Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \rb through|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb Shishak|שִׁישָֽׁק׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb Nevertheless|כִּ֥י\rb*, \rb they will become|יִהְיוּ־\rb* \rb his|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb servants|לַעֲבָדִ֑ים\rb*, \rb so that they may learn|וְיֵדְעוּ֙\rb* \rb the difference between serving Me|עֲב֣וֹדָתִ֔י\rb* \rb and serving|וַעֲבוֹדַ֖ת\rb* \rb the kings|מַמְלְכ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of other lands|הָאֲרָצֽוֹת׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 9 \rb So King|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb Shishak|שִׁישַׁ֥ק\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַיִם֮\rb* \rb attacked|וַיַּ֨עַל\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַם֒\rb* \rb and seized|וַיִּקַּ֞ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the treasures|אֹצְר֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |אֹֽצְרוֹת֙\rb* \rb of the royal|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb palace|בֵּ֣ית\rb*. \rb He took|לָקָ֑ח\rb* \rb everything|הַכֹּ֖ל\rb*, \rb including|וַיִּקַּח֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the gold|הַזָּהָ֔ב\rb* \rb shields|מָגִנֵּ֣י\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹֽה׃\rb* \rb had made|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb Then King|הַמֶּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb Rehoboam|רְחַבְעָם֙\rb* \rb made|וַיַּ֨עַשׂ\rb* \rb bronze|נְחֹ֑שֶׁת\rb* \rb shields|מָגִנֵּ֖י\rb* \rb in their place|תַּחְתֵּיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and committed them|וְהִפְקִ֗יד\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the care|יַד֙\rb* \rb of the captains|שָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the guard|הָרָצִ֔ים\rb* \rb on duty|הַשֹּׁ֣מְרִ֔ים\rb* \rb at the entrance|פֶּ֖תַח\rb* \rb to the royal|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb palace|בֵּ֥ית\rb*. \v 11 \rb And|וַיְהִ֛י\rb* \rb whenever|מִדֵּי־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb entered|ב֥וֹא\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb the guards|הָרָצִים֙\rb* \rb would go with him|בָּ֤אוּ\rb*, \rb bearing the shields|וּנְשָׂא֔וּם\rb*, \rb and later they would return them|וֶהֱשִׁב֖וּם\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the guardroom|הָרָצִֽים׃\rb*\rb |תָּ֥א\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb Because Rehoboam humbled himself|וּבְהִכָּֽנְע֗וֹ\rb*, \rb the anger|אַף־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb turned away|שָׁ֤ב\rb* \rb from him|מִמֶּ֙נּוּ֙\rb*, \rb and He did not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb destroy him completely|לְהַשְׁחִ֖ית\rb*\rb |לְכָלָ֑ה\rb*. \rb Indeed|וְגַם֙\rb*, \rb conditions|דְּבָרִ֥ים\rb* \rb were|הָיָ֖ה\rb* \rb good|טוֹבִֽים׃ס\rb* \rb in Judah|בִּֽיהוּדָ֔ה\rb*.
\s1 Rehoboam’s Reign and Death
\r (1 Kings 14:21–24)
\p \v 13 \rb Thus King|הַמֶּ֧לֶךְ\rb* \rb Rehoboam|רְחַבְעָ֛ם\rb* \rb established himself|וַיִּתְחַזֵּ֞ק\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \rb and reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֑ךְ\rb*.\rb |כִּ֣י\rb* \rb He was|רְחַבְעָ֨ם\rb* \rb forty-one|אַרְבָּעִ֣ים\rb*\rb |וְאַחַ֣ת\rb* \rb years old|בֶן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָה֩\rb* \rb when he became king|בְּמָלְכ֜וֹ\rb*, \rb and he reigned|מָלַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb seventeen|וּֽשֲׁבַ֨ע\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֥ה\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֣ה׀\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּֽירוּשָׁלִַ֗ם\rb*, \rb the city|הָ֠עִיר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb had chosen|בָּחַ֨ר\rb* \rb from all|מִכֹּל֙\rb* \rb the tribes|שִׁבְטֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb in which to put|לָשׂ֨וּם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb His Name|שְׁמ֥וֹ\rb*.\rb |שָׁם֙\rb* \rb His mother’s|אִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb name|וְשֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb was Naamah|נַעֲמָ֖ה\rb* \rb the Ammonite|הָֽעַמֹּנִֽית׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb And Rehoboam did evil|וַיַּ֖עַשׂ\rb*\rb |הָרָ֑ע\rb* \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb he did not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb set|הֵכִין֙\rb* \rb his heart|לִבּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb to seek|לִדְר֖וֹשׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb Now the acts|וְדִבְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Rehoboam|רְחַבְעָ֗ם\rb*, \rb from first|הָרִאשֹׁנִים֙\rb* \rb to last|וְהָאֲ֣חַרוֹנִ֔ים\rb*, \rb are they|הֲלֹא־\rb* \rb not|הֵ֨ם\rb* \rb written|כְּתוּבִ֜ים\rb* \rb in the records|בְּדִבְרֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Shemaiah|שְׁמַֽעְיָ֧ה\rb* \rb the Prophet|הַנָּבִ֛יא\rb* \rb and of Iddo|וְעִדּ֥וֹ\rb* \rb the Seer|הַחֹזֶ֖ה\rb* \rb concerning the genealogies|לְהִתְיַחֵ֑שׂ\rb*? \rb There was war|וּמִלְחֲמ֧וֹת\rb* \rb between Rehoboam|רְחַבְעָ֛ם\rb* \rb and Jeroboam|וְיָרָבְעָ֖ם\rb* \rb throughout|כָּל־\rb* \rb their days|הַיָּמִֽים׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb And Rehoboam|רְחַבְעָם֙\rb* \rb rested|וַיִּשְׁכַּ֤ב\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb his fathers|אֲבֹתָ֔יו\rb* \rb and was buried|וַיִּקָּבֵ֖ר\rb* \rb in the City|בְּעִ֣יר\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֑יד\rb*. \rb And his son|בְנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Abijah|אֲבִיָּ֥ה\rb*\f + \fr 12:16 \fqa Abijah \ft is a variant of \fqa Abijam\ft ; see 1 Kings 14:31.\f* \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֛ךְ\rb* \rb in his place|תַּחְתָּֽיו׃פ\rb*.
\c 13
\s1 Abijah Reigns in Judah
\r (1 Kings 15:1–8)
\p \v 1 \rb In the eighteenth|שְׁמוֹנֶ֥ה\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֖ה\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַ֛ת\rb* \rb of Jeroboam’s|יָרָבְעָ֑ם\rb* \rb reign|לַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb*, \rb Abijah|אֲבִיָּ֖ה\rb*\f + \fr 13:1 \fqa Abijah \ft is a variant of \fqa Abijam\ft ; see 1 Kings 14:31.\f* \rb became king|וַיִּמְלֹ֥ךְ\rb* \rb of|עַל־\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb*, \v 2 \rb and he reigned|מָלַךְ֙\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּיר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb three|שָׁל֣וֹשׁ\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִ֗ים\rb*. \rb His mother’s|אִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb name|וְשֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb was Micaiah|מִיכָיָ֥הוּ\rb*\f + \fr 13:2 \ft Hebrew; most LXX manuscripts and Syriac \fqa Maacah\ft ; see 2 Chronicles 11:20 and 1 Kings 15:2.\f* \rb daughter|בַת־\rb*\f + \fr 13:2 \ft Or \fqa granddaughter\f* \rb of Uriel|אוּרִיאֵ֖ל\rb*; \rb she was from|מִן־\rb* \rb Gibeah|גִּבְעָ֑ה\rb*.
\p \rb And there was|הָיְתָ֛ה\rb* \rb war|וּמִלְחָמָ֥ה\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb Abijah|אֲבִיָּ֖ה\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֥ין\rb* \rb and Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָֽם׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb Abijah|אֲבִיָּ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb went|וַיֶּאְסֹ֨ר\rb* \rb into battle|הַמִּלְחָמָ֗ה\rb* \rb with an army|בְּחַ֙יִל֙\rb*\rb |גִּבּוֹרֵ֣י\rb*\rb |מִלְחָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb of 400,000|אַרְבַּע־\rb*\rb |מֵא֥וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶ֖לֶף\rb* \rb chosen|בָּח֑וּרס\rb* \rb men|אִ֣ישׁ\rb*, \rb while Jeroboam|וְיָרָבְעָ֗ם\rb* \rb drew up|עָרַ֤ךְ\rb* \rb in formation|מִלְחָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb against him|עִמּוֹ֙\rb* \rb with 800,000|בִּשְׁמוֹנֶ֨ה\rb*\rb |מֵא֥וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶ֛לֶף\rb* \rb chosen|בָּח֖וּר\rb* \rb and mighty|גִּבּ֥וֹר\rb* \rb men|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb of valor|חָֽיִל׃ס\rb*.
\s1 Civil War against Jeroboam
\p \v 4 \rb Then Abijah|אֲבִיָּ֗ה\rb* \rb stood|וַיָּ֣קָם\rb* \rb on|מֵעַל֙\rb* \rb Mount|לְהַ֣ר\rb* \rb Zemaraim|צְמָרַ֔יִם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb in the hill country|בְּהַ֣ר\rb* \rb of Ephraim|אֶפְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Hear me|שְׁמָע֖וּנִי\rb*, \rb O Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֥ם\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*! \v 5 \rb Do you not|הֲלֹ֤א\rb*\rb |לָכֶם֙\rb* \rb know|לָדַ֔עַת\rb* \rb that|כִּ֞י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה׀\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb*, \rb has given|נָתַ֨ן\rb* \rb the kingship|מַמְלָכָ֧ה\rb* \rb of|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb to David|לְדָוִ֛יד\rb* \rb and his descendants|וּלְבָנָ֖יו\rb* \rb forever|לְעוֹלָ֑ם\rb* \rb by a covenant|בְּרִ֥ית\rb* \rb of salt|מֶֽלַח׃ס\rb*\f + \fr 13:5 \ft That is, a perpetual covenant\f*? \v 6 \rb Yet Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֣ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Nebat|נְבָ֔ט\rb*, \rb a servant|עֶ֖בֶד\rb* \rb of Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֣ה\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֑יד\rb*, \rb rose up|וַיָּ֙קָם֙\rb* \rb and rebelled|וַיִּמְרֹ֖ד\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb his master|אֲדֹנָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb Then worthless|רֵקִים֙\rb* \rb and wicked|בְלִיַּ֔עַל\rb* \rb men|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb gathered|וַיִּקָּבְצ֣וּ\rb* \rb around him|עָלָ֗יו\rb*\rb |אֲנָשִׁ֤ים\rb* \rb to resist|וַיִּֽתְאַמְּצ֖וּ\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb Rehoboam|רְחַבְעָ֣ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֑ה\rb* \rb when he|וּרְחַבְעָ֗ם\rb* \rb was|הָ֤יָה\rb* \rb young|נַ֙עַר֙\rb*, \rb inexperienced|וְרַךְ־\rb*,\rb |לֵבָ֔ב\rb* \rb and unable|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb to resist|הִתְחַזַּ֖ק\rb* \rb them|לִפְנֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb And now|וְעַתָּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb think|אֹֽמְרִ֗ים\rb* \rb you can resist|לְהִתְחַזֵּק֙\rb*\rb |לִפְנֵי֙\rb* \rb the kingdom|מַמְלֶ֣כֶת\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb which is in the hands|בְּיַ֖ד\rb* \rb of David’s|דָוִ֑יד\rb* \rb descendants|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*. \rb You|וְאַתֶּם֙\rb* \rb are indeed a vast|רָ֔ב\rb* \rb army|הָמ֣וֹן\rb*, \rb and you have with you|וְעִמָּכֶם֙\rb* \rb the golden|זָהָ֔ב\rb* \rb calves|עֶגְלֵ֣י\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֖ם\rb* \rb made|עָשָׂ֥ה\rb* \rb for you|לָכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb as gods|לֵאלֹהִֽים׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb But did you not|הֲלֹ֤א\rb* \rb drive out|הִדַּחְתֶּם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the priests|כֹּהֲנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb*, \rb and the Levites|וְהַלְוִיִּ֑ם\rb*? \rb And did you not make|וַתַּעֲשׂ֨וּ\rb* \rb priests|כֹּהֲנִים֙\rb* \rb for yourselves|לָכֶ֤ם\rb* \rb as do the peoples|כְּעַמֵּ֣י\rb* \rb of other lands|הָאֲרָצ֔וֹת\rb*? \rb Now whoever|כָּל־\rb* \rb comes|הַבָּ֗א\rb* \rb to consecrate|לְמַלֵּ֨א\rb* \rb himself|יָד֜וֹ\rb* \rb with a young bull|בְּפַ֤ר\rb*\rb |בֶּן־\rb*\rb |בָּקָר֙\rb* \rb and seven|שִׁבְעָ֔ה\rb* \rb rams|וְאֵילִ֣ם\rb* \rb can become|וְהָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb a priest|כֹהֵ֖ן\rb* \rb of things that are not|לְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb gods|אֱלֹהִֽים׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb But as for us|וַאֲנַ֛חְנוּ\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb is our God|אֱלֹהֵ֖ינוּ\rb*. \rb We have not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb forsaken Him|עֲזַבְנֻ֑הוּ\rb*; \rb the priests|וְכֹ֨הֲנִ֜ים\rb* \rb who minister|מְשָׁרְתִ֤ים\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָה֙\rb* \rb are sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֔ן\rb*, \rb and the Levites|וְהַלְוִיִּ֖ם\rb* \rb attend to their duties|בַּמְלָֽאכֶת׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb Every morning|בַּבֹּֽקֶר־\rb*\rb |בַּבֹּ֣קֶר\rb* \rb and every evening|וּבָעֶֽרֶב־\rb*\rb |בָּעֶ֣רֶב\rb* \rb they present|וּמַקְטִרִ֣ים\rb* \rb burnt offerings|עֹל֣וֹת\rb* \rb and fragrant|סַמִּים֩\rb* \rb incense|וּקְטֹֽרֶת־\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֡ה\rb*. \rb They set out the rows|וּמַעֲרֶ֨כֶת\rb* \rb of showbread|לֶ֜חֶם\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the ceremonially clean|הַטָּה֗וֹר\rb* \rb table|הַשֻּׁלְחָ֣ן\rb*, \rb and every evening|בָּעֶ֣רֶב\rb*\rb |בָּעֶ֔רֶב\rb* \rb they light|לְבָעֵר֙\rb* \rb the lamps|וְנֵרֹתֶ֙יהָ֙\rb* \rb of the gold|הַזָּהָ֤ב\rb* \rb lampstand|וּמְנוֹרַ֨ת\rb*.\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb We|אֲנַ֔חְנוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb are carrying out|שֹׁמְרִ֣ים\rb* \rb the requirements|מִשְׁמֶ֖רֶת\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֑ינוּ\rb*, \rb while you|וְאַתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb have forsaken|עֲזַבְתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb Him|אֹתֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb Now behold|וְהִנֵּה֩\rb*, \rb God Himself is|הָאֱלֹהִ֧ים׀\rb* \rb with us|עִמָּ֨נוּ\rb* \rb as our head|בָרֹ֜אשׁ\rb*, \rb and His priests|וְכֹהֲנָ֛יו\rb* \rb with their trumpets|וַחֲצֹצְר֥וֹת\rb* \rb sound|לְהָרִ֣יעַ\rb* \rb the battle call|הַתְּרוּעָ֖ה\rb* \rb against you|עֲלֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb O children|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb*, \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb fight|תִּלָּֽחֲמ֛וּ\rb* \rb against|עִם־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵֽי־\rb* \rb of your fathers|אֲבֹתֵיכֶ֖ם\rb*, \rb for|כִּי־\rb* \rb you will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb succeed|תַצְלִֽיחוּ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 13 \rb Now Jeroboam|וְיָֽרָבְעָ֗ם\rb* \rb had sent troops|לָב֖וֹא\rb* \rb around|הֵסֵב֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to ambush|הַמַּאְרָ֔ב\rb* \rb from the rear|מֵֽאַחֲרֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb so that while he was|וַיִּֽהְיוּ֙\rb* \rb in front|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb*, \rb the ambush|וְהַמַּאְרָ֖ב\rb* \rb was behind them|מֵאַחֲרֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb When Judah|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb* \rb turned|וַיִּפְנ֣וּ\rb* \rb and discovered|וְהִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb that the battle|הַמִּלְחָמָה֙\rb* \rb was both before|פָּנִ֣ים\rb* \rb and behind them|וְאָח֔וֹר\rb*, \rb they cried out|וַֽיִּצְעֲק֖וּ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֑ה\rb*. \rb Then the priests|וְהַכֹּ֣הֲנִ֔ים\rb* \rb blew|מַחֲצֹצְרִים\rb* \rb the trumpets|בַּחֲצֹצְרֽוֹת׃\rb*, \v 15 \rb and the men|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb*\rb |וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb raised the battle cry|וַיָּרִ֖יעוּ\rb*. \rb And when they|אִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb raised the cry|בְּהָרִ֙יעַ֙\rb*, \rb God|וְהָאֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb routed|נָגַ֤ף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Jeroboam|יָֽרָבְעָם֙\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb Abijah|אֲבִיָּ֖ה\rb* \rb and Judah|וִיהוּדָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb So the Israelites|בְנֵי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb fled|וַיָּנ֥וּסוּ\rb* \rb before|מִפְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb delivered them|וַיִּתְּנֵ֥ם\rb* \rb into their hands|בְּיָדָֽם׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb Then Abijah|אֲבִיָּ֥ה\rb* \rb and his people|וְעַמּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb struck|וַיַּכּ֥וּ\rb* \rb them|בָהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb with a mighty|רַבָּ֑ה\rb* \rb blow|מַכָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb and 500,000|חֲמֵשׁ־\rb*\rb |מֵא֥וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶ֖לֶף\rb* \rb chosen|בָּחֽוּר׃\rb* \rb men|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb of Israel|מִיִּשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb fell|וַיִּפְּל֤וּ\rb* \rb slain|חֲלָלִים֙\rb*. \v 18 \rb Thus the Israelites|בְנֵי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb were subdued|וַיִּכָּנְע֥וּ\rb* \rb at that|הַהִ֑יא\rb* \rb time|בָּעֵ֣ת\rb*, \rb and the men|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb prevailed|וַיֶּֽאֶמְצוּ֙\rb* \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb they relied|נִשְׁעֲנ֔וּ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of their fathers|אֲבוֹתֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb Abijah|אֲבִיָּה֮\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb pursued|וַיִּרְדֹּ֣ף\rb* \rb Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָם֒\rb* \rb and captured|וַיִּלְכֹּ֤ד\rb* \rb some cities|עָרִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb from him|מִמֶּ֙נּוּ֙\rb*:\rb |בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb Bethel|אֵל֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Jeshanah|יְשָׁנָ֖ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb*, \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Ephron|עֶפְרוֹן\rb*, \rb along with their villages|וּבְנֹתֶֽיהָ׃\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֛ם\rb* \rb did not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb again|ע֖וֹד\rb* \rb recover|עָצַ֧ר\rb* \rb his power|כֹּֽחַ־\rb* \rb during the days|בִּימֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Abijah|אֲבִיָּ֑הוּ\rb*, \rb and the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb struck him down|וַיִּגְּפֵ֥הוּ\rb* \rb and he died|וַיָּמֹֽת׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb But Abijah|אֲבִיָּ֔הוּ\rb* \rb grew strong|וַיִּתְחַזֵּ֣ק\rb*, \rb married|וַיִּ֨שָּׂא־\rb*\rb |ל֔וֹ\rb* \rb fourteen|אַרְבַּ֣ע\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֑ה\rb* \rb wives|נָשִׁ֖ים\rb*, \rb and became the father|וַיּ֗וֹלֶד\rb* \rb of twenty-two|עֶשְׂרִ֤ים\rb*\rb |וּשְׁנַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb sons|בָּנִ֔ים\rb* \rb and sixteen|וְשֵׁ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֖ה\rb* \rb daughters|בָּנֽוֹת׃ס\rb*. \v 22 \rb Now the rest|וְיֶ֙תֶר֙\rb* \rb of the acts|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Abijah|אֲבִיָּ֔ה\rb*, \rb along with his ways|וּדְרָכָ֖יו\rb* \rb and his words|וּדְבָרָ֑יו\rb*, \rb are written|כְּתוּבִ֕ים\rb* \rb in the Treatise|בְּמִדְרַ֖שׁ\rb*\f + \fr 13:22 \ft Or \fqa Exposition \ft or \fqa Study\f* \rb of the Prophet|הַנָּבִ֥יא\rb* \rb Iddo|עִדּֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\c 14
\s1 Asa Reigns in Judah
\r (1 Kings 15:9–15)
\p \v 1 \rb Then Abijah|אֲבִיָּ֜ה\rb* \rb rested|וַיִּשְׁכַּ֨ב\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb his fathers|אֲבֹתָ֗יו\rb* \rb and was buried|וַיִּקְבְּר֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֹתוֹ֙\rb* \rb in the City|בְּעִ֣יר\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֔יד\rb*. \rb And his son|בְנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Asa|אָסָ֥א\rb* \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֛ךְ\rb* \rb in his place|תַּחְתָּ֑יו\rb*, \rb and in his days|בְּיָמָ֛יו\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb was at peace|שָׁקְטָ֥ה\rb* \rb for ten|עֶ֥שֶׂר\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִֽים׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb And Asa|אָסָא֙\rb* \rb did|וַיַּ֤עַשׂ\rb* \rb what was good|הַטּ֣וֹב\rb* \rb and right|וְהַיָּשָׁ֔ר\rb* \rb in the eyes|בְּעֵינֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb his God|אֱלֹהָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb He removed|וַיָּ֛סַר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the foreign|הַנֵּכָ֖ר\rb* \rb altars|מִזְבְּח֥וֹת\rb* \rb and high places|וְהַבָּמ֑וֹת\rb*, \rb shattered|וַיְשַׁבֵּר֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the sacred pillars|הַמַּצֵּב֔וֹת\rb*, \rb and chopped down|וַיְגַדַּ֖ע\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Asherah poles|הָאֲשֵׁרִֽים׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb He commanded|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb the people of Judah|לִֽיהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb to seek|לִדְר֕וֹשׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of their fathers|אֲבוֹתֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb and to observe|וְלַעֲשׂ֖וֹת\rb* \rb the law|הַתּוֹרָ֥ה\rb* \rb and the commandments|וְהַמִּצְוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb He also removed|וַיָּ֙סַר֙\rb* \rb the high places|הַבָּמ֖וֹת\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and incense altars|הַֽחַמָּנִ֑ים\rb* \rb from all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb the cities|עָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and under him|לְפָנָֽיו׃\rb* \rb the kingdom|הַמַּמְלָכָ֖ה\rb* \rb was at peace|וַתִּשְׁקֹ֥ט\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb Because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֗רֶץ\rb* \rb was at peace|שָׁקְטָ֣ה\rb*, \rb Asa built|וַיִּ֛בֶן\rb* \rb fortified|מְצוּרָ֖ה\rb* \rb cities|עָרֵ֥י\rb* \rb in Judah|בִּיהוּדָ֑ה\rb*. \rb In those|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb days|בַּשָּׁנִ֣ים\rb* \rb no one|וְאֵין־\rb* \rb made war|מִלְחָמָה֙\rb* \rb with him|עִמּ֤וֹ\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |לֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb had given him rest|הֵנִ֥יחַ\rb*. \v 7 \rb So he said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to the people of Judah|לִֽיהוּדָ֜ה\rb*, “\rb Let us build|נִבְנֶ֣ה׀\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֗לֶּה\rb* \rb cities|הֶעָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb and surround them|וְנָסֵ֨ב\rb* \rb with walls|חוֹמָ֣ה\rb* \rb and towers|וּמִגְדָּלִים֮\rb*, \rb with doors|דְּלָתַ֣יִם\rb* \rb and bars|וּבְרִיחִים֒\rb*. \rb The land|הָאָ֜רֶץ\rb* \rb is still|עוֹדֶ֨נּוּ\rb* \rb ours|לְפָנֵ֗ינוּ\rb* \rb because|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb we have sought|דָרַ֙שְׁנוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֔ינוּ\rb*. \rb We have sought Him|דָּרַ֕שְׁנוּ\rb*, \rb and He has given us rest|וַיָּ֥נַֽח\rb* \rb on|לָ֖נוּ\rb* \rb every side|מִסָּבִ֑יב\rb*.” \rb So they built|וַיִּבְנ֖וּ\rb* \rb and prospered|וַיַּצְלִֽיחוּ׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb Asa|לְאָסָ֗א\rb* \rb had|וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb an army|חַיִל֮\rb* \rb of 300,000 men|שְׁלֹ֣שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵא֣וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶ֔לֶףס\rb* \rb from Judah|מִֽיהוּדָה֙\rb* \rb bearing|נֹשֵׂ֣א\rb* \rb large shields|צִנָּ֣ה\rb* \rb and spears|וָרֹמַח֒\rb*, \rb and 280,000 men|מָאתַ֥יִם\rb*\rb |וּשְׁמוֹנִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אָ֑לֶף\rb* \rb from Benjamin|וּמִבִּנְיָמִ֗ן\rb* \rb bearing|נֹשְׂאֵ֤י\rb* \rb small shields|מָגֵן֙\rb* \rb and drawing|וְדֹ֣רְכֵי\rb* \rb the bow|קֶ֔שֶׁת\rb*. \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb these were|אֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb mighty men|גִּבּ֥וֹרֵי\rb* \rb of valor|חָֽיִל׃\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb Then Zerah|זֶ֣רַח\rb* \rb the Cushite|הַכּוּשִׁ֗י\rb* \rb came|וַיֵּצֵ֨א\rb* \rb against them|אֲלֵיהֶ֜ם\rb* \rb with an army|בְּחַ֙יִל֙\rb* \rb of 1,000,000 men|אֶ֣לֶף\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִ֔ים\rb*\f + \fr 14:9 \ft Or \fqa an army of thousands and thousands\ft ; Hebrew \fqa an army of a thousand thousands\f* \rb and 300|שְׁלֹ֣שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵא֑וֹת\rb* \rb chariots|וּמַרְכָּב֖וֹת\rb*, \rb and they advanced|וַיָּבֹ֖א\rb* \rb as far as|עַד־\rb* \rb Mareshah|מָרֵשָֽׁה׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb So Asa|אָסָ֖א\rb* \rb marched out|וַיֵּצֵ֥א\rb* \rb against him|לְפָנָ֑יו\rb* \rb and lined up|וַיַּֽעַרְכוּ֙\rb* \rb in battle formation|מִלְחָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb in the Valley|בְּגֵ֥יא\rb* \rb of Zephathah|צְפַ֖תָה\rb* \rb near Mareshah|לְמָרֵשָֽׁה׃\rb*.\f + \fr 14:10 \ft Or \fqa the valley north of Mareshah\f*
\p \v 11 \rb Then Asa|אָסָ֜א\rb* \rb cried out|וַיִּקְרָ֨א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb his God|אֱלֹהָיו֮\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמַר֒\rb*: “\rb O LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*, \rb there is no one|אֵֽין־\rb* \rb besides You|עִמְּךָ֤\rb* \rb to help|לַעְזוֹר֙\rb*\rb |בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb the powerless|לְאֵ֣ין\rb*\rb |כֹּ֔חַ\rb* \rb against the mighty|רַב֙\rb*. \rb Help us|עָזְרֵ֜נוּ\rb*, \rb O LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb we rely|נִשְׁעַ֔נּוּ\rb* \rb on You|עָלֶ֣יךָ\rb*, \rb and in Your name|וּבְשִׁמְךָ֣\rb* \rb we have come|בָ֔אנוּ\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb multitude|הֶהָמ֖וֹן\rb*. \rb O LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb*, \rb You|אַ֔תָּה\rb* \rb are our God|אֱלֹהֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb*. \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb let a mere mortal|אֱנֽוֹשׁ׃ס\rb* \rb prevail|יַעְצֹ֥ר\rb* \rb against You|עִמְּךָ֖\rb*.”
\p \v 12 \rb So the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb struck down|וַיִּגֹּ֤ף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Cushites|הַכּוּשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb Asa|אָסָ֖א\rb* \rb and|וְלִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and the Cushites|הַכּוּשִֽׁים׃\rb* \rb fled|וַיָּנֻ֖סוּ\rb*. \v 13 \rb Then Asa|אָסָ֜א\rb* \rb and his army|וְהָעָ֣ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |עִמּוֹ֮\rb* \rb pursued them|וַיִּרְדְּפֵ֨ם\rb* \rb as far as|עַד־\rb* \rb Gerar|לִגְרָר֒\rb*. \rb The Cushites|מִכּוּשִׁים֙\rb* \rb fell|וַיִּפֹּ֤ל\rb* \rb and could not|לְאֵ֣ין\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֣ם\rb* \rb recover|מִֽחְיָ֔ה\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb they were crushed|נִשְׁבְּר֥וּ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |וְלִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb and His army|מַחֲנֵ֑הוּ\rb*. \rb So the people of Judah carried off|וַיִּשְׂא֥וּ\rb* \rb a great amount of|הַרְבֵּ֥ה\rb*\rb |מְאֹֽד׃\rb* \rb plunder|שָׁלָ֖ל\rb* \v 14 \rb and attacked|וַיַּכּ֗וּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֤ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the cities|הֶֽעָרִים֙\rb* \rb around|סְבִיב֣וֹת\rb* \rb Gerar|גְּרָ֔ר\rb*, \rb because|כִּי־\rb* \rb the terror|פַֽחַד־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb had fallen|הָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb upon them|עֲלֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb They plundered|וַיָּבֹ֙זּוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the cities|הֶ֣עָרִ֔ים\rb*, \rb since|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb there was|הָיְתָ֥ה\rb* \rb much|רַבָּ֖ה\rb* \rb plunder|בִזָּ֥ה\rb* \rb there|בָהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb They also|וְגַם־\rb* \rb attacked|הִכּ֑וּ\rb* \rb the tents|אָהֳלֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the herdsmen|מִקְנֶ֖ה\rb* \rb and carried off|וַיִּשְׁבּ֨וּ\rb* \rb many|לָרֹב֙\rb* \rb sheep|צֹ֤אן\rb* \rb and camels|וּגְמַלִּ֔ים\rb*. \rb Then they returned|וַיָּשֻׁ֖בוּ\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃ס\rb*.
\c 15
\s1 The Prophecy of Azariah
\p \v 1 \rb Now the Spirit|ר֥וּחַ\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb* \rb came|הָיְתָ֥ה\rb* \rb upon|עָלָ֖יו\rb* \rb Azariah|וַעֲזַרְיָ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Oded|עוֹדֵ֔ד\rb*. \v 2 \rb So he went out|וַיֵּצֵא֮\rb* \rb to meet|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Asa|אָסָא֒\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to him|ל֔וֹ\rb*, “\rb Listen to me|שְׁמָע֕וּנִי\rb*, \rb Asa|אָסָ֖א\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֣ה\rb* \rb and Benjamin|וּבִנְיָמִ֑ן\rb*. \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb is with you|עִמָּכֶם֙\rb* \rb when you are|בִּֽהְיֽוֹתְכֶ֣ם\rb* \rb with Him|עִמּ֔וֹ\rb*. \rb If|וְאִֽם־\rb* \rb you seek Him|תִּדְרְשֻׁ֙הוּ֙\rb*, \rb He will be found|יִמָּצֵ֣א\rb* \rb by you|לָכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb but if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb you forsake Him|תַּעַזְבֻ֖הוּ\rb*, \rb He will forsake|יַעֲזֹ֥ב\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶֽם׃ס\rb*. \v 3 \rb For many|רַבִּ֖ים\rb* \rb years|וְיָמִ֥ים\rb* \rb Israel|לְיִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb has been without|לְלֹ֣א׀\rb* \rb the true|אֱמֶ֗ת\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb*, \rb without|וּלְלֹ֛א\rb* \rb a priest|כֹּהֵ֥ן\rb* \rb to instruct them|מוֹרֶ֖ה\rb*, \rb and without|וּלְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb the law|תוֹרָֽה׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb But in their distress|בַּצַּר־\rb*\rb |ל֔וֹ\rb* \rb they turned|וַיָּ֙שָׁב֙\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb and sought Him|וַיְבַקְשֻׁ֖הוּ\rb*, \rb and He was found|וַיִּמָּצֵ֥א\rb* \rb by them|לָהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb In those|הָהֵ֔ם\rb* \rb days|וּבָעִתִּ֣ים\rb* \rb there was no|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb safety|שָׁל֖וֹם\rb* \rb for travelers|לַיּוֹצֵ֣א\rb*\rb |וְלַבָּ֑א\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb the residents|יוֹשְׁבֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the lands|הָאֲרָצֽוֹת׃\rb* \rb had|עַ֥ל\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb many|רַבּ֔וֹת\rb* \rb conflicts|מְהוּמֹ֣ת\rb*. \v 6 \rb Nation|גוֹי־\rb* \rb was crushed|וְכֻתְּת֥וּ\rb* \rb by nation|בְּג֖וֹי\rb*, \rb and city|וְעִ֣יר\rb* \rb by city|בְּעִ֑יר\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֥ים\rb* \rb afflicted them|הֲמָמָ֖ם\rb* \rb with all kinds of|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb adversity|צָרָֽה׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb But as for you|וְאַתֶּ֣ם\rb*, \rb be strong|חִזְק֔וּ\rb*; \rb do not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb be discouraged|יִרְפּ֖וּ\rb*\rb |יְדֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb your work|לִפְעֻלַּתְכֶֽם׃ס\rb* \rb will be|יֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb rewarded|שָׂכָ֖ר\rb*.”
\s1 Asa’s Reforms
\r (1 Kings 15:9–15)
\p \v 8 \rb When Asa|אָסָ֜א\rb* \rb heard|וְכִשְׁמֹ֨עַ\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֗לֶּה\rb* \rb words|הַדְּבָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb and the prophecy|וְהַנְּבוּאָה֮\rb* \rb of Azariah son of Oded|עֹדֵ֣ד\rb*\f + \fr 15:8 \ft Vulgate and Syriac (see also verse 1 and LXX); Hebrew does not include \fqa Azariah son of\ft .\f* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִיא֒\rb*, \rb he took courage|הִתְחַזַּ֗ק\rb* \rb and removed|וַיַּעֲבֵ֤ר\rb* \rb the detestable idols|הַשִּׁקּוּצִים֙\rb* \rb from|וּמִן־\rb* \rb the whole|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb land|אֶ֤רֶץ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb* \rb and Benjamin|וּבִנְיָמִ֔ן\rb* \rb and from the cities|הֶ֣עָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb he had captured|לָכַ֖ד\rb* \rb in the hill country|מֵהַ֣ר\rb* \rb of Ephraim|אֶפְרָ֑יִם\rb*. \rb He then restored|וַיְחַדֵּשׁ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the altar|מִזְבַּ֣ח\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֕ר\rb* \rb was in front|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the portico|אוּלָ֥ם\rb* \rb of the LORD’s temple|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb And he assembled|וַיִּקְבֹּ֗ץ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb* \rb and Benjamin|וּבִנְיָמִ֔ן\rb*, \rb along with those from the tribes of Ephraim|מֵאֶפְרַ֥יִם\rb*, \rb Manasseh|וּמְנַשֶּׁ֖ה\rb*, \rb and Simeon|וּמִשִּׁמְע֑וֹן\rb* \rb who had settled|וְהַגָּרִים֙\rb* \rb among them|עִמָּהֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb great numbers|לָרֹ֔ב\rb* \rb had come over|נָפְל֨וּ\rb* \rb to him|עָלָ֤יו\rb* \rb from Israel|מִיִּשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb when they saw|בִּרְאֹתָ֕ם\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb his God|אֱלֹהָ֖יו\rb* \rb was with him|עִמּֽוֹ׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb So they gathered together|וַיִּקָּבְצ֥וּ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \rb in the third|הַשְּׁלִישִׁ֑י\rb* \rb month|בַּחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of the fifteenth|חֲמֵשׁ־\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֖ה\rb* \rb year|לִשְׁנַ֥ת\rb* \rb of Asa’s|אָסָֽא׃\rb* \rb reign|לְמַלְכ֥וּת\rb*. \v 11 \rb At that|הַה֔וּא\rb* \rb time|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb they sacrificed|וַיִּזְבְּח֤וּ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָה֙\rb* \rb seven|שְׁבַ֣ע\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֔וֹת\rb* \rb oxen|בָּקָר֙\rb* \rb and seven|שִׁבְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb thousand|אֲלָפִֽים׃\rb* \rb sheep|וְצֹ֖אן\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb all the plunder|הַשָּׁלָ֖ל\rb* \rb they had brought back|הֵבִ֑יאוּ\rb*. \v 12 \rb Then they entered|וַיָּבֹ֣אוּ\rb* \rb into a covenant|בַבְּרִ֔ית\rb* \rb to seek|לִדְר֕וֹשׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of their fathers|אֲבוֹתֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb with all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb their heart|לְבָבָ֖ם\rb* \rb and|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb soul|נַפְשָֽׁם׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb And|וְכֹ֨ל\rb* \rb whoever|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb would not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb seek|יִדְרֹ֛שׁ\rb* \rb the LORD|לַיהוָ֥ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb would be put to death|יוּמָ֑ת\rb*, \rb whether|לְמִן־\rb* \rb young|קָטֹן֙\rb* \rb or|וְעַד־\rb* \rb old|גָּד֔וֹל\rb*, \rb man|לְמֵאִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb or|וְעַד־\rb* \rb woman|אִשָּֽׁה׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb They took an oath|וַיִּשָּֽׁבְעוּ֙\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb with a loud|גָּד֖וֹל\rb* \rb voice|בְּק֥וֹל\rb*, \rb with shouting|וּבִתְרוּעָ֑ה\rb*, \rb trumpets|וּבַחֲצֹצְר֖וֹת\rb*, \rb and rams’ horns|וּבְשׁוֹפָרֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb And all|כָל־\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֜ה\rb* \rb rejoiced|וַיִּשְׂמְח֨וּ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the oath|הַשְּׁבוּעָ֗ה\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb they had sworn|נִשְׁבָּ֔עוּ\rb* \rb it with all|בְכָל־\rb* \rb their heart|לְבָבָם֙\rb*. \rb They had sought Him|בִּקְשֻׁ֔הוּ\rb* \rb earnestly|וּבְכָל־\rb*\rb |רְצוֹנָ֣ם\rb*, \rb and He was found|וַיִּמָּצֵ֖א\rb* \rb by them|לָהֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb So the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb gave them rest|וַיָּ֧נַח\rb* \rb on every side|מִסָּבִֽיב׃\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb King|הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb Asa|אָסָ֣א\rb* \rb also|וְגַֽם־\rb* \rb removed|הֱסִירָהּ֙\rb* \rb his grandmother|אֵ֣ם׀\rb*\f + \fr 15:16 \ft Hebrew \fqa his mother\f* \rb Maacah|מַעֲכָ֞ה\rb* \rb from her position as queen mother|מִגְּבִירָ֔ה\rb* \rb because|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb she had made|עָשְׂתָ֥ה\rb* \rb a detestable|מִפְלָ֑צֶת\rb* \rb Asherah pole|לַאֲשֵׁרָ֖ה\rb*. \rb Asa|אָסָא֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb chopped down|וַיִּכְרֹ֤ת\rb* \rb the pole|מִפְלַצְתָּ֔הּ\rb*, \rb crushed it|וַיָּ֕דֶק\rb*, \rb and burned|וַיִּשְׂרֹ֖ף\rb* \rb it in the Kidron|קִדְרֽוֹן׃\rb* \rb Valley|בְּנַ֥חַל\rb*. \v 17 \rb The high places|וְהַ֨בָּמ֔וֹת\rb* \rb were not|לֹא־\rb* \rb removed|סָ֖רוּ\rb* \rb from Israel|מִיִּשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb but|רַ֧ק\rb* \rb Asa’s|אָסָ֛א\rb* \rb heart|לְבַב־\rb* \rb was|הָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb fully devoted|שָׁלֵ֖ם\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb his days|יָמָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 18 \rb And he brought|וַיָּבֵ֞א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb into the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb* \rb the silver|כֶּ֥סֶף\rb* \rb and gold|וְזָהָ֖ב\rb* \rb and the articles|וְכֵלִֽים׃\rb* \rb that he|קָדְשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb and his father|אָבִ֛יו\rb* \rb had dedicated|וְקָֽדָשָׁ֖יו\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb And there was|הָיָ֑תָה\rb* \rb no|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb war|וּמִלְחָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb until|עַ֛ד\rb* \rb the thirty-fifth|שְׁלֹשִׁ֥ים\rb*\rb |וְחָמֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb year|שְׁנַת־\rb* \rb of Asa’s|אָסָֽא׃ס\rb* \rb reign|לְמַלְכ֥וּת\rb*.
\c 16
\s1 War between Asa and Baasha
\r (1 Kings 15:16–22)
\p \v 1 \rb In the thirty-sixth|שְׁלֹשִׁ֤ים\rb*\rb |וָשֵׁשׁ֙\rb*\rb |לְמַלְכ֣וּת\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַ֨ת\rb* \rb of Asa’s reign|אָסָ֔א\rb*, \rb Baasha|בַּעְשָׁ֤א\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb went up|עָלָ֞ה\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb and fortified|וַיִּ֖בֶן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Ramah|הָרָמָ֑ה\rb*\rb |לְבִלְתִּ֗י\rb* \rb to prevent|תֵּ֚ת\rb* \rb anyone from leaving|יוֹצֵ֣א\rb* \rb or entering the territory|וָבָ֔א\rb* \rb of Asa|לְאָסָ֖א\rb* \rb king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb So Asa|אָסָ֜א\rb* \rb withdrew|וַיֹּצֵ֨א\rb* \rb the silver|כֶּ֣סֶף\rb* \rb and gold|וְזָהָ֗ב\rb* \rb from the treasuries|מֵאֹֽצְר֛וֹת\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb and the royal|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb palace|וּבֵ֣ית\rb*, \rb and he sent it|וַיִּשְׁלַ֗ח\rb* \rb with this message|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb*\rb |בֶּן־\rb* \rb Ben-hadad|הֲדַד֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Aram|אֲרָ֔ם\rb*, \rb who was ruling|הַיּוֹשֵׁ֥ב\rb* \rb in Damascus|בְּדַרְמֶ֖שֶׂק\rb*: \v 3 “\rb Let there be a treaty|בְּרִית֙\rb*\f + \fr 16:3 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa berit \ft are translated in most passages as \fqa covenant\ft ; twice in this verse.\f* \rb between me and you|בֵּינִ֣י\rb* \rb as there was between|וּבֵינֶ֔ךָ\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֥ין\rb* \rb my father|אָבִ֖י\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֣ין\rb* \rb and your father|אָבִ֑יךָ\rb*. \rb See|הִנֵּ֨ה\rb*, \rb I have sent|שָׁלַ֤חְתִּֽי\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֙\rb* \rb silver|כֶּ֣סֶף\rb* \rb and gold|וְזָהָ֔ב\rb*. \rb Now go|לֵ֞ךְ\rb* \rb and break|הָפֵ֣ר\rb* \rb your treaty|בְּרִֽיתְךָ֗\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb Baasha|בַּעְשָׁא֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb so that he will withdraw|וְיַעֲלֶ֖ה\rb* \rb from me|מֵעָלָֽי׃\rb*.”
\p \v 4 \rb And Ben-hadad|הֲדַ֜ד\rb* \rb listened|וַיִּשְׁמַ֨ע\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Asa|אָסָ֗א\rb* \rb and sent|וַ֠יִּשְׁלַח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the commanders|שָׂרֵ֨י\rb* \rb of his armies|הַחֲיָלִ֤ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb the cities|עָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb conquering|וַיַּכּוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Ijon|עִיּ֣וֹן\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Dan|דָּ֔ן\rb*,\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb*\rb |אָבֵ֣ל\rb* \rb Abel-maim|מָ֑יִם\rb*,\f + \fr 16:4 \fqa Abel-maim \ft was also known as \fqa Abel-beth-maacah\ft ; see 1 Kings 15:20.\f*\rb |וְאֵ֥ת\rb* \rb and all|כָּֽל־\rb* \rb the store|מִסְכְּנ֖וֹת\rb* \rb cities|עָרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Naphtali|נַפְתָּלִֽי׃\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb |וַיְהִי֙\rb* \rb When Baasha|בַּעְשָׁ֔א\rb* \rb learned of this|כִּשְׁמֹ֣עַ\rb*, \rb he stopped|וַיֶּחְדַּ֕ל\rb* \rb fortifying|מִבְּנ֖וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Ramah|הָרָמָ֑ה\rb* \rb and abandoned|וַיַּשְׁבֵּ֖ת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his work|מְלַאכְתּֽוֹ׃ס\rb*. \v 6 \rb Then King|הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb Asa|וְאָסָ֣א\rb* \rb brought|לָקַח֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all the men|כָּל־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and they carried away|וַיִּשְׂא֞וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the stones|אַבְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Ramah|הָֽרָמָה֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the timbers|עֵצֶ֔יהָ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb Baasha|בַּעְשָׁ֑א\rb* \rb had used for building|בָּנָ֖ה\rb*. \rb And with these materials|בָּהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb he built up|וַיִּ֣בֶן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Geba|גֶּ֖בַע\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Mizpah|הַמִּצְפָּֽה׃ס\rb*.
\s1 Hanani’s Message to Asa
\p \v 7 \rb At that|הַהִ֗יא\rb* \rb time|וּבָעֵ֣ת\rb* \rb Hanani|חֲנָ֣נִי\rb* \rb the seer|הָרֹאֶ֔ה\rb* \rb came|בָּ֚א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb King|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Asa|אָסָ֖א\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb and told|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb him|אֵלָ֗יו\rb*, “\rb Because you have relied|בְּהִשָּׁ֨עֶנְךָ֜\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Aram|אֲרָם֙\rb* \rb and not|וְלֹ֤א\rb*\rb |נִשְׁעַ֙נְתָּ֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb*,\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֗ן\rb* \rb the army|חֵ֥יל\rb* \rb of the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Aram|אֲרָ֖ם\rb* \rb has escaped|נִמְלַ֛ט\rb* \rb from your hand|מִיָּדֶֽךָ׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb Were|הָי֨וּ\rb* \rb not|הֲלֹ֧א\rb* \rb the Cushites|הַכּוּשִׁ֣ים\rb*\f + \fr 16:8 \ft That is, people from the upper Nile region\f* \rb and Libyans|וְהַלּוּבִ֗ים\rb* \rb a vast|לָרֹ֛ב\rb* \rb army|לְחַ֧יִל׀\rb* \rb with many|לְהַרְבֵּ֣ה\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb chariots|לְרֶ֥כֶב\rb* \rb and horsemen|וּלְפָרָשִׁ֖ים\rb*? \rb Yet because you relied|וּבְהִשָּֽׁעֶנְךָ֥\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb He delivered them|נְתָנָ֥ם\rb* \rb into your hand|בְּיָדֶֽךָ׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the eyes|עֵינָ֞יו\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb roam to and fro|מְשֹׁטְט֤וֹת\rb* \rb over all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb*, \rb to show Himself strong|לְ֠הִתְחַזֵּק\rb* \rb on behalf of those|עִם־\rb* \rb whose hearts|לְבָבָ֥ם\rb* \rb are fully devoted|שָׁלֵ֛ם\rb* \rb to Him|אֵלָ֖יו\rb*. \rb You have acted foolishly|נִסְכַּ֣לְתָּ\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb this matter|זֹ֑את\rb*. \rb From now on|מֵעַ֔תָּה\rb*, \rb therefore|כִּ֣י\rb*, \rb you will be at|יֵ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |עִמְּךָ֖\rb* \rb war|מִלְחָמֽוֹת׃\rb*.”
\p \v 10 \rb Asa|אָסָ֜א\rb* \rb was angry|וַיִּכְעַ֨ס\rb* \rb with|אֶל־\rb* \rb the seer|הָרֹאֶ֗ה\rb* \rb and became|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb so enraged|בְזַ֥עַף\rb*\rb |עִמּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb this matter|זֹ֑את\rb* \rb that he put the man|וַֽיִּתְּנֵ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb in prison|בֵּ֣ית\rb*\rb |הַמַּהְפֶּ֔כֶת\rb*. \rb And at the same|הַהִֽיא׃\rb* \rb time|בָּעֵ֥ת\rb* \rb Asa|אָסָ֛א\rb* \rb oppressed|וַיְרַצֵּ֥ץ\rb* \rb some of|מִן־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb*.
\s1 The Death and Burial of Asa
\p \v 11 \rb Now|וְהִנֵּה֙\rb* \rb the acts|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Asa|אָסָ֔א\rb*, \rb from beginning|הָרִאשׁוֹנִ֖ים\rb* \rb to end|וְהָאַחֲרוֹנִ֑ים\rb*, \rb are indeed|הִנָּ֤ם\rb* \rb written|כְּתוּבִים֙\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the Book|סֵ֣פֶר\rb* \rb of the Kings|הַמְּלָכִ֔ים\rb* \rb of Judah|לִיהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb and Israel|וְיִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb In the thirty-ninth|שְׁלוֹשִׁ֨ים\rb*\rb |וָתֵ֤שַׁע\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַת֩\rb* \rb of his reign|לְמַלְכוּתוֹ֙\rb*, \rb Asa|אָסָ֡א\rb* \rb became diseased|וַיֶּחֱלֶ֣א\rb* \rb in his feet|בְּרַגְלָ֔יו\rb*, \rb and|עַד־\rb* \rb his disease|חָלְי֑וֹ\rb* \rb became increasingly severe|לְמַ֖עְלָה\rb*. \rb Yet even|וְגַם־\rb* \rb in his illness|בְּחָלְיוֹ֙\rb* \rb he did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb seek|דָרַ֣שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb but|כִּ֖י\rb* \rb only the physicians|בָּרֹפְאִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb So in the forty-first|אַרְבָּעִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וְאַחַ֖ת\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַ֛ת\rb* \rb of his reign|לְמָלְכֽוֹ׃\rb*, \rb Asa|אָסָ֖א\rb* \rb died|וַיָּ֕מָת\rb* \rb and rested|וַיִּשְׁכַּ֥ב\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb his fathers|אֲבֹתָ֑יו\rb*. \v 14 \rb And he was buried|וַיִּקְבְּרֻ֣הוּ\rb* \rb in the tomb|בְקִבְרֹתָ֗יו\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he had cut out|כָּֽרָה־\rb* \rb for himself|לוֹ֮\rb* \rb in the City|בְּעִ֣יר\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִיד֒\rb*. \rb They laid him|וַיַּשְׁכִּיבֻ֗הוּ\rb* \rb on a bier|בַּמִּשְׁכָּב֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb was full of|מִלֵּא֙\rb* \rb spices|בְּשָׂמִ֣ים\rb* \rb and various|וּזְנִ֔ים\rb* \rb blended|מַעֲשֶׂ֑ה\rb* \rb perfumes|מְרֻקָּחִ֖ים\rb*;\rb |בְּמִרְקַ֣חַת\rb* \rb then they made a great|גְּדוֹלָ֥ה\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb*\rb |לִמְאֹֽד׃פ\rb* \rb fire|וַיִּשְׂרְפוּ־\rb* \rb in his honor|שְׂרֵפָ֖ה\rb*.
\c 17
\s1 Jehoshaphat Reigns in Judah
\r (1 Kings 15:23–24)
\p \v 1 \rb Asa’s son|בְּנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Jehoshaphat|יְהוֹשָׁפָ֥ט\rb* \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֛ךְ\rb* \rb in his place|תַּחְתָּ֑יו\rb*, \rb and he strengthened himself|וַיִּתְחַזֵּ֖ק\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb He stationed|וַיִּ֨תֶּן־\rb* \rb troops|חַ֔יִל\rb* \rb in every|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb fortified|הַבְּצֻר֑וֹת\rb* \rb city|עָרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb and put|וַיִּתֵּ֤ן\rb* \rb garrisons|נְצִיבִים֙\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb and in the cities|וּבְעָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb his father|אָבִֽיו׃\rb* \rb Asa|אָסָ֥א\rb* \rb had captured|לָכַ֖ד\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb Now the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb was|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb Jehoshaphat|יְהוֹשָׁפָ֑ט\rb* \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb he walked|הָלַ֗ךְ\rb* \rb in the earlier|הָרִ֣אשֹׁנִ֔ים\rb* \rb ways|בְּדַרְכֵ֞י\rb*\f + \fr 17:3 \ft Or \fqa in his early years he walked in the ways\f* \rb of his father|אָבִיו֙\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֤יד\rb*. \rb He did not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb seek|דָרַ֖שׁ\rb* \rb the Baals|לַבְּעָלִֽים׃\rb*, \v 4 \rb but|כִּ֠י\rb* \rb he sought|דָּרָ֔שׁ\rb* \rb the God|לֵֽאלֹהֵ֤י\rb* \rb of his father|אָבִיו֙\rb* \rb and walked|הָלָ֑ךְ\rb* \rb by His commandments|וּבְמִצְוֺתָ֖יו\rb* \rb rather than|וְלֹ֖א\rb* \rb the practices|כְּמַעֲשֵׂ֥ה\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb So the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb established|וַיָּ֨כֶן\rb* \rb the kingdom|הַמַּמְלָכָה֙\rb* \rb in his hand|בְּיָד֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and all|כָל־\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֛ה\rb* \rb brought|וַיִּתְּנ֧וּ\rb* \rb him|לִיהוֹשָׁפָ֑ט\rb* \rb tribute|מִנְחָ֖ה\rb*, \rb so that|וַֽיְהִי־\rb* \rb he had|ל֥וֹ\rb* \rb an abundance|לָרֹֽב׃\rb* \rb of riches|עֹֽשֶׁר־\rb* \rb and honor|וְכָב֖וֹד\rb*. \v 6 \rb And his heart|לִבּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb took delight|וַיִּגְבַּ֥הּ\rb*\f + \fr 17:6 \ft Or \fqa was exalted \ft or \fqa was courageous\f* \rb in the ways|בְּדַרְכֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*; \rb furthermore|וְע֗וֹד\rb*, \rb he removed|הֵסִ֛יר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the high places|הַבָּמ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Asherah poles|הָאֲשֵׁרִ֖ים\rb* \rb from Judah|מִיהוּדָֽה׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb In the third|שָׁל֜וֹשׁ\rb* \rb year|וּבִשְׁנַ֨ת\rb* \rb of his reign|לְמָלְכ֗וֹ\rb*, \rb Jehoshaphat sent|שָׁלַ֤ח\rb* \rb his officials|לְשָׂרָיו֙\rb*\rb |לְבֶן־\rb* \rb Ben-hail|חַ֙יִל֙\rb*, \rb Obadiah|וּלְעֹבַדְיָ֣ה\rb*, \rb Zechariah|וְלִזְכַרְיָ֔ה\rb*, \rb Nethanel|וְלִנְתַנְאֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb and Micaiah|וּלְמִיכָיָ֑הוּ\rb* \rb to teach|לְלַמֵּ֖ד\rb* \rb in the cities|בְּעָרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb*, \v 8 \rb accompanied by|וְעִמָּהֶ֣ם\rb* \rb certain Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֗ם\rb* — \rb Shemaiah|שְֽׁמַֽעְיָ֡הוּ\rb*, \rb Nethaniah|וּנְתַנְיָ֡הוּ\rb*, \rb Zebadiah|וּזְבַדְיָ֡הוּ\rb*, \rb Asahel|וַעֲשָׂהאֵ֡ל\rb*, \rb Shemiramoth|וּשְׁמִרִימוֹת\rb*, \rb Jehonathan|וִֽיהוֹנָתָן֩\rb*, \rb Adonijah|וַאֲדֹ֨נִיָּ֧הוּ\rb*, \rb Tobijah|וְטֽוֹבִיָּ֛הוּ\rb*,\rb |וְט֥וֹב\rb* \rb and Tob-adonijah|אֲדוֹנִיָּ֖ה\rb* — \rb along with|וְעִמָּהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִֽים׃\rb* \rb Elishama|אֱלִישָׁמָ֥ע\rb* \rb and Jehoram|וִֽיהוֹרָ֖ם\rb*\rb |הַלְוִיִּ֑ם\rb*. \v 9 \rb They taught|וַֽיְלַמְּדוּ֙\rb* \rb throughout Judah|בִּֽיהוּדָ֔ה\rb*, \rb taking with them|וְעִ֨מָּהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb the Book|סֵ֖פֶר\rb* \rb of the Law|תּוֹרַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*. \rb They went|וַיָּסֹ֙בּוּ֙\rb* \rb throughout|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the towns|עָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb and taught|וַֽיְלַמְּד֖וּ\rb* \rb the people|בָּעָֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb And the dread|פַּ֣חַד\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb fell|וַיְהִ֣י׀\rb* \rb upon|עַ֚ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the kingdoms|מַמְלְכ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the lands|הָֽאֲרָצ֔וֹת\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb surrounded|סְבִיב֣וֹת\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb*, \rb so that they did not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb make war|נִלְחֲמ֖וּ\rb* \rb against|עִם־\rb* \rb Jehoshaphat|יְהוֹשָׁפָֽט׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb Some|וּמִן־\rb* \rb Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֗ים\rb* \rb also brought|מְבִיאִ֧ים\rb* \rb gifts|מִנְחָ֖ה\rb* \rb and silver|וְכֶ֣סֶף\rb* \rb as tribute|מַשָּׂ֑א\rb* \rb to Jehoshaphat|לִֽיהוֹשָׁפָ֛ט\rb*, \rb and|גַּ֣ם\rb* \rb the Arabs|הָֽעַרְבִיאִ֗ים\rb* \rb brought|מְבִיאִ֥ים\rb* \rb him|לוֹ֙\rb* \rb 7,700|שִׁבְעַ֤ת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִים֙\rb*\rb |וּשְׁבַ֣ע\rb*\rb |מֵא֔וֹת\rb* \rb rams|אֵילִ֔ים\rb* \rb and 7,700|שִׁבְעַ֥ת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִ֖ים\rb*\rb |וּשְׁבַ֥ע\rb*\rb |מֵאֽוֹת׃פ\rb* \rb goats|וּתְיָשִׁ֕ים\rb* \rb from their flocks|צֹ֕אן\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb |וַיְהִ֧י\rb* \rb Jehoshaphat|יְהוֹשָׁפָ֛ט\rb* \rb grew stronger|הֹלֵ֥ךְ\rb*\rb |וְגָדֵ֖ל\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb and stronger|לְמָ֑עְלָה\rb*, \rb and he built|וַיִּ֧בֶן\rb* \rb fortresses|בִּירָנִיּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb and store|מִסְכְּנֽוֹת׃\rb* \rb cities|וְעָרֵ֥י\rb* \rb in Judah|בִּֽיהוּדָ֛ה\rb* \v 13 \rb and kept vast|רַבָּ֛ה\rb* \rb supplies|וּמְלָאכָ֥ה\rb* \rb in the cities|בְּעָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb*. \rb He also had|הָ֥יָה\rb* \rb warriors|מִלְחָמָ֛ה\rb*\rb |וְאַנְשֵׁ֧י\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb* \rb who were mighty men|גִּבּ֥וֹרֵי\rb* \rb of valor|חַ֖יִל\rb*. \v 14 \rb These|וְאֵ֥לֶּה\rb* \rb are their numbers|פְקֻדָּתָ֖ם\rb* \rb according to the houses|לְבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of their fathers|אֲבוֹתֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \rb From Judah|לִֽיהוּדָה֙\rb*, \rb the commanders|שָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of thousands|אֲלָפִ֔ים\rb*:
\li2 \rb Adnah|עַדְנָ֣ה\rb* \rb the commander|הַשָּׂ֔ר\rb*, \rb and with him|וְעִמּוֹ֙\rb* \rb 300,000|שְׁלֹ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵא֖וֹת\rb*\rb |אָֽלֶף׃ס\rb* \rb mighty men|גִּבּ֣וֹרֵי\rb* \rb of valor|חַ֔יִל\rb*;
\li2 \v 15 \rb next to|וְעַל־\rb* \rb him|יָד֖וֹ\rb*, \rb Jehohanan|יְהוֹחָנָ֣ן\rb* \rb the commander|הַשָּׂ֑ר\rb*, \rb and with him|וְעִמּ֕וֹ\rb* \rb 280,000|מָאתַ֥יִם\rb*\rb |וּשְׁמוֹנִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אָֽלֶף׃ס\rb*;
\li2 \v 16 \rb and next to|וְעַל־\rb* \rb him|יָדוֹ֙\rb*, \rb Amasiah|עֲמַסְיָ֣ה\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Zichri|זִכְרִ֔י\rb*, \rb the volunteer|הַמִּתְנַדֵּ֖ב\rb* \rb for the LORD|לַיהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and with him|וְעִמּ֛וֹ\rb* \rb 200,000|מָאתַ֥יִם\rb*\rb |אֶ֖לֶף\rb* \rb mighty men|גִּבּ֥וֹר\rb* \rb of valor|חָֽיִל׃ס\rb*.
\b 
\li1 \v 17 \rb From|וּמִ֨ן־\rb* \rb Benjamin|בִּנְיָמִ֔ן\rb*:
\li2 \rb Eliada|אֶלְיָדָ֑ע\rb*, \rb a mighty man|גִּבּ֥וֹר\rb* \rb of valor|חַ֖יִל\rb*, \rb and with him|וְעִמּ֛וֹ\rb* \rb 200,000|מָאתַ֥יִם\rb*\rb |אָֽלֶף׃ס\rb* \rb armed|נֹֽשְׁקֵי־\rb* \rb with bows|קֶ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb and shields|וּמָגֵ֖ן\rb*;
\li2 \v 18 \rb and next to|וְעַל־\rb* \rb him|יָד֖וֹ\rb*, \rb Jehozabad|יְהוֹזָבָ֑ד\rb*, \rb and with him|וְעִמּ֛וֹ\rb* \rb 180,000|מֵאָֽה־\rb*\rb |וּשְׁמוֹנִ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֶ֖לֶף\rb* \rb armed|חֲלוּצֵ֥י\rb* \rb for battle|צָבָֽא׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb These were the men|אֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb who served|הַמְשָׁרְתִ֣ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb*, \rb besides|מִלְּבַ֞ד\rb* \rb those|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he|הַמֶּ֛לֶךְ\rb* \rb stationed|נָתַ֥ן\rb* \rb in the fortified|הַמִּבְצָ֖ר\rb* \rb cities|בְּעָרֵ֥י\rb* \rb throughout|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָֽה׃פ\rb*.
\c 18
\s1 Jehoshaphat Allies with Ahab
\r (1 Kings 22:1–12)
\p \v 1 \rb Now Jehoshaphat|לִֽיהוֹשָׁפָ֛ט\rb* \rb had|וַיְהִ֧י\rb* \rb an abundance|לָרֹ֑ב\rb* \rb of riches|עֹ֥שֶׁר\rb* \rb and honor|וְכָב֖וֹד\rb*, \rb and he allied himself with Ahab|לְאַחְאָֽב׃\rb* \rb by marriage|וַיִּתְחַתֵּ֖ן\rb*. \v 2 \rb And some years|שָׁנִ֤ים\rb* \rb later|לְקֵ֨ץ\rb* \rb he went down|וַיֵּרֶד֩\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb visit Ahab|אַחְאָב֙\rb* \rb in Samaria|לְשֹׁ֣מְר֔וֹן\rb*, \rb where Ahab|אַחְאָ֜ב\rb* \rb sacrificed|וַיִּֽזְבַּֽח־\rb* \rb many|לָרֹ֔ב\rb* \rb sheep|צֹ֤אן\rb* \rb and cattle|וּבָקָר֙\rb* \rb for him|ל֨וֹ\rb* \rb and the people|וְלָעָ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb with him|עִמּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb and urged him|וַיְסִיתֵ֕הוּ\rb* \rb to march up|לַעֲל֖וֹת\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Ramoth-gilead|רָמ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |גִּלְעָֽד׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb Ahab|אַחְאָ֣ב\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֜אמֶר\rb* \rb Jehoshaphat|יְהֽוֹשָׁפָט֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb*, “\rb Will you go|הֲתֵלֵ֥ךְ\rb* \rb with me|עִמִּ֖י\rb* \rb against Ramoth-gilead|רָמֹ֣ת\rb*\rb |גִּלְעָ֑ד\rb*?”
\p \rb And Jehoshaphat replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb I am|כָּמ֤וֹנִי\rb* \rb as you are|כָמ֙וֹךָ֙\rb*, \rb and my people are|עַמִּ֔י\rb* \rb your people|וּכְעַמְּךָ֣\rb*; \rb we will join you|וְעִמְּךָ֖\rb* \rb in the war|בַּמִּלְחָמָֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 4 \rb But Jehoshaphat|יְהוֹשָׁפָ֖ט\rb* \rb also said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, “\rb Please|נָ֥א\rb* \rb inquire|דְּרָשׁ־\rb* \rb first|כַיּ֖וֹם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb for the word|דְּבַ֥ר\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 5 \rb So the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb assembled|וַיִּקְבֹּ֨ץ\rb* \rb the prophets|הַנְּבִאִים֮\rb*, \rb four|אַרְבַּ֣ע\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֣וֹת\rb* \rb men|אִישׁ֒\rb*, \rb and asked them|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Should we go|הֲנֵלֵ֞ךְ\rb* \rb to war|לַמִּלְחָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb Ramoth-gilead|רָמֹ֥ת\rb*\rb |גִּלְעָ֛ד\rb*, \rb or|אִם־\rb* \rb should we refrain|אֶחְדָּ֑ל\rb*?”
\p “\rb Go up|עֲלֵ֔ה\rb*,” \rb they replied|וַיֹּאמְר֣וּ\rb*, “\rb and God|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb will deliver it|וְיִתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb into the hand|בְּיַ֥ד\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 6 \rb But Jehoshaphat|יְה֣וֹשָׁפָ֔ט\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb Is there not|הַאֵ֨ין\rb* \rb still|ע֑וֹד\rb* \rb a prophet|נָבִ֛יא\rb* \rb of the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb here|פֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb of whom we can inquire|מֵאֹתֽוֹ׃\rb*\rb |וְנִדְרְשָׁ֖ה\rb*? ”
\p \v 7 \rb The king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֣ל׀\rb* \rb answered|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |יְהוֹשָׁפָ֡ט\rb*, “\rb There is still|ע֣וֹד\rb* \rb one|אֶחָ֡ד\rb* \rb man|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb through whom we can inquire|לִדְרוֹשׁ֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb*,\rb |מֵֽאֹת֜וֹ\rb* \rb but I|וַאֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb hate him|שְׂנֵאתִ֗יהוּ\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he never|אֵ֠ינֶנּוּ\rb* \rb prophesies|מִתְנַבֵּ֨א\rb* \rb anything good|לְטוֹבָה֙\rb* \rb for me|עָלַ֤י\rb*, \rb but only|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb bad|לְרָעָ֔ה\rb*. \rb He|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb is Micaiah|מִיכָ֣יְהוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Imlah|יִמְלָ֑א\rb*.”
\p “\rb The king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb should not|אַל־\rb* \rb say|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb that|כֵּֽן׃\rb*!” \rb Jehoshaphat|יְה֣וֹשָׁפָ֔ט\rb* \rb replied|יֹאמַ֥ר\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb So the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb called|וַיִּקְרָא֙\rb* \rb one|אֶחָ֑ד\rb* \rb of his officials|סָרִ֖יס\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Bring|מַהֵ֖ר\rb* \rb Micaiah|מִיכָהוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Imlah at once|יִמְלָֽא׃\rb*.”
\p \v 9 \rb Dressed|מְלֻבָּשִׁ֤ים\rb* \rb in royal attire|בְּגָדִים֙\rb*, \rb the king|וּמֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֡ל\rb* \rb and Jehoshaphat|וִֽיהוֹשָׁפָ֣ט\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֡ה\rb*\rb |אִ֨ישׁ\rb* \rb were sitting|יוֹשְׁבִים֩\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb their thrones|כִּסְא֜וֹ\rb*\rb |וְיֹשְׁבִ֣ים\rb* \rb at the threshing floor|בְּגֹ֔רֶן\rb* \rb by the entrance|פֶּ֖תַח\rb* \rb of the gate|שַׁ֣עַר\rb* \rb of Samaria|שֹׁמְר֑וֹן\rb*, \rb with all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the prophets|הַ֨נְּבִיאִ֔ים\rb* \rb prophesying|מִֽתְנַבְּאִ֖ים\rb* \rb before them|לִפְנֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb Now Zedekiah|צִדְקִיָּ֥הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶֽן־\rb* \rb of Chenaanah|כְּנַעֲנָ֖ה\rb* \rb had made|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb for himself|ל֛וֹ\rb* \rb iron|בַרְזֶ֑ל\rb* \rb horns|קַרְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb and declared|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר\rb*: ‘\rb With these|בְּאֵ֛לֶּה\rb* \rb you shall gore|תְּנַגַּ֥ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Arameans|אֲרָ֖ם\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb they are finished off|כַּלּוֹתָֽם׃\rb*.’”
\p \v 11 \rb And all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the prophets|הַ֨נְּבִאִ֔ים\rb* \rb were prophesying|נִבְּאִ֥ים\rb* \rb the same|כֵּ֖ן\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, “\rb Go up|עֲלֵ֞ה\rb* \rb to Ramoth-gilead|רָמֹ֤ת\rb*\rb |גִּלְעָד֙\rb* \rb and triumph|וְהַצְלַ֔ח\rb*, \rb for the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb will deliver it|וְנָתַ֥ן\rb* \rb into the hand|בְּיַ֥ד\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb*.”
\s1 Micaiah Prophesies against Ahab
\r (1 Kings 22:13–28)
\p \v 12 \rb Then the messenger|וְהַמַּלְאָ֞ךְ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb had gone|הָלַ֣ךְ׀\rb* \rb to call|לִקְרֹ֣א\rb* \rb Micaiah|לְמִיכָ֗יְהוּ\rb* \rb instructed him|דִּבֶּ֤ר\rb*, “\rb Behold|הִנֵּ֞ה\rb*, \rb with one|פֶּֽה־\rb* \rb accord|אֶחָ֥ד\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֧י\rb* \rb of the prophets|הַנְּבִאִ֛ים\rb* \rb are favorable|ט֖וֹב\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb*. \rb So please|נָ֧א\rb* \rb let your words|דְבָרְךָ֛\rb* \rb be|וִֽיהִי־\rb* \rb like|כְּאַחַ֥ד\rb* \rb theirs|מֵהֶ֖ם\rb*, \rb and speak|וְדִבַּ֥רְתָּ\rb* \rb favorably|טּֽוֹב׃\rb*.”
\p \v 13 \rb But Micaiah|מִיכָ֑יְהוּ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*, “\rb As surely as the LORD|יְהוָ֕ה\rb*\rb |כִּ֛י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb lives|חַי־\rb*, \rb I will speak|אֲדַבֵּֽר׃\rb* \rb whatever|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb my God|אֱלֹהַ֖י\rb*\rb |אֹת֥וֹ\rb* \rb tells me|יֹאמַ֥ר\rb*.”
\p \v 14 \rb When Micaiah arrived|וַיָּבֹא֮\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |הַמֶּלֶךְ֒\rb*, \rb the king|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb him|אֵלָ֗יו\rb*, “\rb Micaiah|מִיכָה֙\rb*, \rb should we go|הֲנֵלֵ֞ךְ\rb* \rb to war|לַמִּלְחָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb Ramoth-gilead|רָמֹ֥ת\rb*\rb |גִּלְעָ֛ד\rb*, \rb or|אִם־\rb* \rb should we refrain|אֶחְדָּ֑ל\rb*?”
\p “\rb Go up|עֲל֣וּ\rb* \rb and triumph|וְהַצְלִ֔יחוּ\rb*,” \rb Micaiah replied|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb for they will be delivered|וְיִנָּתְנ֖וּ\rb* \rb into your hand|בְּיֶדְכֶֽם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 15 \rb But the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָיו֙\rb*, “\rb How many|עַד־\rb*\rb |כַּמֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb times|פְעָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb must I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb make you swear|מַשְׁבִּיעֶ֑ךָ\rb*\rb |אֲ֠שֶׁר\rb* \rb not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb to tell me|תְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֵלַ֛י\rb* \rb anything but|רַק־\rb* \rb the truth|אֱמֶ֖ת\rb* \rb in the name|בְּשֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*?”
\p \v 16 \rb So Micaiah declared|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb I saw|רָאִ֤יתִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb scattered|נְפוֹצִ֣ים\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the hills|הֶֽהָרִ֔ים\rb*
\q2 \rb like sheep|כַּצֹּ֕אן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb without|אֵין־\rb* \rb a shepherd|רֹעֶ֑ה\rb*.
\q1 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*, ‘\rb These people|לָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb have no|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb master|אֲדֹנִ֣ים\rb*;
\q2 \rb let each one|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb return|יָשׁ֥וּבוּ\rb* \rb home|לְבֵית֖וֹ\rb* \rb in peace|בְּשָׁלֽוֹם׃\rb*.’”
\p \v 17 \rb Then the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Jehoshaphat|יְהוֹשָׁפָ֑ט\rb*, “\rb Did I not|הֲלֹא֙\rb* \rb tell|אָמַ֣רְתִּי\rb* \rb you|אֵלֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb that he never|לֹא־\rb* \rb prophesies|יִתְנַבֵּ֥א\rb* \rb good|ט֖וֹב\rb* \rb for me|עָלַ֛י\rb*, \rb but only|כִּ֥י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb bad|לְרָֽע׃ס\rb*?”
\p \v 18 \rb Micaiah continued|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Therefore|לָכֵ֖ן\rb* \rb hear|שִׁמְע֣וּ\rb* \rb the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*: \rb I saw|רָאִ֤יתִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb sitting|יוֹשֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb His throne|כִּסְא֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the host|צְבָ֤א\rb* \rb of heaven|הַשָּׁמַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb standing|עֹֽמְדִ֔ים\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb His right|יְמִינ֖וֹ\rb* \rb and on His left|וּשְׂמֹאלֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, ‘\rb Who|מִ֤י\rb* \rb will entice|יְפַתֶּה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Ahab|אַחְאָ֣ב\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb to march up|וְיַ֕עַל\rb* \rb and fall|וְיִפֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb at Ramoth-gilead|בְּרָמ֣וֹת\rb*\rb |גִּלְעָ֑ד\rb*?’
\p \rb And one|זֶ֚ה\rb* \rb suggested|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb* \rb this|כָּ֔כָה\rb*, \rb and another|וְזֶ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֹמֵ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֹמֵ֣ר\rb* \rb that|כָּֽכָה׃\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb Then a spirit|הָר֗וּחַ\rb* \rb came forward|וַיֵּצֵ֣א\rb*, \rb stood|וַֽיַּעֲמֹד֙\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and said|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*, ‘\rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb will entice him|אֲפַתֶּ֑נּוּ\rb*.’
\p ‘\rb By what means|בַּמָּֽה׃\rb*?’ \rb asked|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֖יו\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb And he replied|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, ‘\rb I will go out|אֵצֵא֙\rb* \rb and be|וְהָיִ֙יתִי֙\rb* \rb a lying|שֶׁ֔קֶר\rb* \rb spirit|לְר֣וּחַ\rb* \rb in the mouths|בְּפִ֖י\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb his prophets|נְבִיאָ֑יו\rb*.’
\p ‘\rb You will surely entice him|תְּפַתֶּה֙\rb* \rb and|וְגַם־\rb* \rb prevail|תּוּכָ֔ל\rb*,’ \rb said the LORD|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*. ‘\rb Go|צֵ֖א\rb* \rb and do|וַעֲשֵׂה־\rb* \rb it|כֵֽן׃\rb*.’
\p \v 22 \rb So|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb you see|הִנֵּ֨ה\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb has put|נָתַ֤ן\rb* \rb a lying|שֶׁ֔קֶר\rb* \rb spirit|ר֣וּחַ\rb* \rb in the mouths|בְּפִ֖י\rb* \rb of these|אֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb prophets of yours|נְבִיאֶ֣יךָ\rb*, \rb and the LORD|וַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb has pronounced|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb disaster|רָעָֽה׃ס\rb* \rb against you|עָלֶ֖יךָ\rb*.”
\p \v 23 \rb Then Zedekiah|צִדְקִיָּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶֽן־\rb* \rb of Chenaanah|כְּנַעֲנָ֔ה\rb* \rb went up|וַיִּגַּשׁ֙\rb*, \rb struck|וַיַּ֥ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Micaiah|מִיכָ֖יְהוּ\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the face|הַלֶּ֑חִי\rb*, \rb and demanded|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Which|אֵ֣י\rb*\rb |זֶ֤ה\rb* \rb way|הַדֶּ֙רֶךְ֙\rb* \rb did the Spirit|רֽוּחַ־\rb* \rb of the LORD go|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb when He departed|עָבַ֧ר\rb* \rb from me|מֵאִתִּ֖י\rb* \rb to speak|לְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb with you|אֹתָֽךְ׃\rb*?”
\p \v 24 \rb Micaiah|מִיכָ֔יְהוּ\rb*\rb |הִנְּךָ֥\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb You will soon see|רֹאֶ֖ה\rb*, \rb on that|הַה֑וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb when|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you go|תָּב֛וֹא\rb* \rb and hide|לְהֵחָבֵֽא׃\rb* \rb in an inner|חֶ֥דֶר\rb* \rb room|בְּחֶ֖דֶר\rb*.”
\p \v 25 \rb And the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb declared|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb Take|קְחוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Micaiah|מִיכָ֔יְהוּ\rb* \rb and return him|וַהֲשִׁיבֻ֖הוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Amon|אָמ֣וֹן\rb* \rb the governor|שַׂר־\rb* \rb of the city|הָעִ֑יר\rb* \rb and to|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb Joash|יוֹאָ֖שׁ\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb*, \v 26 \rb and tell them|וַאֲמַרְתֶּ֗ם\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּ֚ה\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר\rb*: ‘\rb Put|שִׂ֥ימוּ\rb* \rb this man|זֶ֖ה\rb* \rb in prison|בֵּ֣ית\rb*\rb |הַכֶּ֑לֶא\rb* \rb and feed him|וְהַאֲכִלֻ֜הוּ\rb* \rb only bread|לֶ֤חֶם\rb*\rb |לַ֙חַץ֙\rb* \rb and water|וּמַ֣יִם\rb*\rb |לַ֔חַץ\rb* \rb until|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb I return|שׁוּבִ֥י\rb* \rb safely|בְשָׁלֽוֹם׃\rb*.’”
\p \v 27 \rb But Micaiah|מִיכָ֔יְהוּ\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb you ever return|שׁ֤וֹב\rb*\rb |תָּשׁוּב֙\rb* \rb safely|בְּשָׁל֔וֹם\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has not|לֹא־\rb* \rb spoken through me|דִבֶּ֥ר\rb*.” \rb Then he added|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Take heed|שִׁמְע֖וּ\rb*, \rb all|כֻּלָּֽם׃פ\rb* \rb you people|עַמִּ֥ים\rb*!”
\s1 Ahab’s Defeat and Death
\r (1 Kings 22:29–40)
\p \v 28 \rb So the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb and Jehoshaphat|וִֽיהוֹשָׁפָ֥ט\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb went up|וַיַּ֧עַל\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Ramoth-gilead|רָמֹ֥ת\rb*\rb |גִּלְעָֽד׃\rb*. \v 29 \rb And the king|מֶ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֜ל\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Jehoshaphat|יְהוֹשָׁפָ֗ט\rb*, “\rb I will disguise myself|הִתְחַפֵּשׂ֙\rb* \rb and go|וָב֣וֹא\rb* \rb into battle|בַמִּלְחָמָ֔ה\rb*, \rb but you|וְאַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb wear|לְבַ֣שׁ\rb* \rb your royal robes|בְּגָדֶ֑יךָ\rb*.” \rb So the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb disguised himself|וַיִּתְחַפֵּשׂ֙\rb* \rb and went|וַיָּבֹ֖אוּ\rb* \rb into battle|בַּמִּלְחָמָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 30 \rb Now the king|וּמֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Aram|אֲרָ֡ם\rb* \rb had ordered|צִוָּה֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his chariot|הָרֶ֤כֶב\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb commanders|שָׂרֵ֨י\rb*, “\rb Do not|לֹ֚א\rb* \rb fight|תִּלָּ֣חֲמ֔וּ\rb* \rb with anyone|אֶת־\rb*, \rb small|הַקָּטֹ֖ן\rb* \rb or|אֶת־\rb* \rb great|הַגָּד֑וֹל\rb*, \rb except|כִּ֛י\rb*\rb |אִֽם־\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*\rb |לְבַדּֽוֹ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 31 \rb |וַיְהִ֡י\rb* \rb When the chariot|הָרֶ֜כֶב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb commanders|שָׂרֵ֨י\rb* \rb saw|כִּרְאוֹת֩\rb* \rb Jehoshaphat|יְהוֹשָׁפָ֗ט\rb*, \rb they|וְהֵ֤מָּה\rb* \rb said|אָֽמְרוּ֙\rb*, “\rb This|ה֔וּא\rb* \rb is the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֣ל\rb*!” \rb So they turned|וַיָּסֹ֥בּוּ\rb* \rb to fight|לְהִלָּחֵ֑ם\rb* \rb against him|עָלָ֖יו\rb*, \rb but Jehoshaphat|יְהֽוֹשָׁפָט֙\rb* \rb cried out|וַיִּזְעַ֤ק\rb*, \rb and the LORD|וַֽיהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb helped him|עֲזָר֔וֹ\rb*. \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb drew them away|וַיְסִיתֵ֥ם\rb* \rb from him|מִמֶּֽנּוּ׃\rb*. \v 32 \rb And when the chariot|הָרֶ֔כֶב\rb* \rb commanders|שָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb saw|כִּרְאוֹת֙\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb he was|וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb not|לֹא־\rb*\rb |הָיָ֖ה\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb they turned back|וַיָּשֻׁ֖בוּ\rb* \rb from pursuing him|מֵאַחֲרָֽיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 33 \rb However, a certain man|וְאִ֗ישׁ\rb* \rb drew|מָשַׁ֤ךְ\rb* \rb his bow|בַּקֶּ֙שֶׁת֙\rb* \rb without taking special aim|לְתֻמּ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and he struck|וַיַּךְ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb the joints|הַדְּבָקִ֖ים\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֣ין\rb* \rb of his armor|הַשִּׁרְיָ֑ן\rb*. \rb So the king said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to his charioteer|לָֽרַכָּ֗ב\rb*, “\rb Turn around|הֲפֹ֧ךְ\rb*\rb |יָדֶיךָ\rb*\f + \fr 18:33 \ft Literally \fqa Turn your hand\f* \rb and take me out|וְהוֹצֵאתַ֥נִי\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb the battle|הַֽמַּחֲנֶ֖ה\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb I am badly wounded|הָחֳלֵֽיתִי׃\rb*!”
\p \v 34 \rb The battle|הַמִּלְחָמָה֙\rb* \rb raged|וַתַּ֤עַל\rb* \rb throughout that|הַה֔וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb*, \rb and the king|וּמֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb*\rb |הָיָ֨ה\rb* \rb propped himself up|מַעֲמִ֧יד\rb* \rb in his chariot|בַּמֶּרְכָּבָ֛ה\rb* \rb facing|נֹ֥כַח\rb* \rb the Arameans|אֲרָ֖ם\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb evening|הָעָ֑רֶב\rb*. \rb And at sunset|בּ֥וֹא\rb*\rb |הַשָּֽׁמֶשׁ׃\rb* \rb he died|וַיָּ֕מָת\rb*\rb |לְעֵ֖ת\rb*.
\c 19
\s1 Jehoshaphat Reproved by Jehu
\p \v 1 \rb When Jehoshaphat|יְהוֹשָׁפָ֨ט\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֧ה\rb* \rb had returned|וַ֠יָּשָׁב\rb* \rb safely|בְּשָׁל֖וֹם\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his home|בֵּית֛וֹ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|לִֽירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*, \v 2 \rb Jehu|יֵה֣וּא\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Hanani|חֲנָ֘נִי֮\rb* \rb the seer|הַחֹזֶה֒\rb* \rb went out|וַיֵּצֵ֣א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb confront him|פָּנָ֗יו\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Jehoshaphat|יְהוֹשָׁפָ֔ט\rb*, “\rb Should you help|לַעְזֹ֔ר\rb* \rb the wicked|הֲלָרָשָׁ֣ע\rb* \rb and love|תֶּאֱהָ֑ב\rb* \rb those who hate|וּלְשֹׂנְאֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*? \rb Because of this|וּבָזֹאת֙\rb*, \rb the wrath|קֶּ֔צֶף\rb* \rb of the LORD is|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*\rb |מִלִּפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb upon you|עָלֶ֣יךָ\rb*. \v 3 \rb However|אֲבָ֕ל\rb*, \rb some|דְּבָרִ֥ים\rb* \rb good|טוֹבִ֖ים\rb* \rb is found|נִמְצְא֣וּ\rb* \rb in you|עִמָּ֑ךְ\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you have removed|בִעַ֤רְתָּ\rb* \rb the Asherah poles|הָאֲשֵׁרוֹת֙\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb and have set|וַהֲכִינ֥וֹתָ\rb* \rb your heart|לְבָבְךָ֖\rb* \rb on seeking|לִדְרֹ֥שׁ\rb* \rb God|הָֽאֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb*.”
\s1 Jehoshaphat’s Reforms
\p \v 4 \rb Jehoshaphat|יְהוֹשָׁפָ֖ט\rb* \rb lived|וַיֵּ֥שֶׁב\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָ֑םס\rb*, \rb and once again|וַיָּ֜שָׁב\rb* \rb he went out|וַיֵּצֵ֣א\rb* \rb among the people|בָעָ֗ם\rb*\rb |מִבְּאֵ֥ר\rb* \rb from Beersheba|שֶׁ֙בַע֙\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the hill country|הַ֣ר\rb* \rb of Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb and turned them back|וַיְשִׁיבֵ֕ם\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of their fathers|אֲבוֹתֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb He appointed|וַיַּעֲמֵ֨ד\rb* \rb judges|שֹֽׁפְטִ֜ים\rb* \rb in the land|בָּאָ֗רֶץ\rb*, \rb in each of|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the fortified|הַבְּצֻר֖וֹת\rb* \rb cities|עָרֵ֧י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֛ה\rb*. \v 6 \rb Then he said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the judges|הַשֹּֽׁפְטִ֗ים\rb*, “\rb Consider carefully|רְאוּ֙\rb* \rb what|מָֽה־\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb do|עֹשִׂ֔ים\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb you are not|לֹ֧א\rb* \rb judging|תִּשְׁפְּט֖וּ\rb* \rb for man|לְאָדָ֛ם\rb*, \rb but|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb for the LORD|לַיהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb who is with you|וְעִמָּכֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |בִּדְבַ֥ר\rb* \rb when you render judgment|מִשְׁפָּֽט׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb And now|וְעַתָּ֕ה\rb*, \rb may the fear|פַֽחַד־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb be|יְהִ֥י\rb* \rb upon you|עֲלֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb Be careful|שִׁמְר֣וּ\rb* \rb what you do|וַעֲשׂ֔וּ\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֗ינוּ\rb* \rb there is no|אֵ֞ין\rb* \rb injustice|עַוְלָ֛ה\rb* \rb or partiality|וּמַשֹּׂ֥א\rb*\rb |פָנִ֖ים\rb* \rb or bribery|וּמִקַּח־\rb*\rb |שֹֽׁחַד׃\rb*.”
\p \v 8 \rb Moreover|וְגַ֣ם\rb*, \rb Jehoshaphat|יְהוֹשָׁפָ֜ט\rb* \rb appointed|הֶעֱמִ֨יד\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּ֠ירוּשָׁלִַם\rb* \rb some of|מִן־\rb* \rb the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֣ם\rb*, \rb priests|וְהַכֹּהֲנִ֗ים\rb*, \rb and heads|וּמֵרָאשֵׁ֤י\rb* \rb of the Israelite|לְיִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb families|הָאָבוֹת֙\rb* \rb to judge|לְמִשְׁפַּ֥ט\rb* \rb on behalf of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb and to settle disputes|וְלָרִ֑יב\rb*. \rb And they lived|וַיָּשֻׁ֖בוּ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb He commanded them|וַיְצַ֥ו\rb*,\rb |עֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*,\rb |כֹּ֤ה\rb* “\rb You must serve|תַעֲשׂוּן֙\rb* \rb faithfully|בֶּאֱמוּנָ֖ה\rb* \rb and wholeheartedly|שָׁלֵֽם׃\rb*\rb |וּבְלֵבָ֥ב\rb* \rb in the fear|בְּיִרְאַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*. \v 10 \rb For every|וְכָל־\rb* \rb dispute|רִיב֩\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb comes|יָב֨וֹא\rb* \rb before you|עֲלֵיכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb from your brothers|מֵאֲחֵיכֶ֣ם׀\rb* \rb who dwell|הַיֹּשְׁבִ֣ים\rb* \rb in their cities|בְּעָרֵיהֶ֗ם\rb*— \rb whether|בֵּֽין־\rb* \rb it regards bloodshed|דָּ֣ם׀\rb* \rb or some other violation|לְדָם֮\rb* \rb of|בֵּין־\rb* \rb law|תּוֹרָ֣ה\rb*, \rb commandments|לְמִצְוָה֮\rb*, \rb statutes|לְחֻקִּ֣ים\rb*, \rb or ordinances|וּלְמִשְׁפָּטִים֒\rb*— \rb you are to warn them|וְהִזְהַרְתֶּ֣ם\rb*,\rb |אֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb so that they will not|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb incur guilt|יֶאְשְׁמוּ֙\rb* \rb before the LORD|לַיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and wrath|קֶ֥צֶף\rb* \rb will not come|וְהָֽיָה־\rb* \rb upon you|עֲלֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and|וְעַל־\rb* \rb your brothers|אֲחֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb Do|תַעֲשׂ֖וּן\rb* \rb this|כֹּ֥ה\rb*, \rb and you will not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb incur guilt|תֶאְשָֽׁמוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb Note that|וְהִנֵּ֡ה\rb* \rb Amariah|אֲמַרְיָ֣הוּ\rb*, \rb the chief|הָרֹ֨אשׁ\rb* \rb priest|כֹהֵן֩\rb*, \rb will be over you|עֲלֵיכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb in all|לְכֹ֣ל\rb* \rb that pertains|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb to the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*, \rb and Zebadiah|וּזְבַדְיָ֨הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Ishmael|יִשְׁמָעֵ֜אל\rb*, \rb the ruler|הַנָּגִ֤יד\rb* \rb of the house|לְבֵית־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb*, \rb in all|לְכֹ֣ל\rb* \rb that pertains|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb to the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*. \rb And the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֖ם\rb* \rb will serve as officers|וְשֹׁטְרִ֥ים\rb* \rb before you|לִפְנֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb Act|וַעֲשׂ֔וּ\rb* \rb resolutely|חִזְק֣וּ\rb*; \rb may the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb be|וִיהִ֥י\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb the upright|הַטּֽוֹב׃פ\rb*!”
\c 20
\s1 War against Jehoshaphat
\p \v 1 \rb |וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb After this|אַֽחֲרֵיכֵ֡ן\rb*, \rb the Moabites|בְנֵי־\rb*\rb |מוֹאָב֩\rb* \rb and Ammonites|וּבְנֵ֨י\rb*\rb |עַמּ֜וֹן\rb*, \rb together with|וְעִמָּהֶ֧ם׀\rb* \rb some of the Meunites|מֵֽהָעַמּוֹנִ֛ים\rb*,\f + \fr 20:1 \ft Some LXX manuscripts (see also 2 Chronicles 26:7); Hebrew \fqa together with some other Ammonites \ft or \fqa together with some besides the Ammonites\f* \rb came|בָּ֣אוּ\rb* \rb to make war|לַמִּלְחָמָֽה׃\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb Jehoshaphat|יְהוֹשָׁפָ֖ט\rb*. \v 2 \rb Then some men came|וַיָּבֹ֗אוּ\rb* \rb and told|וַיַּגִּ֤ידוּ\rb* \rb Jehoshaphat|לִֽיהוֹשָׁפָט֙\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* “\rb A vast|רָ֛ב\rb* \rb army|הָמ֥וֹן\rb* \rb is coming|בָּ֣א\rb* \rb against you|עָלֶ֜יךָ\rb* \rb from Edom|מֵאֲרָ֑ם\rb*,\f + \fr 20:2 \ft One Hebrew manuscript; most Hebrew manuscripts, LXX, and Vulgate \fqa Aram\f* \rb from beyond|מֵעֵ֥בֶר\rb* \rb the Sea|לַיָּ֖ם\rb*;\f + \fr 20:2 \ft That is, the Dead Sea\f* \rb they are already|וְהִנָּם֙\rb*\rb |בְּחַֽצְצ֣וֹן\rb* \rb in Hazazon-tamar|תָּמָ֔ר\rb*” \rb (that is|הִ֖יא\rb*, \rb En-gedi|עֵ֥ין\rb*\rb |גֶּֽדִי׃\rb*).
\p \v 3 \rb Jehoshaphat|יְהוֹשָׁפָ֛ט\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb was alarmed|וַיִּרָ֕א\rb* \rb and set|וַיִּתֵּ֧ן\rb* \rb his face|פָּנָ֖יו\rb* \rb to seek|לִדְר֣וֹשׁ\rb* \rb the LORD|לַיהוָ֑ה\rb*. \rb And he proclaimed|וַיִּקְרָא־\rb* \rb a fast|צ֖וֹם\rb* \rb throughout|עַל־\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb So the people of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb gathered|וַיִּקָּבְצ֣וּ\rb* \rb to seek|לְבַקֵּ֖שׁ\rb* \rb the LORD|מֵֽיְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and indeed|גַּ֚ם\rb*, \rb they came|בָּ֖אוּ\rb* \rb from all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb the cities|עָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb to seek|לְבַקֵּ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Him|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\s1 Jehoshaphat’s Prayer
\p \v 5 \rb Then Jehoshaphat|יְהוֹשָׁפָ֗ט\rb* \rb stood|וַיַּעֲמֹ֣ד\rb* \rb in the assembly|בִּקְהַ֧ל\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֛ה\rb* \rb and Jerusalem|וִירוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \rb in the house|בְּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb in front of|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the new|הַחֲדָשָֽׁה׃\rb* \rb courtyard|הֶחָצֵ֥ר\rb* \v 6 \rb and said|וַיֹּאמַ֗ר\rb*, “\rb O LORD|יְהוָ֞ה\rb*, \rb God|אֱלֹהֵ֤י\rb* \rb of our fathers|אֲבֹתֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb*, \rb are You|אַתָּֽה־\rb*\rb |ה֤וּא\rb* \rb not|הֲלֹ֨א\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb who is in heaven|בַּשָּׁמַ֔יִם\rb*, \rb and do You|וְאַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb not rule|מוֹשֵׁ֔ל\rb* \rb over all|בְּכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the kingdoms|מַמְלְכ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֑ם\rb*? \rb Power|כֹּ֣חַ\rb* \rb and might|וּגְבוּרָ֔ה\rb* \rb are in Your hand|וּבְיָדְךָ֙\rb*, \rb and no|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb one can stand|לְהִתְיַצֵּֽב׃\rb* \rb against You|עִמְּךָ֖\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb Our God|אֱלֹהֵ֗ינוּ\rb*, \rb did You|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb not|הֲלֹ֣א׀\rb* \rb drive out|הוֹרַ֙שְׁתָּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the inhabitants|יֹשְׁבֵי֙\rb* \rb of this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb before|מִלִּפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb Your people|עַמְּךָ֣\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb and give it|וַֽתִּתְּנָ֗הּ\rb* \rb forever|לְעוֹלָֽם׃\rb* \rb to the descendants|לְזֶ֛רַע\rb* \rb of Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֥ם\rb* \rb Your friend|אֹֽהַבְךָ֖\rb*? \v 8 \rb They have lived|וַיֵּשְׁב֖וּ־\rb* \rb in the land|בָ֑הּ\rb* \rb and have built|וַיִּבְנ֨וּ\rb* \rb in it|בָּ֛הּ\rb* \rb a sanctuary|מִקְדָּ֖שׁ\rb* \rb for Your Name|לְשִׁמְךָ֥\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 9 ‘\rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb disaster|רָעָ֗ה\rb* \rb comes|תָּב֨וֹא\rb* \rb upon us|עָלֵ֜ינוּ\rb*— \rb whether sword|חֶרֶב֮\rb* \rb or judgment|שְׁפוֹט֮\rb*,\f + \fr 20:9 \ft Or \fqa the sword of judgment\f* \rb plague|וְדֶ֣בֶר\rb* \rb or famine|וְרָעָב֒\rb*— \rb we will stand|נַֽעַמְדָ֞ה\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֨י\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb temple|הַבַּ֤יִת\rb* \rb and before You|וּלְפָנֶ֔יךָ\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb Your Name|שִׁמְךָ֖\rb* \rb is in this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb temple|בַּבַּ֣יִת\rb*. \rb We will cry out|וְנִזְעַ֥ק\rb* \rb to You|אֵלֶ֛יךָ\rb* \rb in our distress|מִצָּרָתֵ֖נוּ\rb*, \rb and You will hear us|וְתִשְׁמַ֥ע\rb* \rb and save us|וְתוֹשִֽׁיעַ׃\rb*.’
\p \v 10 \rb And now|וְעַתָּ֡ה\rb*, \rb here are|הִנֵּה֩\rb* \rb the men|בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Ammon|עַמּ֨וֹן\rb*, \rb Moab|וּמוֹאָ֜ב\rb*, \rb and Mount|וְהַר־\rb* \rb Seir|שֵׂעִ֗יר\rb*, \rb whom|אֲ֠שֶׁר\rb* \rb You did not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb let|נָתַ֤תָּה\rb* \rb Israel|לְיִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb invade|לָב֣וֹא\rb* \rb when they came|בְּבֹאָ֖ם\rb* \rb out of the land|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb*. \rb So|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb Israel turned away|סָ֥רוּ\rb* \rb from them|מֵעֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and did not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb destroy them|הִשְׁמִידֽוּם׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb See|וְהִ֨נֵּה־\rb* \rb how they|הֵ֔ם\rb* \rb are repaying|גֹּמְלִ֖ים\rb* \rb us|עָלֵ֑ינוּ\rb* \rb by coming|לָבוֹא֙\rb* \rb to drive us out|לְגָ֣רְשֵׁ֔נוּ\rb* \rb of the possession|מִיְּרֻשָּׁתְךָ֖\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb You gave us as an inheritance|הֽוֹרַשְׁתָּֽנוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb Our God|אֱלֹהֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb*, \rb will You not|הֲלֹ֣א\rb* \rb judge|תִשְׁפָּט־\rb* \rb them|בָּ֔ם\rb*? \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ין\rb*\rb |בָּ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb we are powerless|כֹּ֔חַ\rb* \rb before|לִ֠פְנֵי\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb vast|הָרָ֛ב\rb* \rb army|הֶהָמ֥וֹן\rb* \rb that comes|הַבָּ֣א\rb* \rb against us|עָלֵ֑ינוּ\rb*. \rb We|וַאֲנַ֗חְנוּ\rb* \rb do not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb know|נֵדַע֙\rb* \rb what|מַֽה־\rb* \rb to do|נַּעֲשֶׂ֔ה\rb*, \rb but|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb our eyes are|עֵינֵֽינוּ׃\rb* \rb upon You|עָלֶ֖יךָ\rb*.”
\p \v 13 \rb Meanwhile all the men|וְכָ֨ל־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb*, \rb with|גַּם־\rb* \rb their wives|נְשֵׁיהֶ֥ם\rb* \rb and children|וּבְנֵיהֶֽם׃פ\rb* \rb and little ones|טַפָּ֖ם\rb*, \rb were standing|עֹמְדִ֖ים\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*.
\s1 The Prophecy of Jahaziel
\p \v 14 \rb Then the Spirit|ר֣וּחַ\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb came|הָיְתָ֤ה\rb* \rb upon|עָלָיו֙\rb* \rb Jahaziel|וְיַחֲזִיאֵ֡ל\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Zechariah|זְכַרְיָ֡הוּ\rb*, \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Benaiah|בְּ֠נָיָה\rb*, \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jeiel|יְעִיאֵ֧ל\rb*, \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Mattaniah|מַתַּנְיָ֛ה\rb*, \rb a Levite|הַלֵּוִ֖י\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb Asaph’s|אָסָ֑ף\rb* \rb descendants|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*, \rb as he stood in the midst|בְּת֖וֹךְ\rb* \rb of the assembly|הַקָּהָֽל׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb And he said|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Listen|הַקְשִׁ֤יבוּ\rb*, \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb you people|וְיֹשְׁבֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb* \rb and Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb*! \rb Listen, King|וְהַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb Jehoshaphat|יְהוֹשָׁפָ֑ט\rb*! \rb This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb*\rb |אַ֠תֶּם\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֨ר\rb*: ‘\rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִּֽירְא֤וּ\rb*\rb |וְאַל־\rb* \rb or discouraged|תֵּחַ֙תּוּ֙\rb* \rb because of|מִפְּנֵ֨י\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb vast|הָרָב֙\rb* \rb army|הֶהָמ֤וֹן\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the battle|הַמִּלְחָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb does not belong|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb to you|לָכֶ֛ם\rb*, \rb but|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb to God|לֵאלֹהִֽים׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb Tomorrow|מָחָר֙\rb* \rb you are to march down|רְד֣וּ\rb* \rb against them|עֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*. \rb You will see them|הִנָּ֥ם\rb* \rb coming up|עֹלִ֖ים\rb* \rb the Ascent|בְּמַעֲלֵ֣ה\rb* \rb of Ziz|הַצִּ֑יץ\rb*, \rb and you will find|וּמְצָאתֶ֤ם\rb* \rb them|אֹתָם֙\rb* \rb at the end|בְּס֣וֹף\rb* \rb of the valley|הַנַּ֔חַל\rb* \rb facing|פְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the Wilderness|מִדְבַּ֥ר\rb* \rb of Jeruel|יְרוּאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb You|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb need not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb fight|לְהִלָּחֵ֣ם\rb* \rb this battle|בָּזֹ֑את\rb*. \rb Take up your positions|הִתְיַצְּב֣וּ\rb*, \rb stand firm|עִמְד֡וּ\rb*, \rb and see|וּרְא֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the salvation|יְשׁוּעַת֩\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb on your behalf|עִמָּכֶ֜ם\rb*, \rb O Judah|יְהוּדָ֣ה\rb* \rb and Jerusalem|וִֽירוּשָׁלִַ֗ם\rb*. \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִּֽירְאוּ֙\rb*\rb |וְאַל־\rb* \rb or discouraged|תֵּחַ֔תּוּ\rb*. \rb Go out|צְא֣וּ\rb* \rb and face them|לִפְנֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb tomorrow|מָחָר֙\rb*, \rb for the LORD|וַיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb is with you|עִמָּכֶֽם׃\rb*.’”
\p \v 18 \rb Then Jehoshaphat|יְהוֹשָׁפָ֛ט\rb* \rb bowed|וַיִּקֹּ֧ד\rb* \rb facedown|אַפַּ֖יִם\rb*\rb |אָ֑רְצָה\rb*, \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|וְיֹשְׁבֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֞ה\rb* \rb and Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֗ם\rb* \rb fell down|נָֽפְלוּ֙\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb to worship|לְהִֽשְׁתַּחֲוֺ֖ת\rb* \rb Him|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb And the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֛ם\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the Kohathites|הַקְּהָתִ֖ים\rb*\rb |וּמִן־\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb and Korahites|הַקָּרְחִ֑ים\rb* \rb stood up|וַיָּקֻ֧מוּ\rb* \rb to praise|לְהַלֵּ֗ל\rb* \rb the LORD|לַיהוָה֙\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb shouting in a very loud|גָּד֖וֹל\rb*\rb |לְמָֽעְלָה׃\rb* \rb voice|בְּק֥וֹל\rb*.
\s1 The Enemies Destroy Themselves
\p \v 20 \rb Early in the morning|בַבֹּ֔קֶר\rb* \rb they got up|וַיַּשְׁכִּ֣ימוּ\rb* \rb and left|וַיֵּצְא֖וּ\rb* \rb for the Wilderness|לְמִדְבַּ֣ר\rb* \rb of Tekoa|תְּק֑וֹעַ\rb*. \rb As they set out|וּבְצֵאתָ֞ם\rb*, \rb Jehoshaphat|יְהוֹשָׁפָ֗ט\rb* \rb stood up|עָמַ֣ד\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb Hear me|שְׁמָע֗וּנִי\rb*, \rb O people|וְיֹשְׁבֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb* \rb and Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb*. \rb Believe|הַאֲמִ֜ינוּ\rb* \rb in the LORD|בַּיהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶם֙\rb*, \rb and you will be upheld|וְתֵ֣אָמֵ֔נוּ\rb*; \rb believe|הַאֲמִ֥ינוּ\rb* \rb in His prophets|בִנְבִיאָ֖יו\rb*, \rb and you will succeed|וְהַצְלִֽיחוּ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 21 \rb Then Jehoshaphat consulted|וַיִּוָּעַץ֙\rb* \rb with|אֶל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb and appointed those|וַיַּעֲמֵ֤ד\rb* \rb who would sing|מְשֹֽׁרֲרִים֙\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and praise|וּֽמְהַֽלְלִ֖ים\rb* \rb the splendor|לְהַדְרַת־\rb* \rb of His holiness|קֹ֑דֶשׁ\rb*. \rb As they went out|בְּצֵאת֙\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the army|הֶֽחָל֔וּץ\rb*, \rb they were singing|וְאֹֽמְרִים֙\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb Give thanks|הוֹד֣וּ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֔ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb His loving devotion|חַסְדּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb endures forever|לְעוֹלָ֖ם\rb*.”
\p \v 22 \rb The moment|וּבְעֵת֩\rb* \rb they began|הֵחֵ֨לּוּ\rb* \rb their shouts|בְרִנָּ֜ה\rb* \rb and praises|וּתְהִלָּ֗ה\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה׀\rb* \rb set|נָתַ֣ן\rb* \rb ambushes|מְ֠אָֽרְבִים\rb* \rb against the men|עַל־\rb* \rb of Ammon|בְּנֵ֨י\rb*\rb |עַמּ֜וֹן\rb*, \rb Moab|מוֹאָ֧ב\rb*, \rb and Mount|וְהַר־\rb* \rb Seir|שֵׂעִ֛יר\rb* \rb who had come|הַבָּאִ֥ים\rb* \rb against Judah|לִֽיהוּדָ֖ה\rb*, \rb and they were defeated|וַיִּנָּגֵֽפוּ׃\rb*. \v 23 \rb The Ammonites|בְּנֵ֨י\rb*\rb |עַמּ֧וֹן\rb* \rb and Moabites|וּמוֹאָ֛ב\rb* \rb rose up|וַ֠יַּֽעַמְדוּ\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb the inhabitants|יֹשְׁבֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Mount|הַר־\rb* \rb Seir|שֵׂעִ֖יר\rb*, \rb devoting them|לְהַחֲרִ֣ים\rb* \rb to destruction|וּלְהַשְׁמִ֑יד\rb*.\f + \fr 20:23 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa cherem \ft refer to the giving over of things or persons to the LORD, either by destroying them or by giving them as an offering.\f* \rb And when they had finished off|וּכְכַלּוֹתָם֙\rb* \rb the inhabitants|בְּיוֹשְׁבֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Seir|שֵׂעִ֔יר\rb*, \rb they helped|עָזְר֥וּ\rb* \rb to destroy|לְמַשְׁחִֽית׃\rb* \rb one|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb another|בְּרֵעֵ֖הוּ\rb*.
\p \v 24 \rb When the men of Judah|וִֽיהוּדָ֛ה\rb* \rb came|בָּ֥א\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb a place overlooking|הַמִּצְפֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb the wilderness|לַמִּדְבָּ֑ר\rb*, \rb they looked|וַיִּפְנוּ֙\rb* \rb for|אֶל־\rb* \rb the vast army|הֶ֣הָמ֔וֹן\rb*, \rb but there|וְהִנָּ֧ם\rb* \rb were only corpses|פְּגָרִ֛ים\rb* \rb lying|נֹפְלִ֥ים\rb* \rb on the ground|אַ֖רְצָה\rb*; \rb no one|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb had escaped|פְּלֵיטָֽה׃\rb*. \v 25 \rb Then Jehoshaphat|יְהוֹשָׁפָ֣ט\rb* \rb and his people|וְעַמּוֹ֮\rb* \rb went|וַיָּבֹ֨א\rb* \rb to carry off|לָבֹ֣ז\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the plunder|שְׁלָלָם֒\rb*, \rb and they found|וַיִּמְצְאוּ֩\rb* \rb on the bodies|וּפְגָרִים֙\rb*\rb |בָהֶ֨ם\rb* \rb an abundance|לָרֹ֜ב\rb* \rb of goods|וּרְכ֤וּשׁ\rb* \rb and valuables|חֲמֻד֔וֹת\rb*\rb |וּכְלֵ֣י\rb*\f + \fr 20:25 \ft Some Hebrew manuscripts and Vulgate \fqa they found among them an abundance of goods and clothing and valuables\f* —\rb |וַיְנַצְּל֥וּ\rb* \rb more than|לְאֵ֣ין\rb* \rb they could carry away|מַשָּׂ֑א\rb*. \rb They were|וַיִּֽהְי֞וּ\rb* \rb gathering|בֹּזְזִ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the plunder|הַשָּׁלָ֖ל\rb* \rb for three|שְׁלוֹשָׁ֛ה\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֧ים\rb* \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb there was so much|רַב־\rb*\rb |הֽוּא׃\rb*.
\s1 The Joyful Return
\p \v 26 \rb On the fourth|הָרְבִעִ֗י\rb* \rb day|וּבַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb they assembled|נִקְהֲלוּ֙\rb* \rb in the Valley|לְעֵ֣מֶק\rb* \rb of Beracah|בְּרָכָ֔ה\rb*,\f + \fr 20:26 \fqa Beracah \ft means \fqa blessing\ft .\f*\rb |כִּי־\rb* \rb where|שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb they blessed|בֵּרֲכ֣וּ\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*. \rb Therefore|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֡ן\rb* \rb that|הַה֛וּא\rb* \rb place|הַמָּק֥וֹם\rb* \rb is called|קָֽרְא֞וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |שֵׁ֨ם\rb* \rb the Valley|עֵ֥מֶק\rb* \rb of Beracah|בְּרָכָ֖ה\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb this day|הַיּֽוֹם׃\rb*.
\p \v 27 \rb Then all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the men|אִ֨ישׁ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֤ה\rb* \rb and Jerusalem|וִֽירוּשָׁלִַ֙ם֙\rb*,\rb |וַ֠יָּשֻׁבוּ\rb* \rb with Jehoshaphat|וִֽיהוֹשָׁפָ֣ט\rb* \rb at their head|בְּרֹאשָׁ֔ם\rb*, \rb returned|לָשׁ֥וּב\rb* \rb joyfully|בְּשִׂמְחָ֑ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb had made them rejoice|שִׂמְּחָ֥ם\rb* \rb over their enemies|מֵֽאוֹיְבֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 28 \rb So they entered|וַיָּבֹ֙אוּ֙\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb and went into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֖ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb with harps|בִּנְבָלִ֥ים\rb*, \rb lyres|וּבְכִנֹּר֖וֹת\rb*, \rb and trumpets|וּבַחֲצֹצְר֑וֹת\rb*.
\p \v 29 \rb And the fear|פַּ֣חַד\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִי֙\rb* \rb upon|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the kingdoms|מַמְלְכ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the lands|הָאֲרָצ֑וֹת\rb* \rb when they heard|בְּשָׁמְעָ֕ם\rb* \rb that|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb had fought|נִלְחַ֣ם\rb* \rb against|עִ֖ם\rb* \rb the enemies|אוֹיְבֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 30 \rb Then Jehoshaphat’s|יְהוֹשָׁפָ֑ט\rb* \rb kingdom|מַלְכ֣וּת\rb* \rb was at peace|וַתִּשְׁקֹ֖ט\rb*, \rb for his God|אֱלֹהָ֖יו\rb* \rb had given him rest|וַיָּ֧נַֽח\rb* \rb on every side|מִסָּבִֽיב׃פ\rb*.
\s1 Summary of Jehoshaphat’s Reign
\r (1 Kings 22:41–50)
\p \v 31 \rb So Jehoshaphat|יְהוֹשָׁפָ֖ט\rb* \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֥ךְ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb*. \rb He was thirty-five|שְׁלֹשִׁים֩\rb*\rb |וְחָמֵ֨שׁ\rb* \rb years old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֜ה\rb* \rb when he became king|בְּמָלְכ֗וֹ\rb*, \rb and he reigned|מָלַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּֽירוּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb twenty-five|וְעֶשְׂרִ֨ים\rb*\rb |וְחָמֵ֤שׁ\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָה֙\rb*. \rb His mother’s|אִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb name|וְשֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb was Azubah|עֲזוּבָ֖ה\rb* \rb daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Shilhi|שִׁלְחִֽי׃\rb*.
\p \v 32 \rb And Jehoshaphat walked|וַיֵּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb in the way|בְּדֶ֛רֶךְ\rb* \rb of his father|אָבִ֥יו\rb* \rb Asa|אָסָ֖א\rb* \rb and did not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb turn away|סָ֣ר\rb* \rb from it|מִמֶּ֑נָּה\rb*; \rb he did|לַעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb* \rb what was right|הַיָּשָׁ֖ר\rb* \rb in the eyes|בְּעֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 33 \rb The high places|הַבָּמ֖וֹת\rb*, \rb however|אַ֥ךְ\rb*, \rb were not|לֹא־\rb* \rb removed|סָ֑רוּ\rb*; \rb the people|הָעָם֙\rb* \rb had not|לֹא־\rb* \rb yet|וְע֤וֹד\rb* \rb set|הֵכִ֣ינוּ\rb* \rb their hearts|לְבָבָ֔ם\rb* \rb on the God|לֵאלֹהֵ֖י\rb* \rb of their fathers|אֲבֹתֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 34 \rb As for the rest|וְיֶ֙תֶר֙\rb* \rb of the acts|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Jehoshaphat|יְהוֹשָׁפָ֔ט\rb*, \rb from beginning|הָרִאשֹׁנִ֖ים\rb* \rb to end|וְהָאַחֲרֹנִ֑ים\rb*, \rb they are indeed|הִנָּ֣ם\rb* \rb written|כְּתוּבִ֗ים\rb* \rb in the Chronicles|בְּדִבְרֵי֙\rb* \rb of Jehu|יֵה֣וּא\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Hanani|חֲנָ֔נִי\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb are recorded|הֹֽעֲלָ֔ה\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the Book|סֵ֖פֶר\rb* \rb of the Kings|מַלְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.
\s1 Jehoshaphat’s Fleet Is Wrecked
\p \v 35 \rb Later|וְאַחֲרֵיכֵ֗ן\rb*, \rb Jehoshaphat|יְהוֹשָׁפָ֣ט\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb made an alliance|אֶתְחַבַּר֙\rb* \rb with|עִ֖ם\rb* \rb Ahaziah|אֲחַזְיָ֣ה\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb who|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb acted|לַעֲשֽׂוֹת׃\rb* \rb wickedly|הִרְשִׁ֥יעַ\rb*.\f + \fr 20:35 \ft Or \fqa who made him act wickedly \ft or \fqa by which he acted wickedly\f* \v 36 \rb They agreed|וַיְחַבְּרֵ֣הוּ\rb*\rb |עִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb to make|לַעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb* \rb ships|אֳנִיּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb to go|לָלֶ֣כֶת\rb* \rb to Tarshish|תַּרְשִׁ֑ישׁ\rb*,\f + \fr 20:36 \ft Or \fqa a fleet of trading ships\f* \rb and these were built|וַיַּעֲשׂ֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֳנִיּ֖וֹת\rb*\rb |בְּעֶצְי֥וֹן\rb* \rb in Ezion-geber|גָּֽבֶר׃\rb*.
\p \v 37 \rb Then Eliezer|אֱלִיעֶ֤זֶר\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Dodavahu|דֹּדָוָ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb of Mareshah|מִמָּ֣רֵשָׁ֔ה\rb* \rb prophesied|וַיִּתְנַבֵּ֞א\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb Jehoshaphat|יְהוֹשָׁפָ֖ט\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, “\rb Because you have allied yourself|כְּהִֽתְחַבֶּרְךָ֣\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb Ahaziah|אֲחַזְיָ֗הוּ\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb has destroyed|פָּרַ֤ץ\rb* \rb your works|מַעֲשֶׂ֔יךָ\rb*.”
\p \rb So the ships|אֳנִיּ֔וֹת\rb* \rb were wrecked|וַיִּשָּׁבְר֣וּ\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb and were unable|עָצְר֖וּ\rb* \rb to sail|לָלֶ֥כֶת\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Tarshish|תַּרְשִֽׁישׁ׃\rb*.\f + \fr 20:37 \ft Or \fqa set sail to trade\f*
\c 21
\s1 Jehoram Reigns in Judah
\r (2 Kings 8:16–19)
\p \v 1 \rb And Jehoshaphat|יְהֽוֹשָׁפָט֙\rb* \rb rested|וַיִּשְׁכַּ֤ב\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb his fathers|אֲבֹתָ֔יו\rb* \rb and was buried|וַיִּקָּבֵ֥ר\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb them|אֲבֹתָ֖יו\rb* \rb in the City|בְּעִ֣יר\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֑יד\rb*. \rb And his son|בְּנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Jehoram|יְהוֹרָ֥ם\rb* \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֛ךְ\rb* \rb in his place|תַּחְתָּֽיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb Jehoram’s brothers|אַחִ֞ים\rb*, \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Jehoshaphat|יְהוֹשָׁפָ֗ט\rb*, \rb were Azariah|עֲזַרְיָ֤ה\rb*, \rb Jehiel|וִֽיחִיאֵל֙\rb*, \rb Zechariah|וּזְכַרְיָ֣הוּ\rb*, \rb Azariah|וַעֲזַרְיָ֔הוּ\rb*, \rb Michael|וּמִיכָאֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb and Shephatiah|וּשְׁפַטְיָ֑הוּ\rb*; \rb these were|אֵ֕לֶּה\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb sons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Jehoshaphat|יְהוֹשָׁפָ֖ט\rb* \rb king|מֶ֥לֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.\f + \fr 21:2 \ft That is, Judah; in 2 Chronicles, Judah is occasionally called Israel, as representative of the true Israel.\f* \v 3 \rb Their father|אֲ֠בִיהֶם\rb* \rb had given them|וַיִּתֵּ֣ן\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֣ם׀\rb* \rb many|רַבּ֜וֹת\rb* \rb gifts|מַתָּנ֨וֹת\rb* \rb of silver|לְכֶ֤סֶף\rb* \rb and gold|וּלְזָהָב֙\rb* \rb and precious things|וּלְמִגְדָּנ֔וֹת\rb*, \rb as well as|עִם־\rb* \rb the fortified|מְצֻר֖וֹת\rb* \rb cities|עָרֵ֥י\rb* \rb in Judah|בִּֽיהוּדָ֑ה\rb*; \rb but|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb he gave|נָתַ֥ן\rb* \rb the kingdom|הַמַּמְלָכָ֛ה\rb* \rb to Jehoram|לִֽיהוֹרָ֖ם\rb* \rb because|כִּי־\rb* \rb he|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb was the firstborn|הַבְּכֽוֹר׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb When Jehoram|יְהוֹרָ֜ם\rb* \rb had established himself|וַיָּ֨קָם\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb his father’s|אָבִיו֙\rb* \rb kingdom|מַמְלֶ֤כַת\rb*, \rb he strengthened himself|וַיִּתְחַזַּ֔ק\rb* \rb by putting|וַיַּהֲרֹ֥ג\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to the sword|בֶּחָ֑רֶב\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb his brothers|אֶחָ֖יו\rb* \rb along with|וְגַ֖ם\rb* \rb some of the princes|מִשָּׂרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb Jehoram|יְהוֹרָ֣ם\rb* \rb was thirty-two|שְׁלֹשִׁ֥ים\rb*\rb |וּשְׁתַּ֛יִם\rb* \rb years old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֖ה\rb* \rb when he became king|בְּמָלְכ֑וֹ\rb*, \rb and he reigned|מָלַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb* \rb eight|וּשְׁמוֹנֶ֣ה\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִ֔ים\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb And Jehoram walked|וַיֵּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb in the ways|בְּדֶ֣רֶךְ׀\rb* \rb of the kings|מַלְכֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb*, \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Ahab|אַחְאָ֔ב\rb* \rb had done|עָשׂוּ֙\rb*. \rb For|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb he|לּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb married|אִשָּׁ֑ה\rb* \rb a daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Ahab|אַחְאָ֔ב\rb*\rb |הָ֥יְתָה\rb* \rb and did|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb evil|הָרַ֖ע\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb Yet the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb was unwilling|וְלֹא־\rb*\rb |אָבָ֣ה\rb* \rb to destroy|לְהַשְׁחִית֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֔יד\rb*, \rb because of|לְמַ֣עַן\rb* \rb the covenant|הַבְּרִ֔ית\rb* \rb He had made|כָּרַ֖ת\rb* \rb with David|לְדָוִ֑יד\rb*, \rb and since|וְכַאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb He had promised|אָמַ֗ר\rb* \rb to maintain|לָתֵ֨ת\rb* \rb a lamp|נִ֛יר\rb* \rb for David|ל֥וֹ\rb* \rb and his descendants|וּלְבָנָ֖יו\rb* \rb forever|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִֽים׃\rb*.
\s1 Edom and Libnah Rebel
\r (2 Kings 8:20–24)
\p \v 8 \rb In the days of Jehoram|בְּיָמָיו֙\rb*, \rb Edom|אֱד֔וֹם\rb* \rb rebelled|פָּשַׁ֣ע\rb* \rb against|מִתַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb the hand|יַד־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb and appointed|וַיַּמְלִ֥יכוּ\rb* \rb their own|עֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb So Jehoram|יְהוֹרָם֙\rb* \rb crossed|וַיַּֽעֲבֹ֤ר\rb* \rb into Edom|עִם־\rb* \rb with his officers|שָׂרָ֔יו\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his chariots|הָרֶ֖כֶב\rb*. \rb When the Edomites|אֱדוֹם֙\rb* \rb surrounded|הַסּוֹבֵ֣ב\rb* \rb him|אֵלָ֔יו\rb* \rb and|וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb his chariot|הָרָֽכֶב׃\rb* \rb commanders|שָׂרֵ֥י\rb*,\rb |עִמּ֑וֹ\rb*\rb |וַיְהִי֙\rb* \rb he rose up|קָ֣ם\rb* \rb and attacked|וַיַּ֗ךְ\rb*\f + \fr 21:9 \ft Or \fqa he went out and escaped\f* \rb by night|לַ֔יְלָה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb So to|עַ֚ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb Edom|אֱד֜וֹם\rb* \rb has been in rebellion|וַיִּפְשַׁ֨ע\rb* \rb against|מִתַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb the hand of|יַד־\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb*. \rb Likewise|אָ֣ז\rb*, \rb Libnah|לִבְנָ֛ה\rb* \rb rebelled|תִּפְשַׁ֥ע\rb* \rb against|מִתַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb his hand|יָד֑וֹ\rb* \rb at the same|הַהִ֖יא\rb* \rb time|בָּעֵ֥ת\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb Jehoram had forsaken|עָזַ֔ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of his fathers|אֲבֹתָֽיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb Jehoram|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb had also|גַּם־\rb* \rb built|עָשָֽׂה־\rb* \rb high places|בָמ֖וֹת\rb* \rb on the hills|בְּהָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb*; \rb he had caused the people|יֹשְׁבֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb to prostitute themselves|וַיֶּ֙זֶן֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and had led Judah|יְהוּדָֽה׃פ\rb* \rb astray|וַיַּדַּ֖ח\rb*.\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\s1 Elijah’s Letter to Jehoram
\p \v 12 \rb Then a letter|מִכְתָּ֔ב\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֤א\rb* \rb to Jehoram|אֵלָיו֙\rb* \rb from Elijah|מֵֽאֵלִיָּ֥הוּ\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֖יא\rb*, \rb which stated|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*:
\pmo “\rb This is what|כֹּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵי֙\rb* \rb of your father|אָבִ֔יךָ\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֣יד\rb*, \rb says|אָמַ֣ר\rb*:
\pmo ‘\rb |תַּ֗חַת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb You have not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb walked|הָלַ֙כְתָּ֙\rb* \rb in the ways|בְּדַרְכֵי֙\rb* \rb of your father|אָבִ֔יךָ\rb* \rb Jehoshaphat|יְהוֹשָׁפָ֣ט\rb* \rb or|וּבְדַרְכֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Asa|אָסָ֥א\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb*, \v 13 \rb but you have walked|וַתֵּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb in the ways|בְּדֶ֙רֶךְ֙\rb* \rb of the kings|מַלְכֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb and have caused Judah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the people|יֹשְׁבֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb to prostitute themselves|וַתַּזְנֶ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*, \rb just as the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Ahab|אַחְאָ֑ב\rb* \rb prostituted itself|כְּהַזְנ֖וֹת\rb*. \rb You have also|וְגַ֨ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb killed|הָרָֽגְתָּ׃\rb* \rb your brothers|אַחֶ֧יךָ\rb*, \rb your father’s|אָבִ֛יךָ\rb* \rb family|בֵית־\rb*, \rb who were better|הַטּוֹבִ֥ים\rb* \rb than you|מִמְּךָ֖\rb*.
\pmo \v 14 \rb So behold|הִנֵּ֣ה\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb is about to strike|נֹגֵ֛ף\rb* \rb your people|בְּעַמֶּ֑ךָ\rb*, \rb your sons|וּבְבָנֶ֥יךָ\rb*, \rb your wives|וּבְנָשֶׁ֖יךָ\rb*, \rb and all|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb your possessions|רְכוּשֶֽׁךָ׃\rb* \rb with a serious|גְדוֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb blow|מַגֵּפָ֥ה\rb*. \v 15 \rb And day|יָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb after|עַל־\rb* \rb day|יָמִֽים׃\rb* \rb you yourself|וְאַתָּ֛ה\rb* \rb will suffer from a severe|רַבִּ֖ים\rb* \rb illness|בָּחֳלָיִ֥ים\rb*, \rb a disease|בְּמַחֲלֵ֣ה\rb* \rb of your bowels|מֵעֶ֑יךָ\rb*, \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb it|הַחֹ֔לִי\rb* \rb causes|מִן־\rb* \rb your bowels|מֵעֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb to come out|יֵצְא֤וּ\rb*.’”
\s1 Jehoram’s Disease and Death
\p \v 16 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb stirred|וַיָּ֨עַר\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb Jehoram|יְהוֹרָ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb the spirit|ר֤וּחַ\rb* \rb of the Philistines|הַפְּלִשְׁתִּים֙\rb* \rb and Arabs|וְהָ֣עַרְבִ֔ים\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb lived near|יַ֥ד\rb* \rb the Cushites|כּוּשִֽׁים׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb So they went to war|וַיַּעֲל֤וּ\rb* \rb against Judah|בִֽיהוּדָה֙\rb*, \rb invaded it|וַיִּבְקָע֔וּהָ\rb*, \rb and carried off|וַיִּשְׁבּ֗וּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֤ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the possessions|הָרְכוּשׁ֙\rb* \rb found|הַנִּמְצָ֣א\rb* \rb in the king’s|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb palace|לְבֵית־\rb*, \rb along with|וְגַם־\rb* \rb his sons|בָּנָ֖יו\rb* \rb and wives|וְנָשָׁ֑יו\rb*; \rb not|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb a son|בֵּ֔ן\rb* \rb was left|נִשְׁאַר־\rb* \rb to him|לוֹ֙\rb* \rb except|כִּ֥י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb Jehoahaz|יְהוֹאָחָ֖ז\rb*,\f + \fr 21:17 \fqa Jehoahaz \ft is a variant of \fqa Ahaziah\ft ; see 2 Chronicles 22:1.\f* \rb his youngest|קְטֹ֥ן\rb*\rb |בָּנָֽיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb After|וְאַחֲרֵ֖י\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb this|זֹ֑את\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה׀\rb* \rb afflicted Jehoram|נְגָפ֨וֹ\rb* \rb with an incurable|לְאֵ֥ין\rb*\rb |מַרְפֵּֽא׃\rb* \rb disease|לָחֳלִ֖י\rb* \rb of the bowels|בְּמֵעָ֛יו\rb*. \v 19 \rb This continued|וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb day|לְיָמִ֣ים׀\rb* \rb after day|מִיָּמִ֡ים\rb*\rb |וּכְעֵת֩\rb* \rb until two|שְׁנַ֗יִם\rb* \rb full years|לְיָמִ֣ים\rb* \rb had passed|צֵ֨את\rb*. \rb Finally|הַקֵּ֜ץ\rb*, \rb his intestines|מֵעָיו֙\rb* \rb came out|יָצְא֤וּ\rb* \rb because of|עִם־\rb* \rb his disease|חָלְי֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and he died|וַיָּ֖מָת\rb* \rb in severe|רָעִ֑ים\rb* \rb pain|בְּתַחֲלֻאִ֣ים\rb*. \rb And his people|עַמּ֛וֹ\rb* \rb did not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb make|עָ֨שׂוּ\rb* \rb a fire|שְׂרֵפָ֖ה\rb* \rb in his honor|ל֥וֹ\rb* \rb as they had done|כִּשְׂרֵפַ֥ת\rb* \rb for his fathers|אֲבֹתָֽיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb Jehoram was|הָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb thirty-two|שְׁלֹשִׁ֤ים\rb*\rb |וּשְׁתַּ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb years old|בֶּן־\rb* \rb when he became king|בְמָלְכ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and he reigned|מָלַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb eight|וּשְׁמוֹנֶ֣ה\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִ֔ים\rb*. \rb He died|וַיֵּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb*, \rb to no|בְּלֹ֣א\rb* \rb one’s regret|חֶמְדָּ֔ה\rb*, \rb and was buried|וַֽיִּקְבְּרֻ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb in the City|בְּעִ֣יר\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֔יד\rb*, \rb but not|וְלֹ֖א\rb* \rb in the tombs|בְּקִבְר֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the kings|הַמְּלָכִֽים׃\rb*.
\c 22
\s1 Ahaziah Reigns in Judah
\r (2 Kings 8:25–29)
\p \v 1 \rb Then the people|יוֹשְׁבֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֜ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb made Ahaziah|אֲחַזְיָ֨הוּ\rb*, \rb the youngest|הַקָּטֹן֙\rb* \rb son of Jehoram|בְנ֤וֹ\rb*, \rb king|וַיַּמְלִיכוּ֩\rb* \rb in his place|תַּחְתָּ֔יו\rb*, \rb since|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb the raiders|הַגְּד֔וּד\rb* \rb who had come|הַבָּ֥א\rb* \rb into the camp|לַֽמַּחֲנֶ֑ה\rb* \rb with the Arabs|בָֽעַרְבִ֖ים\rb*\f + \fr 22:1 \ft Or \fqa since the marauding bands of Arabs\f* \rb had killed|הָרַ֣ג\rb* \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb the older sons|הָרִאשֹׁנִים֙\rb*. \rb So Ahaziah|אֲחַזְיָ֥הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Jehoram|יְהוֹרָ֖ם\rb* \rb became king|וַיִּמְלֹ֛ךְ\rb*\rb |מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָֽה׃פ\rb*. \v 2 \rb Ahaziah|אֲחַזְיָ֣הוּ\rb* \rb was twenty-two|אַרְבָּעִ֨ים\rb*\rb |וּשְׁתַּ֤יִם\rb*\f + \fr 22:2 \ft Some LXX manuscripts and Syriac (see also 2 Kings 8:26); Hebrew \fqa forty-two\f* \rb years old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָה֙\rb* \rb when he became king|בְמָלְכ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and he reigned|מָלַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּֽירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb one|אַחַ֔ת\rb* \rb year|וְשָׁנָ֣ה\rb*. \rb His mother’s|אִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb name|וְשֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb was Athaliah|עֲתַלְיָ֖הוּ\rb*, \rb the granddaughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Omri|עָמְרִֽי׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb Ahaziah|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb also|גַּם־\rb* \rb walked|הָלַ֔ךְ\rb* \rb in the ways|בְּדַרְכֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Ahab|אַחְאָ֑ב\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb his mother|אִמּ֛וֹ\rb*\rb |הָיְתָ֥ה\rb* \rb was his counselor|יֽוֹעַצְתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb in wickedness|לְהַרְשִֽׁיעַ׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb And he did|וַיַּ֧עַשׂ\rb* \rb evil|הָרַ֛ע\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb as the house|כְּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of Ahab had done|אַחְאָ֑ב\rb*, \rb for|כִּי־\rb* \rb to his|לֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb destruction|לְמַשְׁחִ֥ית\rb* \rb they|הֵ֜מָּה\rb* \rb were|הָֽיוּ־\rb* \rb his|ל֣וֹ\rb* \rb counselors|יֽוֹעֲצִ֗ים\rb* \rb after|אַחֲרֵ֛י\rb* \rb the death|מ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of his father|אָבִ֖יו\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb Ahaziah also|גַּ֣ם\rb* \rb followed|הָלַךְ֒\rb* \rb their counsel|בַּעֲצָתָם֮\rb* \rb and went|וַיֵּלֶךְ֩\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb Joram|יְהוֹרָ֨ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ahab|אַחְאָ֜ב\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb to fight|לַמִּלְחָמָ֛ה\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb Hazael|חֲזָאֵ֥ל\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Aram|אֲרָ֖ם\rb* \rb at Ramoth-gilead|בְּרָמ֣וֹת\rb*\rb |גִּלְעָ֑ד\rb*. \rb But the Arameans|הָֽרַמִּ֖ים\rb*\f + \fr 22:5 \ft Some LXX manuscripts \fqa the archers\f* \rb wounded|וַיַּכּ֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Joram|יוֹרָֽם׃\rb*.\f + \fr 22:5 \ft Hebrew \fqa Jehoram\ft , a variant of \fqa Joram\ft ; also in verses 6 and 7\f* \v 6 \rb So he returned|וַיָּ֜שָׁב\rb* \rb to Jezreel|בְיִזְרְעֶ֗אל\rb* \rb to recover|לְהִתְרַפֵּ֣א\rb* \rb from|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb the wounds|הַמַּכִּים֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb they had inflicted on him|הִכֻּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb at Ramah|בָֽרָמָ֔ה\rb*\f + \fr 22:6 \fqa Ramah \ft is a variant of \fqa Ramoth\ft ; see verse 5.\f* \rb when he fought|בְּהִלָּ֣חֲמ֔וֹ\rb* \rb against|אֶת־\rb* \rb Hazael|חֲזָהאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Aram|אֲרָ֑ם\rb*. \rb Then Ahaziah|וַעֲזַרְיָ֨הוּ\rb*\f + \fr 22:6 \ft Some Hebrew manuscripts, LXX, Vulgate, and Syriac (see also 2 Kings 8:29); most Hebrew manuscripts \fqa Azariah\f* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Jehoram|יְהוֹרָ֜ם\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb* \rb went down|יָרַ֡ד\rb* \rb to Jezreel|בְּיִזְרְעֶ֖אל\rb* \rb to visit|לִרְא֞וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Joram|יְהוֹרָ֧ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ahab|אַחְאָ֛ב\rb*, \rb because|כִּי־\rb* \rb Joram|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb had been wounded|חֹלֶ֥ה\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb Ahaziah’s|אֲחַזְיָ֔הוּ\rb* \rb downfall|תְּבוּסַ֣ת\rb* \rb came|הָיְתָה֙\rb* \rb from God|וּמֵֽאֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb when he went|לָב֖וֹא\rb* \rb to visit|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joram|יוֹרָ֑ם\rb*. \rb When Ahaziah arrived|וּבְבֹא֗וֹ\rb*, \rb he went out|יָצָ֤א\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb Joram|יְהוֹרָם֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb meet Jehu|יֵה֣וּא\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb*\f + \fr 22:7 \ft Or \fqa grandson\ft ; see 2 Kings 9:14.\f* \rb of Nimshi|נִמְשִׁ֔י\rb*, \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb had anointed|מְשָׁח֣וֹ\rb* \rb to destroy|לְהַכְרִ֖ית\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Ahab|אַחְאָֽב׃\rb*.
\s1 Jehu Kills the Princes of Judah
\r (2 Kings 9:14–29)
\p \v 8 \rb |וַיְהִ֕י\rb* \rb So while Jehu|יֵה֖וּא\rb* \rb was executing judgment|כְּהִשָּׁפֵ֥ט\rb* \rb on|עִם־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Ahab|אַחְאָ֑ב\rb*, \rb he found|וַיִּמְצָא֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the rulers|שָׂרֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֜ה\rb* \rb and the sons|וּבְנֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Ahaziah’s|אֲחַזְיָ֛הוּ\rb* \rb brothers|אֲחֵ֧י\rb* \rb who were serving|מְשָׁרְתִ֥ים\rb* \rb Ahaziah|לַאֲחַזְיָ֖הוּ\rb*, \rb and he killed them|וַיַּהַרְגֵֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb Then Jehu looked for|וַיְבַקֵּשׁ֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Ahaziah|אֲחַזְיָ֨הוּ\rb*, \rb and Jehu’s soldiers captured him|וַֽיִּלְכְּדֻ֜הוּ\rb* \rb while he|וְה֧וּא\rb* \rb was hiding|מִתְחַבֵּ֣א\rb* \rb in Samaria|בְשֹֽׁמְר֗וֹן\rb*. \rb So Ahaziah was brought|וַיְבִאֻ֣הוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Jehu|יֵהוּא֮\rb* \rb and put to death|וַיְמִתֻהוּ֒\rb*. \rb They buried him|וַֽיִּקְבְּרֻ֔הוּ\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb they said|אָֽמְרוּ֙\rb*, “\rb He|ה֔וּא\rb* \rb is the grandson|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jehoshaphat|יְהוֹשָׁפָ֣ט\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb sought|דָּרַ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb with all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb his heart|לְבָב֑וֹ\rb*.”
\p \rb So no one was left|וְאֵין֙\rb* \rb from the house|לְבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of Ahaziah|אֲחַזְיָ֔הוּ\rb* \rb with|לַעְצֹ֥ר\rb* \rb the strength|כֹּ֖חַ\rb* \rb to rule the kingdom|לְמַמְלָכָֽה׃\rb*.
\s1 Athaliah and Joash
\r (2 Kings 11:1–3)
\p \v 10 \rb When Athaliah|וַעֲתַלְיָ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb the mother|אֵ֣ם\rb* \rb of Ahaziah|אֲחַזְיָ֔הוּ\rb* \rb saw|רָאֲתָ֖ה\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb her son|בְּנָ֑הּ\rb* \rb was dead|מֵ֣ת\rb*, \rb she proceeded|וַתָּ֗קָם\rb* \rb to annihilate|וַתְּדַבֵּ֛ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the royal|הַמַּמְלָכָ֖ה\rb* \rb heirs|זֶ֥רַע\rb* \rb of the house|לְבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb |וַתִּקַּח֩\rb* \rb But Jehoshabeath|יְהוֹשַׁבְעַ֨ת\rb*\f + \fr 22:11 \fqa Jehoshabeath \ft is a variant of \fqa Jehosheba\ft ; twice in this verse; see 2 Kings 11:2.\f* \rb daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of King Jehoram|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took Joash|יוֹאָ֣שׁ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ahaziah|אֲחַזְיָ֗הוּ\rb* \rb and stole him away|וַתִּגְנֹ֤ב\rb*\rb |אֹתוֹ֙\rb* \rb from among|מִתּ֤וֹךְ\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb who were being murdered|הַמּ֣וּמָתִ֔ים\rb*, \rb and she put|וַתִּתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb him|אֹת֛וֹ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and his nurse|מֵֽינִקְתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb in a bedroom|בַּחֲדַ֣ר\rb*\rb |הַמִּטּ֑וֹת\rb*. \rb Because Jehoshabeath|יְהוֹשַׁבְעַ֣ת\rb*, \rb the daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Jehoram|יְהוֹרָ֡ם\rb* \rb and the wife|אֵשֶׁת֩\rb* \rb of Jehoiada|יְהוֹיָדָ֨ע\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֜ן\rb*, \rb was|הָיְתָ֨ה\rb* \rb Ahaziah’s|אֲחַזְיָ֛הוּ\rb* \rb sister|אֲח֧וֹת\rb*, \rb she hid Joash|וַתַּסְתִּירֵ֡הוּ\rb* \rb from|מִפְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb Athaliah|עֲתַלְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb so that she could not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb kill him|הֱמִיתָֽתְהוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb And Joash remained|וַיְהִ֤י\rb* \rb hidden|מִתְחַבֵּ֖א\rb* \rb with them|אִתָּם֙\rb* \rb in the house|בְּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of God|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb for six|שֵׁ֣שׁ\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִ֖ים\rb* \rb while Athaliah|וַעֲתַלְיָ֖ה\rb* \rb ruled|מֹלֶ֥כֶת\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָֽרֶץ׃פ\rb*.
\c 23
\s1 Joash Anointed King of Judah
\r (2 Kings 11:4–12)
\p \v 1 \rb Then in the seventh|הַשְּׁבִעִ֜ית\rb* \rb year|וּבַשָּׁנָ֨ה\rb*, \rb Jehoiada|יְהוֹיָדָ֗ע\rb* \rb strengthened himself|הִתְחַזַּ֣ק\rb* \rb and made|וַיִּקַּ֣ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb a covenant|בַבְּרִֽית׃\rb* \rb with|עִמּ֥וֹ\rb* \rb the commanders|שָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of hundreds|הַמֵּא֡וֹת\rb* — \rb with Azariah|לַעֲזַרְיָ֣הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Jeroham|יְרֹחָ֡ם\rb*, \rb Ishmael|וּלְיִשְׁמָעֵ֣אל\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jehohanan|יְ֠הוֹחָנָן\rb*, \rb Azariah|וְלַֽעֲזַרְיָ֨הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Obed|עוֹבֵ֜ד\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Maaseiah|מַעֲשֵׂיָ֧הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Adaiah|עֲדָיָ֛הוּ\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Elishaphat|אֱלִישָׁפָ֥ט\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Zichri|זִכְרִ֖י\rb*. \v 2 \rb So they went throughout|וַיָּסֹ֙בּוּ֙\rb* \rb Judah|בִּֽיהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb and gathered|וַיִּקְבְּצ֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Levites|הַלְוִיִּם֙\rb* \rb from all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb the cities|עָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb and the heads|וְרָאשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb of the families|הָאָב֖וֹת\rb* \rb of Israel|לְיִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*. \rb And when they came|וַיָּבֹ֖אוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*, \v 3 \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb assembly|הַקָּהָ֥ל\rb* \rb made|וַיִּכְרֹ֨ת\rb* \rb a covenant|בְּרִ֛ית\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb in the house|בְּבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*.
\p “\rb Behold|הִנֵּ֤ה\rb*, \rb the king’s|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb*!” \rb said Jehoiada|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֗ם\rb*. “\rb He must reign|יִמְלֹ֔ךְ\rb*, \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb promised|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb concerning|עַל־\rb* \rb the descendants|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of David|דָוִֽיד׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb This|זֶ֥ה\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֖ר\rb* \rb is what|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you are to do|תַּעֲשׂ֑וּ\rb*: \rb A third|הַשְּׁלִשִׁ֨ית\rb* \rb of you|מִכֶּ֜ם\rb* \rb priests|לַכֹּֽהֲנִים֙\rb* \rb and Levites|וְלַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb* \rb who come on duty|בָּאֵ֣י\rb* \rb on the Sabbath|הַשַּׁבָּ֗ת\rb* \rb shall keep watch|לְשֹֽׁעֲרֵ֖י\rb* \rb at the doors|הַסִּפִּֽים׃\rb*, \v 5 \rb a third|וְהַשְּׁלִשִׁית֙\rb* \rb shall be at the royal|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb palace|בְּבֵ֣ית\rb*, \rb and a third|וְהַשְּׁלִשִׁ֖ית\rb* \rb at the Foundation|הַיְס֑וֹד\rb* \rb Gate|בְּשַׁ֣עַר\rb*, \rb while all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the others|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb are to be in the courtyards|בְּחַצְר֖וֹת\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb No|וְאַל־\rb* \rb one is to enter|יָב֣וֹא\rb* \rb the house|בֵית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb except|כִּ֤י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb the priests|הַכֹּֽהֲנִים֙\rb* \rb and those Levites|לַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb* \rb who serve|וְהַמְשָׁרְתִ֣ים\rb*; \rb they|הֵ֥מָּה\rb* \rb may enter|יָבֹ֖אוּ\rb* \rb because|כִּי־\rb* \rb they|הֵ֑מָּה\rb* \rb are consecrated|קֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb but all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb are to obey|יִשְׁמְר֖וּ\rb* \rb the requirement|מִשְׁמֶ֥רֶת\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb The Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֨ם\rb* \rb must surround|וְהִקִּיפוּ֩\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb*\rb |סָבִ֗יב\rb*\rb |אִ֚ישׁ\rb* \rb with weapons|וְכֵלָ֣יו\rb* \rb in hand|בְּיָד֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and anyone who enters|וְהַבָּ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the temple|הַבַּ֖יִת\rb* \rb must be put to death|יוּמָ֑ת\rb*. \rb You must stay|וִֽהְי֥וּ\rb* \rb close|אֶת־\rb* \rb to the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb wherever he goes|בְּבֹא֥וֹ\rb*\rb |וּבְצֵאתֽוֹ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 8 \rb So the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֜ם\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb* \rb did|וַיַּעֲשׂ֨וּ\rb* \rb everything|כְּכֹ֣ל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Jehoiada|יְהוֹיָדָ֣ע\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵן֒\rb* \rb had ordered|צִוָּה֮\rb*. \rb Each of them|אִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקְחוּ֙\rb* \rb his men|אֲנָשָׁ֔יו\rb*— \rb those coming on duty|בָּאֵ֣י\rb* \rb on the Sabbath|הַשַּׁבָּ֔ת\rb* \rb and|עִ֖ם\rb* \rb those going off duty|יוֹצְאֵ֣י\rb*\rb |הַשַּׁבָּ֑ת\rb*— \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb Jehoiada|יְהוֹיָדָ֥ע\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֖ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb released any of|פָטַ֛ר\rb* \rb the divisions|הַֽמַּחְלְקֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb Then Jehoiada|יְהוֹיָדָ֨ע\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֜ן\rb* \rb gave|וַיִּתֵּן֩\rb* \rb to the commanders|לְשָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of hundreds|הַמֵּא֗וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the spears|הַֽחֲנִיתִים֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the large|הַמָּגִנּוֹת֙\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb small shields|הַשְּׁלָטִ֔ים\rb* \rb of King|לַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֑יד\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb were in the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb He stationed|וַיַּעֲמֵ֨ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the troops|הָעָ֜ם\rb*\rb |וְאִ֣ישׁ׀\rb*, \rb with their weapons|שִׁלְח֣וֹ\rb* \rb in hand|בְיָד֗וֹ\rb*, \rb surrounding|סָבִֽיב׃\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb by the altar|לַמִּזְבֵּ֖חַ\rb* \rb and the temple|וְלַבָּ֑יִת\rb*,\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb from the south|הַיְמָנִית֙\rb* \rb side|מִכֶּ֨תֶף\rb*\rb |הַבַּ֤יִת\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the north|הַשְּׂמָאלִ֔ית\rb* \rb side|כֶּ֤תֶף\rb* \rb of the temple|הַבַּ֙יִת֙\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb Then Jehoiada and his sons brought out|וַיּוֹצִ֣יאוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb*, \rb put|וַיִּתְּנ֤וּ\rb* \rb the crown|הַנֵּ֙זֶר֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb on him|עָלָיו֙\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb presented him with the Testimony|הָ֣עֵד֔וּת\rb*, \rb and proclaimed him king|וַיַּמְלִ֖יכוּ\rb*.\rb |אֹת֑וֹ\rb* \rb They|יְהוֹיָדָ֣ע\rb*\rb |וּבָנָ֔יו\rb* \rb anointed him|וַיִּמְשָׁחֻ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb and shouted|וַיֹּאמְר֖וּ\rb*, “\rb Long live|יְחִ֥י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃ס\rb*!”
\s1 The Death of Athaliah
\r (2 Kings 11:13–16)
\p \v 12 \rb When Athaliah|עֲתַלְיָ֗הוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb heard|וַתִּשְׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb the noise|ק֤וֹל\rb* \rb of the people|הָעָם֙\rb* \rb running|הָֽרָצִ֔ים\rb* \rb and cheering|וְהַֽמְהַֽלְלִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb*, \rb she went out|וַתָּב֥וֹא\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb them|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb in the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb And she looked|וַתֵּ֡רֶא\rb* \rb and saw|וְהִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּלֶךְ֩\rb* \rb standing|עוֹמֵ֨ד\rb* \rb by|עַֽל־\rb* \rb his pillar|עַמּוּד֜וֹ\rb* \rb at the entrance|בַּמָּב֗וֹא\rb*. \rb The officers|וְהַשָּׂרִ֣ים\rb* \rb and trumpeters|וְהַחֲצֹצְרוֹת֮\rb* \rb were beside|עַל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּלֶךְ֒\rb*, \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|עַ֨ם\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֜רֶץ\rb* \rb were rejoicing|שָׂמֵ֗חַ\rb* \rb and blowing|וְתוֹקֵ֙עַ֙\rb* \rb trumpets|בַּחֲצֹ֣צְר֔וֹת\rb*, \rb while the singers|וְהַמְשֽׁוֹרֲרִים֙\rb* \rb with musical|הַשִּׁ֔יר\rb* \rb instruments|בִּכְלֵ֣י\rb* \rb were leading|וּמוֹדִיעִ֖ים\rb* \rb the praises|לְהַלֵּ֑ל\rb*.
\p \rb Then Athaliah|עֲתַלְיָ֙הוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb tore|וַתִּקְרַ֤ע\rb* \rb her clothes|בְּגָדֶ֔יהָ\rb* \rb and screamed|וַתֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Treason|קֶ֥שֶׁר\rb*, \rb treason|קָֽשֶׁר׃ס\rb*!”
\p \v 14 \rb And Jehoiada|יְהוֹיָדָ֨ע\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֜ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb sent out|וַיּוֹצֵא֩\rb* \rb the commanders|שָׂרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of hundreds|הַמֵּא֣וֹת׀\rb* \rb in charge of|פְּקוּדֵ֣י\rb* \rb the army|הַחַ֗יִל\rb*, \rb saying|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*,\rb |אֲלֵהֶם֙\rb* “\rb Bring her out|הֽוֹצִיא֙וּהָ֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb between|מִבֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb the ranks|הַשְּׂדֵר֔וֹת\rb*,\f + \fr 23:14 \ft Or \fqa out from the precincts\f* \rb and put to|יוּמַ֣ת\rb* \rb the sword|בֶּחָ֑רֶב\rb* \rb anyone who follows|וְהַבָּ֥א\rb* \rb her|אַחֲרֶ֖יהָ\rb*.” \rb For|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb* \rb had said|אָמַ֣ר\rb*, “\rb She must not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb be put to death|תְמִית֖וּהָ\rb* \rb in the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 15 \rb So they seized|וַיָּשִׂ֤ימוּ\rb* \rb Athaliah|יָדַ֔יִם\rb* \rb as she reached|וַתָּב֛וֹא\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the entrance|מְב֥וֹא\rb* \rb of the Horse|הַסּוּסִ֖ים\rb* \rb Gate|שַֽׁעַר־\rb* \rb on the palace grounds|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb*\rb |בֵּ֣ית\rb*, \rb and there|שָֽׁם׃פ\rb* \rb they put her to death|וַיְמִית֖וּהָ\rb*.
\s1 Jehoiada Restores the Worship of the LORD
\r (2 Kings 11:17–21)
\p \v 16 \rb Then Jehoiada|יְהוֹיָדָע֙\rb* \rb made|וַיִּכְרֹ֤ת\rb* \rb a covenant|בְּרִ֔ית\rb* \rb between himself|בֵּינ֕וֹ\rb* \rb and|וּבֵ֥ין\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb and the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֣ין\rb* \rb that they would be|לִהְי֥וֹת\rb* \rb the LORD’s|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb people|לְעָ֖ם\rb*. \v 17 \rb So all|כָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֤ם\rb* \rb went|וַיָּבֹ֨אוּ\rb* \rb to the temple|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of Baal|הַבַּ֙עַל֙\rb* \rb and tore it down|וַֽיִּתְּצֻ֔הוּ\rb*.\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb They smashed the altars|מִזְבְּחֹתָ֥יו\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and idols|צְלָמָ֖יו\rb* \rb to pieces|שִׁבֵּ֑רוּ\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֗ת\rb* \rb and killed|הָרְג֖וּ\rb* \rb Mattan|מַתָּן֙\rb* \rb the priest|כֹּהֵ֣ן\rb* \rb of Baal|הַבַּ֔עַל\rb* \rb in front of|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the altars|הַֽמִּזְבְּחֽוֹת׃\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb Moreover , Jehoiada|יְהוֹיָדָ֨ע\rb* \rb put|וַיָּשֶׂם֩\rb* \rb the oversight|פְּקֻדֹּ֜ת\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb into the hands|בְּיַ֨ד\rb* \rb of the Levitical|הַלְוִיִּם֮\rb* \rb priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֣ים\rb*, \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb David|דָּוִיד֮\rb* \rb had appointed|חָלַ֣ק\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֒\rb*, \rb to offer|לְֽהַעֲל֞וֹת\rb* \rb burnt offerings|עֹל֣וֹת\rb* \rb to the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb as written|כַּכָּת֛וּב\rb* \rb in the Law|בְּתוֹרַ֥ת\rb* \rb of Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb*, \rb with rejoicing|בְּשִׂמְחָ֣ה\rb* \rb and song|וּבְשִׁ֑יר\rb*,\rb |עַ֖ל\rb* \rb as ordained|יְדֵ֥י\rb* \rb by David|דָוִֽיד׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb He stationed|וַֽיַּעֲמֵד֙\rb* \rb gatekeepers|הַשּׁ֣וֹעֲרִ֔ים\rb* \rb at|עַֽל־\rb* \rb the gates|שַׁעֲרֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb so that no one who was|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb in any|לְכָל־\rb* \rb way|דָּבָֽר׃\rb* \rb unclean|טָמֵ֖א\rb* \rb could enter|יָבֹ֥א\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb And he took with him|וַיִּקַּ֣ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the commanders|שָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of hundreds|הַמֵּא֡וֹת\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the nobles|הָֽאַדִּירִים֩\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the rulers|הַמּֽוֹשְׁלִ֨ים\rb* \rb of the people|בָּעָ֜ם\rb*,\rb |וְאֵ֣ת׀\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|עַ֣ם\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֗רֶץ\rb*, \rb and they brought the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb down|וַיּ֤וֹרֶד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb from the house|מִבֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and entered|וַיָּבֹ֛אוּ\rb* \rb the royal|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb palace|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb through|בְּתֽוֹךְ־\rb* \rb the Upper|הָֽעֶלְי֖וֹן\rb* \rb Gate|שַׁ֥עַר\rb*. \rb They seated|וַיּוֹשִׁ֙יבוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb King Joash|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb on|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb the royal|הַמַּמְלָכָֽה׃\rb* \rb throne|כִּסֵּ֥א\rb*, \v 21 \rb and all|כָל־\rb* \rb the people|עַם־\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb rejoiced|וַיִּשְׂמְח֥וּ\rb*. \rb And the city|וְהָעִ֣יר\rb* \rb was quiet|שָׁקָ֑טָה\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb because Athaliah|עֲתַלְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb had been put to|הֵמִ֥יתוּ\rb* \rb the sword|בֶחָֽרֶב׃ס\rb*.
\c 24
\s1 Joash Repairs the Temple
\r (2 Kings 12:1–16)
\p \v 1 \rb Joash|יֹאָ֣שׁ\rb* \rb was seven|שֶׁ֤בַע\rb* \rb years old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנִים֙\rb* \rb when he became king|בְּמָלְכ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and he reigned|מָלַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּֽירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb forty|וְאַרְבָּעִ֣ים\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb*. \rb His mother’s|אִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb name|וְשֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb was Zibiah|צִבְיָ֖ה\rb*;\rb |מִבְּאֵ֥ר\rb* \rb she was from Beersheba|שָֽׁבַע׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb And Joash|יוֹאָ֛שׁ\rb* \rb did|וַיַּ֧עַשׂ\rb* \rb what was right|הַיָּשָׁ֖ר\rb* \rb in the eyes|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the days|יְמֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Jehoiada|יְהוֹיָדָ֥ע\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵֽן׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb Jehoiada|יְהוֹיָדָ֖ע\rb* \rb took|וַיִּשָּׂא־\rb* \rb for him|ל֥וֹ\rb* \rb two|שְׁתָּ֑יִם\rb* \rb wives|נָשִׁ֣ים\rb*, \rb and he had|וַיּ֖וֹלֶד\rb* \rb sons|בָּנִ֥ים\rb* \rb and daughters|וּבָנֽוֹת׃\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb Some time later|וַיְהִ֖י\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵיכֵ֑ן\rb*, \rb Joash|יוֹאָ֔שׁ\rb* \rb set|הָיָה֙\rb*\rb |עִם־\rb* \rb his heart|לֵ֣ב\rb* \rb on repairing|לְחַדֵּ֖שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb So he gathered|וַיִּקְבֹּץ֮\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֣ים\rb* \rb and Levites|וְהַלְוִיִּם֒\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Go out|צְא֣וּ\rb* \rb to the cities|לְעָרֵ֪י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֟ה\rb* \rb and collect|וְקִבְצוּ֩\rb* \rb the money|כֶּ֜סֶף\rb* \rb due|מִדֵּ֤י\rb* \rb annually|שָׁנָה֙\rb*\rb |בְּשָׁנָ֔ה\rb* \rb from all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֨ל\rb*, \rb to repair|לְחַזֵּ֣ק׀\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of your God|אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶ֗ם\rb*.\rb |וְאַתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb Do it|לַדָּבָ֑ר\rb* \rb quickly|תְּמַהֲר֣וּ\rb*.”
\p \rb The Levites, however|הַֽלְוִיִּֽם׃\rb*, \rb did not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb make haste|מִֽהֲר֖וּ\rb*. \v 6 \rb So the king|הַמֶּלֶךְ֮\rb* \rb called|וַיִּקְרָ֣א\rb* \rb Jehoiada|לִֽיהוֹיָדָ֣ע\rb* \rb the high|הָרֹאשׁ֒\rb* \rb priest and said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Why|מַדּ֙וּעַ֙\rb* \rb have you not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb required|דָרַ֣שְׁתָּ\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb* \rb to bring|לְהָבִ֞יא\rb* \rb from Judah|מִֽיהוּדָ֣ה\rb* \rb and Jerusalem|וּמִֽירוּשָׁלִַ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the tax imposed|מַשְׂאַת֙\rb* \rb by Moses|מֹשֶׁ֣ה\rb* \rb the servant|עֶֽבֶד־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and by the assembly|וְהַקָּהָ֖ל\rb* \rb of Israel|לְיִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb for the Tent|לְאֹ֖הֶל\rb* \rb of the Testimony|הָעֵדֽוּת׃\rb*?”
\p \v 7 \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb the sons|בָּנֶ֥יהָ\rb* \rb of that wicked woman|הַמִּרְשַׁ֔עַת\rb* \rb Athaliah|עֲתַלְיָ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb had broken into|פָרְצ֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb* \rb and had even|וְגַם֙\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb used|עָשׂ֖וּ\rb* \rb the sacred objects|קָדְשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb of the house|בֵית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb for the Baals|לַבְּעָלִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb At the king’s|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb command|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb a|אֶחָ֑ד\rb* \rb chest|אֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb was made|וַֽיַּעֲשׂ֖וּ\rb* \rb and placed|וַֽיִּתְּנֻ֛הוּ\rb* \rb outside|חֽוּצָה׃\rb*, \rb at the gate|בְּשַׁ֥עַר\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*. \v 9 \rb And a proclamation|ק֞וֹל\rb* \rb was issued|וַיִּתְּנוּ־\rb* \rb in Judah|בִּֽיהוּדָ֣ה\rb* \rb and Jerusalem|וּבִֽירוּשָׁלִַ֗ם\rb* \rb that they were to bring|לְהָבִ֤יא\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָה֙\rb* \rb the tax|מַשְׂאַ֞ת\rb* \rb imposed by Moses|מֹשֶׁ֧ה\rb* \rb the servant|עֶֽבֶד־\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֛ים\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb in the wilderness|בַּמִּדְבָּֽר׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb All|כָל־\rb* \rb the officers|הַשָּׂרִ֖ים\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֑ם\rb* \rb rejoiced|וַיִּשְׂמְח֥וּ\rb* \rb and brought their contributions|וַיָּבִ֛יאוּ\rb*, \rb and they dropped them|וַיַּשְׁלִ֥יכוּ\rb* \rb in the chest|לָאָר֖וֹן\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb it was full|לְכַלֵּֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb |וַיְהִ֡י\rb* \rb Whenever|בְּעֵת֩\rb* \rb the chest|הָֽאָר֜וֹן\rb* \rb was brought|יָבִ֨יא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb by|בְּיַ֣ד\rb* \rb the Levites|הַלְוִיִּם֒\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּלֶךְ֮\rb* \rb overseers|פְּקֻדַּ֣ת\rb* \rb and they saw|וְכִרְאוֹתָ֞ם\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb there was a large amount|רַ֣ב\rb* \rb of money|הַכֶּ֗סֶף\rb*, \rb the royal|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb scribe|סוֹפֵ֤ר\rb* \rb and the officer|וּפְקִיד֙\rb* \rb of the high|הָרֹ֔אשׁ\rb* \rb priest|כֹּהֵ֣ן\rb* \rb would come|וּבָ֨א\rb* \rb and empty|וִיעָ֙רוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the chest|הָ֣אָר֔וֹן\rb* \rb and carry it|וְיִשָּׂאֻ֖הוּ\rb* \rb back|וִֽישִׁיבֻ֣הוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb its place|מְקֹמ֑וֹ\rb*. \rb They did|עָשׂוּ֙\rb* \rb this|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb daily|לְי֣וֹם׀\rb*\rb |בְּי֔וֹם\rb* \rb and gathered|וַיַּֽאַסְפוּ־\rb* \rb the money|כֶ֖סֶף\rb* \rb in abundance|לָרֹֽב׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb Then the king|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb and Jehoiada|וִֽיהוֹיָדָ֗ע\rb* \rb would give the money|וַיִּתְּנֵ֨הוּ\rb* \rb to those who|אֶל־\rb* \rb supervised|עוֹשֵׂה֙\rb*\rb |מְלֶ֙אכֶת֙\rb* \rb the labor|עֲבוֹדַ֣ת\rb* \rb on the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |וַיִּֽהְי֤וּ\rb* \rb to hire|שֹׂכְרִים֙\rb* \rb stonecutters|חֹצְבִ֣ים\rb* \rb and carpenters|וְחָרָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb to restore|לְחַדֵּ֖שׁ\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb as well as|וְ֠גַם\rb* \rb workers|לְחָרָשֵׁ֤י\rb* \rb in iron|בַרְזֶל֙\rb* \rb and bronze|וּנְחֹ֔שֶׁת\rb* \rb to repair|לְחַזֵּ֖ק\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb So the workmen|וַֽיַּעֲשׂוּ֙\rb*\rb |הַמְּלָאכָ֔ה\rb* \rb labored|עֹשֵׂ֣י\rb*, \rb and in their hands|בְּיָדָ֑ם\rb* \rb the repair|אֲרוּכָ֛ה\rb* \rb work|לַמְּלָאכָ֖ה\rb* \rb progressed|וַתַּ֧עַל\rb*. \rb They restored|וַֽיַּעֲמִ֜ידוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֧ית\rb* \rb of God|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֛ים\rb* \rb according|עַל־\rb* \rb to its specifications|מַתְכֻּנְתּ֖וֹ\rb*, \rb and they reinforced it|וַֽיְאַמְּצֻֽהוּ׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb When they were finished|וּֽכְכַלּוֹתָ֡ם\rb*, \rb they brought|הֵבִ֣יאוּ\rb* \rb the rest|שְׁאָ֣ר\rb* \rb of the money|הַכֶּ֗סֶף\rb* \rb to|לִפְנֵי֩\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb and Jehoiada|וִֽיהוֹיָדָ֜ע\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and with it were made|וַיַּעֲשֵׂ֨הוּ\rb* \rb articles|כֵלִ֤ים\rb* \rb for the house|לְבֵית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* — \rb utensils|כְּלֵ֣י\rb* \rb for the service|שָׁרֵ֔ת\rb* \rb and for the burnt offerings|וְהַעֲל֣וֹת\rb*, \rb dishes|וְכַפּ֔וֹת\rb*, \rb and other objects|וּכְלֵ֥י\rb* \rb of gold|זָהָ֖ב\rb* \rb and silver|וָכָ֑סֶף\rb*.
\p \rb Throughout|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb the days|יְמֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Jehoiada|יְהוֹיָדָֽע׃פ\rb*,\rb |וַ֠יִּֽהְיוּ\rb* \rb burnt offerings|עֹל֤וֹת\rb* \rb were presented|מַעֲלִ֨ים\rb* \rb regularly|תָּמִ֔יד\rb* \rb in the house|בְּבֵית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*.
\s1 Jehoiada’s Death and Burial
\p \v 15 \rb When Jehoiada was old|וַיִּזְקַ֧ן\rb* \rb and full of|וַיִּשְׂבַּ֥ע\rb* \rb years|יָמִ֖ים\rb*, \rb he|יְהוֹיָדָ֛ע\rb* \rb died|וַיָּמֹ֑ת\rb* \rb at the age|שָׁנָ֖ה\rb* \rb of 130|מֵאָ֧ה\rb*\rb |וּשְׁלֹשִׁ֛ים\rb*\rb |בֶּן־\rb*\rb |בְּמוֹתֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb And Jehoiada was buried|וַיִּקְבְּרֻ֥הוּ\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb the kings|הַמְּלָכִ֑ים\rb* \rb in the City|בְעִיר־\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֖יד\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he had done|עָשָׂ֤ה\rb* \rb what was good|טוֹבָה֙\rb* \rb in Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb for|וְעִ֥ם\rb* \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb and His temple|וּבֵיתֽוֹ׃ס\rb*.
\s1 The Wickedness of Joash
\p \v 17 \rb After|וְאַֽחֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb the death|מוֹת֙\rb* \rb of Jehoiada, however|יְה֣וֹיָדָ֔ע\rb*, \rb the officials|שָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb came|בָּ֚אוּ\rb* \rb and paid homage|וַיִּֽשְׁתַּחֲו֖וּ\rb* \rb to the king|לַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb*, \rb and|אָ֛ז\rb* \rb he|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb listened|שָׁמַ֥ע\rb* \rb to them|אֲלֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 18 \rb They abandoned|וַיַּֽעַזְב֗וּ\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֤ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of their fathers|אֲבוֹתֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb and served|וַיַּֽעַבְד֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Asherah poles|הָאֲשֵׁרִ֖ים\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and idols|הָֽעֲצַבִּ֑ים\rb*. \rb So wrath|קֶ֗צֶף\rb* \rb came|וַֽיְהִי־\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb* \rb and Jerusalem|וִיר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb for this|זֹֽאת׃\rb* \rb guilt of theirs|בְּאַשְׁמָתָ֖ם\rb*. \v 19 \rb Nevertheless, the LORD sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֤ח\rb*\rb |בָּהֶם֙\rb* \rb prophets|נְבִאִ֔ים\rb* \rb to bring the people back|לַהֲשִׁיבָ֖ם\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Him|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and to testify|וַיָּעִ֥ידוּ\rb* \rb against them|בָ֖ם\rb*, \rb but they would not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb listen|הֶאֱזִֽינוּ׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb Then the Spirit|וְר֣וּחַ\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb came upon|לָֽבְשָׁה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Zechariah|זְכַרְיָה֙\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jehoiada|יְהוֹיָדָ֣ע\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb*, \rb who stood up|וַֽיַּעֲמֹ֖ד\rb* \rb before|מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb the people|לָעָ֑ם\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶ֜ם\rb*, “\rb This is what|כֹּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר\rb*: ‘\rb Why|לָמָה֩\rb* \rb do you|אַתֶּ֨ם\rb* \rb transgress|עֹבְרִ֜ים\rb* \rb the commandments|מִצְוֺ֤ת\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb so that you cannot|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb prosper|תַצְלִ֔יחוּ\rb*? \rb Because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you have forsaken|עֲזַבְתֶּ֥ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb He has forsaken|וַיַּֽעֲזֹ֥ב\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶֽם׃\rb*.’”
\p \v 21 \rb But they conspired|וַיִּקְשְׁר֣וּ\rb* \rb against Zechariah|עָלָ֔יו\rb*, \rb and by order|בְּמִצְוַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb*, \rb they stoned him|וַיִּרְגְּמֻ֥הוּ\rb*\rb |אֶ֖בֶן\rb* \rb in the courtyard|בַּחֲצַ֖ר\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb Thus King|הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb Joash|יוֹאָ֣שׁ\rb* \rb failed to|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb remember|זָכַ֞ר\rb* \rb the kindness|הַחֶ֙סֶד֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb Zechariah’s father|אָבִיו֙\rb* \rb Jehoiada|יְהוֹיָדָ֤ע\rb* \rb had extended|עָשָׂ֜ה\rb* \rb to him|עִמּ֔וֹ\rb*. \rb Instead, Joash killed|וַֽיַּהֲרֹ֖ג\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Jehoiada’s son|בְּנ֑וֹ\rb*. \rb As he lay dying|וּכְמוֹת֣וֹ\rb*, \rb Zechariah said|אָמַ֔ר\rb*, “\rb May the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb see this|יֵ֥רֶא\rb* \rb and call you to account|וְיִדְרֹֽשׁ׃פ\rb*.”
\s1 The Death of Joash
\r (2 Kings 12:17–21)
\p \v 23 \rb |וַיְהִ֣י׀\rb* \rb In the spring|לִתְקוּפַ֣ת\rb*\rb |הַשָּׁנָ֗ה\rb*,\f + \fr 24:23 \ft Literally \fqa At the turn of the year\f* \rb the army of Aram|אֲרָם֒\rb* \rb went to war|עָלָ֣ה\rb* \rb against Joash|עָלָיו֮\rb*.\rb |חֵ֣יל\rb* \rb They entered|וַיָּבֹ֗אוּ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb* \rb and Jerusalem|וִיר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb and destroyed|וַיַּשְׁחִ֛יתוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the leaders|שָׂרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb*\rb |מֵעָ֑ם\rb*, \rb and they sent|שִׁלְּח֖וּ\rb* \rb all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the plunder|שְׁלָלָ֥ם\rb* \rb to their king|לְמֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb in Damascus|דַּרְמָֽשֶׂק׃\rb*. \v 24 \rb Although|כִּי֩\rb* \rb the Aramean|אֲרָ֗ם\rb* \rb army|חֵ֣יל\rb* \rb had come|בָּ֣אוּ׀\rb* \rb with only a few|בְמִצְעַ֨ר\rb* \rb men|אֲנָשִׁ֜ים\rb*, \rb the LORD|וַֽיהוָה֙\rb* \rb delivered|נָתַ֨ן\rb* \rb into their hand|בְּיָדָ֥ם\rb* \rb a very|מְאֹ֔ד\rb* \rb great|לָרֹ֣ב\rb* \rb army|חַ֙יִל֙\rb*. \rb Because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb Judah had forsaken|עָֽזְב֔וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of their fathers|אֲבוֹתֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb judgment|שְׁפָטִֽים׃\rb* \rb was executed|עָשׂ֥וּ\rb* \rb on|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Joash|יוֹאָ֖שׁ\rb*.
\p \v 25 \rb And when the Arameans had withdrawn|וּבְלֶכְתָּ֣ם\rb*\rb |מִמֶּ֗נּוּ\rb*, \rb they left|עָזְב֣וּ\rb* \rb Joash|אֹתוֹ֮\rb* \rb severely|רַבִּים֒\rb* \rb wounded|בְּמַחֲלִיִּים\rb*. \rb His own servants|עֲבָדָ֗יו\rb* \rb conspired|הִתְקַשְּׁר֨וּ\rb* \rb against him|עָלָ֜יו\rb* \rb for shedding the blood|בִּדְמֵי֙\rb* \rb of the son|בְּנֵי֙\rb*\f + \fr 24:25 \ft LXX and Vulgate; Hebrew \fqa of the sons\f* \rb of Jehoiada|יְהוֹיָדָ֣ע\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb*, \rb and they killed him|וַיַּֽהַרְגֻ֥הוּ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb his bed|מִטָּת֖וֹ\rb*. \rb So he died|וַיָּמֹ֑ת\rb* \rb and was buried|וַֽיִּקְבְּרֻ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb in the City|בְּעִ֣יר\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֔יד\rb*, \rb but not|וְלֹ֥א\rb*\rb |קְבָרֻ֖הוּ\rb* \rb in the tombs|בְּקִבְר֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the kings|הַמְּלָכִֽים׃ס\rb*. \v 26 \rb Those|וְאֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb who conspired|הַמִּתְקַשְּׁרִ֣ים\rb* \rb against Joash|עָלָ֑יו\rb* \rb were Zabad|זָבָ֗ד\rb*\f + \fr 24:26 \fqa Zabad \ft is a variant of \fqa Jozabad\ft ; see 2 Kings 12:21.\f* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Shimeath|שִׁמְעָת֙\rb* \rb the Ammonitess|הָֽעַמּוֹנִ֔ית\rb* \rb and Jehozabad|וִיה֣וֹזָבָ֔ד\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Shimrith|שִׁמְרִ֖ית\rb*\f + \fr 24:26 \fqa Shimrith \ft is a variant of \fqa Shomer\ft ; see 2 Kings 12:21.\f* \rb the Moabitess|הַמּוֹאָבִֽית׃\rb*.
\p \v 27 \rb The accounts of the sons of Joash|וּבָנָ֞יו\rb* \rb and the many|וְרֹב\rb* \rb pronouncements|הַמַּשָּׂ֣א\rb* \rb about him|עָלָ֗יו\rb*, \rb and of the restoration|וִיסוֹד֙\rb*\f + \fr 24:27 \ft Or \fqa founding\f* \rb of the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*, \rb are indeed|הִנָּ֣ם\rb* \rb written|כְּתוּבִ֔ים\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the Treatise|מִדְרַ֖שׁ\rb*\f + \fr 24:27 \ft Or \fqa Exposition \ft or \fqa Study\f* \rb of the Book|סֵ֣פֶר\rb* \rb of the Kings|הַמְּלָכִ֑ים\rb*. \rb And his son|בְנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Amaziah|אֲמַצְיָ֥הוּ\rb* \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֛ךְ\rb* \rb in his place|תַּחְתָּֽיו׃פ\rb*.
\c 25
\s1 Amaziah Reigns in Judah
\r (2 Kings 14:1–7)
\p \v 1 \rb Amaziah|אֲמַצְיָ֔הוּ\rb* \rb was twenty-five|עֶשְׂרִ֨ים\rb*\rb |וְחָמֵ֤שׁ\rb* \rb years old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָה֙\rb* \rb when he became king|מָלַ֣ךְ\rb*, \rb and he reigned|מָלַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb twenty-nine|וְעֶשְׂרִ֣ים\rb*\rb |וָתֵ֙שַׁע֙\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb*. \rb His mother’s|אִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb name|וְשֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb was Jehoaddan|יְהוֹעַדָּ֖ן\rb*; \rb she was from Jerusalem|מִירוּשָׁלָֽיִם׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb And he did what was|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb right|הַיָּשָׁ֖ר\rb* \rb in the eyes|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb but|רַ֕ק\rb* \rb not|לֹ֖א\rb* \rb wholeheartedly|בְּלֵבָ֥ב\rb*\rb |שָׁלֵֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb |וַיְהִ֕י\rb* \rb As soon as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb the kingdom|הַמַּמְלָכָ֖ה\rb* \rb was firmly|חָזְקָ֥ה\rb* \rb in his grasp|עָלָ֑יו\rb*, \rb Amaziah executed|וַֽיַּהֲרֹג֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the servants|עֲבָדָ֔יו\rb* \rb who had murdered|הַמַּכִּ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his father|אָבִֽיו׃\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֥לֶךְ\rb*. \v 4 \rb Yet|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb he did not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb put their sons|בְּנֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb to death|הֵמִ֑ית\rb*, \rb but acted|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb according to what is written|כַכָּת֣וּב\rb* \rb in the Law|בַּתּוֹרָ֡ה\rb*, \rb in the Book|בְּסֵ֣פֶר\rb* \rb of Moses|מֹשֶׁה֩\rb*, \rb where|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb commanded|צִוָּ֨ה\rb*: “\rb Fathers|אָב֤וֹת\rb* \rb must not|לֹא־\rb* \rb be put to death|יָמ֨וּתוּ\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb their children|בָּנִים֙\rb*, \rb and children|וּבָנִים֙\rb* \rb must not|לֹא־\rb* \rb be put to death|יָמ֣וּתוּ\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb their fathers|אָב֔וֹת\rb*;\rb |כִּ֛י\rb* \rb each|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb is to die|יָמֽוּתוּ׃פ\rb* \rb for his own sin|בְּחֶטְא֖וֹ\rb*.”\f + \fr 25:4 \ft Deuteronomy 24:16\f*
\s1 Amaziah’s Victories
\p \v 5 \rb Then Amaziah|אֲמַצְיָ֙הוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb gathered|וַיִּקְבֹּ֤ץ\rb* \rb the people of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb*\rb |וַיַּֽעֲמִידֵ֣ם\rb* \rb and assigned them according to their families|אָב֗וֹת\rb*\rb |לְבֵית־\rb* \rb to commanders|לְשָׂרֵ֤י\rb* \rb of thousands|הָאֲלָפִים֙\rb* \rb and|וּלְשָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of hundreds|הַמֵּא֔וֹת\rb*. \rb And he numbered|וַֽיִּפְקְדֵ֗ם\rb* \rb those twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֤ים\rb* \rb years of age|לְמִבֶּ֨ן\rb*\rb |שָׁנָה֙\rb* \rb or older|וָמַ֔עְלָה\rb* \rb throughout|לְכָל־\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb and Benjamin|וּבִנְיָמִ֑ן\rb* \rb and found|וַיִּמְצָאֵ֗ם\rb* \rb 300,000|שְׁלֹשׁ־\rb*\rb |מֵא֨וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶ֤לֶף\rb* \rb chosen men|בָּחוּר֙\rb* \rb able to serve|יוֹצֵ֣א\rb* \rb in the army|צָבָ֔א\rb*, \rb bearing|אֹחֵ֖ז\rb* \rb the spear|רֹ֥מַח\rb* \rb and shield|וְצִנָּֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb He also hired|וַיִּשְׂכֹּ֣ר\rb* \rb 100,000|בְּמֵאָ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֶ֛לֶף\rb* \rb mighty men|גִּבּ֥וֹר\rb* \rb of valor|חָ֖יִל\rb* \rb from Israel|מִיִּשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb for a hundred|מֵ֥אָה\rb* \rb talents|כִכַּר־\rb* \rb of silver|כָּֽסֶף׃\rb*.\f + \fr 25:6 \fqa 100 talents \ft is approximately 3.77 tons or 3.42 metric tons of silver; also in verse 9.\f* \v 7 \rb But a man|וְאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb came|בָּ֤א\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָיו֙\rb* \rb and said|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, “\rb O king|הַמֶּ֕לֶךְ\rb*, \rb do not let|אַל־\rb* \rb the army|צְבָ֣א\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb go|יָבֹ֥א\rb* \rb with you|עִמְּךָ֖\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb is not|אֵ֤ין\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* — \rb not with any|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb of the Ephraimites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |אֶפְרָֽיִם׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb Even|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֔ה\rb* \rb go|בֹּ֣א\rb* \rb and fight|עֲשֵׂ֖ה\rb* \rb bravely|חֲזַ֣ק\rb* \rb in battle|לַמִּלְחָמָ֑ה\rb*, \rb God|הָֽאֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb will overthrow you|יַכְשִֽׁילְךָ֤\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the enemy|אוֹיֵ֔ב\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb God|בֵּאלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb has|יֶשׁ־\rb* \rb power|כֹּ֛חַ\rb* \rb to help|לַעְז֥וֹר\rb* \rb and power to overthrow|וּלְהַכְשִֽׁיל׃\rb*.”
\p \v 9 \rb Amaziah|אֲמַצְיָ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb the man|לְאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*, “\rb What|וּמַֽה־\rb* \rb should I do|לַּעֲשׂוֹת֙\rb* \rb about the hundred|לִמְאַ֣ת\rb* \rb talents|הַכִּכָּ֔ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I have given|נָתַ֖תִּי\rb* \rb to the troops|לִגְד֣וּד\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*?”
\p \rb And the man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of God|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*\rb |יֵ֚שׁ\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb The LORD|לַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb is able to give|לָ֥תֶת\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֖\rb* \rb much more|הַרְבֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb than this|מִזֶּֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 10 \rb So Amaziah|אֲמַצְיָ֗הוּ\rb* \rb dismissed|וַיַּבְדִּילֵ֣ם\rb* \rb the troops|לְהַגְּדוּד֙\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb had come|בָּ֤א\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָיו֙\rb* \rb from Ephraim|מֵֽאֶפְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb and sent them|לָלֶ֖כֶת\rb* \rb home|לִמְקוֹמָ֑ם\rb*. \rb And they were furious|וַיִּ֨חַר\rb*\rb |אַפָּ֤ם\rb*\rb |מְאֹד֙\rb* \rb with Judah|בִּֽיהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb and returned|וַיָּשׁ֥וּבוּ\rb* \rb home|לִמְקוֹמָ֖ם\rb* \rb in great|בָּחֳרִי־\rb* \rb anger|אָֽף׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb Amaziah, however|וַאֲמַצְיָ֙הוּ֙\rb*, \rb summoned his strength|הִתְחַזַּ֔ק\rb* \rb and led|וַיִּנְהַג֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his troops|עַמּ֔וֹ\rb*\rb |וַיֵּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb to the Valley of Salt|גֵּ֣יא\rb*,\rb |הַמֶּ֑לַח\rb* \rb where he struck down|וַיַּ֥ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb 10,000|עֲשֶׂ֥רֶת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִֽים׃\rb* \rb men|בְּנֵי־\rb* \rb of Seir|שֵׂעִ֖יר\rb*, \v 12 \rb and the army|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb also captured|שָׁבוּ֙\rb* \rb 10,000 men|וַעֲשֶׂ֨רֶת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִ֜ים\rb* \rb alive|חַיִּ֗ים\rb*. \rb They took them|וַיְבִיא֖וּם\rb* \rb to the top|לְרֹ֣אשׁ\rb* \rb of a cliff|הַסָּ֑לַע\rb*\rb |מֵֽרֹאשׁ־\rb*\rb |הַסֶּ֖לַע\rb* \rb and threw them down|וַיַּשְׁלִיכ֛וּם\rb* \rb so that all|וְכֻלָּ֥ם\rb* \rb were dashed to pieces|נִבְקָֽעוּ׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb Meanwhile|וּבְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the troops|הַגְּד֗וּד\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb Amaziah|אֲמַצְיָ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb had dismissed|הֵשִׁ֤יב\rb*\rb |מִלֶּ֤כֶת\rb*\rb |עִמּוֹ֙\rb* \rb from battle|לַמִּלְחָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb raided|וַֽיִּפְשְׁטוּ֙\rb* \rb the cities|בְּעָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb*, \rb from Samaria|מִשֹּׁמְר֖וֹן\rb* \rb to|וְעַד־\rb*\rb |בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb Beth-horon|חוֹר֑וֹן\rb*. \rb They struck down|וַיַּכּ֤וּ\rb*\rb |מֵהֶם֙\rb* \rb 3,000 people|שְׁלֹ֣שֶׁת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִ֔ים\rb* \rb and carried off|וַיָּבֹ֖זּוּ\rb* \rb a great deal of|רַבָּֽה׃ס\rb* \rb plunder|בִּזָּ֥ה\rb*.
\s1 Amaziah Rebuked for Idolatry
\p \v 14 \rb |וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb When|אַחֲרֵ֨י\rb* \rb Amaziah|אֲמַצְיָ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb returned|ב֤וֹא\rb* \rb from the slaughter|מֵֽהַכּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of|אֶת־\rb* \rb the Edomites|אֲדוֹמִ֔ים\rb*, \rb he brought back|וַיָּבֵ֗א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the gods|אֱלֹהֵי֙\rb* \rb of the Seirites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |שֵׂעִ֔יר\rb*, \rb set them up|וַיַּֽעֲמִידֵ֥ם\rb* \rb as his own|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb gods|לֵאלֹהִ֑ים\rb*, \rb bowed|יִֽשְׁתַּחֲוֶ֖ה\rb* \rb before them|וְלִפְנֵיהֶ֥ם\rb*, \rb and burned sacrifices|יְקַטֵּֽר׃\rb* \rb to them|וְלָהֶ֥ם\rb*. \v 15 \rb Therefore the anger|אַ֥ף\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb burned|וַיִּֽחַר־\rb* \rb against Amaziah|בַּאֲמַצְיָ֑הוּ\rb*, \rb and He sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֤ח\rb* \rb him|אֵלָיו֙\rb* \rb a prophet|נָבִ֔יא\rb*, \rb who said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Why|לָ֤מָּה\rb* \rb have you sought|דָרַ֙שְׁתָּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this people’s|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb gods|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb could not|לֹא־\rb* \rb deliver|הִצִּ֥ילוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb them|עַמָּ֖ם\rb* \rb from your hand|מִיָּדֶֽךָ׃\rb*?”
\p \v 16 \rb |וַיְהִ֣י׀\rb* \rb While he was still speaking|בְּדַבְּר֣וֹ\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֗יו\rb*, \rb the king asked|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Have we made you|נְתַנּ֔וּךָ\rb* \rb the counselor|הַלְיוֹעֵ֤ץ\rb* \rb to the king|לַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb*? \rb Stop|חֲדַל־\rb*! \rb Why|לָ֣מָּה\rb* \rb be struck down|יַכּ֑וּךָ\rb*?”
\p \rb So the prophet|הַנָּבִ֗יא\rb* \rb stopped|וַיֶּחְדַּ֣ל\rb*, \rb but he said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb I know|יָדַ֗עְתִּי\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb has determined|יָעַ֤ץ\rb* \rb to destroy you|לְהַשְׁחִיתֶ֔ךָ\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you have done|עָשִׂ֣יתָ\rb* \rb this|זֹּ֔את\rb* \rb and have not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb heeded|שָׁמַ֖עְתָּ\rb* \rb my advice|לַעֲצָתִֽי׃פ\rb*.”
\s1 Jehoash Defeats Amaziah
\r (2 Kings 14:8–14)
\p \v 17 \rb Then Amaziah|אֲמַצְיָ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb took counsel|וַיִּוָּעַ֗ץ\rb* \rb and sent|וַ֠יִּשְׁלַח\rb* \rb word to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb Jehoash|יוֹאָ֨שׁ\rb*\f + \fr 25:17 \fqa Jehoash \ft is a variant of \fqa Joash\ft ; also in verses 18, 21, 23, and 25.\f* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jehoahaz|יְהוֹאָחָ֧ז\rb*, \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jehu|יֵה֛וּא\rb*. “\rb Come|לְךָ\rb*, \rb let us meet|נִתְרָאֶ֥ה\rb* \rb face to face|פָנִֽים׃\rb*,” \rb he said|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb But Jehoash|יוֹאָ֣שׁ\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb replied|וַיִּשְׁלַ֞ח\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Amaziah|אֲמַצְיָ֣הוּ\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָה֮\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹר֒\rb*: “\rb A thistle|הַח֜וֹחַ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in Lebanon|בַּלְּבָנ֗וֹן\rb* \rb sent|שָׁ֠לַח\rb* \rb a message to|אֶל־\rb* \rb a cedar|הָאֶ֜רֶז\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb in Lebanon|בַּלְּבָנוֹן֙\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, ‘\rb Give|תְּנָֽה־\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your daughter|בִּתְּךָ֥\rb* \rb to my son|לִבְנִ֖י\rb* \rb in marriage|לְאִשָּׁ֑ה\rb*.’ \rb Then a wild|הַשָּׂדֶה֙\rb* \rb beast|חַיַּ֤ת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in Lebanon|בַּלְּבָנ֔וֹן\rb* \rb came along|וַֽתַּעֲבֹ֞ר\rb* \rb and trampled|וַתִּרְמֹ֖ס\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the thistle|הַחֽוֹחַ׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb You have said|אָמַ֗רְתָּ\rb*, ‘\rb Look|הִנֵּ֤ה\rb*, \rb I have defeated|הִכִּ֙יתָ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Edom|אֱד֔וֹם\rb*,’ \rb and your heart|לִבְּךָ֖\rb* \rb has become proud|וּנְשָׂאֲךָ֥\rb* \rb and boastful|לְהַכְבִּ֑יד\rb*. \rb Now|עַתָּה֙\rb* \rb stay|שְׁבָ֣ה\rb* \rb at home|בְּבֵיתֶ֔ךָ\rb*. \rb Why|לָ֤מָּה\rb* \rb should you stir up|תִתְגָּרֶה֙\rb* \rb trouble|בְּרָעָ֔ה\rb* \rb so that you fall|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* — \rb you|וְנָ֣פַלְתָּ֔\rb* \rb and Judah|וִיהוּדָ֥ה\rb* \rb with you|עִמָּֽךְ׃\rb*?”
\p \v 20 \rb But Amaziah|אֲמַצְיָ֔הוּ\rb* \rb would not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb listen|שָׁמַ֣ע\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb this had come|הִ֔יא\rb* \rb from God|מֵהָֽאֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb in order to|לְמַ֖עַן\rb* \rb deliver them|תִּתָּ֣ם\rb* \rb into the hand of Jehoash|בְּיָ֑ד\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb they had sought|דָֽרְשׁ֔וּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the gods|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Edom|אֱדֽוֹם׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb So Jehoash|יוֹאָ֤שׁ\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb advanced|וַיַּ֨עַל\rb*, \rb and he|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb and Amaziah|וַאֲמַצְיָ֣הוּ\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb faced|פָנִ֔ים\rb* \rb each other|וַיִּתְרָא֣וּ\rb*\rb |בְּבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb at Beth-shemesh|שֶׁ֖מֶשׁ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb in Judah|לִיהוּדָֽה׃\rb*. \v 22 \rb And Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb was routed|וַיִּנָּ֥גֶף\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb and every man|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb fled|וַיָּנֻ֖סוּ\rb* \rb to his own home|לְאֹהָלָֽיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 23 \rb |וְאֵת֩\rb*\rb |בְּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb There at Beth-shemesh|שָׁ֑מֶשׁ\rb*, \rb Jehoash|יוֹאָ֣שׁ\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb captured|תָּפַ֛שׂ\rb* \rb Amaziah|אֲמַצְיָ֨הוּ\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֜ה\rb*, \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Joash|יוֹאָ֥שׁ\rb*, \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jehoahaz|יְהוֹאָחָ֗ז\rb*.\f + \fr 25:23 \fqa Jehoahaz \ft is a variant of \fqa Ahaziah\ft .\f*
\p \rb Then Jehoash brought him|וַיְבִיאֵ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|יְר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb and broke down|וַיִּפְרֹ֞ץ\rb* \rb the wall|בְּחוֹמַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֗ם\rb* \rb from the Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb Gate|מִשַּׁ֤עַר\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the Corner|הַפּוֹנֶ֔ה\rb* \rb Gate|שַׁ֣עַר\rb* — \rb a section of four|אַרְבַּ֥ע\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֖וֹת\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּֽה׃\rb*.\f + \fr 25:23 \fqa 400 cubits \ft is approximately 600 feet or 182.9 meters.\f* \v 24 \rb He took all|וְכָֽל־\rb* \rb the gold|הַזָּהָ֣ב\rb* \rb and silver|וְהַכֶּ֡סֶף\rb* \rb and|וְאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the articles|הַ֠כֵּלִים\rb* \rb found|הַנִּמְצְאִ֨ים\rb* \rb in the house|בְּבֵית־\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֜ים\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb*\rb |עֹבֵ֣ד\rb* \rb Obed-edom|אֱד֗וֹם\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb in the treasuries|אֹצְרוֹת֙\rb* \rb of the royal|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb palace|בֵּ֣ית\rb*, \rb as well as|וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb some hostages|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |הַתַּֽעֲרֻב֑וֹת\rb*. \rb Then he returned|וַיָּ֖שָׁב\rb* \rb to Samaria|שֹׁמְרֽוֹן׃פ\rb*.
\s1 The Death of Amaziah
\r (2 Kings 14:17–20)
\p \v 25 \rb Amaziah|אֲמַצְיָ֤הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Joash|יוֹאָשׁ֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb lived|וַיְחִ֨י\rb* \rb for fifteen|חֲמֵ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֖ה\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָֽה׃\rb* \rb after|אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb the death|מ֔וֹת\rb* \rb of Jehoash|יוֹאָ֥שׁ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jehoahaz|יְהוֹאָחָ֖ז\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*. \v 26 \rb As for the rest|וְיֶ֙תֶר֙\rb* \rb of the acts|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Amaziah|אֲמַצְיָ֔הוּ\rb*, \rb from beginning|הָרִאשֹׁנִ֖ים\rb* \rb to end|וְהָאַחֲרוֹנִ֑ים\rb*, \rb are they not|הֲלֹא֙\rb*\rb |הִנָּ֣ם\rb* \rb written|כְּתוּבִ֔ים\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the Book|סֵ֥פֶר\rb* \rb of the Kings|מַלְכֵי־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb and Israel|וְיִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*?
\p \v 27 \rb From the time|וּמֵעֵ֗ת\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Amaziah|אֲמַצְיָ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb turned|סָ֤ר\rb* \rb from following|מֵאַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb a conspiracy|קֶ֛שֶׁר\rb* \rb was formed|וַיִּקְשְׁר֨וּ\rb* \rb against him|עָלָ֥יו\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb*, \rb and he fled|וַיָּ֣נָס\rb* \rb to Lachish|לָכִ֑ישָׁה\rb*. \rb But men were sent|וַיִּשְׁלְח֤וּ\rb* \rb after him|אַחֲרָיו֙\rb* \rb to Lachish|לָכִ֔ישָׁה\rb*, \rb and they killed him|וַיְמִיתֻ֖הוּ\rb* \rb there|שָֽׁם׃\rb*. \v 28 \rb They carried him back|וַיִּשָּׂאֻ֖הוּ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb horses|הַסּוּסִ֑ים\rb* \rb and buried|וַֽיִּקְבְּר֥וּ\rb* \rb him|אֹת֛וֹ\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb his fathers|אֲבֹתָ֖יו\rb* \rb in the City|בְּעִ֥יר\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb*.\f + \fr 25:28 \ft Most Hebrew manuscripts; some Hebrew manuscripts, LXX, Vulgate, and Syriac \fqa City of David\ft ; see 2 Kings 14:20.\f*
\c 26
\s1 Uzziah Reigns in Judah
\r (2 Kings 14:21–22; 2 Kings 15:1–7)
\p \v 1 \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|עַ֤ם\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקְח֞וּ\rb* \rb Uzziah|עֻזִּיָּ֔הוּ\rb*,\f + \fr 26:1 \fqa Uzziah \ft is also called \fqa Azariah\ft ; throughout this chapter; see 2 Kings 14:21.\f* \rb who|וְה֕וּא\rb* \rb was sixteen|שֵׁ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֖ה\rb* \rb years old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and made him king|וַיַּמְלִ֣יכוּ\rb*\rb |אֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb in place of|תַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֥יו\rb* \rb Amaziah|אֲמַצְיָֽהוּ׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb Uzziah was the one|ה֚וּא\rb* \rb who rebuilt|בָּנָ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Eloth|אֵיל֔וֹת\rb*\f + \fr 26:2 \fqa Eloth \ft is a variant of \fqa Elath\ft ; see LXX, 2 Kings 14:22, and 2 Kings 16:6.\f* \rb and restored|וַיְשִׁיבֶ֖הָ\rb* \rb it to Judah|לִֽיהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb after|אַחֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb King Amaziah|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*\f + \fr 26:2 \ft Literally \fqa after the king\f* \rb rested|שְׁכַֽב־\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb his fathers|אֲבֹתָֽיו׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb Uzziah|עֻזִּיָּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb was sixteen|שֵׁ֨שׁ\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֤ה\rb* \rb years old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָה֙\rb* \rb when he became king|בְמָלְכ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and he reigned|מָלַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb fifty-two|וַחֲמִשִּׁ֤ים\rb*\rb |וּשְׁתַּ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb*. \rb His mother’s|אִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb name|וְשֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb was Jecoliah|יְכִילְיָה\rb*; \rb she was from|מִן־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb And he did|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb what was right|הַיָּשָׁ֖ר\rb* \rb in the eyes|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb just as|כְּכֹ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb his father|אָבִֽיו׃\rb* \rb Amaziah|אֲמַצְיָ֥הוּ\rb* \rb had done|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb*. \v 5 \rb |וַיְהִי֙\rb* \rb He sought|לִדְרֹ֣שׁ\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb throughout the days|בִּימֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Zechariah|זְכַרְיָ֔הוּ\rb*, \rb who instructed him|הַמֵּבִ֖ין\rb* \rb in the fear|בִּרְאֹ֣ת\rb*\f + \fr 26:5 \ft Many Hebrew manuscripts, LXX, and Syriac; other Hebrew manuscripts \fqa through the vision\f* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb*. \rb And as long as|וּבִימֵי֙\rb* \rb he sought|דָּרְשׁ֣וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִֽים׃ס\rb* \rb gave him success|הִצְלִיח֖וֹ\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb Uzziah went out|וַיֵּצֵא֙\rb* \rb to wage war|וַיִּלָּ֣חֶם\rb* \rb against the Philistines|בַּפְּלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb*, \rb and he tore down|וַיִּפְרֹ֞ץ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the walls|ח֣וֹמַת\rb* \rb of Gath|גַּ֗ת\rb*,\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb*\rb |חוֹמַ֣ת\rb* \rb Jabneh|יַבְנֵ֔ה\rb*, \rb and|וְאֵ֖ת\rb*\rb |חוֹמַ֣ת\rb* \rb Ashdod|אַשְׁדּ֑וֹד\rb*. \rb Then he built|וַיִּבְנֶ֣ה\rb* \rb cities|עָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb near Ashdod|בְּאַשְׁדּ֖וֹד\rb* \rb and among the Philistines|וּבַפְּלִשְׁתִּֽים׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb God|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֜ים\rb* \rb helped him|וַיַּעְזְרֵ֨הוּ\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֧ים\rb*, \rb against|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the Arabs|הָעַרְבִיִּים\rb* \rb living|הַיֹּשְׁבִ֥ים\rb*\rb |בְּגוּר־\rb* \rb in Gur-baal|בָּ֖עַל\rb*, \rb and against the Meunites|וְהַמְּעוּנִֽים׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb The Ammonites|הָֽעַמּוֹנִ֛ים\rb* \rb brought|וַיִּתְּנ֧וּ\rb* \rb tribute|מִנְחָ֖ה\rb* \rb to Uzziah|לְעֻזִּיָּ֑הוּ\rb*, \rb and his fame|שְׁמוֹ֙\rb* \rb spread|וַיֵּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb as far|עַד־\rb* \rb as the border|לְב֣וֹא\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb he had become|עַד־\rb* \rb exceedingly|לְמָֽעְלָה׃\rb* \rb powerful|הֶחֱזִ֖יק\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb Uzziah|עֻזִּיָּ֤הוּ\rb* \rb built|וַיִּ֨בֶן\rb* \rb towers|מִגְדָּלִים֙\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּיר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb at|עַל־\rb* \rb the Corner|הַפִּנָּ֛ה\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb Gate|שַׁ֧עַר\rb*, \rb the Valley|הַגַּ֖יְא\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb Gate|שַׁ֥עַר\rb*, \rb and the angle in the wall|הַמִּקְצ֑וֹעַ\rb*, \rb and he fortified them|וַֽיְחַזְּקֵֽם׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb Since|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb he had|הָ֣יָה\rb* \rb much|רַבִּ֔ים\rb* \rb livestock|מִקְנֶה־\rb* \rb in the foothills|וּבַשְּׁפֵלָ֖ה\rb*\f + \fr 26:10 \ft Hebrew \fqa Shephelah \ft or \fqa lowlands\ft ; that is, the western foothills of Judea\f* \rb and in the plain|וּבַמִּישׁ֑וֹר\rb*, \rb he built|וַיִּ֨בֶן\rb* \rb towers|מִגְדָּלִ֜ים\rb* \rb in the desert|בַּמִּדְבָּ֗ר\rb* \rb and dug|וַיַּחְצֹב֙\rb* \rb many|רַּב֙\rb* \rb cisterns|בֹּר֣וֹת\rb*. \rb And since|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he was|הָיָֽה׃ס\rb* \rb a lover|אֹהֵ֥ב\rb* \rb of the soil|אֲדָמָ֖ה\rb*, \rb he had farmers|אִכָּרִ֣ים\rb* \rb and vinedressers|וְכֹֽרְמִ֗ים\rb* \rb in the hill country|בֶּהָרִים֙\rb* \rb and in the fertile fields|וּבַכַּרְמֶ֔ל\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb Uzziah|לְעֻזִּיָּ֡הוּ\rb* \rb had|וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb an army|חַיִל֩\rb* \rb ready|עֹשֵׂ֨ה\rb* \rb for battle|מִלְחָמָ֜ה\rb* \rb that went out|יוֹצְאֵ֧י\rb* \rb to war|צָבָ֣א\rb* \rb by assigned divisions|לִגְד֗וּד\rb*\rb |פְּקֻדָּתָ֔ם\rb*, \rb as recorded|בְּמִסְפַּר֙\rb* \rb by|בְּיַד֙\rb* \rb Jeiel|יְעוּאֵל\rb* \rb the scribe|הַסּוֹפֵ֔ר\rb* \rb and Maaseiah|וּמַעֲשֵׂיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb the officer|הַשּׁוֹטֵ֑ר\rb* \rb under|עַ֚ל\rb* \rb the direction|יַד־\rb* \rb of Hananiah|חֲנַנְיָ֔הוּ\rb*, \rb one of the royal|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb officers|מִשָּׂרֵ֖י\rb*. \v 12 \rb The total|כֹּ֠ל\rb* \rb number|מִסְפַּ֞ר\rb* \rb of family|הָאָבוֹת֙\rb* \rb leaders|רָאשֵׁ֤י\rb* \rb of the mighty men|לְגִבּ֣וֹרֵי\rb* \rb of valor|חָ֔יִל\rb* \rb was 2,600|אַלְפַּ֖יִם\rb*\rb |וְשֵׁ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵאֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb Under|וְעַל־\rb* \rb their authority|יָדָם֩\rb* \rb was an army|חֵ֨יל\rb*\rb |צָבָ֜א\rb* \rb of 307,500|שְׁלֹ֧שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵא֣וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶ֗לֶף\rb*\rb |וְשִׁבְעַ֤ת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִים֙\rb*\rb |וַחֲמֵ֣שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵא֔וֹת\rb* \rb trained|עוֹשֵׂ֥י\rb* \rb for war|מִלְחָמָ֖ה\rb*, \rb a powerful|בְּכֹ֣חַ\rb* \rb force|חָ֑יִל\rb* \rb to support|לַעְזֹ֥ר\rb* \rb the king|לַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb his enemies|הָאוֹיֵֽב׃\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb Uzziah|עֻזִּיָּ֜הוּ\rb* \rb supplied|וַיָּכֶן֩\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֨ם\rb* \rb the entire|לְכָל־\rb* \rb army|הַצָּבָ֗א\rb* \rb with shields|מָגִנִּ֤ים\rb*, \rb spears|וּרְמָחִים֙\rb*, \rb helmets|וְכ֣וֹבָעִ֔ים\rb*, \rb armor|וְשִׁרְיֹנ֖וֹת\rb*, \rb bows|וּקְשָׁת֑וֹת\rb*, \rb and slingstones|וּלְאַבְנֵ֖י\rb*\rb |קְלָעִֽים׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb And in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִַ֨ם\rb* \rb he made|וַיַּ֣עַשׂ׀\rb* \rb skillfully|חוֹשֵׁ֗ב\rb* \rb designed|מַחֲשֶׁ֣בֶת\rb* \rb devices|חִשְּׁבֹנ֜וֹת\rb* \rb to shoot|לִירוֹא֙\rb*\f + \fr 26:15 \ft Or \fqa to protect those who shoot\f* \rb arrows|בַּֽחִצִּ֔ים\rb* \rb and catapult large|גְּדֹל֑וֹת\rb* \rb stones|וּבָאֲבָנִ֖ים\rb* \rb from|לִהְי֤וֹת\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb the towers|הַמִּגְדָּלִים֙\rb* \rb and|וְעַל־\rb* \rb corners|הַפִּנּ֔וֹת\rb*. \rb So his fame|שְׁמוֹ֙\rb* \rb spread|וַיֵּצֵ֤א\rb* \rb far and wide|לְמֵ֣רָח֔וֹק\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he was helped|לְהֵעָזֵ֖ר\rb* \rb tremendously|הִפְלִ֥יא\rb* \rb until|עַ֥ד\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he became powerful|חָזָֽק׃\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb But when Uzziah became powerful|וּכְחֶזְקָת֗וֹ\rb*, \rb his arrogance|גָּבַ֤הּ\rb*\rb |לִבּוֹ֙\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb led to his own destruction|לְהַשְׁחִ֔ית\rb*. \rb He was unfaithful|וַיִּמְעַ֖ל\rb* \rb to the LORD|בַּיהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb his God|אֱלֹהָ֑יו\rb*, \rb for he entered|וַיָּבֹא֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the temple|הֵיכַ֣ל\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb to burn incense|לְהַקְטִ֖יר\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the altar|מִזְבַּ֥ח\rb* \rb of incense|הַקְּטֹֽרֶת׃\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb Then Azariah|עֲזַרְיָ֣הוּ\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֑ן\rb*, \rb along with|וְעִמּ֞וֹ\rb* \rb eighty|שְׁמוֹנִ֖ים\rb*\rb |בְּנֵי־\rb* \rb brave|חָֽיִל׃\rb* \rb priests|כֹּהֲנִ֧ים׀\rb* \rb of the LORD|לַיהוָ֛ה\rb*, \rb went in|וַיָּבֹ֥א\rb* \rb after him|אַחֲרָ֖יו\rb*. \v 18 \rb They took their stand|וַיַּעַמְד֞וּ\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb Uzziah|עֻזִּיָּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֤אמְרוּ\rb*, “\rb Uzziah|עֻזִּיָּ֗הוּ\rb*, \rb you have no|לֹא־\rb* \rb right to offer incense|לְהַקְטִיר֙\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb*. \rb Only|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the priests|לַכֹּהֲנִ֧ים\rb*, \rb the descendants|בְּנֵי־\rb* \rb of Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֛ן\rb*, \rb are consecrated|הַמְקֻדָּשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb to burn incense|לְהַקְטִ֑יר\rb*. \rb Leave|צֵ֤א\rb* \rb the sanctuary|הַמִּקְדָּשׁ֙\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb you have acted unfaithfully|מָעַ֔לְתָּ\rb*; \rb you will not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb receive honor|לְכָב֖וֹד\rb* \rb from the LORD|מֵיְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb*.”
\p \v 19 \rb Uzziah|עֻזִּיָּ֔הוּ\rb*, \rb with a censer|מִקְטֶ֖רֶת\rb* \rb in his hand|וּבְיָד֥וֹ\rb* \rb to offer incense|לְהַקְטִ֑יר\rb*, \rb was enraged|וַיִּזְעַף֙\rb*. \rb But while he raged|וּבְזַעְפּ֣וֹ\rb* \rb against|עִם־\rb* \rb the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֗ים\rb* \rb in their presence|לִפְנֵ֤י\rb*\rb |הַכֹּֽהֲנִים֙\rb* \rb in the house|בְּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb before|מֵעַ֖ל\rb* \rb the altar|לְמִזְבַּ֥ח\rb* \rb of incense|הַקְּטֹֽרֶת׃\rb*, \rb leprosy|וְ֠הַצָּרַעַת\rb*\f + \fr 26:19 \fqa Leprosy \ft was a term used for various skin diseases; see Leviticus 13.\f* \rb broke out|זָרְחָ֨ה\rb* \rb on his forehead|בְמִצְח֜וֹ\rb*. \v 20 \rb When Azariah|עֲזַרְיָהוּ֩\rb* \rb the chief|הָרֹ֜אשׁ\rb* \rb priest|כֹהֵ֨ן\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֗ים\rb* \rb turned|וַיִּ֣פֶן\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֡יו\rb* \rb and saw|וְהִנֵּה־\rb* \rb his|ה֤וּא\rb* \rb leprous|מְצֹרָע֙\rb* \rb forehead|בְּמִצְח֔וֹ\rb*, \rb they rushed him|וַיַּבְהִל֖וּהוּ\rb* \rb out|מִשָּׁ֑ם\rb*. \rb Indeed|וְגַם־\rb*, \rb he himself|הוּא֙\rb* \rb hurried|נִדְחַ֣ף\rb* \rb to get out|לָצֵ֔את\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb had afflicted him|נִגְּע֖וֹ\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb So King|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb Uzziah|עֻזִּיָּ֨הוּ\rb* \rb was|וַיְהִי֩\rb* \rb a leper|מְצֹרָ֣ע׀\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb the day|י֣וֹם\rb* \rb of his death|מוֹת֗וֹ\rb*. \rb He lived|וַיֵּ֜שֶׁב\rb*\rb |בֵּ֤ית\rb* \rb in isolation|הַחָפְשׁוּת\rb*, \rb leprous|מְצֹרָ֔ע\rb* \rb and|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb cut off|נִגְזַ֖ר\rb* \rb from the house|מִבֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb while his son|בְּנוֹ֙\rb* \rb Jotham|וְיוֹתָ֤ם\rb* \rb had charge|עַל־\rb* \rb of the royal|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb palace|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb and governed|שׁוֹפֵ֖ט\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the people|עַ֥ם\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb As for the rest|וְיֶ֙תֶר֙\rb* \rb of the acts|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Uzziah|עֻזִּיָּ֔הוּ\rb*, \rb from beginning|הָרִאשֹׁנִ֖ים\rb* \rb to end|וְהָאֲחֲרֹנִ֑ים\rb*, \rb they are recorded|כָּתַ֛ב\rb* \rb by the prophet|הַנָּבִֽיא׃\rb* \rb Isaiah|יְשַֽׁעְיָ֥הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Amoz|אָמ֖וֹץ\rb*. \v 23 \rb And Uzziah|עֻזִּיָּ֜הוּ\rb* \rb rested|וַיִּשְׁכַּ֨ב\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb his fathers|אֲבֹתָ֗יו\rb* \rb and was buried|וַיִּקְבְּר֨וּ\rb*\rb |אֹת֤וֹ\rb* \rb near|עִם־\rb* \rb them|אֲבֹתָיו֙\rb*\f + \fr 26:23 \ft Literally \fqa with his fathers\f* \rb in a field|בִּשְׂדֵ֤ה\rb* \rb of burial|הַקְּבוּרָה֙\rb* \rb that belonged|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb to the kings|לַמְּלָכִ֔ים\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the people said|אָמְר֖וּ\rb*, “\rb He was|ה֑וּא\rb* \rb a leper|מְצוֹרָ֣ע\rb*.” \rb And his son|בְּנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Jotham|יוֹתָ֥ם\rb* \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֛ךְ\rb* \rb in his place|תַּחְתָּֽיו׃פ\rb*.
\c 27
\s1 Jotham Reigns in Judah
\r (2 Kings 15:32–38)
\p \v 1 \rb Jotham|יוֹתָ֣ם\rb* \rb was twenty-five|עֶשְׂרִ֨ים\rb*\rb |וְחָמֵ֤שׁ\rb* \rb years old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָה֙\rb* \rb when he became king|בְּמָלְכ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and he reigned|מָלַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּֽירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb sixteen|וְשֵׁשׁ־\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֣ה\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb*. \rb His mother’s|אִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb name|וְשֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb was Jerushah|יְרוּשָׁ֖ה\rb*\f + \fr 27:1 \fqa Jerushah \ft is a variant of \fqa Jerusha\ft ; see 2 Kings 15:33.\f* \rb daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Zadok|צָדֽוֹק׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb And he did|וַיַּ֨עַשׂ\rb* \rb what was right|הַיָּשָׁ֜ר\rb* \rb in the eyes|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*, \rb just as|כְּכֹ֤ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֔יו\rb* \rb Uzziah|עֻזִּיָּ֣הוּ\rb*\f + \fr 27:2 \fqa Uzziah \ft is also called \fqa Azariah\ft ; see 2 Kings 14:21.\f* \rb had done|עָשָׂה֙\rb*. \rb In addition|רַ֕ק\rb*, \rb he did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb enter|בָ֖א\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the temple|הֵיכַ֣ל\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*. \rb But the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb still|וְע֥וֹד\rb* \rb behaved corruptly|מַשְׁחִיתִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb Jotham|ה֗וּא\rb* \rb rebuilt|בָּנָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Upper|הָעֶלְי֑וֹן\rb* \rb Gate|שַׁ֥עַר\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb and he worked|בָּנָ֖ה\rb* \rb extensively|לָרֹֽב׃\rb* \rb on the wall|וּבְחוֹמַ֥ת\rb* \rb at the hill of Ophel|הָעֹ֛פֶל\rb*. \v 4 \rb He also built|בָּנָ֖ה\rb* \rb cities|וְעָרִ֥ים\rb* \rb in the hill country|בְּהַר־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb and fortresses|בִּֽירָנִיּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb and towers|וּמִגְדָּלִֽים׃\rb* \rb in the forests|וּבֶחֳרָשִׁ֣ים\rb*\rb |בָּנָ֔ה\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb Jotham|וְ֠הוּא\rb* \rb waged war|נִלְחַ֞ם\rb* \rb against|עִם־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of the Ammonites|בְּנֵי־\rb*\rb |עַמּוֹן֮\rb* \rb and defeated them|וַיֶּחֱזַ֣ק\rb*,\rb |עֲלֵיהֶם֒\rb* \rb and that|הַהִ֗יא\rb* \rb year|בַּשָּׁנָ֣ה\rb* \rb they|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |עַמּ֜וֹן\rb* \rb gave|וַיִּתְּנוּ־\rb* \rb him|ל֨וֹ\rb* \rb a hundred|מֵאָה֙\rb* \rb talents|כִּכַּר־\rb* \rb of silver|כֶּ֔סֶף\rb*,\f + \fr 27:5 \fqa 100 talents \ft is approximately 3.77 tons or 3.42 metric tons of silver.\f* \rb ten|וַעֲשֶׂ֨רֶת\rb* \rb thousand|אֲלָפִ֤ים\rb* \rb cors|כֹּרִים֙\rb* \rb of wheat|חִטִּ֔ים\rb*,\f + \fr 27:5 \fqa 10,000 cors \ft is approximately 62,400 bushels or 2.2 million liters (probably about 1,920 tons or 1,740 metric tons of wheat).\f* \rb and ten|עֲשֶׂ֣רֶת\rb* \rb thousand cors|אֲלָפִ֑ים\rb* \rb of barley|וּשְׂעוֹרִ֖ים\rb*.\f + \fr 27:5 \fqa 10,000 cors \ft is approximately 62,400 bushels or 2.2 million liters (probably about 1,450 tons or 1,315 metric tons of barley).\f* \rb They|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |עַמּ֔וֹןס\rb* \rb paid|הֵשִׁ֤יבוּ\rb* \rb him|לוֹ֙\rb* \rb the same|זֹ֗את\rb* \rb in the second|הַשֵּׁנִ֖ית\rb* \rb and third|וְהַשְּׁלִשִֽׁית׃\rb* \rb years|וּבַשָּׁנָ֥ה\rb*. \v 6 \rb So Jotham|יוֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb grew powerful|וַיִּתְחַזֵּ֖ק\rb* \rb because|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb he ordered|הֵכִ֣ין\rb* \rb his ways|דְּרָכָ֔יו\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb his God|אֱלֹהָֽיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb As for the rest|וְיֶתֶר֙\rb* \rb of the acts|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Jotham|יוֹתָ֔ם\rb*, \rb along with all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his wars|מִלְחֲמֹתָ֖יו\rb* \rb and his ways|וּדְרָכָ֑יו\rb*, \rb they are indeed|הִנָּ֣ם\rb* \rb written|כְּתוּבִ֔ים\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the Book|סֵ֥פֶר\rb* \rb of the Kings|מַלְכֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb and Judah|וִיהוּדָֽה׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb He was|הָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb twenty-five|עֶשְׂרִ֧ים\rb*\rb |וְחָמֵ֛שׁ\rb* \rb years old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֖ה\rb* \rb when he became king|בְמָלְכ֑וֹ\rb*, \rb and he reigned|מָלַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb* \rb sixteen|וְשֵׁשׁ־\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֣ה\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb*. \v 9 \rb And Jotham|יוֹתָם֙\rb* \rb rested|וַיִּשְׁכַּ֤ב\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb his fathers|אֲבֹתָ֔יו\rb* \rb and was buried|וַיִּקְבְּר֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb in the City|בְּעִ֣יר\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֑יד\rb*. \rb And his son|בְּנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Ahaz|אָחָ֥ז\rb* \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֛ךְ\rb* \rb in his place|תַּחְתָּֽיו׃פ\rb*.
\c 28
\s1 Ahaz Reigns in Judah
\r (2 Kings 16:1–9)
\p \v 1 \rb Ahaz|אָחָ֣ז\rb* \rb was twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֤ים\rb* \rb years old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָה֙\rb* \rb when he became king|בְּמָלְכ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and he reigned|מָלַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb sixteen|וְשֵׁשׁ־\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֣ה\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb*. \rb And unlike David|כְּדָוִ֥יד\rb* \rb his father|אָבִֽיו׃\rb*, \rb he did not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb do|עָשָׂ֧ה\rb* \rb what was right|הַיָּשָׁ֛ר\rb* \rb in the eyes|בְּעֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*. \v 2 \rb Instead, he walked|וַיֵּ֕לֶךְ\rb* \rb in the ways|בְּדַרְכֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the kings|מַלְכֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb and even|וְגַ֧ם\rb* \rb made|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb* \rb cast images|מַסֵּכ֛וֹת\rb* \rb of the Baals|לַבְּעָלִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb Moreover, Ahaz|וְה֥וּא\rb* \rb burned incense|הִקְטִ֖יר\rb* \rb in the Valley|בְּגֵ֣יא\rb*\rb |בֶן־\rb* \rb of Ben-hinnom|הִנֹּ֑ם\rb* \rb and sacrificed|וַיַּבְעֵ֤ר\rb* \rb his sons|בָּנָיו֙\rb* \rb in the fire|בָּאֵ֔שׁ\rb*,\f + \fr 28:3 \ft Literally \fqa passed his sons through the fire\f* \rb according to the abominations|כְּתֹֽעֲבוֹת֙\rb* \rb of the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֔ם\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb had driven out|הֹרִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb before|מִפְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb And he sacrificed|וַיְזַבֵּ֧חַ\rb* \rb and burned incense|וַיְקַטֵּ֛ר\rb* \rb on the high places|בַּבָּמ֖וֹת\rb*, \rb on|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the hills|הַגְּבָע֑וֹת\rb*, \rb and under|וְתַ֖חַת\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb green|רַעֲנָֽן׃\rb* \rb tree|עֵ֥ץ\rb*.
\s1 Aram Defeats Judah
\r (Isaiah 1:1–9)
\p \v 5 \rb So the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb his God|אֱלֹהָיו֮\rb* \rb delivered Ahaz|וַֽיִּתְּנֵ֜הוּ\rb* \rb into the hand|בְּיַ֣ד\rb* \rb of the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Aram|אֲרָם֒\rb*, \rb who attacked|וַיַּ֨כּוּ־\rb* \rb him|ב֔וֹ\rb* \rb and took|וַיִּשְׁבּ֤וּ\rb*\rb |מִמֶּ֙נּוּ֙\rb* \rb many|גְדוֹלָ֔ה\rb*\rb |וַיָּבִ֖יאוּ\rb* \rb captives|שִׁבְיָ֣ה\rb* \rb to Damascus|דַּרְמָ֑שֶׂק\rb*.
\p \rb Ahaz was also|וְ֠גַם\rb* \rb delivered|נִתָּ֔ן\rb* \rb into the hand|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb of the king|מֶ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*, \rb who struck|וַיַּךְ־\rb* \rb him|בּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb with great|גְדוֹלָֽה׃ס\rb* \rb force|מַכָּ֥ה\rb*. \v 6 \rb For in one|אֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb day|בְּי֥וֹם\rb* \rb Pekah|פֶּ֨קַח\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Remaliah|רְמַלְיָ֜הוּ\rb* \rb killed|וַיַּהֲרֹג֩\rb* \rb 120,000|מֵאָ֨ה\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֶ֛לֶף\rb*\rb |הַכֹּ֣ל\rb* \rb valiant|חָ֑יִל\rb* \rb men|בְּנֵי־\rb* \rb in Judah|בִּֽיהוּדָ֗ה\rb*. \rb This happened because they had forsaken|בְּעָזְבָ֕ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of their fathers|אֲבוֹתָֽם׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb Zichri|זִכְרִ֣י׀\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb a mighty man|גִּבּ֣וֹר\rb* \rb of Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֗יִם\rb*, \rb killed|וַֽיַּהֲרֹ֞ג\rb* \rb Maaseiah|מַעֲשֵׂיָ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Azrikam|עַזְרִיקָ֖ם\rb* \rb the governor|נְגִ֣יד\rb* \rb of the palace|הַבָּ֑יִת\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Elkanah|אֶלְקָנָ֖ה\rb* \rb the second|מִשְׁנֵ֥ה\rb* \rb to the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃ס\rb*. \v 8 \rb Then the Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֨ל\rb* \rb took 200,000|מָאתַ֣יִם\rb*\rb |אֶ֗לֶף\rb* \rb captives|וַיִּשְׁבּוּ֩\rb* \rb from their kinsmen|מֵֽאֲחֵיהֶ֜ם\rb*— \rb women|נָשִׁים֙\rb*, \rb sons|בָּנִ֣ים\rb*, \rb and daughters|וּבָנ֔וֹת\rb*. \rb They also|וְגַם־\rb* \rb carried off|בָּזְז֣וּ\rb*\rb |מֵהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb a great deal of|רָ֖ב\rb* \rb plunder|שָׁלָ֥ל\rb* \rb and brought|וַיָּבִ֥יאוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb it|הַשָּׁלָ֖ל\rb* \rb to Samaria|לְשֹׁמְרֽוֹן׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb But a prophet|נָבִ֥יא\rb* \rb of the LORD|לַֽיהוָה֮\rb* \rb named|שְׁמוֹ֒\rb* \rb Oded|עֹדֵ֣ד\rb* \rb was|הָיָ֨ה\rb* \rb there|וְ֠שָׁם\rb*, \rb and he went out|וַיֵּצֵ֗א\rb* \rb to meet|לִפְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb the army|הַצָּבָא֙\rb* \rb that returned|הַבָּ֣א\rb* \rb to Samaria|לְשֹׁמְר֔וֹן\rb*. “\rb Look|הִ֠נֵּה\rb*,” \rb he said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶ֗ם\rb*, “\rb because of His wrath|בַּחֲמַ֨ת\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵֽי־\rb* \rb of your fathers|אֲבוֹתֵיכֶ֛ם\rb*, \rb has delivered them|נְתָנָ֣ם\rb* \rb into your hand|בְּיֶדְכֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb But you have slaughtered|וַתַּֽהַרְגוּ־\rb* \rb them|בָ֣ם\rb* \rb in a rage|בְזַ֔עַף\rb* \rb that reaches up|הִגִּֽיעַ׃\rb* \rb to heaven|לַשָּׁמַ֖יִם\rb*. \v 10 \rb And now|וְ֠עַתָּה\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb intend|אֹמְרִ֔ים\rb* \rb to reduce to slavery|לִכְבֹּ֛שׁ\rb* \rb the men|לַעֲבָדִ֥ים\rb* \rb and women|וְלִשְׁפָח֖וֹת\rb*\rb |בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֤ה\rb* \rb and Jerusalem|וִֽירוּשָׁלִַ֙ם֙\rb*. \rb But are you|אַתֶּם֙\rb*\rb |עִמָּכֶ֣ם\rb* \rb not|הֲלֹ֤א\rb* \rb also|רַק־\rb* \rb guilty|אֲשָׁמ֔וֹת\rb* \rb before the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*? \v 11 \rb Now therefore|וְעַתָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb listen to me|שְׁמָע֔וּנִי\rb* \rb and return|וְהָשִׁ֙יבוּ֙\rb* \rb the captives|הַשִּׁבְיָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you took|שְׁבִיתֶ֖ם\rb* \rb from your kinsmen|מֵאֲחֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb the fierce anger|חֲר֥וֹן\rb*\rb |אַף־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb is upon you|עֲלֵיכֶֽם׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 12 \rb Then some|אֲנָשִׁ֜ים\rb* \rb of the leaders|מֵרָאשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb of the Ephraimites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |אֶפְרַ֗יִם\rb*\f + \fr 28:12 \ft That is, the leaders of the northern kingdom of Israel\f*— \rb Azariah|עֲזַרְיָ֤הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Jehohanan|יְהֽוֹחָנָן֙\rb*, \rb Berechiah|בֶּרֶכְיָ֣הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Meshillemoth|מְשִׁלֵּמ֔וֹת\rb*,\f + \fr 28:12 \fqa Meshillemoth \ft is a variant of \fqa Meshillemith\ft ; see 1 Chronicles 9:12.\f* \rb Jehizkiah|וִֽיחִזְקִיָּ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Shallum|שַׁלֻּ֔ם\rb*, \rb and Amasa|וַעֲמָשָׂ֖א\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Hadlai|חַדְלָ֑י\rb*— \rb stood|וַיָּקֻ֨מוּ\rb* \rb in opposition to|עַל־\rb* \rb those arriving|הַבָּאִ֖ים\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the war|הַצָּבָֽא׃\rb*. \v 13 “\rb You must not|לֹא־\rb* \rb bring|תָבִ֤יאוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the captives|הַשִּׁבְיָה֙\rb* \rb here|הֵ֔נָּה\rb*,” \rb they said|וַיֹּאמְר֣וּ\rb*, “\rb for|כִּי֩\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb are proposing|אֹמְרִ֔ים\rb* \rb to bring guilt|לְאַשְׁמַ֨ת\rb* \rb upon us|עָלֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb* \rb from the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb and to add|לְהֹסִ֥יף\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb our sins|חַטֹּאתֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb and|וְעַל־\rb* \rb our guilt|אַשְׁמָתֵ֑ינוּ\rb*. \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb our|לָ֔נוּ\rb* \rb guilt|אַשְׁמָה֙\rb* \rb is great|רַבָּ֤ה\rb*, \rb and fierce anger|וַחֲר֥וֹן\rb*\rb |אָ֖ף\rb* \rb is upon|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 14 \rb So the armed men|הֶֽחָל֗וּץ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb left|וַיַּעֲזֹ֣ב\rb* \rb the captives|הַשִּׁבְיָה֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the plunder|הַבִּזָּ֔ה\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the leaders|הַשָּׂרִ֖ים\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the assembly|הַקָּהָֽל׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb Then the men|הָאֲנָשִׁים֩\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb were designated|נִקְּב֨וּ\rb* \rb by name|בְשֵׁמ֜וֹת\rb* \rb arose|וַיָּקֻ֣מוּ\rb*, \rb took charge|וַיַּחֲזִ֣יקוּ\rb* \rb of the captives|בַשִּׁבְיָ֗ה\rb*,\rb |וְכָֽל־\rb* \rb and provided from|מִן־\rb* \rb the plunder|הַשָּׁלָל֒\rb* \rb clothing|הִלְבִּ֣ישׁוּ\rb* \rb for the naked|מַעֲרֻמֵּיהֶם֮\rb*. \rb They clothed them|וַיַּלְבִּשׁ֣וּם\rb*, \rb gave them sandals|וַ֠יַּנְעִלוּם\rb* \rb and food|וַיַּאֲכִל֨וּם\rb* \rb and drink|וַיַּשְׁק֜וּם\rb*, \rb anointed their wounds|וַיְסֻכ֗וּם\rb*, \rb and put|וַיְנַהֲל֤וּם\rb* \rb all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the feeble|כּוֹשֵׁ֔ל\rb* \rb on donkeys|בַּחֲמֹרִים֙\rb*. \rb So they brought them|וַיְבִיא֛וּם\rb* \rb to Jericho|יְרֵח֥וֹ\rb*, \rb the City|עִיר־\rb* \rb of Palms|הַתְּמָרִ֖ים\rb*, \rb to|אֵ֣צֶל\rb* \rb their brothers|אֲחֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb Then they returned|וַיָּשׁ֖וּבוּ\rb* \rb to Samaria|שֹׁמְרֽוֹן׃פ\rb*.
\s1 The Idolatry of Ahaz
\r (2 Kings 16:10–20)
\p \v 16 \rb At that|הַהִ֗יא\rb* \rb time|בָּעֵ֣ת\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֧לֶךְ\rb* \rb Ahaz|אָחָ֛ז\rb* \rb sent|שָׁלַ֞ח\rb* \rb for help|לַעְזֹ֥ר\rb* \rb from|עַל־\rb* \rb the king|מַלְכֵ֥י\rb*\f + \fr 28:16 \ft LXX, Syriac, and Vulgate (see also 2 Kings 16:7); Hebrew \fqa kings\f* \rb of Assyria|אַשּׁ֖וּר\rb*. \v 17 \rb The Edomites|אֲדוֹמִ֖ים\rb* \rb had again|וְע֥וֹד\rb* \rb come|בָּ֑אוּ\rb* \rb and attacked|וַיַּכּ֥וּ\rb* \rb Judah|בִיהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb and carried away|וַיִּשְׁבּוּ־\rb* \rb captives|שֶֽׁבִי׃\rb*. \v 18 \rb The Philistines|וּפְלִשְׁתִּ֣ים\rb* \rb had also raided|פָּשְׁט֗וּ\rb* \rb the cities|בְּעָרֵ֨י\rb* \rb of the foothills|הַשְּׁפֵלָ֣ה\rb*\f + \fr 28:18 \ft Hebrew \fqa Shephelah \ft or \fqa lowlands\ft ; that is, the western foothills of Judea\f* \rb and the Negev|וְהַנֶּגֶב֮\rb* \rb of Judah|לִֽיהוּדָה֒\rb*, \rb capturing|וַֽ֠יִּלְכְּדוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and occupying|וַיֵּשְׁב֖וּ\rb*\rb |שָֽׁם׃\rb*\rb |בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb Beth-shemesh|שֶׁ֨מֶשׁ\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Aijalon|אַיָּל֜וֹן\rb*, \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Gederoth|הַגְּדֵר֗וֹת\rb*, \rb as well as|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Soco|שׂוֹכ֤וֹ\rb*\rb |וּבְנוֹתֶ֙יהָ֙\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Timnah|תִּמְנָ֣ה\rb*\rb |וּבְנוֹתֶ֔יהָ\rb*, \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Gimzo|גִּמְז֖וֹ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb with their villages|בְּנֹתֶ֑יהָ\rb*. \v 19 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb humbled|הִכְנִ֤יעַ\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb because|בַּעֲב֖וּר\rb* \rb Ahaz|אָחָ֣ז\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*\f + \fr 28:19 \ft That is, Judah; in 2 Chronicles, Judah is occasionally called Israel, as representative of the true Israel.\f*\rb |כִּ֤י\rb* \rb had thrown off restraint|הִפְרִ֙יעַ֙\rb* \rb in Judah|בִּֽיהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb and had been most unfaithful|וּמָע֥וֹל\rb*\rb |מַ֖עַל\rb* \rb to the LORD|בַּיהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb |תִּלְּגַ֥ת\rb* \rb Then Tiglath-pileser|פִּלְנְאֶ֖סֶר\rb*\f + \fr 28:20 \ft Hebrew \fqa Tilgath-pilneser\ft , a variant spelling of \fqa Tiglath-pileser\f* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Assyria|אַשּׁ֑וּר\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֣א\rb* \rb to Ahaz|עָלָ֔יו\rb* \rb but afflicted|וַיָּ֥צַר\rb* \rb him|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb rather than|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb strengthening him|חֲזָקֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb Although|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb Ahaz|אָחָז֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had taken a portion|חָלַ֤ק\rb* \rb from the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb from|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the royal|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb palace|בֵּ֥ית\rb*, \rb and from the princes|וְהַשָּׂרִ֑ים\rb* \rb and had presented|וַיִּתֵּן֙\rb* \rb it to the king|לְמֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Assyria|אַשּׁ֔וּר\rb*, \rb it did not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb help|לְעֶזְרָ֖ה\rb* \rb him|לֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb In the time|וּבְעֵת֙\rb* \rb of his distress|הָצֵ֣ר\rb*, \rb King|הַמֶּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb Ahaz|אָחָֽז׃\rb*\rb |ה֖וּא\rb* \rb became even more|וַיּ֖וֹסֶף\rb* \rb unfaithful|לִמְע֣וֹל\rb* \rb to the LORD|בַּיהוָ֑ה\rb*. \v 23 \rb He sacrificed|וַיִּזְבַּ֗ח\rb* \rb to the gods|לֵֽאלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Damascus|דַרְמֶשֶׂק֮\rb*, \rb who had defeated|הַמַּכִּ֣ים\rb* \rb him|בּוֹ֒\rb*, \rb and he said|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Because|כִּ֠י\rb* \rb the gods|אֱלֹהֵ֤י\rb* \rb of the kings|מַלְכֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Aram|אֲרָם֙\rb* \rb have helped|מַעְזְרִ֣ים\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָ֔ם\rb*, \rb I will sacrifice|אֲזַבֵּ֖חַ\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶ֥ם\rb* \rb that they may help me|וְיַעְזְר֑וּנִי\rb*.” \rb But these gods|וְהֵ֛ם\rb* \rb were|הָֽיוּ־\rb* \rb the downfall|לְהַכְשִׁיל֖וֹ\rb* \rb of Ahaz|ל֥וֹ\rb* \rb and of all|וּלְכָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.
\p \v 24 \rb Then Ahaz|אָחָ֜ז\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb gathered up|וַיֶּאֱסֹ֨ף\rb* \rb the articles|כְּלֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the house|בֵית־\rb* \rb of God|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb*, \rb cut them|כְּלֵ֣י\rb*\rb |בֵית־\rb*\rb |הָֽאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb into pieces|וַיְקַצֵּץ֙\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb shut|וַיִּסְגֹּ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the doors|דַּלְת֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and set up|וַיַּ֨עַשׂ\rb* \rb altars|מִזְבְּח֛וֹת\rb* \rb of his own|ל֧וֹ\rb* \rb on every|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb street corner|פִּנָּ֖ה\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*. \v 25 \rb In every|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb city|עִ֨יר\rb*\rb |וָעִ֤יר\rb* \rb of Judah|לִֽיהוּדָה֙\rb* \rb he built|עָשָׂ֣ה\rb* \rb high places|בָמ֔וֹת\rb* \rb to offer incense|לְקַטֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb to other|אֲחֵרִ֑ים\rb* \rb gods|לֵֽאלֹהִ֣ים\rb*, \rb and so he provoked|וַיַּכְעֵ֕ס\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of his fathers|אֲבֹתָֽיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 26 \rb As for the rest|וְיֶ֤תֶר\rb* \rb of the acts of Ahaz|דְּבָרָיו֙\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his ways|דְּרָכָ֔יו\rb*, \rb from beginning|הָרִאשֹׁנִ֖ים\rb* \rb to end|וְהָאַחֲרוֹנִ֑ים\rb*, \rb they are indeed|הִנָּ֣ם\rb* \rb written|כְּתוּבִ֔ים\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the Book|סֵ֥פֶר\rb* \rb of the Kings|מַלְכֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb and Israel|וְיִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 27 \rb And Ahaz|אָחָ֜ז\rb* \rb rested|וַיִּשְׁכַּ֨ב\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb his fathers|אֲבֹתָ֗יו\rb* \rb and was buried|וַֽיִּקְבְּרֻ֤הוּ\rb* \rb in the city|בָעִיר֙\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|בִּיר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb*, \rb but|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb he was not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb placed|הֱבִיאֻ֔הוּ\rb* \rb in the tombs|לְקִבְרֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the kings|מַלְכֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*. \rb And his son|בְנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Hezekiah|יְחִזְקִיָּ֥הֽוּ\rb* \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֛ךְ\rb* \rb in his place|תַּחְתָּֽיו׃פ\rb*.
\c 29
\s1 Hezekiah Cleanses the Temple
\r (2 Kings 18:1–12)
\p \v 1 \rb Hezekiah|יְחִזְקִיָּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb was twenty-five|עֶשְׂרִ֤ים\rb*\rb |וְחָמֵשׁ֙\rb* \rb years old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֔ה\rb* \rb when he became king|מָלַ֗ךְ\rb*, \rb and he reigned|מָלַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb twenty-nine|וְעֶשְׂרִ֤ים\rb*\rb |וָתֵ֙שַׁע֙\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb*. \rb His mother’s|אִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb name|וְשֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb was Abijah|אֲבִיָּ֖ה\rb*,\f + \fr 29:1 \fqa Abijah \ft is a variant of \fqa Abi\ft ; see 2 Kings 18:2.\f* \rb the daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Zechariah|זְכַרְיָֽהוּ׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb And he did|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb what was right|הַיָּשָׁ֖ר\rb* \rb in the eyes|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb just as|כְּכֹ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb his father|אָבִֽיו׃\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֥יד\rb* \rb had done|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb |ה֣וּא\rb* \rb In the first|הָרִאשׁ֗וֹן\rb* \rb month|בַּחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of the first|הָרִאשׁוֹנָ֨ה\rb* \rb year|בַשָּׁנָה֩\rb* \rb of his reign|לְמָלְכ֜וֹ\rb*, \rb Hezekiah opened|פָּתַ֛ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and repaired|וַֽיְחַזְּקֵֽם׃\rb* \rb the doors|דַּלְת֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*. \v 4 \rb Then he brought in|וַיָּבֵ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֖ים\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֑ם\rb* \rb and gathered them|וַיַּֽאַסְפֵ֖ם\rb* \rb in the square|לִרְח֥וֹב\rb* \rb on the east side|הַמִּזְרָֽח׃\rb*.
\p \v 5 “\rb Listen to me|שְׁמָע֣וּנִי\rb*, \rb O Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֑ם\rb*,” \rb he said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*. “\rb Consecrate|הִֽתְקַדְּשׁ֗וּ\rb* \rb yourselves now|עַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb and consecrate|וְקַדְּשׁוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֤ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of your fathers|אֲבֹתֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*. \rb Remove|וְהוֹצִ֥יאוּ\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the Holy Place|הַקֹּֽדֶשׁ׃\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb every impurity|הַנִּדָּ֖ה\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb our fathers|אֲבֹתֵ֗ינוּ\rb* \rb were unfaithful|מָעֲל֣וּ\rb* \rb and did|וְעָשׂ֥וּ\rb* \rb evil|הָרַ֛ע\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה־\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֖ינוּ\rb*. \rb They abandoned Him|וַיַּֽעַזְבֻ֑הוּ\rb*, \rb turned their faces|פְנֵיהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb away|וַיַּסֵּ֧בּוּ\rb* \rb from the dwelling place|מִמִּשְׁכַּ֥ן\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb and turned|וַיִּתְּנוּ־\rb* \rb their backs on Him|עֹֽרֶף׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb They also|גַּ֣ם\rb* \rb shut|סָֽגְר֞וּ\rb* \rb the doors|דַּלְת֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the portico|הָאוּלָ֗ם\rb* \rb and extinguished|וַיְכַבּוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the lamps|הַנֵּר֔וֹת\rb*. \rb They did not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb burn|הִקְטִ֑ירוּ\rb* \rb incense|וּקְטֹ֖רֶת\rb* \rb or|לֹא־\rb* \rb present|הֶעֱל֣וּ\rb* \rb burnt offerings|וְעֹלָה֙\rb* \rb in the Holy Place|בַקֹּ֔דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of the God|לֵאלֹהֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb Therefore, the wrath|קֶ֣צֶף\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb has fallen|וַיְהִי֙\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb and Jerusalem|וִירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb*, \rb and He has made them|וַיִּתְּנֵ֤ם\rb* \rb an object of terror|לִזְוָעָה\rb*, \rb horror|לְשַׁמָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb and scorn|וְלִשְׁרֵקָ֔ה\rb*, \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb can see|רֹאִ֖ים\rb* \rb with your own eyes|בְּעֵינֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb For behold|וְהִנֵּ֛ה\rb*, \rb this|זֹֽאת׃\rb* \rb is why|עַל־\rb* \rb our fathers|אֲבוֹתֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb have fallen|נָפְל֥וּ\rb* \rb by the sword|בֶּחָ֑רֶב\rb*, \rb and our sons|וּבָנֵ֨ינוּ\rb* \rb and daughters|וּבְנוֹתֵ֧ינוּ\rb* \rb and wives|וְנָשֵׁ֛ינוּ\rb* \rb are in captivity|בַּשְּׁבִ֖י\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb Now|עַתָּה֙\rb* \rb it is in|עִם־\rb* \rb my heart|לְבָבִ֔י\rb* \rb to make|לִכְר֣וֹת\rb* \rb a covenant|בְּרִ֔ית\rb* \rb with the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb so that His fierce anger|חֲר֥וֹן\rb*\rb |אַפּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb will turn away|וְיָשֹׁ֥ב\rb* \rb from us|מִמֶּ֖נּוּ\rb*. \v 11 \rb Now|עַתָּ֖ה\rb*, \rb my sons|בָּנַ֕י\rb*, \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be negligent|תִּשָּׁל֑וּ\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb has chosen|בָּחַ֣ר\rb* \rb you|בָכֶ֞ם\rb* \rb to stand|לַעֲמֹ֤ד\rb* \rb before Him|לְפָנָיו֙\rb*, \rb to serve Him|לְשָׁ֣רְת֔וֹ\rb*, \rb to|וְלִהְי֥וֹת\rb* \rb minister|מְשָׁרְתִ֥ים\rb* \rb before Him|ל֖וֹ\rb*, \rb and to burn incense|וּמַקְטִרִֽים׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 12 \rb Then the Levites|הַ֠לְוִיִּם\rb* \rb set to work|וַיָּקֻ֣מוּ\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \rb Mahath|מַ֣חַת\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Amasai|עֲמָשַׂ֞י\rb* \rb and Joel|וְיוֹאֵ֣ל\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Azariah|עֲזַרְיָהוּ֮\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the Kohathites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |הַקְּהָתִי֒\rb*;
\li1 \rb Kish|קִ֚ישׁ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Abdi|עַבְדִּ֔י\rb* \rb and Azariah|וַעֲזַרְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jehallelel|יְהַלֶּלְאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb from the Merarites|מְרָרִ֔י\rb*;
\li1 \rb Joah|יוֹאָח֙\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Zimmah|זִמָּ֔ה\rb* \rb and Eden|וְעֵ֖דֶן\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Joah|יוֹאָֽח׃\rb* \rb from|וּמִן־\rb* \rb the Gershonites|הַגֵּ֣רְשֻׁנִּ֔י\rb*;
\li1 \v 13 \rb Shimri|שִׁמְרִ֖י\rb* \rb and Jeuel|וִיעוּאֵל\rb* \rb from|וּמִן־\rb* \rb the Elizaphanites|בְּנֵי֙\rb*\rb |אֱלִ֣יצָפָ֔ן\rb*;
\li1 \rb Zechariah|זְכַרְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb and Mattaniah|וּמַתַּנְיָֽהוּ׃ס\rb* \rb from|וּמִן־\rb* \rb the Asaphites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |אָסָ֔ף\rb*;
\li1 \v 14 \rb Jehiel|יְחוּאֵל\rb* \rb and Shimei|וְשִׁמְעִ֑יס\rb* \rb from|וּמִן־\rb* \rb the Hemanites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |הֵימָ֖ן\rb*;
\li1 \rb and Shemaiah|שְׁמַֽעְיָ֖ה\rb* \rb and Uzziel|וְעֻזִּיאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb from|וּמִן־\rb* \rb the Jeduthunites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יְדוּת֔וּן\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb When they had assembled|וַיַּֽאַסְפ֤וּ\rb* \rb their brothers|אֲחֵיהֶם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and consecrated themselves|וַיִּֽתְקַדְּשׁ֔וּ\rb*, \rb they went in|וַיָּבֹ֥אוּ\rb* \rb to cleanse|לְטַהֵ֖ר\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*, \rb according to the command|כְמִצְוַת־\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb by the words|בְּדִבְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb So the priests|הַ֠כֹּהֲנִים\rb* \rb went|וַיָּבֹ֣אוּ\rb* \rb inside|לִפְנִ֣ימָה\rb* \rb the house|בֵית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֮\rb* \rb to cleanse it|לְטַהֵר֒\rb*, \rb and they brought out|וַיּוֹצִ֗יאוּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֤ת\rb* \rb to the courtyard|לַחֲצַ֖ר\rb*\rb |יְהוָ֑ה\rb*\rb |בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the unclean things|הַטֻּמְאָה֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb they found|מָֽצְאוּ֙\rb* \rb in the temple|בְּהֵיכַ֣ל\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*. \rb Then the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb* \rb took these things|וַֽיְקַבְּלוּ֙\rb* \rb and carried them|לְהוֹצִ֥יא\rb* \rb out|חֽוּצָה׃\rb* \rb to the Kidron|קִדְר֖וֹן\rb* \rb Valley|לְנַֽחַל־\rb*. \v 17 \rb They began|וַ֠יָּחֵלּוּ\rb* \rb the consecration|לְקַדֵּשׁ֒\rb* \rb on the first|בְּאֶחָ֞ד\rb* \rb day of the first|הָרִאשׁוֹן֮\rb* \rb month|לַחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb and on the eighth|שְׁמוֹנָ֣ה\rb* \rb day|וּבְי֧וֹם\rb* \rb of the month|לַחֹ֗דֶשׁ\rb* \rb they reached|בָּ֚אוּ\rb* \rb the portico|לְאוּלָ֣ם\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*. \rb For eight more|שְׁמוֹנָ֑ה\rb* \rb days|לְיָמִ֣ים\rb* \rb they consecrated|וַיְקַדְּשׁ֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of the LORD itself|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb finishing|כִּלּֽוּ׃ס\rb* \rb on the sixteenth|שִׁשָּׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֛ר\rb* \rb day|וּבְי֨וֹם\rb* \rb of the first|הָרִאשׁ֖וֹן\rb* \rb month|לַחֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb Then they went|וַיָּב֤וֹאוּ\rb* \rb in|פְנִ֙ימָה֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb and reported|וַיֹּ֣אמְר֔וּ\rb*, “\rb We have cleansed|טִהַ֖רְנוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the entire|כָּל־\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the altar|מִזְבַּ֤ח\rb* \rb of burnt offering|הָעוֹלָה֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb with all|כָּל־\rb* \rb its utensils|כֵּלָ֔יו\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the table|שֻׁלְחַ֥ן\rb* \rb of the showbread|הַֽמַּעֲרֶ֖כֶת\rb* \rb with|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb its utensils|כֵּלָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb Moreover|וְאֵ֣ת\rb*, \rb we have prepared|הֵכַ֣נּוּ\rb* \rb and consecrated|וְהִקְדָּ֑שְׁנוּ\rb*\rb |וְהִנָּ֕ם\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the articles|הַכֵּלִ֗ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb Ahaz|אָחָ֧ז\rb* \rb in his unfaithfulness|בְּמַעֲל֖וֹ\rb* \rb cast aside|הִזְנִיחַ֩\rb* \rb during his reign|בְּמַלְכוּת֛וֹ\rb*. \rb They are now in front|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the altar|מִזְבַּ֥ח\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*.”
\s1 Hezekiah Restores Temple Worship
\p \v 20 \rb Early the next morning|וַיַּשְׁכֵּם֙\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb Hezekiah|יְחִזְקִיָּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb gathered|וַיֶּאֱסֹ֕ף\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֑יר\rb* \rb officials|שָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb and went|וַיַּ֖עַל\rb* \rb up to the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb They brought|וַיָּבִ֣יאוּ\rb* \rb seven|שִׁבְעָה֩\rb* \rb bulls|פָרִים־\rb*, \rb seven|שִׁבְעָ֜ה\rb* \rb rams|וְאֵילִ֨ים\rb*, \rb seven|שִׁבְעָ֗ה\rb* \rb lambs|וּכְבָשִׂ֣ים\rb*, \rb and seven|שִׁבְעָה֙\rb* \rb male goats|וּצְפִירֵ֨י\rb*\rb |עִזִּ֤ים\rb* \rb as a sin offering|לְחַטָּ֔את\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb the kingdom|הַמַּמְלָכָ֥ה\rb*, \rb for|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the sanctuary|הַמִּקְדָּ֖שׁ\rb*, \rb and for|וְעַל־\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb*. \rb And the king commanded|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb the priests|הַכֹּ֣הֲנִ֔ים\rb*, \rb the descendants|לִבְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Aaron|אַהֲרֹן֙\rb*, \rb to offer them|לְהַעֲל֖וֹת\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the altar|מִזְבַּ֥ח\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb So they slaughtered|וַֽיִּשְׁחֲטוּ֙\rb* \rb the bulls|הַבָּקָ֔ר\rb*, \rb and the priests|הַכֹּֽהֲנִים֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיְקַבְּל֤וּ\rb* \rb the blood|הַדָּ֔ם\rb* \rb and splattered|וַֽיִּזְרְק֖וּ\rb* \rb it on the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֑חָה\rb*. \rb They slaughtered|וַיִּשְׁחֲט֣וּ\rb* \rb the rams|הָאֵלִ֗ים\rb* \rb and splattered|וַיִּזְרְק֤וּ\rb* \rb the blood|הַדָּם֙\rb* \rb on the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֔חָה\rb*. \rb And they slaughtered|וַֽיִּשְׁחֲטוּ֙\rb* \rb the lambs|הַכְּבָשִׂ֔ים\rb* \rb and splattered|וַיִּזְרְק֥וּ\rb* \rb the blood|הַדָּ֖ם\rb* \rb on the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּֽחָה׃\rb*.
\p \v 23 \rb Then they brought|וַיַּגִּ֙ישׁוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the goats|שְׂעִירֵ֣י\rb* \rb for the sin offering|הַֽחַטָּ֔את\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb and the assembly|וְהַקָּהָ֑ל\rb*, \rb who laid|וַיִּסְמְכ֥וּ\rb* \rb their hands|יְדֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb on them|עֲלֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 24 \rb And the priests|הַכֹּ֣הֲנִ֔ים\rb* \rb slaughtered the goats|וַיִּשְׁחָטוּם֙\rb* \rb and put their blood|דָּמָם֙\rb* \rb on the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֔חָה\rb* \rb for a sin offering|וַֽיְחַטְּא֤וּ\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to make atonement|לְכַפֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb had ordered|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb the burnt offering|הָעוֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb and the sin offering|וְהַחַטָּֽאת׃\rb* \rb for all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*.
\p \v 25 \rb Hezekiah stationed|וַיַּֽעֲמֵ֨ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֜ם\rb* \rb in the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb with cymbals|בִּמְצִלְתַּ֙יִם֙\rb*, \rb harps|בִּנְבָלִ֣ים\rb*, \rb and lyres|וּבְכִנֹּר֔וֹת\rb* \rb according to the command|בְּמִצְוַ֥ת\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֛יד\rb*, \rb of Gad|וְגָ֥ד\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb seer|חֹזֵֽה־\rb*, \rb and of Nathan|וְנָתָ֣ן\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֑יא\rb*. \rb For|כִּ֧י\rb* \rb the command|הַמִּצְוָ֖ה\rb* \rb had come from|בְיַד־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb through|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb His prophets|נְבִיאָֽיו׃ס\rb*. \v 26 \rb The Levites|הַלְוִיִּם֙\rb* \rb stood|וַיַּֽעַמְד֤וּ\rb* \rb with the instruments|בִּכְלֵ֣י\rb* \rb of David|דָוִ֔יד\rb*, \rb and the priests|וְהַכֹּהֲנִ֖ים\rb* \rb with the trumpets|בַּחֲצֹצְרֽוֹת׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 27 \rb And Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֔הוּ\rb* \rb ordered|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb that the burnt offering|הָעֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb be sacrificed|לְהַעֲל֥וֹת\rb* \rb on the altar|לְהַמִּזְבֵּ֑חַ\rb*. \rb When|וּבְעֵ֞ת\rb* \rb the burnt offering|הָֽעוֹלָ֗ה\rb* \rb began|הֵחֵ֣ל\rb*, \rb the song|שִׁיר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb and the trumpets|וְהַחֲצֹ֣צְר֔וֹת\rb* \rb began as well|הֵחֵ֤ל\rb*, \rb accompanied by|וְעַ֨ל־\rb*\rb |יְדֵ֔י\rb* \rb the instruments|כְּלֵ֖י\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֥יד\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 28 \rb The whole|וְכָל־\rb* \rb assembly|הַקָּהָל֙\rb* \rb was worshiping|מִֽשְׁתַּחֲוִ֔ים\rb*, \rb the singers|וְהַשִּׁ֣יר\rb* \rb were singing|מְשׁוֹרֵ֔ר\rb*, \rb and the trumpeters|וְהַחֲצֹצְר֖וֹת\rb* \rb were playing|מַחֲצֹצְרִים\rb*. \rb All this|הַכֹּ֕ל\rb* \rb continued until|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb the burnt offering|הָעֹלָֽה׃\rb* \rb was completed|לִכְל֥וֹת\rb*.
\p \v 29 \rb When the offerings|לְהַעֲל֑וֹת\rb* \rb were completed|וּכְכַלּ֖וֹת\rb*, \rb the king|הַמֶּ֛לֶךְ\rb* \rb and all|וְכָֽל־\rb* \rb those present|הַנִּמְצְאִ֥ים\rb* \rb with him|אִתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb bowed down|כָּרְע֗וּ\rb* \rb and worshiped|וַיִּֽשְׁתַּחֲוֽוּ׃\rb*. \v 30 \rb Then King|הַמֶּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb Hezekiah|יְחִזְקִיָּ֨הוּ\rb* \rb and his officials|וְהַשָּׂרִים֙\rb* \rb ordered|וַ֠יֹּאמֶר\rb* \rb the Levites|לַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb* \rb to sing praises|לְהַלֵּל֙\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb in the words|בְּדִבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of David|דָוִ֖יד\rb* \rb and of Asaph|וְאָסָ֣ף\rb* \rb the seer|הַחֹזֶ֑ה\rb*. \rb So they sang praises|וַֽיְהַלְלוּ֙\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb with gladness|לְשִׂמְחָ֔ה\rb* \rb and bowed down|וַֽיִּקְּד֖וּ\rb* \rb and worshiped|וַיִּֽשְׁתַּחֲוֽוּ׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 31 \rb Then|וַיַּ֨עַן\rb* \rb Hezekiah|יְחִזְקִיָּ֜הוּ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Now|עַתָּ֨ה\rb* \rb that you have consecrated|מִלֵּאתֶ֤ם\rb* \rb yourselves|יֶדְכֶם֙\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֔ה\rb*,\f + \fr 29:31 \ft Or \fqa filled your hand for the LORD\f* \rb come near|גֹּ֧שׁוּ\rb* \rb and bring|וְהָבִ֛יאוּ\rb* \rb sacrifices|זְבָחִ֥ים\rb* \rb and thank offerings|וְתוֹד֖וֹת\rb* \rb to the house|לְבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*.”
\p \rb So the assembly|הַקָּהָל֙\rb* \rb brought|וַיָּבִ֤יאוּ\rb* \rb sacrifices|זְבָחִ֣ים\rb* \rb and thank offerings|וְתוֹד֔וֹת\rb*, \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb whose hearts|לֵ֖ב\rb* \rb were willing|נְדִ֥יב\rb* \rb brought burnt offerings|עֹלֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 32 \rb The number|מִסְפַּ֣ר\rb* \rb of burnt offerings|הָעֹלָה֮\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the assembly|הַקָּהָל֒\rb* \rb brought|הֵבִ֣יאוּ\rb* \rb was|וַיְהִ֞י\rb* \rb seventy|שִׁבְעִ֔ים\rb* \rb bulls|בָּקָ֣ר\rb*, \rb a hundred|מֵאָ֖ה\rb* \rb rams|אֵילִ֥ים\rb*, \rb and two hundred|מָאתָ֑יִם\rb* \rb lambs|כְּבָשִׂ֣ים\rb*; \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|אֵֽלֶּה׃\rb* \rb were for a burnt offering|לְעֹלָ֥ה\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb*. \v 33 \rb And the consecrated offerings were|וְֽהַקֳּדָשִׁ֑ים\rb* \rb six|שֵׁ֣שׁ\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֔וֹת\rb* \rb bulls|בָּקָר֙\rb* \rb and three|שְׁלֹ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb thousand|אֲלָפִֽים׃\rb* \rb sheep|וְצֹ֖אן\rb*.
\p \v 34 \rb However|רַ֤ק\rb*, \rb since there were|הָי֣וּ\rb* \rb not enough|לִמְעָ֔ט\rb* \rb priests|הַכֹּֽהֲנִים֙\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֣א\rb*\rb |יָֽכְל֔וּ\rb* \rb to skin|לְהַפְשִׁ֖יט\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the burnt offerings|הָעֹל֑וֹת\rb*, \rb their Levite|הַלְוִיִּ֗ם\rb* \rb brothers|אֲחֵיהֶ֣ם\rb* \rb helped them|וַֽיְּחַזְּק֞וּם\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb the work|הַמְּלָאכָה֙\rb* \rb was finished|כְּל֤וֹת\rb* \rb and until|וְעַ֣ד\rb* \rb the priests|הַכֹּֽהֲנִ֔ים\rb* \rb had consecrated themselves|יִתְקַדְּשׁ֣וּ\rb*. \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb the Levites|הַלְוִיִּם֙\rb* \rb had been more diligent|יִשְׁרֵ֣י\rb*\rb |לֵבָ֔ב\rb* \rb in consecrating themselves|לְהִתְקַדֵּ֖שׁ\rb* \rb than the priests had been|מֵֽהַכֹּהֲנִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 35 \rb Furthermore|וְגַם־\rb*, \rb the burnt offerings were abundant|עֹלָ֨ה\rb*\rb |לָרֹ֜ב\rb*, \rb along with the fat|בְּחֶלְבֵ֧י\rb* \rb of the peace offerings|הַשְּׁלָמִ֛ים\rb* \rb and the drink offerings|וּבַנְּסָכִ֖ים\rb* \rb for the burnt offerings|לָעֹלָ֑ה\rb*. \rb So the service|עֲבוֹדַ֥ת\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb was established|וַתִּכּ֖וֹן\rb*. \v 36 \rb Then Hezekiah|יְחִזְקִיָּ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb rejoiced|וַיִּשְׂמַ֤ח\rb* \rb at what|עַ֛ל\rb* \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb had prepared|הַהֵכִ֥ין\rb* \rb for the people|לָעָ֑ם\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb everything|הַדָּבָֽר׃פ\rb* \rb had been accomplished|הָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb so quickly|בְּפִתְאֹ֖ם\rb*.
\c 30
\s1 Hezekiah Proclaims a Passover
\p \v 1 \rb Then Hezekiah|יְחִזְקִיָּ֜הוּ\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֨ח\rb* \rb word throughout|עַל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֣ל\rb* \rb and Judah|וִֽיהוּדָ֗ה\rb*, \rb and he also|וְגַֽם־\rb* \rb wrote|כָּתַב֙\rb* \rb letters|אִגְּרוֹת֙\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֣יִם\rb* \rb and Manasseh|וּמְנַשֶּׁ֔ה\rb* \rb inviting them to come|לָב֥וֹא\rb* \rb to the house|לְבֵית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּֽירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb to keep|לַעֲשׂ֣וֹת\rb* \rb the Passover|פֶּ֔סַח\rb* \rb of the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb For the king|הַמֶּ֧לֶךְ\rb* \rb and his officials|וְשָׂרָ֛יו\rb* \rb and the whole|וְכָל־\rb* \rb assembly|הַקָּהָ֖ל\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb had decided|וַיִּוָּעַ֨ץ\rb* \rb to keep|לַעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb* \rb the Passover|הַפֶּ֖סַח\rb* \rb in the second|הַשֵּׁנִֽי׃\rb* \rb month|בַּחֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb*,\f + \fr 30:2 \ft See Numbers 9:9–12.\f* \v 3 \rb since|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb they had been unable|לֹ֧א\rb*\rb |יָכְל֛וּ\rb* \rb to keep it|לַעֲשֹׂת֖וֹ\rb* \rb at the regular|הַהִ֑יא\rb*\rb |כִּ֤י\rb* \rb time|בָּעֵ֣ת\rb*, \rb because not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb enough|לְמַדַּ֔י\rb* \rb priests|הַכֹּהֲנִים֙\rb* \rb had consecrated themselves|הִתְקַדְּשׁ֣וּ\rb* \rb and the people|וְהָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb had not|לֹא־\rb* \rb been gathered|נֶאֶסְפ֥וּ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|לִֽירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb This plan|הַדָּבָ֖ר\rb* \rb pleased|וַיִּישַׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb and|וּבְעֵינֵ֖י\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb assembly|הַקָּהָֽל׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb So they established|וַיַּֽעֲמִ֣ידוּ\rb* \rb a decree|דָבָ֗ר\rb* \rb to circulate|לְהַעֲבִ֨יר\rb* \rb a proclamation|ק֤וֹל\rb* \rb throughout|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*,\rb |מִבְּאֵֽר־\rb* \rb from Beersheba|שֶׁ֣בַע\rb* \rb to|וְעַד־\rb* \rb Dan|דָּ֔ן\rb*, \rb that the people should come|לָב֞וֹא\rb* \rb to keep|לַעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb* \rb the Passover|פֶּ֛סַח\rb* \rb of the LORD|לַיהוָ֥ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb*. \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb they had not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb observed it|עָשׂ֖וּ\rb* \rb in great numbers|לָרֹ֛ב\rb* \rb as prescribed|כַּכָּתֽוּב׃\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb At the command|וּכְמִצְוַ֥ת\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*, \rb the couriers|הָרָצִ֨ים\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּלְכוּ֩\rb* \rb throughout|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb and Judah|וִֽיהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb with letters|בָּֽאִגְּר֜וֹת\rb* \rb from|מִיַּ֧ד\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb and his officials|וְשָׂרָ֗יו\rb*, \rb which read|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*:
\pmo “\rb Children|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb*, \rb return|שׁ֚וּבוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵי֙\rb* \rb of Abraham|אַבְרָהָם֙\rb*, \rb Isaac|יִצְחָ֣ק\rb*, \rb and Israel|וְיִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb so that He may return|וְיָשֹׁב֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb those of you who remain|הַנִּשְׁאֶ֣רֶת\rb*, \rb who have escaped|הַפְּלֵיטָ֔ה\rb* \rb the grasp|מִכַּ֖ף\rb* \rb of the kings|מַלְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Assyria|אַשּֽׁוּר׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb Do not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb be|תִּֽהְי֗וּ\rb* \rb like your fathers|כַּאֲבֽוֹתֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb and brothers|וְכַ֣אֲחֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb were unfaithful|מָעֲל֔וּ\rb* \rb to the LORD|בַּיהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of their fathers|אֲבוֹתֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb so that He made them|וַיִּתְּנֵ֣ם\rb* \rb an object of horror|לְשַׁמָּ֔ה\rb*, \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb can see|רֹאִֽים׃\rb*.
\pmo \v 8 \rb Now|עַתָּ֕ה\rb* \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb stiffen|תַּקְשׁ֥וּ\rb* \rb your necks|עָרְפְּכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb as your fathers did|כַּאֲבוֹתֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb Submit|תְּנוּ־\rb*\rb |יָ֣ד\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb and come|וּבֹ֤אוּ\rb* \rb to His sanctuary|לְמִקְדָּשׁוֹ֙\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb He has consecrated|הִקְדִּ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb forever|לְעוֹלָ֔ם\rb*. \rb Serve|וְעִבְדוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb so that His fierce anger|חֲר֥וֹן\rb*\rb |אַפּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb will turn away|וְיָשֹׁ֥ב\rb* \rb from you|מִכֶּ֖ם\rb*. \v 9 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb if you return|בְשׁוּבְכֶ֞ם\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*, \rb your brothers|אֲחֵיכֶ֨ם\rb* \rb and sons|וּבְנֵיכֶ֤ם\rb* \rb will receive mercy|לְרַחֲמִים֙\rb* \rb in the presence|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of their captors|שֽׁוֹבֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and will return|וְלָשׁ֖וּב\rb* \rb to this|הַזֹּ֑את\rb* \rb land|לָאָ֣רֶץ\rb*. \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb is gracious|חַנּ֤וּן\rb* \rb and merciful|וְרַחוּם֙\rb*; \rb He will not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb turn His face|פָּנִים֙\rb* \rb away|יָסִ֤יר\rb* \rb from you|מִכֶּ֔ם\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb you return|תָּשׁ֖וּבוּ\rb* \rb to Him|אֵלָֽיו׃פ\rb*.”
\p \v 10 \rb And|וַיִּֽהְי֨וּ\rb* \rb the couriers|הָרָצִ֜ים\rb* \rb traveled|עֹבְרִ֨ים\rb* \rb from city|מֵעִ֧יר׀\rb* \rb to city|לָעִ֛יר\rb* \rb through the land|בְּאֶֽרֶץ־\rb* \rb of Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֥יִם\rb* \rb and Manasseh|וּמְנַשֶּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb as|וְעַד־\rb* \rb far as Zebulun|זְבֻל֑וּן\rb*\rb |וַיִּֽהְיוּ֙\rb*, \rb but the people scorned|מַשְׂחִיקִ֣ים\rb*\rb |עֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and mocked|וּמַלְעִגִ֖ים\rb* \rb them|בָּֽם׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb Nevertheless|אַךְ־\rb*, \rb some|אֲנָשִׁ֛ים\rb* \rb from Asher|מֵאָשֵׁ֥ר\rb*, \rb Manasseh|וּמְנַשֶּׁ֖ה\rb*, \rb and Zebulun|וּמִזְּבֻל֑וּן\rb* \rb humbled|נִֽכְנְע֔וּ\rb* \rb themselves and came|וַיָּבֹ֖אוּ\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|לִירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb Moreover|גַּ֣ם\rb*, \rb the power|יַ֣ד\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb was|הָֽיְתָה֙\rb* \rb on the people|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb in Judah|בִּיהוּדָ֗ה\rb* \rb to give them|לָתֵ֥ת\rb* \rb one|אֶחָ֑ד\rb* \rb heart|לֵ֣ב\rb* \rb to obey|לַעֲשׂ֞וֹת\rb* \rb the command|מִצְוַ֥ת\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּ֛לֶךְ\rb* \rb and his officials|וְהַשָּׂרִ֖ים\rb* \rb according to the word|בִּדְבַ֥ר\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\s1 Hezekiah Celebrates the Passover
\p \v 13 \rb In the second|הַשֵּׁנִ֑י\rb* \rb month|בַּחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb a very|מְאֹֽד׃\rb* \rb great|לָרֹ֥ב\rb* \rb assembly|קָהָ֖ל\rb*\rb |עַם־\rb*\rb |רָ֔ב\rb* \rb gathered|וַיֵּֽאָסְפ֤וּ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֙ם֙\rb* \rb to celebrate|לַעֲשׂ֛וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Feast|חַ֥ג\rb* \rb of Unleavened Bread|הַמַּצּ֖וֹת\rb*.\f + \fr 30:13 \ft That is, the seven-day period after the Passover during which no leaven may be eaten; see Exodus 12:14–20.\f* \v 14 \rb They proceeded|וַיָּקֻ֕מוּ\rb* \rb to remove|וַיָּסִ֙ירוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the altars|הַֽמִּזְבְּח֔וֹת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֤ת\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb and to take away|הֵסִ֔ירוּ\rb* \rb the incense altars|הַֽמְקַטְּרוֹת֙\rb* \rb and throw them|וַיַּשְׁלִ֖יכוּ\rb* \rb into the Kidron|קִדְרֽוֹן׃\rb* \rb Valley|לְנַ֥חַל\rb*. \v 15 \rb And on the fourteenth|בְּאַרְבָּעָ֥ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֖ר\rb* \rb day of the second|הַשֵּׁנִ֑י\rb* \rb month|לַחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb they slaughtered|וַיִּשְׁחֲט֣וּ\rb* \rb the Passover lamb|הַפֶּ֔סַח\rb*. \rb The priests|וְהַכֹּהֲנִ֨ים\rb* \rb and Levites|וְהַלְוִיִּ֤ם\rb* \rb were ashamed|נִכְלְמוּ֙\rb*, \rb and they consecrated themselves|וַיִּֽתְקַדְּשׁ֔וּ\rb* \rb and brought|וַיָּבִ֥יאוּ\rb* \rb burnt offerings|עֹל֖וֹת\rb* \rb to the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb They stood|וַיַּֽעַמְד֤וּ\rb* \rb at|עַל־\rb* \rb their prescribed|כְּמִשְׁפָּטָ֔ם\rb* \rb posts|עָמְדָם֙\rb*, \rb according to the Law|כְּתוֹרַ֖ת\rb* \rb of Moses|מֹשֶׁ֣ה\rb* \rb the man|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb*. \rb The priests|הַכֹּֽהֲנִים֙\rb* \rb splattered|זֹרְקִ֣ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the blood|הַדָּ֔ם\rb*, \rb which they received from the hand|מִיַּ֖ד\rb* \rb of the Levites|הַלְוִיִּֽם׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb Since|כִּי־\rb* \rb there were many|רַבַּ֥ת\rb* \rb in the assembly|בַּקָּהָ֖ל\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb had not|לֹא־\rb* \rb consecrated themselves|הִתְקַדָּ֑שׁוּ\rb*, \rb the Levites|וְהַלְוִיִּ֞ם\rb* \rb were in charge of|עַל־\rb* \rb slaughtering|שְׁחִיטַ֣ת\rb* \rb the Passover|הַפְּסָחִ֗ים\rb* \rb lambs for every|לְכֹל֙\rb* \rb unclean person|לֹ֣א\rb*\rb |טָה֔וֹר\rb* \rb to consecrate the lambs|לְהַקְדִּ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb A large number|מַרְבִּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the people|הָעָ֡ם\rb*— \rb many|רַ֠בַּת\rb* \rb from Ephraim|מֵֽאֶפְרַ֨יִם\rb*, \rb Manasseh|וּמְנַשֶּׁ֜ה\rb*, \rb Issachar|יִשָּׂשכָ֤ר\rb*, \rb and Zebulun|וּזְבֻלוּן֙\rb*— \rb had not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb purified themselves|הִטֶּהָ֔רוּ\rb*, \rb yet|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb they ate|אָכְל֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Passover|הַפֶּ֖סַח\rb*, \rb contrary|בְּלֹ֣א\rb* \rb to what was written|כַכָּת֑וּב\rb*. \rb But|כִּי֩\rb* \rb Hezekiah|יְחִזְקִיָּ֤הוּ\rb* \rb interceded|הִתְפַּלֵּ֨ל\rb* \rb for them|עֲלֵיהֶם֙\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, “\rb May the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb*, \rb who is good|הַטּ֖וֹב\rb*, \rb provide atonement for|יְכַפֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb everyone|בְּעַֽד׃\rb* \v 19 \rb who|כָּל־\rb* \rb sets|הֵכִ֔ין\rb* \rb his heart|לְבָב֣וֹ\rb* \rb on seeking|לִדְר֛וֹשׁ\rb* \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִ֥ים׀\rb* — \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of his fathers|אֲבוֹתָ֑יו\rb* — \rb even if he is not cleansed|וְלֹ֖א\rb* \rb according to the purification|כְּטָהֳרַ֥ת\rb* \rb rules of the sanctuary|הַקֹּֽדֶשׁ׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 20 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb heard|וַיִּשְׁמַ֤ע\rb* \rb Hezekiah|יְחִזְקִיָּ֔הוּ\rb* \rb and healed|וַיִּרְפָּ֖א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָֽם׃ס\rb*. \v 21 \rb The Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִ֠שְׂרָאֵל\rb* \rb who were present|הַנִּמְצְאִ֨ים\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּֽירוּשָׁלִַ֜ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb celebrated|וַיַּעֲשׂ֣וּ\rb* \rb the Feast|חַ֧ג\rb* \rb of Unleavened Bread|הַמַּצּ֛וֹת\rb* \rb for seven|שִׁבְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb with great|גְדוֹלָ֑ה\rb* \rb joy|בְּשִׂמְחָ֣ה\rb*, \rb and the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֧ם\rb* \rb and priests|וְהַכֹּהֲנִ֛ים\rb* \rb praised|וּֽמְהַלְלִ֣ים\rb* \rb the LORD|לַ֠יהוָה\rb* \rb day|י֣וֹם׀\rb* \rb after day|בְּי֞וֹם\rb*, \rb accompanied by loud|עֹ֖ז\rb* \rb instruments of praise|בִּכְלֵי־\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָֽה׃ס\rb*.\f + \fr 30:21 \ft Or \fqa day after day, with all their strength to the LORD. \ft Literally \fqa day after day, with loud instruments to the LORD.\f* \v 22 \rb And Hezekiah|יְחִזְקִיָּ֗הוּ\rb* \rb encouraged|וַיְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |לֵב֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb*\rb |הַמַּשְׂכִּילִ֥ים\rb* \rb who performed skillfully|שֵֽׂכֶל־\rb*\rb |ט֖וֹב\rb* \rb before the LORD|לַיהוָ֑ה\rb*. \rb For seven|שִׁבְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb days|הַיָּמִ֔ים\rb* \rb they ate|וַיֹּאכְל֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their assigned portion|הַמּוֹעֵד֙\rb*, \rb sacrificing|מְזַבְּחִים֙\rb* \rb peace|שְׁלָמִ֔ים\rb* \rb offerings|זִבְחֵ֣י\rb* \rb and giving thanks|וּמִ֨תְוַדִּ֔ים\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of their fathers|אֲבוֹתֵיהֶֽם׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 23 \rb The whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb assembly|הַקָּהָ֔ל\rb* \rb agreed|וַיִּוָּֽעֲצוּ֙\rb* \rb to observe|לַעֲשׂ֕וֹת\rb* \rb seven|שִׁבְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb more|אֲחֵרִ֑ים\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֖ים\rb*, \rb so they observed|וַיַּֽעֲשׂ֥וּ\rb* \rb seven|שִׁבְעַת־\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb with joy|שִׂמְחָֽה׃\rb*. \v 24 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְ֠הוּדָה\rb* \rb contributed|הֵרִ֨ים\rb* \rb a thousand|אֶ֣לֶף\rb* \rb bulls|פָּרִים֮\rb* \rb and seven|וְשִׁבְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb thousand|אֲלָפִ֣ים\rb* \rb sheep|צֹאן֒ס\rb* \rb for the assembly|לַקָּהָ֜ל\rb*, \rb and the officials|וְהַשָּׂרִ֞ים\rb* \rb contributed|הֵרִ֤ימוּ\rb* \rb a thousand|אֶ֔לֶף\rb* \rb bulls|פָּרִ֣ים\rb* \rb and ten|עֲשֶׂ֣רֶת\rb* \rb thousand|אֲלָפִ֑ים\rb* \rb sheep|וְצֹ֖אן\rb* \rb for the assembly|לַקָּהָל֙\rb*, \rb and a great number|לָרֹֽב׃\rb* \rb of priests|כֹהֲנִ֖ים\rb* \rb consecrated themselves|וַיִּֽתְקַדְּשׁ֥וּ\rb*.
\p \v 25 \rb Then the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb assembly|קְהַ֣ל\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb* \rb rejoiced|וַֽיִּשְׂמְח֣וּ׀\rb* \rb along with the priests|וְהַכֹּהֲנִים֙\rb* \rb and Levites|וְהַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb* \rb and the whole|וְכָל־\rb* \rb assembly|הַקָּהָ֖ל\rb* \rb that had come|הַבָּאִ֣ים\rb* \rb from Israel|מִיִּשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb including the foreigners|וְהַגֵּרִ֗ים\rb* \rb who had come|הַבָּאִים֙\rb*\rb |מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb from Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb and those who lived|וְהַיּוֹשְׁבִ֖ים\rb* \rb in Judah|בִּיהוּדָֽה׃\rb*. \v 26 \rb So there was|וַתְּהִ֥י\rb* \rb great|גְדוֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb rejoicing|שִׂמְחָֽה־\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּֽירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֠י\rb* \rb nothing|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb like this had happened|כָזֹ֖את\rb* \rb there|בִּירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃ס\rb* \rb since the days|מִימֵ֞י\rb* \rb of Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֤ה\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִיד֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*.
\p \v 27 \rb Then the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֤ים\rb* \rb and the Levites|הַלְוִיִּם֙\rb* \rb stood|וַיָּקֻ֜מוּ\rb* \rb to bless|וַיְבָרֲכ֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb*, \rb and God heard|וַיִּשָּׁמַ֖ע\rb* \rb their voice|בְּקוֹלָ֑ם\rb*, \rb and their prayer|תְפִלָּתָ֛ם\rb* \rb came|וַתָּב֧וֹא\rb* \rb into His holy dwelling|לִמְע֥וֹן\rb* \rb place|קָדְשׁ֖וֹ\rb* \rb in heaven|לַשָּׁמָֽיִם׃פ\rb*.
\c 31
\s1 The Destruction of Idols
\p \v 1 \rb When all|כָּל־\rb* \rb this|זֹ֗את\rb* \rb had ended|וּכְכַלּ֣וֹת\rb*,\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֥ל\rb* \rb in attendance|הַֽנִּמְצְאִים֮\rb* \rb went out|יָצְא֨וּ\rb* \rb to the cities|לְעָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָה֒\rb* \rb and broke up|וַיְשַׁבְּר֣וּ\rb* \rb the sacred pillars|הַמַּצֵּב֣וֹת\rb*, \rb chopped down|וַיְגַדְּע֣וּ\rb* \rb the Asherah poles|הָאֲשֵׁרִ֡ים\rb*, \rb and tore down|וַיְנַתְּצ֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the high places|הַ֠בָּמוֹת\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and altars|הַֽמִּזְבְּחֹ֞ת\rb* \rb throughout|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֧ה\rb* \rb and Benjamin|וּבִנְיָמִ֛ן\rb*, \rb as well as in Ephraim|וּבְאֶפְרַ֥יִם\rb* \rb and Manasseh|וּמְנַשֶּׁ֖ה\rb*, \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb they had utterly destroyed them all|לְכַלֵּ֑ה\rb*. \rb Then all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֧י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb returned|וַיָּשׁ֜וּבוּ\rb* \rb to their cities|לְעָרֵיהֶֽם׃ס\rb*, \rb each|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb to his own property|לַאֲחֻזָּת֖וֹ\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb Hezekiah|יְחִזְקִיָּ֡הוּ\rb* \rb reestablished|וַיַּעֲמֵ֣ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the divisions|מַחְלְק֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֣ים\rb* \rb and Levites|וְ֠הַלְוִיִּם\rb*\rb |עַֽל־\rb* — \rb each of them|אִ֣ישׁ׀\rb*\rb |מַחְלְקוֹתָ֞ם\rb* \rb according to|כְּפִ֣י\rb* \rb their duties|עֲבֹדָת֗וֹ\rb* \rb as priests|לַכֹּהֲנִים֙\rb* \rb or Levites|וְלַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb* — \rb for the burnt offerings|לְעֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb and peace offerings|וְלִשְׁלָמִ֑ים\rb*, \rb for ministry|לְשָׁרֵת֙\rb*, \rb for giving thanks|וּלְהֹד֣וֹת\rb*, \rb and for singing praises|וּלְהַלֵּ֔ל\rb* \rb at the gates|בְּשַׁעֲרֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the LORD’s|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb* \rb dwelling|מַחֲנ֥וֹת\rb*.
\s1 Contributions for Worship
\p \v 3 \rb The king|הַמֶּ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb contributed|וּמְנָת֩\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb his own possessions|רְכוּשׁ֜וֹ\rb* \rb for the regular morning|הַבֹּ֣קֶר\rb* \rb and evening|וְהָעֶ֔רֶב\rb*\rb |וְהָ֣עֹל֔וֹת\rb* \rb burnt offerings|לָעֹל֗וֹת\rb* \rb and for the burnt offerings|לְעֹלוֹת֙\rb* \rb on the Sabbaths|לַשַּׁבָּת֖וֹת\rb*, \rb New Moons|וְלֶחֳדָשִׁ֣ים\rb*, \rb and appointed feasts|וְלַמֹּעֲדִ֑ים\rb*, \rb as written|כַּכָּת֖וּב\rb* \rb in the Law|בְּתוֹרַ֥ת\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb Moreover, he commanded|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb the people|לָעָם֙\rb* \rb living|לְיוֹשְׁבֵ֣י\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb to make|לָתֵ֕ת\rb* \rb a contribution|מְנָ֥ת\rb* \rb for the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֖ים\rb* \rb and Levites|וְהַלְוִיִּ֑ם\rb* \rb so that|לְמַ֥עַן\rb* \rb they could devote themselves|יֶחֶזְק֖וּ\rb* \rb to the Law|בְּתוֹרַ֥ת\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb As soon as the order|הַדָּבָ֗ר\rb* \rb went out|וְכִפְרֹ֣ץ\rb*, \rb the Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb generously provided|הִרְבּ֤וּ\rb* \rb the firstfruits|רֵאשִׁ֣ית\rb* \rb of the grain|דָּגָ֗ן\rb*, \rb new wine|תִּיר֤וֹשׁ\rb*, \rb oil|וְיִצְהָר֙\rb*, \rb and honey|וּדְבַ֔שׁ\rb*, \rb and of all|וְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the produce|תְּבוּאַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the field|שָׂדֶ֑ה\rb*, \rb and they brought in|הֵבִֽיאוּ׃\rb* \rb an abundance|לָרֹ֖ב\rb* — \rb a tithe|וּמַעְשַׂ֥ר\rb* \rb of everything|הַכֹּ֛ל\rb*. \v 6 \rb And the Israelites|וּבְנֵ֧י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֣ל\rb* \rb and Judahites|וִֽיהוּדָ֗ה\rb* \rb who lived|הַיּֽוֹשְׁבִים֮\rb* \rb in the cities|בְּעָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָה֒\rb*\rb |הֵ֗ם\rb* \rb also|גַּם־\rb* \rb brought|הֵבִ֕יאוּ\rb* \rb a tithe|מַעְשַׂ֤ר\rb* \rb of their herds|בָּקָר֙\rb* \rb and flocks|וָצֹ֔אן\rb* \rb and a tithe|וּמַעְשַׂ֣ר\rb* \rb of the holy things|קָֽדָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb consecrated|הַמְקֻדָּשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb their God|אֱלֹהֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb and they laid them|וַֽיִּתְּנ֖וּ\rb* \rb in large heaps|עֲרֵמ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |עֲרֵמֽוֹת׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb In the third|הַשְּׁלִשִׁ֔י\rb* \rb month|בַּחֹ֙דֶשׁ֙\rb* \rb they began|הֵחֵ֥לּוּ\rb* \rb building up|לְיִסּ֑וֹד\rb* \rb the heaps|הָעֲרֵמ֖וֹת\rb*, \rb and they finished|כִּלּֽוּ׃ס\rb* \rb in the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֖י\rb* \rb month|וּבַחֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb*. \v 8 \rb When Hezekiah|יְחִזְקִיָּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb and his officials|וְהַשָּׂרִ֔ים\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֙אוּ֙\rb* \rb and viewed|וַיִּרְא֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the heaps|הָעֲרֵמ֑וֹת\rb*, \rb they blessed|וַֽיְבָרֲכוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb and His people|עַמּ֥וֹ\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb Then Hezekiah|יְחִזְקִיָּ֗הוּ\rb* \rb questioned|וַיִּדְרֹ֣שׁ\rb* \rb the priests|הַכֹּֽהֲנִ֛ים\rb* \rb and Levites|וְהַלְוִיִּ֖ם\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb about|עַל־\rb* \rb the heaps|הָעֲרֵמֽוֹת׃\rb*, \v 10 \rb and Azariah|עֲזַרְיָ֧הוּ\rb*, \rb the chief|הָרֹ֖אשׁ\rb* \rb priest|הַכֹּהֵ֛ן\rb* \rb of the household|לְבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of Zadok|צָד֑וֹק\rb*,\rb |וַ֠יֹּאמֶר\rb* \rb answered|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb him|אֵלָ֗יו\rb*, “\rb Since the people began|מֵהָחֵ֨ל\rb* \rb to bring|לָבִ֣יא\rb* \rb their contributions|הַתְּרוּמָ֜ה\rb* \rb into the house|בֵית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*, \rb we have had enough|וְשָׂב֤וֹעַ\rb* \rb to eat|אָכ֨וֹל\rb*, \rb and there is plenty|לָר֔וֹב\rb* \rb left over|וְהוֹתֵר֙\rb*,\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb because|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb has blessed|בֵּרַ֣ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb His people|עַמּ֔וֹ\rb*; \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃ס\rb* \rb great abundance|הֶהָמ֥וֹן\rb* \rb is what is left over|וְהַנּוֹתָ֖ר\rb*.”\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\s1 Hezekiah Organizes the Priests
\p \v 11 \rb Then Hezekiah|יְחִזְקִיָּ֗הוּ\rb* \rb commanded them|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to prepare|לְהָכִ֧ין\rb* \rb storerooms|לְשָׁכ֛וֹת\rb* \rb in the house|בְּבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb and they did so|וַיָּכִֽינוּ׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb And they faithfully brought in|וַיָּבִ֨יאוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |בֶּאֱמוּנָ֑ה\rb* \rb the contributions|הַתְּרוּמָ֧ה\rb*, \rb tithes|וְהַֽמַּעֲשֵׂ֛ר\rb*, \rb and dedicated gifts|וְהַקֳּדָשִׁ֖ים\rb*. \rb Conaniah|כּוֹנַנְיָהוּ\rb* \rb the Levite|הַלֵּוִ֔י\rb* \rb was the officer|נָגִיד֙\rb* \rb in charge of them|וַעֲלֵיהֶ֤ם\rb*, \rb and his brother|אָחִ֖יהוּ\rb* \rb Shimei|וְשִׁמְעִ֥י\rb* \rb was second|מִשְׁנֶֽה׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb Jehiel|וִֽיחִיאֵ֡ל\rb*, \rb Azaziah|וַ֠עֲזַזְיָהוּ\rb*, \rb Nahath|וְנַ֨חַת\rb*, \rb Asahel|וַעֲשָׂהאֵ֜ל\rb*, \rb Jerimoth|וִֽירִימ֤וֹת\rb*, \rb Jozabad|וְיוֹזָבָד֙\rb*, \rb Eliel|וֶאֱלִיאֵ֣ל\rb*, \rb Ismachiah|וְיִסְמַכְיָ֔הוּ\rb*, \rb Mahath|וּמַ֖חַת\rb*, \rb and Benaiah|וּבְנָיָ֑הוּ\rb* \rb were overseers|פְּקִידִ֗ים\rb* \rb under the authority|מִיַּ֤ד\rb* \rb of Conaniah|כָּונַנְיָהוּ\rb* \rb and his brother|אָחִ֔יו\rb* \rb Shimei|וְשִׁמְעִ֣י\rb*, \rb by appointment|בְּמִפְקַד֙\rb* \rb of King|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb Hezekiah|יְחִזְקִיָּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb and of Azariah|וַעֲזַרְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb the chief official|נְגִ֥יד\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb Kore|וְקוֹרֵ֨א\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Imnah|יִמְנָ֤ה\rb* \rb the Levite|הַלֵּוִי֙\rb*, \rb the keeper|הַשּׁוֹעֵ֣ר\rb* \rb of the East Gate|לַמִּזְרָ֔חָה\rb*, \rb was in charge|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb of the freewill offerings|נִדְב֣וֹת\rb* \rb given to God|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb*, \rb distributing|לָתֵת֙\rb* \rb the contributions|תְּרוּמַ֣ת\rb* \rb to the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְקָדְשֵׁ֖י\rb* \rb and the consecrated gifts|הַקֳּדָשִֽׁים׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb Under|וְעַל־\rb* \rb his authority|יָד֡וֹ\rb*, \rb Eden|עֵ֣דֶן\rb*, \rb Miniamin|וּ֠מִנְיָמִן\rb*, \rb Jeshua|וְיֵשׁ֨וּעַ\rb*, \rb Shemaiah|וּֽשְׁמַֽעְיָ֜הוּ\rb*, \rb Amariah|אֲמַרְיָ֧הוּ\rb*, \rb and Shecaniah|וּשְׁכַנְיָ֛הוּ\rb* \rb faithfully|בֶּאֱמוּנָ֑ה\rb* \rb distributed portions|לָתֵ֤ת\rb* \rb to their fellow priests|לַאֲחֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb in their cities|בְּעָרֵ֥י\rb*\rb |הַכֹּהֲנִ֖ים\rb*, \rb according to their divisions|בְּמַחְלְק֔וֹת\rb*, \rb old|כַּגָּד֖וֹל\rb* \rb and young alike|כַּקָּטָֽן׃\rb*.\f + \fr 31:15 \ft Or \fqa whether large or small\f*
\p \v 16 \rb In addition|מִלְּבַ֞ד\rb*, \rb they distributed portions to the males|לִזְכָרִ֗ים\rb* \rb registered by genealogy|הִתְיַחְשָׂ֣ם\rb* \rb who were three|שָׁל֤וֹשׁ\rb* \rb years of age|מִבֶּ֨ן\rb*\rb |שָׁנִים֙\rb* \rb or older|וּלְמַ֔עְלָה\rb* — \rb to all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb who would enter|הַבָּ֥א\rb* \rb the house|לְבֵית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb for their daily|י֣וֹם\rb*\rb |בְּיוֹמ֑וֹ\rb* \rb duties|לִדְבַר־\rb* \rb for service|לַעֲב֣וֹדָתָ֔ם\rb* \rb in the responsibilities|בְּמִשְׁמְרוֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb of their divisions|כְּמַחְלְקוֹתֵיהֶֽם׃\rb* — \v 17 \rb and|וְאֵ֨ת\rb* \rb to the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִים֙\rb* \rb enrolled according to|אֲבוֹתֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb their families|לְבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb in the genealogy|הִתְיַחֵ֤שׂ\rb*, \rb as well as to the Levites|וְהַ֨לְוִיִּ֔ם\rb* \rb twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb* \rb years of age|מִבֶּ֛ן\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֖ה\rb* \rb or older|וּלְמָ֑עְלָה\rb*, \rb according to their responsibilities|בְּמִשְׁמְרוֹתֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and divisions|בְּמַחְלְקוֹתֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 18 \rb The genealogy|וּלְהִתְיַחֵ֗שׂ\rb* \rb included all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the little ones|טַפָּ֧ם\rb*, \rb wives|נְשֵׁיהֶ֛ם\rb*, \rb sons|וּבְנֵיהֶ֥ם\rb*, \rb and daughters|וּבְנוֹתֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb of the whole|לְכָל־\rb* \rb assembly|קָהָ֑ל\rb*. \rb For|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb they had faithfully|בֶאֱמוּנָתָ֖ם\rb* \rb consecrated themselves|יִתְקַדְּשׁוּ־\rb* \rb as holy|קֹֽדֶשׁ׃\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb As for the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֜ים\rb*, \rb the descendants|וְלִבְנֵי֩\rb* \rb of Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֨ן\rb*, \rb who lived on the farmlands around|בִּשְׂדֵ֨י\rb*\rb |מִגְרַ֤שׁ\rb* \rb each of their cities|עָרֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb or in any other|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb city|עִ֣יר\rb*\rb |וָעִ֔יר\rb*, \rb men|אֲנָשִׁ֕ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb were designated|נִקְּב֖וּ\rb* \rb by name|בְּשֵׁמ֑וֹת\rb* \rb to distribute|לָתֵ֣ת\rb* \rb a portion|מָנ֗וֹת\rb* \rb to every|לְכָל־\rb* \rb male|זָכָר֙\rb* \rb among the priests|בַּכֹּ֣הֲנִ֔ים\rb* \rb and to every|וּלְכָל־\rb* \rb Levite|בַּלְוִיִּֽם׃\rb* \rb listed by the genealogies|הִתְיַחֵ֖שׂ\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb So this is what|כָּזֹ֛את\rb* \rb Hezekiah|יְחִזְקִיָּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb did|וַיַּ֧עַשׂ\rb* \rb throughout|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb*. \rb He did|וַיַּ֨עַשׂ\rb* \rb what was good|הַטּ֤וֹב\rb* \rb and upright|וְהַיָּשָׁר֙\rb* \rb and true|וְהָ֣אֱמֶ֔ת\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb his God|אֱלֹהָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb He acted|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb* \rb with all|וּבְכָֽל־\rb* \rb his heart|לְבָב֥וֹ\rb* \rb in every|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb work|מַעֲשֶׂ֞ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he began|הֵחֵ֣ל׀\rb* \rb in the service|בַּעֲבוֹדַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb*, \rb and in the law|וּבַתּוֹרָה֙\rb* \rb and the commandments|וּבַמִּצְוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb in order to seek|לִדְרֹ֖שׁ\rb* \rb his God|לֵֽאלֹהָ֑יו\rb*. \rb And so he prospered|וְהִצְלִֽיחַ׃פ\rb*.
\c 32
\s1 Sennacherib Invades Judah
\r (2 Kings 18:13–16; Psalm 46:1–11)
\p \v 1 \rb After|אַחֲרֵ֨י\rb* \rb all these|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb acts|הַדְּבָרִ֤ים\rb* \rb of faithfulness|וְהָאֱמֶת֙\rb*, \rb Sennacherib|סַנְחֵרִ֣יב\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Assyria|אַשּׁ֑וּר\rb* \rb came|בָּ֖א\rb* \rb and invaded|וַיָּבֹ֣א\rb* \rb Judah|בִֽיהוּדָ֗ה\rb*. \rb He laid siege|וַיִּ֙חַן֙\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the fortified|הַבְּצֻר֔וֹת\rb* \rb cities|הֶעָרִ֣ים\rb*, \rb intending|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb* \rb to conquer them|לְבִקְעָ֥ם\rb* \rb for himself|אֵלָֽיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb When Hezekiah|יְחִזְקִיָּ֔הוּ\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּרְא֙\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb Sennacherib|סַנְחֵרִ֑יב\rb*\rb |וּפָנָ֕יו\rb* \rb had come|בָ֖א\rb* \rb to make war|לַמִּלְחָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*, \v 3 \rb he consulted|וַיִּוָּעַ֗ץ\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb his leaders|שָׂרָיו֙\rb* \rb and mighty men|וְגִבֹּרָ֔יו\rb* \rb about stopping up|לִסְתּוֹם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the waters|מֵימֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the springs|הָעֲיָנ֔וֹת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb outside|מִח֣וּץ\rb* \rb the city|לָעִ֑יר\rb*, \rb and they helped him carry it out|וַֽיַּעְזְרֽוּהוּ׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb Many|רָ֔ב\rb* \rb people|עַם־\rb* \rb assembled|וַיִּקָּבְצ֣וּ\rb* \rb and stopped|וַֽיִּסְתְּמוּ֙\rb* \rb up all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the springs|הַמַּעְיָנ֔וֹת\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the stream|הַנַּ֛חַל\rb* \rb that flowed|הַשּׁוֹטֵ֥ף\rb* \rb through|בְּתוֹךְ־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb*. “\rb Why|לָ֤מָּה\rb* \rb should the kings|מַלְכֵ֣י\rb*\f + \fr 32:4 \ft Hebrew; LXX and Syriac \fqa king\f* \rb of Assyria|אַשּׁ֔וּר\rb* \rb come|יָב֙וֹאוּ֙\rb* \rb and find|וּמָצְא֖וּ\rb* \rb plenty|רַבִּֽים׃\rb* \rb of water|מַ֥יִם\rb*?” \rb they said|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb Then Hezekiah worked resolutely|וַיִּתְחַזַּ֡ק\rb* \rb to rebuild|וַיִּבֶן֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the broken sections of|הַפְּרוּצָ֜ה\rb* \rb the wall|הַחוֹמָ֨ה\rb* \rb and to raise up|וַיַּ֣עַל\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb towers on it|הַמִּגְדָּל֗וֹת\rb*. \rb He also built an|אַחֶ֔רֶת\rb* \rb outer|וְלַח֙וּצָה֙\rb* \rb wall|הַחוֹמָ֣ה\rb* \rb and reinforced|וַיְחַזֵּ֥ק\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the supporting terraces|הַמִּלּ֖וֹא\rb*\f + \fr 32:5 \ft Hebrew \fqa the Millo\f* \rb of the City|עִ֣יר\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֑יד\rb*, \rb and he produced|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb an abundance of|לָרֹ֖ב\rb* \rb weapons|שֶׁ֛לַח\rb* \rb and shields|וּמָגִנִּֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb Hezekiah appointed|וַיִּתֵּ֛ן\rb* \rb military|מִלְחָמ֖וֹת\rb* \rb commanders|שָׂרֵ֥י\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֑ם\rb* \rb and gathered|וַיִּקְבְּצֵ֣ם\rb* \rb the people in|אֵלָ֗יו\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the square|רְחוֹב֙\rb* \rb of the city|הָעִ֔יר\rb* \rb gate|שַׁ֣עַר\rb*. \rb Then he encouraged|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb them|לְבָבָ֖ם\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 7 “\rb Be strong|חִזְק֣וּ\rb* \rb and courageous|וְאִמְצ֔וּ\rb*! \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִּֽירְא֣וּ\rb*\rb |וְאַל־\rb* \rb or discouraged|תֵּחַ֗תּוּ\rb* \rb before|מִפְּנֵי֙\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Assyria|אַשּׁ֔וּר\rb* \rb and|וּמִלִּפְנֵ֖י\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb the vast army|הֶהָמ֣וֹן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb with him|עִמּ֑וֹ\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb there is a greater One|רַ֖ב\rb* \rb with us|עִמָּ֥נוּ\rb* \rb than with him|מֵעִמּֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb With him is only|עִמּוֹ֙\rb* \rb the arm|זְר֣וֹעַ\rb* \rb of flesh|בָּשָׂ֔ר\rb*,\f + \fr 32:8 \ft Or \fqa He has only the strength of his own flesh\f* \rb but with us is|וְעִמָּ֜נוּ\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb* \rb to help us|לְעָזְרֵ֔נוּ\rb* \rb and to fight|וּלְהִלָּחֵ֖ם\rb* \rb our battles|מִלְחֲמֹתֵ֑נוּ\rb*.”
\p \rb So the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb were strengthened|וַיִּסָּמְכ֣וּ\rb* \rb by|עַל־\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Hezekiah|יְחִזְקִיָּ֥הוּ\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָֽה׃פ\rb*.
\s1 Sennacherib Threatens Jerusalem
\r (2 Kings 18:17–37; Isaiah 36:1–22)
\p \v 9 \rb Later|אַ֣חַר\rb*\rb |זֶ֗ה\rb*, \rb as Sennacherib|סַנְחֵרִ֨יב\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Assyria|אַשּׁ֤וּר\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his forces|מֶמְשַׁלְתּ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |עִמּ֑וֹ\rb*\rb |וְהוּא֙\rb* \rb besieged|עַל־\rb* \rb Lachish|לָכִ֔ישׁ\rb*, \rb he sent|שָׁ֠לַח\rb* \rb his servants|עֲבָדָיו֙\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|יְר֣וּשָׁלַ֔יְמָה\rb* \rb with a message|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \rb for King|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Hezekiah|יְחִזְקִיָּ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and|עַל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people of Judah|יְהוּדָ֛ה\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb were in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb*: \v 10 “\rb This is what|כֹּ֣ה\rb* \rb Sennacherib|סַנְחֵרִ֖יב\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Assyria|אַשּׁ֑וּר\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֔ר\rb*: \rb What|מָה֙\rb* \rb is the basis|עַל־\rb* \rb of your|אַתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb confidence|בֹּטְחִ֔ים\rb*, \rb that you remain|וְיֹשְׁבִ֥ים\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb* \rb under siege|בְּמָצ֖וֹר\rb*? \v 11 \rb Is not|הֲלֹ֤א\rb* \rb Hezekiah|יְחִזְקִיָּ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb misleading|מַסִּ֣ית\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb to give you over|לָתֵ֣ת\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb to death|לָמ֛וּת\rb* \rb by famine|בְּרָעָ֥ב\rb* \rb and thirst|וּבְצָמָ֖א\rb* \rb when he says|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, ‘\rb The LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb will deliver us|יַצִּילֵ֕נוּ\rb* \rb from the hand|מִכַּ֖ף\rb* \rb of the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Assyria|אַשּֽׁוּר׃\rb* ?’ \v 12 \rb Did not|הֲלֹא־\rb* \rb Hezekiah|יְחִזְקִיָּ֔הוּ\rb* \rb himself|הוּא֙\rb* \rb remove|הֵסִ֥יר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb His high places|בָּמֹתָ֖יו\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and His altars|מִזְבְּחֹתָ֑יו\rb* \rb and say|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to Judah|לִֽיהוּדָ֤ה\rb* \rb and Jerusalem|וְלִֽירוּשָׁלִַ֙ם֙\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* ‘\rb You must worship|תִּֽשְׁתַּחֲו֖וּ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֨י\rb* \rb one|אֶחָ֛ד\rb* \rb altar|מִזְבֵּ֧חַ\rb*, \rb and on it|וְעָלָ֥יו\rb* \rb you shall burn sacrifices|תַּקְטִֽירוּ׃\rb*’ ?
\p \v 13 \rb Do you not|הֲלֹ֣א\rb* \rb know|תֵדְע֗וּ\rb* \rb what|מֶ֤ה\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb and my fathers|וַאֲבוֹתַ֔י\rb* \rb have done|עָשִׂ֙יתִי֙\rb* \rb to all|לְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the peoples|עַמֵּ֣י\rb* \rb of the lands|הָאֲרָצ֑וֹת\rb*? \rb Have the gods|אֱלֹהֵי֙\rb*\rb |הָאֲרָצ֔וֹת\rb* \rb of these nations|גּוֹיֵ֣\rb* \rb ever been able|הֲיָכ֣וֹל\rb*\rb |יָֽכְל֗וּ\rb* \rb to deliver|לְהַצִּ֥יל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their land|אַרְצָ֖ם\rb* \rb from my hand|מִיָּדִֽי׃\rb*? \v 14 \rb Who|מִ֠י\rb* \rb among all|בְּֽכָל־\rb* \rb the gods|אֱלֹהֵ֞י\rb* \rb of these|הָאֵ֙לֶּה֙\rb* \rb nations|הַגּוֹיִ֤ם\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb my fathers|אֲבוֹתַ֔י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb devoted to destruction|הֶחֱרִ֣ימוּ\rb*\f + \fr 32:14 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa cherem \ft refer to the giving over of things or persons to the LORD, either by destroying them or by giving them as an offering.\f* \rb has been able|יָכ֔וֹל\rb* \rb to deliver|לְהַצִּ֥יל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his people|עַמּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb from my hand|מִיָּדִ֑י\rb*? \rb How then|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb can|יוּכַל֙\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹ֣הֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb deliver|לְהַצִּ֥יל\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb from my hand|מִיָּדִֽי׃\rb*?
\p \v 15 \rb So now|וְעַתָּ֡ה\rb*, \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb let Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֜הוּ\rb* \rb deceive you|יַשִּׁיא֩\rb*,\rb |אֶתְכֶ֨ם\rb* \rb and do not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb let him mislead|יַסִּ֨ית\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֣ם\rb* \rb like this|כָּזֹאת֮\rb*. \rb Do not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb believe|תַּאֲמִ֣ינוּ\rb* \rb him|לוֹ֒\rb*, \rb for|כִּי־\rb* \rb no|לֹ֣א\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb god|אֱל֙וֹהַ֙\rb* \rb of any|כָּל־\rb* \rb nation|גּ֣וֹי\rb* \rb or kingdom|וּמַמְלָכָ֔ה\rb* \rb has been able|יוּכַ֗ל\rb* \rb to deliver|לְהַצִּ֥יל\rb* \rb his people|עַמּ֛וֹ\rb* \rb from my hand|מִיָּדִ֖י\rb* \rb or from the hand|וּמִיַּ֣ד\rb* \rb of my fathers|אֲבוֹתָ֑י\rb*. \rb How much less|אַ֚ף\rb*\rb |כִּ֣י\rb* \rb will your God|אֱ‍ֽלֹהֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |לֹא־\rb* \rb deliver|יַצִּ֥ילוּ\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb from my hand|מִיָּדִֽי׃\rb*!”
\p \v 16 \rb And the servants of Sennacherib|עֲבָדָ֔יו\rb* \rb spoke|דִּבְּר֣וּ\rb* \rb further|וְעוֹד֙\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb* \rb and against|וְעַ֖ל\rb* \rb His servant|עַבְדּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb Hezekiah|יְחִזְקִיָּ֥הוּ\rb*. \v 17 \rb He also wrote|כָּתַ֔ב\rb* \rb letters|וּסְפָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb mocking|לְחָרֵ֕ף\rb* \rb the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb and saying|וְלֵֽאמֹ֨ר\rb* \rb against Him|עָלָ֜יו\rb*:\rb |לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* “\rb Just as the gods|כֵּֽאלֹהֵ֞י\rb* \rb of the nations|גּוֹיֵ֤\rb*\rb |הָאֲרָצוֹת֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb deliver|הִצִּ֤ילוּ\rb* \rb their people|עַמָּם֙\rb* \rb from my hand|מִיָּדִ֔י\rb*, \rb so|כֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֧י\rb* \rb of Hezekiah|יְחִזְקִיָּ֛הוּ\rb* \rb will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb deliver|יַצִּ֞יל\rb* \rb His people|עַמּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb from my hand|מִיָּדִֽי׃\rb*.”
\p \v 18 \rb Then the Assyrians called out|וַיִּקְרְא֨וּ\rb* \rb loudly|בְקוֹל־\rb*\rb |גָּד֜וֹל\rb* \rb in Hebrew|יְהוּדִ֗ית\rb*\f + \fr 32:18 \ft Or \fqa in the dialect of Judah\f* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the people|עַ֤ם\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֙ם֙\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb were on|עַל־\rb* \rb the wall|הַֽחוֹמָ֔ה\rb*, \rb to frighten|לְיָֽרְאָ֖ם\rb* \rb and terrify them|וּֽלְבַהֲלָ֑ם\rb* \rb in order|לְמַ֖עַן\rb* \rb to capture|יִלְכְּד֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִֽיר׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb They spoke|וַֽיְדַבְּר֔וּ\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb as they had spoken against|כְּעַ֗ל\rb* \rb the gods|אֱלֹהֵי֙\rb* \rb of the peoples|עַמֵּ֣י\rb* \rb of the earth|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* — \rb the work|מַעֲשֵׂ֖ה\rb* \rb of human|הָאָדָֽם׃ס\rb* \rb hands|יְדֵ֥י\rb*.
\s1 Jerusalem Delivered from the Assyrians
\r (2 Kings 19:35–37; Isaiah 37:36–38)
\p \v 20 \rb In response|עַל־\rb*\rb |זֹ֑את\rb*, \rb King|הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb Hezekiah|יְחִזְקִיָּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb and the prophet|הַנָּבִ֖יא\rb* \rb Isaiah|וִֽישַֽׁעְיָ֧הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Amoz|אָמ֛וֹץ\rb* \rb cried out|וַֽיִּזְעֲק֖וּ\rb* \rb to heaven|הַשָּׁמָֽיִם׃פ\rb* \rb in prayer|וַיִּתְפַּלֵּ֞ל\rb*, \v 21 \rb and the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֤ח\rb* \rb an angel|מַלְאָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb who annihilated|וַיַּכְחֵ֞ד\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb mighty man|גִּבּ֥וֹר\rb* \rb of valor|חַ֙יִל֙\rb* \rb and every leader|וְנָגִ֣יד\rb* \rb and commander|וְשָׂ֔ר\rb* \rb in the camp|בְּמַחֲנֵ֖ה\rb* \rb of the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Assyria|אַשּׁ֑וּר\rb*. \rb So he withdrew|וַיָּשָׁב֩\rb* \rb to his own land|לְאַרְצ֗וֹ\rb* \rb in disgrace|בְּבֹ֨שֶׁת\rb*\rb |פָּנִ֜ים\rb*. \rb And when he entered|וַיָּבֹא֙\rb* \rb the temple|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of his god|אֱלֹהָ֔יו\rb*,\rb |שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb some of his own sons|מֵעָ֔יו\rb* \rb struck him down|הִפִּילֻ֥הוּ\rb* \rb with the sword|בֶחָֽרֶב׃\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb So the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֣ת׀\rb* \rb saved|וַיּוֹשַׁע֩\rb* \rb Hezekiah|יְחִזְקִיָּ֜הוּ\rb* \rb and the people|יֹשְׁבֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֗ם\rb* \rb from the hands|מִיַּ֛ד\rb* \rb of King|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb Sennacherib|סַנְחֵרִ֥יב\rb* \rb of Assyria|אַשּׁ֖וּר\rb* \rb and|וּמִיַּד־\rb* \rb all others|כֹּ֑ל\rb*, \rb and He gave them rest|וַֽיְנַהֲלֵ֖ם\rb* \rb on every side|מִסָּבִֽיב׃\rb*. \v 23 \rb Many|וְ֠רַבִּים\rb* \rb brought|מְבִיאִ֨ים\rb* \rb offerings|מִנְחָ֤ה\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|לִיר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb for the LORD|לַיהוָה֙\rb* \rb and valuable gifts|וּמִ֨גְדָּנ֔וֹת\rb* \rb for Hezekiah|לִֽיחִזְקִיָּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb king of|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and from|מֵאַֽחֲרֵי־\rb* \rb then on|כֵֽן׃ס\rb* \rb he was exalted|וַיִּנַּשֵּׂ֛א\rb* \rb in the eyes|לְעֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb of all|כָל־\rb* \rb nations|הַגּוֹיִ֖ם\rb*.
\s1 Hezekiah’s Illness and Recovery
\r (2 Kings 20:1–11; Isaiah 38:1–8)
\p \v 24 \rb In those|הָהֵ֔ם\rb* \rb days|בַּיָּמִ֣ים\rb* \rb Hezekiah|יְחִזְקִיָּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb became|עַד־\rb* \rb mortally|לָמ֑וּת\rb* \rb ill|חָלָ֥ה\rb*. \rb So he prayed|וַיִּתְפַּלֵּל֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb who spoke|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to him|ל֔וֹ\rb* \rb and gave|נָ֥תַן\rb* \rb him|לֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb a sign|וּמוֹפֵ֖ת\rb*. \v 25 \rb But because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb his heart|לִבּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb was proud|גָבַ֖הּ\rb*, \rb Hezekiah|יְחִזְקִיָּ֔הוּ\rb* \rb did not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb repay|הֵשִׁ֣יב\rb* \rb the favor shown|כִגְמֻ֤ל\rb* \rb to him|עָלָיו֙\rb*. \rb Therefore wrath|קֶ֔צֶף\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֤י\rb* \rb upon him|עָלָיו֙\rb* \rb and upon|וְעַל־\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb and Jerusalem|וִירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 26 \rb Then Hezekiah|יְחִזְקִיָּ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb humbled|וַיִּכָּנַ֤ע\rb* \rb the pride|בְּגֹ֣בַהּ\rb* \rb of his heart|לִבּ֔וֹ\rb*— \rb he|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb and the people|וְיֹשְׁבֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb*— \rb so that the wrath|קֶ֣צֶף\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb did not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb come|בָ֤א\rb* \rb upon them|עֲלֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb during the days|בִּימֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Hezekiah|יְחִזְקִיָּֽהוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 27 \rb Hezekiah|לִֽיחִזְקִיָּ֛הוּ\rb* \rb had|וַיְהִ֧י\rb* \rb very|מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb great|הַרְבֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb riches|עֹ֥שֶׁר\rb* \rb and honor|וְכָב֖וֹד\rb*, \rb and he made|עָֽשָׂה־\rb*\rb |ל֠וֹ\rb* \rb treasuries|וְאֹֽצָר֣וֹת\rb* \rb for his silver|לְכֶ֨סֶף\rb*, \rb gold|וּלְזָהָ֜ב\rb*, \rb precious|יְקָרָ֗ה\rb* \rb stones|וּלְאֶ֣בֶן\rb*, \rb spices|וְלִבְשָׂמִים֙\rb*, \rb shields|וּלְמָ֣גִנִּ֔ים\rb*, \rb and all|וּלְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb kinds of valuable|חֶמְדָּֽה׃\rb* \rb articles|כְּלֵ֥י\rb*. \v 28 \rb He also made storehouses|וּמִ֨סְכְּנ֔וֹת\rb* \rb for the harvest|לִתְבוּאַ֥ת\rb* \rb of grain|דָּגָ֖ן\rb* \rb and new wine|וְתִיר֣וֹשׁ\rb* \rb and oil|וְיִצְהָ֑ר\rb*, \rb stalls|וְאֻֽרָוֺת֙\rb* \rb for all kinds|לְכָל־\rb* \rb of livestock|בְּהֵמָ֣ה\rb*\rb |וּבְהֵמָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and pens|לָאֲוֵרֽוֹת׃\rb* \rb for the flocks|וַעֲדָרִ֖ים\rb*. \v 29 \rb He made|עָ֣שָׂה\rb* \rb cities|וְעָרִים֙\rb* \rb for himself|ל֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and he acquired herds|וּמִקְנֵה־\rb* \rb of sheep|צֹ֥אן\rb* \rb and cattle|וּבָקָ֖ר\rb* \rb in abundance|לָרֹ֑ב\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb gave|נָֽתַן־\rb* \rb him|לוֹ֙\rb* \rb very|מְאֹֽד׃\rb* \rb great|רַ֥ב\rb* \rb wealth|רְכ֖וּשׁ\rb*.
\p \v 30 \rb It was|וְה֣וּא\rb* \rb Hezekiah|יְחִזְקִיָּ֗הוּ\rb* \rb who blocked|סָתַם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the upper|הָֽעֶלְי֔וֹן\rb* \rb outlet|מוֹצָ֞א\rb* \rb of the Spring|מֵימֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Gihon|גִיחוֹן֙\rb* \rb and channeled|וַֽיַּישְּׁרֵ֥ם\rb* \rb it down|לְמַֽטָּה־\rb* \rb to the west side|מַּעְרָ֖בָה\rb* \rb of the City|לְעִ֣יר\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֑יד\rb*. \rb And Hezekiah|יְחִזְקִיָּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb prospered|וַיַּצְלַ֥ח\rb* \rb in all|בְּכָֽל־\rb* \rb that he did|מַעֲשֵֽׂהוּ׃\rb*. \v 31 \rb And so|וְכֵ֞ן\rb* \rb when ambassadors|בִּמְלִיצֵ֣י׀\rb* \rb of the rulers|שָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֗ל\rb* \rb were sent|הַֽמְשַׁלְּחִ֤ים\rb* \rb to him|עָלָיו֙\rb* \rb to inquire about|לִדְרֹ֗שׁ\rb* \rb the wonder|הַמּוֹפֵת֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb had happened|הָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb in the land|בָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*, \rb God|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb* \rb left him|עֲזָב֖וֹ\rb* \rb alone to test him|לְנַ֨סּוֹת֔וֹ\rb*, \rb that He might know|לָדַ֖עַת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that was in Hezekiah’s heart|בִּלְבָבֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\s1 Hezekiah’s Death
\p \v 32 \rb As for the rest|וְיֶ֛תֶר\rb* \rb of the acts of|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb Hezekiah|יְחִזְקִיָּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb and his deeds of loving devotion|וַחֲסָדָ֑יו\rb*, \rb they are indeed|הִנָּ֣ם\rb* \rb written|כְּתוּבִ֗ים\rb* \rb in the vision|בַּחֲז֞וֹן\rb* \rb of the prophet|הַנָּבִ֔יא\rb* \rb Isaiah|יְשַֽׁעְיָ֤הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Amoz|אָמוֹץ֙\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the Book|סֵ֥פֶר\rb* \rb of the Kings|מַלְכֵי־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb and Israel|וְיִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 33 \rb And Hezekiah rested|וַיִּשְׁכַּ֨ב\rb*\rb |יְחִזְקִיָּ֜הוּ\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb his fathers|אֲבֹתָ֗יו\rb* \rb and was buried|וַֽיִּקְבְּרֻהוּ֮\rb* \rb in the upper|בְּֽמַעֲלֵה֮\rb* \rb tombs|קִבְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of David’s|דָוִיד֒\rb* \rb descendants|בְנֵי־\rb*. \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb and the people|וְיֹשְׁבֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb paid|עָֽשׂוּ־\rb* \rb him|ל֣וֹ\rb* \rb honor|וְכָבוֹד֙\rb* \rb at his death|בְמוֹת֔וֹ\rb*. \rb And his son|בְנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֥ה\rb* \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֛ךְ\rb* \rb in his place|תַּחְתָּֽיו׃פ\rb*.
\c 33
\s1 Manasseh Reigns in Judah
\r (2 Kings 21:1–9)
\p \v 1 \rb Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֣ה\rb* \rb was twelve|שְׁתֵּ֥ים\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֛ה\rb* \rb years old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֖ה\rb* \rb when he became king|בְמָלְכ֑וֹ\rb*, \rb and he reigned|מָלַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb* \rb fifty-five|וַחֲמִשִּׁ֤ים\rb*\rb |וְחָמֵשׁ֙\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb*. \v 2 \rb And he did|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb evil|הָרַ֖ע\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb by following the abominations|כְּתֽוֹעֲבוֹת֙\rb* \rb of the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֔ם\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb had driven out|הוֹרִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb before|מִפְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb For he rebuilt|וַיָּ֗שָׁב\rb*\rb |וַיִּ֙בֶן֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the high places|הַבָּמ֔וֹת\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֑יו\rb* \rb Hezekiah|יְחִזְקִיָּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb had torn down|נִתַּ֖ץ\rb*, \rb and he raised up|וַיָּ֨קֶם\rb* \rb altars|מִזְבְּח֤וֹת\rb* \rb for the Baals|לַבְּעָלִים֙\rb* \rb and made|וַיַּ֣עַשׂ\rb* \rb Asherah poles|אֲשֵׁר֔וֹת\rb*. \rb And he worshiped|וַיִּשְׁתַּ֙חוּ֙\rb* \rb and served|וַֽיַּעֲבֹ֖ד\rb* \rb all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the host|צְבָ֣א\rb* \rb of heaven|הַשָּׁמַ֔יִם\rb*\rb |אֹתָֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb Manasseh also built|וּבָנָ֥ה\rb* \rb altars|מִזְבְּח֖וֹת\rb* \rb in the house|בְּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb of which|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb had said|אָמַ֣ר\rb*, “\rb My Name|שְּׁמִ֖י\rb* \rb will remain|יִֽהְיֶה־\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִַ֥ם\rb* \rb forever|לְעוֹלָֽם׃\rb*.” \v 5 \rb In both|בִּשְׁתֵּ֖י\rb* \rb courtyards|חַצְר֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*, \rb he built|וַיִּ֥בֶן\rb* \rb altars|מִזְבְּח֖וֹת\rb* \rb to all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the host|צְבָ֣א\rb* \rb of heaven|הַשָּׁמָ֑יִם\rb*. \v 6 \rb He|וְהוּא֩\rb* \rb sacrificed|הֶעֱבִ֨יר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his sons|בָּנָ֤יו\rb* \rb in the fire|בָּאֵשׁ֙\rb*\f + \fr 33:6 \ft Literally \fqa made his sons pass through the fire\f* \rb in the Valley|בְּגֵ֣י\rb*\rb |בֶן־\rb* \rb of Ben-hinnom|הִנֹּ֔ם\rb*. \rb He practiced sorcery|וְעוֹנֵ֤ן\rb*, \rb divination|וְנִחֵשׁ֙\rb*, \rb and witchcraft|וְֽכִשֵּׁ֔ף\rb*, \rb and consulted|וְעָ֥שָׂה\rb* \rb mediums|א֖וֹב\rb* \rb and spiritists|וְיִדְּעוֹנִ֑י\rb*. \rb He did|לַעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb* \rb great|הִרְבָּ֗ה\rb* \rb evil|הָרַ֛ע\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb provoking Him to anger|לְהַכְעִיסֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb Manasseh even took the carved|פֶּ֥סֶל\rb* \rb image|הַסֶּ֖מֶל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he had made|עָשָׂ֑ה\rb* \rb and set it up|וַיָּ֕שֶׂם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb in the house|בְּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb*, \rb of which|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb had said|אָמַ֤ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִיד֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and his son|בְנ֔וֹ\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֣ה\rb*, “\rb In this|הַזֶּ֜ה\rb* \rb temple|בַּבַּ֨יִת\rb* \rb and in Jerusalem|וּבִֽירוּשָׁלִַ֗ם\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb I have chosen|בָּחַ֙רְתִּי֙\rb* \rb out of all|מִכֹּל֙\rb* \rb the tribes|שִׁבְטֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb I will establish|אָשִׂ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My Name|שְׁמִ֖י\rb* \rb forever|לְעֵילֽוֹם׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb I will never|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb again|אוֹסִ֗יף\rb* \rb cause the feet|רֶ֣גֶל\rb* \rb of the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb to leave|לְהָסִיר֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |מֵעַל֙\rb* \rb the land|הָֽאֲדָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I assigned|הֶֽעֱמַ֖דְתִּי\rb* \rb to your fathers|לַאֲבֹֽתֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb only|רַ֣ק׀\rb* \rb they are careful|יִשְׁמְר֣וּ\rb* \rb to do|לַעֲשׂ֗וֹת\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I have commanded them|צִוִּיתִ֔ים\rb* \rb through|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶֽׁה׃\rb*— \rb all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the laws|הַתּוֹרָ֛ה\rb*, \rb statutes|וְהַֽחֻקִּ֥ים\rb*, \rb and judgments|וְהַמִּשְׁפָּטִ֖ים\rb*.”
\p \v 9 \rb So Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb led the people|וְיֹשְׁבֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb and Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb astray|וַיֶּ֣תַע\rb*, \rb so that they did|לַעֲשׂ֣וֹת\rb* \rb greater evil|רָ֔ע\rb* \rb than|מִן־\rb* \rb the nations|הַ֨גּוֹיִ֔ם\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb had destroyed|הִשְׁמִ֣יד\rb* \rb before|מִפְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃פ\rb*.
\s1 Manasseh’s Repentance and Restoration
\r (2 Kings 21:10–18)
\p \v 10 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb spoke|וַיְדַבֵּ֧ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and his people|עַמּ֖וֹ\rb*, \rb but they did not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb listen|הִקְשִֽׁיבוּ׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb So the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb brought|וַיָּבֵ֨א\rb* \rb against them|עֲלֵיהֶ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the military|הַצָּבָא֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb commanders|שָׂרֵ֤י\rb* \rb of the king|לְמֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Assyria|אַשּׁ֔וּר\rb*, \rb who captured|וַיִּלְכְּד֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֖ה\rb*, \rb put a hook in his nose|בַּחֹחִ֑ים\rb*, \rb bound him|וַיַּֽאַסְרֻ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb with bronze shackles|בַּֽנְחֻשְׁתַּ֔יִם\rb*, \rb and took him|וַיּוֹלִיכֻ֖הוּ\rb* \rb to Babylon|בָּבֶֽלָה׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb And in his distress|וּכְהָצֵ֣ר\rb*, \rb Manasseh sought|חִלָּ֕ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the favor|פְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb his God|אֱלֹהָ֑יו\rb* \rb and earnestly|מְאֹ֔ד\rb* \rb humbled himself|וַיִּכָּנַ֣ע\rb* \rb before|מִלִּפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of his fathers|אֲבֹתָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb And when he prayed|וַיִּתְפַּלֵּ֣ל\rb* \rb to Him|אֵלָ֗יו\rb*, \rb the LORD received his plea|וַיֵּעָ֤תֶר\rb* \rb and heard|וַיִּשְׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb his petition|תְּחִנָּת֔וֹ\rb*. \rb So He brought him back|וַיְשִׁיבֵ֥הוּ\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \rb and to his kingdom|לְמַלְכוּת֑וֹ\rb*. \rb Then Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֔ה\rb* \rb knew|וַיֵּ֣דַע\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |ה֥וּא\rb* \rb is God|הָֽאֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb After|וְאַחֲרֵי־\rb* \rb this|כֵ֡ן\rb*, \rb Manasseh rebuilt|בָּנָ֣ה\rb* \rb the outer|חִֽיצוֹנָ֣ה׀\rb* \rb wall|חוֹמָ֣ה\rb* \rb of the City|לְעִיר־\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֡יד\rb* \rb from west|מַעְרָבָה֩\rb* \rb of Gihon|לְגִיח֨וֹן\rb* \rb in the valley|בַּנַּ֜חַל\rb* \rb to the entrance|וְלָב֨וֹא\rb* \rb of the Fish|הַדָּגִים֙\rb* \rb Gate|בְשַׁ֤עַר\rb*, \rb and he brought it around|וְסָבַ֣ב\rb* \rb the hill of Ophel|לָעֹ֔פֶל\rb* \rb and heightened it|וַיַּגְבִּיהֶ֖הָ\rb* \rb considerably|מְאֹ֑ד\rb*. \rb He also stationed|וַיָּ֧שֶׂם\rb* \rb military|חַ֛יִל\rb* \rb commanders|שָֽׂרֵי־\rb* \rb in all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the fortified|הַבְּצֻר֖וֹת\rb* \rb cities|הֶעָרִ֥ים\rb* \rb of Judah|בִּיהוּדָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb He removed|וַ֠יָּסַר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the foreign|הַנֵּכָ֤ר\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb gods|אֱלֹהֵ֨י\rb* \rb and the idol|הַסֶּ֙מֶל֙\rb* \rb from the house|מִבֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb along with all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the altars|הַֽמִּזְבְּח֗וֹת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he had built|בָּנָ֛ה\rb* \rb on the temple|בֵּית־\rb*\rb |יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb mount|בְּהַ֥ר\rb*\f + \fr 33:15 \ft Literally \fqa the mountain of the house of the LORD\f* \rb and in Jerusalem|וּבִירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb*, \rb and he dumped them|וַיַּשְׁלֵ֖ךְ\rb* \rb outside|ח֥וּצָה\rb* \rb the city|לָעִֽיר׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb Then he restored|וַיָּכֶן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the altar|מִזְבַּ֣ח\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and sacrificed|וַיִּזְבַּ֣ח\rb* \rb peace offerings|שְׁלָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb and thank|וְתוֹדָ֑ה\rb* \rb offerings|זִבְחֵ֥י\rb* \rb on it|עָלָ֔יו\rb*, \rb and he told|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb Judah|לִֽיהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb to serve|לַעֲב֕וֹד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb Nevertheless|אֲבָל֙\rb*, \rb the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb still|ע֣וֹד\rb* \rb sacrificed|זֹבְחִ֖ים\rb* \rb at the high places|בַּבָּמ֑וֹת\rb*, \rb but only|רַ֖ק\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb their God|אֱלֹהֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb As for the rest|וְיֶ֨תֶר\rb* \rb of the acts|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁה֮\rb*, \rb along with his prayer|וּתְפִלָּת֣וֹ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his God|אֱלֹהָיו֒\rb* \rb and the words|וְדִבְרֵי֙\rb* \rb of the seers|הַֽחֹזִ֔ים\rb* \rb who spoke|הַֽמְדַבְּרִ֣ים\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֔יו\rb* \rb in the name|בְּשֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb they are indeed|הִנָּ֕ם\rb* \rb written in|עַל־\rb* \rb the Chronicles|דִּבְרֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the Kings|מַלְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.\f + \fr 33:18 \ft That is, Judah; in 2 Chronicles, Judah is occasionally called Israel, as representative of the true Israel.\f* \v 19 \rb His prayer|וּתְפִלָּת֣וֹ\rb* \rb and how God received his plea|וְהֵֽעָתֶר־\rb*, \rb as well as all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his sin|חַטָּאת֣וֹ\rb* \rb and unfaithfulness|וּמַעְלוֹ֒\rb*, \rb and the sites|וְהַמְּקֹמ֗וֹת\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb he built|בָּנָ֨ה\rb* \rb high places|בָּמוֹת֙\rb* \rb and set up|וְהֶעֱמִיד֙\rb* \rb Asherah poles|הָאֲשֵׁרִ֣ים\rb* \rb and idols|וְהַפְּסִלִ֔ים\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb he humbled himself|הִכָּנְע֑וֹ\rb*, \rb they are indeed|הִנָּ֣ם\rb* \rb written|כְּתוּבִ֔ים\rb* \rb in|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb the Records|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the Seers|חוֹזָֽי׃\rb*.\f + \fr 33:19 \ft Or \fqa the Records of the Hozai \ft or \fqa the Annals of the Prophets\f* \v 20 \rb And Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁה֙\rb* \rb rested|וַיִּשְׁכַּ֤ב\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb his fathers|אֲבֹתָ֔יו\rb* \rb and was buried|וַֽיִּקְבְּרֻ֖הוּ\rb* \rb at his palace|בֵּית֑וֹ\rb*. \rb And his son|בְּנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Amon|אָמ֥וֹן\rb* \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֛ךְ\rb* \rb in his place|תַּחְתָּֽיו׃פ\rb*.
\s1 Amon Reigns in Judah
\r (2 Kings 21:19–26)
\p \v 21 \rb Amon|אָמ֣וֹן\rb* \rb was twenty-two|עֶשְׂרִ֧ים\rb*\rb |וּשְׁתַּ֛יִם\rb* \rb years old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֖ה\rb* \rb when he became king|בְּמָלְכ֑וֹ\rb*, \rb and he reigned|מָלַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּֽירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb* \rb two|וּשְׁתַּ֣יִם\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִ֔ים\rb*. \v 22 \rb And he did|וַיַּ֤עַשׂ\rb* \rb evil|הָרַע֙\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֑יו\rb* \rb Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֣ה\rb* \rb had done|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb*.
\p \rb Amon|אָמ֖וֹן\rb* \rb served|וַיַּֽעַבְדֵֽם׃\rb* \rb and sacrificed|זִבַּ֥ח\rb* \rb to all|וּֽלְכָל־\rb* \rb the idols|הַפְּסִילִ֗ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֔יו\rb* \rb Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֣ה\rb* \rb had made|עָשָׂה֙\rb*, \v 23 \rb but he did not|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb humble himself|נִכְנַע֙\rb* \rb before|מִלִּפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb as his father|אָבִ֑יו\rb* \rb Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֣ה\rb* \rb had done|כְּהִכָּנַ֖ע\rb*; \rb instead|כִּ֛י\rb*,\rb |ה֥וּא\rb* \rb Amon|אָמ֖וֹן\rb* \rb increased|הִרְבָּ֥ה\rb* \rb his guilt|אַשְׁמָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 24 \rb Then the servants of Amon|עֲבָדָ֔יו\rb* \rb conspired|וַיִּקְשְׁר֤וּ\rb* \rb against him|עָלָיו֙\rb* \rb and killed him|וַיְמִיתֻ֖הוּ\rb* \rb in his palace|בְּבֵיתֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 25 \rb But the people|עַם־\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb killed|וַיַּכּוּ֙\rb* \rb all those|כָּל־\rb* \rb who had conspired|הַקֹּֽשְׁרִ֖ים\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Amon|אָמ֑וֹן\rb*, \rb and they made his son|בְנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Josiah|יֹאשִׁיָּ֥הוּ\rb* \rb king|וַיַּמְלִ֧יכוּ\rb*\rb |עַם־\rb*\rb |הָאָ֛רֶץ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb in his place|תַּחְתָּֽיו׃פ\rb*.
\c 34
\s1 Josiah Reigns in Judah
\r (2 Kings 22:1–2)
\p \v 1 \rb Josiah|יֹאשִׁיָּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb was eight|שְׁמוֹנֶ֥ה\rb* \rb years old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנִ֖ים\rb* \rb when he became king|בְמָלְכ֑וֹ\rb*, \rb and he reigned|מָלַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb* \rb thirty-one|וּשְׁלֹשִׁ֤ים\rb*\rb |וְאַחַת֙\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb*. \v 2 \rb And he did|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb what was right|הַיָּשָׁ֖ר\rb* \rb in the eyes|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and walked|וַיֵּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb in the ways|בְּדַרְכֵי֙\rb* \rb of his father|אָבִ֔יו\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֣יד\rb*; \rb he did not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb turn aside|סָ֖ר\rb* \rb to the right|יָמִ֥ין\rb* \rb or to the left|וּשְׂמֹֽאול׃\rb*.
\s1 Josiah Destroys Idolatry
\r (1 Kings 13:1–10; 2 Kings 23:4–20)
\p \v 3 \rb In the eighth|וּבִשְׁמוֹנֶ֨ה\rb* \rb year|שָׁנִ֜ים\rb* \rb of his reign|לְמָלְכ֗וֹ\rb*, \rb while he|וְהוּא֙\rb* \rb was still|עוֹדֶ֣נּוּ\rb* \rb young|נַ֔עַר\rb*, \rb Josiah began|הֵחֵ֕ל\rb* \rb to seek|לִדְר֕וֹשׁ\rb* \rb the God|לֵאלֹהֵ֖י\rb* \rb of his father|אָבִ֑יו\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֣יד\rb*, \rb and in the twelfth|וּבִשְׁתֵּ֧ים\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֣ה\rb* \rb year|שָׁנָ֗ה\rb* \rb he began|הֵחֵל֙\rb* \rb to cleanse|לְטַהֵ֔ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb* \rb and Jerusalem|וִיר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb the high places|הַבָּמוֹת֙\rb*, \rb the Asherah poles|וְהָ֣אֲשֵׁרִ֔ים\rb*, \rb the carved idols|וְהַפְּסִלִ֖ים\rb*, \rb and the cast images|וְהַמַּסֵּכֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb Then in his presence|לְפָנָ֗יו\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb the altars|מִזְבְּח֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the Baals|הַבְּעָלִ֔ים\rb* \rb were torn down|וַיְנַתְּצ֣וּ\rb*, \rb and he cut to pieces|גִּדֵּ֑עַ\rb* \rb the incense altars|וְהַֽחַמָּנִ֛ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb were above|לְמַ֥עְלָה\rb* \rb them|מֵעֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*. \rb He shattered|שִׁבַּ֣ר\rb* \rb the Asherah poles|וְ֠הָאֲשֵׁרִים\rb*, \rb the carved idols|וְהַפְּסִלִ֤ים\rb*, \rb and the cast images|וְהַמַּסֵּכוֹת֙\rb*, \rb crushed them to dust|וְהֵדַ֔ק\rb*, \rb and scattered them|וַיִּזְרֹק֙\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the graves|הַקְּבָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb of those who had sacrificed|הַזֹּבְחִ֖ים\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb Then he burned|שָׂרַ֖ף\rb* \rb the bones|וְעַצְמוֹת֙\rb* \rb of the priests|כֹּֽהֲנִ֔ים\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb their altars|מִזְבְּחוֹתָים\rb*. \rb So he cleansed|וַיְטַהֵ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb Josiah did the same in the cities|וּבְעָרֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֧ה\rb*, \rb Ephraim|וְאֶפְרַ֛יִם\rb*, \rb and Simeon|וְשִׁמְע֖וֹן\rb*, \rb as|וְעַד־\rb* \rb far as Naphtali|נַפְתָּלִ֑י\rb*, \rb and in the ruins|בְּהַר\rb*\rb |בָּתֵּיהֶם\rb*\f + \fr 34:6 \ft Or \fqa in the regions\f* \rb around them|סָבִֽיב׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb He tore down|וַיְנַתֵּ֣ץ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the altars|הַֽמִּזְבְּח֗וֹת\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Asherah poles|הָאֲשֵׁרִ֤ים\rb*, \rb crushed|כִּתַּ֣ת\rb* \rb the idols|וְהַפְּסִלִים֙\rb* \rb to powder|לְהֵדַ֔ק\rb*, \rb and cut to pieces|גִּדַּ֖ע\rb* \rb all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the incense altars|הַֽחַמָּנִ֥ים\rb* \rb throughout|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*. \rb Then he returned|וַיָּ֖שָׁב\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|לִירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃ס\rb*.
\s1 Josiah Repairs the Temple
\r (2 Kings 22:3–7)
\p \v 8 \rb Now in the eighteenth|שְׁמוֹנֶ֤ה\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵה֙\rb* \rb year|וּבִשְׁנַ֨ת\rb* \rb of his reign|לְמָלְכ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb in order to cleanse|לְטַהֵ֥ר\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb and the temple|וְהַבָּ֑יִת\rb*, \rb Josiah sent|שָׁ֠לַח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Shaphan|שָׁפָ֨ן\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Azaliah|אֲצַלְיָ֜הוּ\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Maaseiah|מַעֲשֵׂיָ֣הוּ\rb* \rb the governor|שַׂר־\rb* \rb of the city|הָעִ֗יר\rb*, \rb and|וְ֠אֵת\rb* \rb Joah|יוֹאָ֤ח\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Joahaz|יֽוֹאָחָז֙\rb*, \rb the recorder|הַמַּזְכִּ֔יר\rb*, \rb to repair|לְחַזֵּ֕ק\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֖ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb his God|אֱלֹהָֽיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb So they went|וַיָּבֹ֜אוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Hilkiah|חִלְקִיָּ֣הוּ׀\rb* \rb the high|הַגָּד֗וֹל\rb* \rb priest|הַכֹּהֵ֣ן\rb* \rb and gave|וַֽיִּתְּנוּ֮\rb* \rb him|אֶת־\rb* \rb the money|הַכֶּסֶף֮\rb* \rb that had been brought|הַמּוּבָ֣א\rb* \rb into the house|בֵית־\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִים֒\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the Levites|הַלְוִיִּם֩\rb* \rb who guarded|שֹׁמְרֵ֨י\rb* \rb the doors|הַסַּ֜ף\rb* \rb had collected|אָסְפֽוּ־\rb* \rb from the people|מִיַּ֧ד\rb* \rb of Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֣ה\rb* \rb and Ephraim|וְאֶפְרַ֗יִם\rb*, \rb from all|וּמִכֹּל֙\rb* \rb the remnant|שְׁאֵרִ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb from all|וּמִכָּל־\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb and Benjamin|וּבִנְיָמִ֑ן\rb*, \rb and from the people|וְיֹשְׁבֵי\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרֽוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb They put it|וַֽיִּתְּנ֗וּ\rb* \rb into|עַל־\rb* \rb the hands|יַד֙\rb* \rb of those supervising|הַמֻּפְקָדִ֖ים\rb*\rb |הַמְּלָאכָ֔ה\rb* \rb the work|עֹשֵׂ֣ה\rb* \rb in the house|בְּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb who in turn gave|וַיִּתְּנ֨וּ\rb* \rb it|אֹת֜וֹ\rb* \rb to the workmen|עוֹשֵׂ֣י\rb*\rb |הַמְּלָאכָ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb*\rb |עֹשִׂים֙\rb* \rb restoring|לִבְדּ֥וֹק\rb* \rb and repairing|וּלְחַזֵּ֖ק\rb* \rb the house|בְּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*. \v 11 \rb They also gave money|וַֽיִּתְּנ֗וּ\rb* \rb to the carpenters|לֶחָֽרָשִׁים֙\rb* \rb and builders|וְלַבֹּנִ֔ים\rb* \rb to buy|לִקְנוֹת֙\rb* \rb dressed|מַחְצֵ֔ב\rb* \rb stone|אַבְנֵ֣י\rb*, \rb as well as timbers|וְעֵצִ֖ים\rb* \rb for couplings|לַֽמְחַבְּר֑וֹת\rb* \rb and beams|וּלְקָרוֹת֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb for the buildings|הַבָּ֣תִּ֔ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the kings|מַלְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb* \rb had allowed to deteriorate|הִשְׁחִ֖יתוּ\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb And the men|וְהָאֲנָשִׁים֩\rb* \rb did|עֹשִׂ֨ים\rb* \rb the work|בַּמְּלָאכָ֗ה\rb*\rb |וַעֲלֵיהֶ֣ם׀\rb* \rb faithfully|בֶּאֱמוּנָ֜ה\rb*. \rb The Levites|הַלְוִיִּם֙\rb* \rb overseeing them|מֻ֠פְקָדִים\rb* \rb were Jahath|יַ֣חַת\rb* \rb and Obadiah|וְעֹבַדְיָ֤הוּ\rb*, \rb descendants|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Merari|מְרָרִ֔י\rb*, \rb and Zechariah|וּזְכַרְיָ֧ה\rb* \rb and Meshullam|וּמְשֻׁלָּ֛ם\rb*,\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb descendants|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Kohath|הַקְּהָתִ֖ים\rb*\rb |לְנַצֵּ֑חַ\rb*. \rb Other Levites|וְהַ֨לְוִיִּ֔ם\rb*, \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb skilled|מֵבִ֖ין\rb* \rb with musical|שִֽׁיר׃\rb* \rb instruments|בִּכְלֵי־\rb*, \v 13 \rb were over|וְעַ֣ל\rb* \rb the laborers|הַסַּבָּלִ֗ים\rb* \rb and supervised|וּֽמְנַצְּחִים֙\rb* \rb all|לְכֹל֙\rb* \rb who did|עֹשֵׂ֣ה\rb* \rb the work|מְלָאכָ֔ה\rb*, \rb task|לַעֲבוֹדָ֖ה\rb* \rb by task|וַעֲבוֹדָ֑ה\rb*. \rb Some of the Levites|וּמֵֽהַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb* \rb were secretaries|סוֹפְרִ֥ים\rb*, \rb officers|וְשֹׁטְרִ֖ים\rb*, \rb and gatekeepers|וְשׁוֹעֲרִֽים׃\rb*.
\s1 Hilkiah Finds the Book of the Law
\r (2 Kings 22:8–13)
\p \v 14 \rb While they were bringing out|וּבְהוֹצִיאָ֣ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the money|הַכֶּ֔סֶף\rb* \rb that had been taken|הַמּוּבָ֖א\rb* \rb into the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb Hilkiah|חִלְקִיָּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb found|מָצָא֙\rb* \rb the Book|סֵ֥פֶר\rb* \rb of the Law|תּֽוֹרַת־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb given by|בְּיַד־\rb*\f + \fr 34:14 \ft Hebrew \fqa the Law of the LORD by the hand of\f* \rb Moses|מֹשֶֽׁה׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb And Hilkiah|חִלְקִיָּ֗הוּ\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb said|וַיַּ֣עַן\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Shaphan|שָׁפָ֣ן\rb* \rb the scribe|הַסּוֹפֵ֔ר\rb*, “\rb I have found|מָצָ֖אתִי\rb* \rb the Book|סֵ֧פֶר\rb* \rb of the Law|הַתּוֹרָ֛ה\rb* \rb in the house|בְּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*!” \rb And he|חִלְקִיָּ֛הוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb gave|וַיִּתֵּ֧ן\rb* \rb it|הַסֵּ֖פֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Shaphan|שָׁפָֽן׃\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb Then Shaphan|שָׁפָ֤ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb brought|וַיָּבֵ֨א\rb* \rb the book|הַסֵּ֙פֶר֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb and|ע֧וֹד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הַמֶּ֛לֶךְ\rb* \rb reported|וַיָּ֨שֶׁב\rb*\rb |דָּבָ֖ר\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, “\rb Your servants|עֲבָדֶ֖יךָ\rb*\rb |הֵ֥ם\rb* \rb are doing|עֹשִֽׂים׃\rb* \rb all|כֹּ֛ל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb has been placed|נִתַּ֥ן\rb* \rb in their hands|בְּיַד־\rb*. \v 17 \rb They have paid out|וַיַּתִּ֕יכוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the money|הַכֶּ֖סֶף\rb* \rb that was found|הַנִּמְצָ֣א\rb* \rb in the house|בְּבֵית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and have put|וַֽיִּתְּנ֗וּהוּ\rb* \rb it into|עַל־\rb* \rb the hands|יַד֙\rb* \rb of the supervisors|הַמֻּפְקָדִ֔ים\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and|יַ֖ד\rb*\rb |עוֹשֵׂ֥י\rb* \rb workers|הַמְּלָאכָֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 18 \rb Moreover , Shaphan|שָׁפָ֤ן\rb* \rb the scribe|הַסּוֹפֵר֙\rb* \rb told|וַיַּגֵּ֞ד\rb* \rb the king|לַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, “\rb Hilkiah|חִלְקִיָּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֑ן\rb* \rb has given|נָ֣תַן\rb* \rb me|לִ֔י\rb* \rb a book|סֵ֚פֶר\rb*.” \rb And Shaphan|שָׁפָ֖ן\rb* \rb read|וַיִּקְרָא־\rb* \rb it|ב֥וֹ\rb* \rb in the presence|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb |וַיְהִי֙\rb* \rb When the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb heard|כִּשְׁמֹ֣עַ\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Law|הַתּוֹרָ֑ה\rb*, \rb he tore|וַיִּקְרַ֖ע\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his clothes|בְּגָדָֽיו׃\rb* \v 20 \rb and|הַמֶּ֡לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb commanded|וַיְצַ֣ו\rb* \rb Hilkiah|חִלְקִיָּ֡הוּ\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Ahikam|אֲחִיקָ֣ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Shaphan|שָׁ֠פָן\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Abdon|עַבְדּ֨וֹן\rb*\f + \fr 34:20 \fqa Abdon \ft is a variant of \fqa Achbor\ft ; see 2 Kings 22:12.\f* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Micah|מִיכָ֜ה\rb*,\f + \fr 34:20 \fqa Micah \ft is a variant of \fqa Micaiah\ft ; see 2 Kings 22:12.\f*\rb |וְאֵ֣ת׀\rb* \rb Shaphan|שָׁפָ֣ן\rb* \rb the scribe|הַסּוֹפֵ֗ר\rb*,\rb |וְאֵ֛ת\rb* \rb and Asaiah|עֲשָׂיָ֥ה\rb* \rb the servant|עֶֽבֶד־\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*: \v 21 “\rb Go|לְכוּ֩\rb* \rb and inquire|דִרְשׁ֨וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb for me|בַּעֲדִ֗י\rb* \rb and for|וּבְעַד֙\rb* \rb those remaining|הַנִּשְׁאָר֙\rb* \rb in Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֣ל\rb* \rb and Judah|וּבִֽיהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb concerning|עַל־\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb in the book|הַסֵּ֖פֶר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb has been found|נִמְצָ֑א\rb*. \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb great is|גְדוֹלָ֤ה\rb* \rb the wrath|חֲמַת־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb has been poured out|נִתְּכָ֣ה\rb* \rb on us|בָ֔נוּ\rb* \rb because|עַל֩\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb our fathers|אֲבוֹתֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb have not|לֹא־\rb* \rb kept|שָׁמְר֤וּ\rb* \rb the word|דְּבַ֣ר\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb by doing|לַעֲשׂ֕וֹת\rb* \rb all|כְּכָל־\rb* \rb that is written|הַכָּת֖וּב\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃פ\rb* \rb book|הַסֵּ֥פֶר\rb*.”
\s1 Huldah’s Prophecy
\r (2 Kings 22:14–20)
\p \v 22 \rb So Hilkiah|חִלְקִיָּ֜הוּ\rb* \rb and those|וַאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the king had designated|הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb and spoke|וַיְדַבְּר֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֵלֶ֖יהָ\rb*\rb |כָּזֹֽאת׃ס\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Huldah|חֻלְדָּ֨ה\rb*\f + \fr 34:22 \ft One Hebrew manuscript, Vulgate, and Syriac; most Hebrew manuscripts \fqa and those the king had told went to Huldah\f* \rb the prophetess|הַנְּבִיאָ֜ה\rb*, \rb the wife|אֵ֣שֶׁת׀\rb* \rb of Shallum|שַׁלֻּ֣ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Tokhath|תּוֹקְהַת\rb*,\f + \fr 34:22 \fqa Tokhath \ft is a variant of \fqa Tikvah\ft ; see 2 Kings 22:14.\f* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Hasrah|חַסְרָה֙\rb*,\f + \fr 34:22 \fqa Hasrah \ft is a variant of \fqa Harhas\ft ; see 2 Kings 22:14.\f* \rb the keeper|שׁוֹמֵ֣ר\rb* \rb of the wardrobe|הַבְּגָדִ֔ים\rb*. \rb She|וְהִ֛יא\rb* \rb lived|יוֹשֶׁ֥בֶת\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb*, \rb in the Second District|בַּמִּשְׁנֶ֑ה\rb*.\f + \fr 34:22 \ft Or \fqa the Second Quarter\ft , a newer section of Jerusalem; Hebrew \fqa the Mishneh\f*
\p \v 23 \rb And Huldah said|וַתֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶ֔ם\rb*, “\rb This is what|כֹּה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb says|אָמַ֥ר\rb*: ‘\rb Tell|אִמְר֣וּ\rb* \rb the man|לָאִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb sent|שָׁלַ֥ח\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֵלָֽי׃ס\rb* \v 24 \rb that this is what|כֹּ֚ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |הִנְנִ֨י\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר\rb*: \rb I am about to bring|מֵבִ֥יא\rb* \rb calamity|רָעָ֛ה\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb place|הַמָּק֥וֹם\rb* \rb and on|וְעַל־\rb* \rb its people|יוֹשְׁבָ֑יו\rb*,\rb |אֵ֤ת\rb* \rb according to all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the curses|הָאָלוֹת֙\rb* \rb written|הַכְּתוּב֣וֹת\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the book|הַסֵּ֔פֶר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb has been read|קָֽרְא֔וּ\rb* \rb in the presence|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb*, \v 25 \rb because|תַּ֣חַת׀\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb they have forsaken Me|עֲזָב֗וּנִי\rb* \rb and burned incense|וַיַּקְטִירוּ\rb* \rb to other|אֲחֵרִ֔ים\rb* \rb gods|לֵֽאלֹהִ֣ים\rb*, \rb that|לְמַ֙עַן֙\rb* \rb they might provoke Me to anger|הַכְעִיסֵ֔נִי\rb* \rb with all|בְּכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the works|מַעֲשֵׂ֣י\rb* \rb of their hands|יְדֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb My wrath|חֲמָתִ֛י\rb* \rb will be poured out|וְתִתַּ֧ךְ\rb* \rb upon this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb place|בַּמָּק֥וֹם\rb* \rb and will not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb be quenched|תִכְבֶּֽה׃\rb*.’
\p \v 26 \rb But as for|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb*, \rb who sent|הַשֹּׁלֵ֤חַ\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶם֙\rb* \rb to inquire|לִדְר֣וֹשׁ\rb* \rb of the LORD|בַּֽיהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb tell him|תֹאמְר֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֑יוס\rb* \rb that|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb says|אָמַ֤ר\rb*: ‘\rb As for the words|הַדְּבָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you heard|שָׁמָֽעְתָּ׃\rb*, \v 27 \rb because|יַ֠עַן\rb* \rb your heart|לְבָ֨בְךָ֜\rb* \rb was tender|רַךְ־\rb* \rb and you humbled yourself|וַתִּכָּנַ֣ע׀\rb* \rb before|מִלִּפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb when you heard|בְּשָׁמְעֲךָ֤\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb His words|דְּבָרָיו֙\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb place|הַמָּק֤וֹם\rb* \rb and against|וְעַל־\rb* \rb its people|יֹ֣שְׁבָ֔יו\rb*, \rb and because you have humbled yourself|וַתִּכָּנַ֣ע\rb* \rb before Me|לְפָנַ֔י\rb* \rb and have torn|וַתִּקְרַ֥ע\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your clothes|בְּגָדֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb and wept|וַתֵּ֣בְךְּ\rb* \rb before Me|לְפָנָ֑י\rb*,\rb |וְגַם־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb have heard you|שָׁמַ֖עְתִּי\rb*,’ \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 28 ‘\rb Now I will indeed|הִנְנִ֨י\rb* \rb gather|אֹֽסִפְךָ֜\rb* \rb you to|אֶל־\rb* \rb your fathers|אֲבֹתֶ֗יךָ\rb*, \rb and you will be gathered|וְנֶאֱסַפְתָּ֣\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb your grave|קִבְרֹתֶיךָ֮\rb* \rb in peace|בְּשָׁלוֹם֒\rb*. \rb Your eyes|עֵינֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb will not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb see|תִרְאֶ֣ינָה\rb* \rb all|בְּכֹל֙\rb* \rb the calamity|הָֽרָעָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb will bring|מֵבִ֛יא\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb place|הַמָּק֥וֹם\rb* \rb and on|וְעַל־\rb* \rb its people|יֹשְׁבָ֑יו\rb*.’”
\p \rb So they brought|וַיָּשִׁ֥יבוּ\rb* \rb her|אֶת־\rb* \rb answer|דָּבָֽר׃פ\rb* \rb back to the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*.
\s1 Josiah Renews the Covenant
\r (2 Kings 23:1–3)
\p \v 29 \rb Then the king|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb summoned|וַיִּשְׁלַ֖ח\rb*\rb |וַיֶּאֱסֹ֕ף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the elders|זִקְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb and Jerusalem|וִירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*. \v 30 \rb And he|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb went up|וַיַּ֣עַל\rb* \rb to the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְ֠הוָה\rb* \rb with all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|וְיֹשְׁבֵ֣י\rb*\rb |אִ֨ישׁ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֜ה\rb* \rb and Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֗ם\rb*, \rb as well as the priests|וְהַכֹּֽהֲנִים֙\rb* \rb and the Levites|וְהַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb*— \rb all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb great|מִגָּד֣וֹל\rb* \rb and|וְעַד־\rb* \rb small|קָטָ֑ן\rb*— \rb and in their hearing|בְאָזְנֵיהֶ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb he read|וַיִּקְרָ֣א\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵי֙\rb* \rb of the Book|סֵ֣פֶר\rb* \rb of the Covenant|הַבְּרִ֔ית\rb* \rb that had been found|הַנִּמְצָ֖א\rb* \rb in the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 31 \rb So the king|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb stood|וַיַּעֲמֹ֨ד\rb* \rb by|עַל־\rb* \rb the pillar|עָמְד֗וֹ\rb* \rb and made|וַיִּכְרֹ֣ת\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb a covenant|הַבְּרִית֮\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֒\rb* \rb to follow|לָלֶ֜כֶת\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb and to keep|וְלִשְׁמ֤וֹר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb His commandments|מִצְוֺתָיו֙\rb*, \rb decrees|וְעֵֽדְוֺתָ֣יו\rb*, \rb and statutes|וְחֻקָּ֔יו\rb* \rb with all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb his heart|לְבָב֖וֹ\rb* \rb and all|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb his soul|נַפְשׁ֑וֹ\rb*, \rb and to carry out|לַעֲשׂוֹת֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the covenant|הַבְּרִ֔ית\rb* \rb that were written|הַכְּתוּבִ֖ים\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb book|הַסֵּ֥פֶר\rb*.
\p \v 32 \rb Then he had everyone|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הַנִּמְצָ֥א\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִירוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \rb and Benjamin|וּבִנְיָמִ֑ן\rb* \rb take a stand in agreement to it|וַיַּעֲמֵ֕ד\rb*\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb*. \rb So all the people|יֹשְׁבֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb carried out|וַֽיַּעֲשׂוּ֙\rb* \rb the covenant|כִּבְרִ֥ית\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of their fathers|אֲבוֹתֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 33 \rb And Josiah|יֹֽאשִׁיָּ֜הוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb removed|וַיָּ֨סַר\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the abominations|הַתּוֹעֵב֗וֹת\rb* \rb from all|מִֽכָּל־\rb* \rb the lands|הָאֲרָצוֹת֮\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb belonging to the Israelites|לִבְנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֒\rb*, \rb and he required|וַֽיַּעֲבֵ֗ד\rb*\rb |אֵ֤ת\rb* \rb everyone|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הַנִּמְצָא֙\rb* \rb in Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb to serve|לַעֲב֖וֹד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb their God|אֱלֹהֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb Throughout|כָּל־\rb* \rb his reign|יָמָ֕יו\rb* \rb they did not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb turn aside|סָ֔רוּ\rb* \rb from following|מֵֽאַחֲרֵ֕י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of their fathers|אֲבוֹתֵיהֶֽם׃פ\rb*.
\c 35
\s1 Josiah Restores the Passover
\r (2 Kings 23:21–27)
\p \v 1 \rb Then Josiah|יֹאשִׁיָּ֧הוּ\rb* \rb kept|וַיַּ֨עַשׂ\rb* \rb the Passover|פֶּ֖סַח\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִֽירוּשָׁלִַ֛ם\rb*, \rb and the Passover lamb|הַפֶּ֔סַח\rb* \rb was slaughtered|וַיִּשְׁחֲט֣וּ\rb* \rb on the fourteenth|בְּאַרְבָּעָ֥ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֖ר\rb* \rb day of the first|הָרִאשֽׁוֹן׃\rb* \rb month|לַחֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb*. \v 2 \rb He appointed|וַיַּעֲמֵ֥ד\rb* \rb the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֖ים\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb their duties|מִשְׁמְרוֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb and encouraged them|וַֽיְחַזְּקֵ֔ם\rb* \rb in the service|לַעֲבוֹדַ֖ת\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb To the Levites|לַ֠לְוִיִּם\rb* \rb who taught|הַמְּבוּנִים\rb* \rb all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֜ל\rb* \rb and were holy|הַקְּדוֹשִׁ֣ים\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֗ה\rb*, \rb Josiah said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*: “\rb Put|תְּנ֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the holy|הַקֹּ֙דֶשׁ֙\rb* \rb ark|אֲרוֹן־\rb* \rb in the temple|בַּ֠בַּיִת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb built|בָּנָ֜ה\rb* \rb by Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֤ה\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִיד֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*. \rb It is not to be|אֵין־\rb* \rb carried around|מַשָּׂ֖א\rb* \rb on your shoulders|בַּכָּתֵ֑ף\rb*. \rb Now|עַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb serve|עִבְדוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb and His people|עַמּ֥וֹ\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb Prepare yourselves|וְהָכִ֥ונוּ\rb* \rb by families|לְבֵית־\rb*\rb |אֲבוֹתֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb in your divisions|כְּמַחְלְקוֹתֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb according to the instructions written|בִּכְתָ֗ב\rb* \rb by David|דָּוִיד֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb and|וּבְמִכְתַּ֖ב\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֥ה\rb* \rb his son|בְנֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb Moreover, stand|וְעִמְד֣וּ\rb* \rb in the Holy Place|בַקֹּ֗דֶשׁ\rb* \rb by the divisions|לִפְלֻגּוֹת֙\rb* \rb of the families|הָֽאָב֔וֹת\rb*\rb |בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of your kinsmen|לַאֲחֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb the lay people|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |הָעָ֑ם\rb*, \rb and by the divisions|וַחֲלֻקַּ֥ת\rb* \rb of the families|אָ֖ב\rb*\rb |בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb of the Levites|לַלְוִיִּֽם׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb Slaughter|וְשַׁחֲט֖וּ\rb* \rb the Passover lambs|הַפָּ֑סַח\rb*, \rb consecrate yourselves|וְהִתְקַדְּשׁוּ֙\rb*, \rb and make preparations|וְהָכִ֣ינוּ\rb* \rb for your fellow countrymen|לַאֲחֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb to carry out|לַעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb* \rb the word|כִּדְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb given by|בְּיַד־\rb*\f + \fr 35:6 \ft Hebrew \fqa the word of the LORD by the hand of\f* \rb Moses|מֹשֶֽׁה׃פ\rb*.”
\p \v 7 \rb From his|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃ס\rb* \rb own|מֵרְכ֥וּשׁ\rb* \rb flocks and herds|צֹ֞אן\rb* \rb Josiah|יֹאשִׁיָּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb contributed|וַיָּ֣רֶם\rb*\rb |לִבְנֵ֪י\rb* \rb 30,000|שְׁלֹשִׁ֣ים\rb*\rb |אֶ֔לֶף\rb* \rb lambs|כְּבָשִׂ֣ים\rb* \rb and|וּבְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb goats|עִזִּים֮\rb* \rb plus 3,000|שְׁלֹ֣שֶׁת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִ֑ים\rb*\rb |אֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb bulls|וּבָקָ֖ר\rb* \rb for the Passover offerings|לַפְּסָחִים֒\rb* \rb for all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֟ם\rb* \rb who were present|הַנִּמְצָ֗א\rb*\rb |לְמִסְפַּר֙\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb His officials|וְשָׂרָ֞יו\rb* \rb also contributed|הֵרִ֑ימוּ\rb* \rb willingly|לִנְדָבָ֥ה\rb* \rb to the people|לָעָ֛ם\rb* \rb and priests|לַכֹּהֲנִ֥ים\rb* \rb and Levites|וְלַלְוִיִּ֖ם\rb*. \rb Hilkiah|חִלְקִיָּ֨ה\rb*, \rb Zechariah|וּזְכַרְיָ֜הוּ\rb*, \rb and Jehiel|וִֽיחִיאֵ֗ל\rb*, \rb the chief officials|נְגִידֵי֙\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*, \rb gave|נָתְנ֣וּ\rb* \rb the priests|לַכֹּהֲנִ֞ים\rb* \rb 2,600|אַלְפַּ֙יִם֙\rb*\rb |וְשֵׁ֣שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵא֔וֹת\rb* \rb Passover offerings|לַפְּסָחִ֗ים\rb* \rb and 300|שְׁלֹ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵאֽוֹת׃\rb* \rb bulls|וּבָקָ֖ר\rb*. \v 9 \rb Additionally, Conaniah|וְכָונַנְיָהוּ\rb* \rb and his brothers|אֶחָ֗יו\rb* \rb Shemaiah|וּשְׁמַֽעְיָ֨הוּ\rb* \rb and Nethanel|וּנְתַנְאֵ֜ל\rb*, \rb as well as Hashabiah|וַחֲשַׁבְיָ֧הוּ\rb*, \rb Jeiel|וִיעִיאֵ֛ל\rb*, \rb and Jozabad|וְיוֹזָבָ֖ד\rb*, \rb officers|שָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֑ם\rb*, \rb contributed|הֵרִ֨ימוּ\rb* \rb to the Levites|לַלְוִיִּ֤ם\rb* \rb 5,000|חֲמֵ֣שֶׁת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִ֔ים\rb* \rb Passover offerings|לַפְּסָחִים֙\rb* \rb and 500|חֲמֵ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵאֽוֹת׃\rb* \rb bulls|וּבָקָ֖ר\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb So the service|הָעֲבוֹדָ֑ה\rb* \rb was prepared|וַתִּכּ֖וֹן\rb*; \rb the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֧ים\rb* \rb stood|וַיַּֽעַמְד֨וּ\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb their places|עָמְדָ֛ם\rb* \rb and the Levites|וְהַלְוִיִּ֥ם\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb their divisions|מַחְלְקוֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb according to the king’s|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb command|כְּמִצְוַ֥ת\rb*. \v 11 \rb And they slaughtered|וַֽיִּשְׁחֲט֖וּ\rb* \rb the Passover lambs|הַפָּ֑סַח\rb*, \rb while the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִים֙\rb* \rb splattered the blood|וַיִּזְרְק֤וּ\rb* \rb handed to them|מִיָּדָ֔ם\rb* \rb and the Levites|וְהַלְוִיִּ֖ם\rb* \rb skinned the animals|מַפְשִׁיטִֽים׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb They set aside|וַיָּסִ֨ירוּ\rb* \rb the burnt offerings|הָעֹלָ֜ה\rb* \rb to be given|לְ֠תִתָּם\rb* \rb to the divisions|לְמִפְלַגּ֤וֹת\rb* \rb of the families|אָבוֹת֙\rb*\rb |לְבֵית־\rb*\rb |לִבְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb to offer|לְהַקְרִיב֙\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb as it is written|כַּכָּת֖וּב\rb* \rb in the Book|בְּסֵ֣פֶר\rb* \rb of Moses|מֹשֶׁ֑ה\rb*. \rb And they did the same|וְכֵ֖ן\rb* \rb with the bulls|לַבָּקָֽר׃\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb They roasted|וַֽיְבַשְּׁל֥וּ\rb* \rb the Passover animals|הַפֶּ֛סַח\rb* \rb on the fire|בָּאֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb according to the regulation|כַּמִּשְׁפָּ֑ט\rb*, \rb and they boiled|בִּשְּׁל֗וּ\rb* \rb the other holy offerings|וְהַקֳּדָשִׁ֣ים\rb* \rb in pots|בַּסִּיר֤וֹת\rb*, \rb kettles|וּבַדְּוָדִים֙\rb*, \rb and bowls|וּבַצֵּ֣לָח֔וֹת\rb* \rb and quickly brought them|וַיָּרִ֖יצוּ\rb* \rb to all|לְכָל־\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the people|הָעָֽם׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb Afterward|וְאַחַ֗ר\rb*, \rb they made preparations|הֵכִ֤ינוּ\rb* \rb for themselves|לָהֶם֙\rb* \rb and for the priests|וְלַכֹּ֣הֲנִ֔ים\rb*, \rb since|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִים֙\rb*, \rb the descendants|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֔ן\rb*, \rb were offering up|בְּהַֽעֲל֛וֹת\rb* \rb burnt offerings|הָעוֹלָ֥ה\rb* \rb and fat|וְהַחֲלָבִ֖ים\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb nightfall|לָ֑יְלָה\rb*. \rb So the Levites|וְהַלְוִיִּם֙\rb* \rb made preparations|הֵכִ֣ינוּ\rb* \rb for themselves|לָהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and for the priests|וְלַכֹּהֲנִ֖ים\rb*, \rb the descendants|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Aaron|אַהֲרֹֽן׃\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb The singers|וְהַמְשֹֽׁרֲרִ֨ים\rb*, \rb the descendants|בְּנֵי־\rb* \rb of Asaph|אָסָ֜ף\rb*, \rb were at|עַל־\rb* \rb their stations|מַעֲמָדָ֗ם\rb* \rb according to the command|כְּמִצְוַ֤ת\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִיד֙\rb*, \rb Asaph|וְאָסָ֞ף\rb*, \rb Heman|וְהֵימָ֤ן\rb*, \rb and Jeduthun|וִֽידֻתוּן֙\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb seer|חוֹזֵ֣ה\rb*. \rb And the gatekeepers|וְהַשֹּׁעֲרִ֖ים\rb* \rb at each gate|לְשַׁ֣עַר\rb*\rb |וָשָׁ֑עַר\rb* \rb did not|אֵ֣ין\rb* \rb need to leave|לָסוּר֙\rb*\rb |מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb their posts|עֲבֹֽדָתָ֔ם\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb their fellow|אֲחֵיהֶ֥ם\rb* \rb Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֖ם\rb* \rb made preparations|הֵכִ֥ינוּ\rb* \rb for them|לָהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb So on that|הַהוּא֙\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֤וֹם\rb* \rb the entire|כָּל־\rb* \rb service|עֲבוֹדַ֨ת\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb was carried out|וַ֠תִּכּוֹן\rb* \rb for celebrating|לַעֲשׂ֣וֹת\rb* \rb the Passover|הַפֶּ֔סַח\rb* \rb and offering|וְהַעֲל֣וֹת\rb* \rb burnt offerings|עֹל֔וֹת\rb* \rb on|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb the altar|מִזְבַּ֣ח\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb according to the command|כְּמִצְוַ֖ת\rb* \rb of King|הַמֶּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb Josiah|יֹאשִׁיָּֽהוּ׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb The Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֧ל\rb* \rb who were present|הַֽנִּמְצְאִ֛ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb also observed|וַיַּעֲשׂ֨וּ\rb* \rb the Passover|הַפֶּ֖סַח\rb* \rb at that|הַהִ֑יא\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb time|בָּעֵ֣ת\rb*, \rb as well as the Feast|חַ֥ג\rb* \rb of Unleavened Bread|הַמַּצּ֖וֹת\rb*\f + \fr 35:17 \ft That is, the seven-day period after the Passover during which no leaven may be eaten; see Exodus 12:14–20.\f* \rb for seven|שִׁבְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִֽים׃\rb*. \v 18 \rb No|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb such|כָּמֹ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb Passover|פֶ֤סַח\rb* \rb had been observed|נַעֲשָׂ֨ה\rb* \rb in Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb since the days|מִימֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֣ל\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֑יא\rb*. \rb None|וְכָל־\rb*\rb |לֹֽא־\rb* \rb of the kings|מַלְכֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֣ל׀\rb* \rb ever observed|עָשׂ֡וּ\rb* \rb a Passover|כַּפֶּ֣סַח\rb* \rb like the one that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Josiah|יֹֽ֠אשִׁיָּהוּ\rb* \rb observed|עָשָׂ֣ה\rb* \rb with the priests|וְהַכֹּהֲנִ֨ים\rb*, \rb the Levites|וְהַלְוִיִּ֤ם\rb*, \rb all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb*, \rb the Israelites|וְיִשְׂרָאֵ֣ל\rb* \rb who were present|הַנִּמְצָ֔א\rb*, \rb and the people|וְיוֹשְׁבֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃ס\rb*. \v 19 \rb In the eighteenth|בִּשְׁמוֹנֶ֤ה\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵה֙\rb* \rb year|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb* \rb of Josiah’s|יֹאשִׁיָּ֑הוּ\rb* \rb reign|לְמַלְכ֖וּת\rb*, \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb Passover|הַפֶּ֥סַח\rb* \rb was observed|נַעֲשָׂ֖ה\rb*.
\s1 The Death of Josiah
\r (2 Kings 23:28–30)
\p \v 20 \rb After|אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb this|זֹ֗את\rb*, \rb when|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb Josiah|יֹֽאשִׁיָּ֙הוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had set|הֵכִ֤ין\rb* \rb the temple in order|הַבַּ֔יִת\rb*, \rb Neco|נְכ֧וֹ\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֛יִם\rb* \rb marched up|עָלָ֞ה\rb* \rb to fight|לְהִלָּחֵ֥ם\rb* \rb at Carchemish|בְּכַרְכְּמִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb by|עַל־\rb* \rb the Euphrates|פְּרָ֑ת\rb*, \rb and Josiah|יֹאשִׁיָּֽהוּ׃\rb* \rb went out|וַיֵּצֵ֥א\rb* \rb to confront him|לִקְרָאת֖וֹ\rb*. \v 21 \rb But Neco sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֣ח\rb* \rb messengers|מַלְאָכִ֣ים׀\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֣יו\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹר֩׀\rb*, “\rb What is the issue between you and me|מַה־\rb*\rb |לִּ֨י\rb*\rb |וָלָ֜ךְ\rb*, \rb O king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb*? \rb I have not|לֹא־\rb* \rb come against|עָלֶ֨יךָ\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֤ה\rb* \rb today|הַיּוֹם֙\rb*, \rb but|כִּ֚י\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb I am fighting|מִלְחַמְתִּ֔י\rb* \rb another dynasty|בֵּ֣ית\rb*, \rb and God|וֵאלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb has told me|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb to hurry|לְבַֽהֲלֵ֑נִי\rb*. \rb So stop|חֲדַל־\rb* \rb opposing God|מֵאֱלֹהִ֥ים\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb is with me|עִמִּ֖י\rb*, \rb or|וְאַל־\rb* \rb He will destroy you|יַשְׁחִיתֶֽךָ׃\rb*!”
\p \v 22 \rb Josiah, however|יֹאשִׁיָּ֨הוּ\rb*,\rb |פָנָ֜יו\rb* \rb did not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb turn away|הֵסֵב֩\rb* \rb from him|מִמֶּ֗נּוּ\rb*; \rb instead|כִּ֤י\rb*, \rb in order to engage him in battle|לְהִלָּחֵֽם־\rb*, \rb he disguised himself|הִתְחַפֵּ֔שׂ\rb*. \rb He did not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb listen|שָׁמַ֛ע\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Neco’s|נְכ֖וֹ\rb* \rb words|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb from the mouth|מִפִּ֣י\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb*, \rb but went|וַיָּבֹ֕א\rb* \rb to fight him|לְהִלָּחֵ֖ם\rb* \rb on the Plain|בְּבִקְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb of Megiddo|מְגִדּֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 23 \rb There the archers|וַיֹּרוּ֙\rb* \rb shot|הַיֹּרִ֔ים\rb* \rb King|לַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb Josiah|יֹאשִׁיָּ֑הוּ\rb*, \rb who|הַמֶּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to his servants|לַעֲבָדָיו֙\rb*, “\rb Take me away|הַעֲבִיר֔וּנִי\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb I am badly|מְאֹֽד׃\rb* \rb wounded|הָחֳלֵ֖יתִי\rb*!”
\p \v 24 \rb So his servants|עֲבָדָ֜יו\rb* \rb took him|וַיַּֽעֲבִירֻ֨הוּ\rb* \rb out|מִן־\rb* \rb of his chariot|הַמֶּרְכָּבָ֗ה\rb*, \rb put him|וַֽיַּרְכִּיבֻהוּ֮\rb* \rb in|עַ֣ל\rb* \rb his second|הַמִּשְׁנֶה֮\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb chariot|רֶ֣כֶב\rb*, \rb and brought him|וַיּוֹלִיכֻ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|יְר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb*, \rb where he died|וַיָּ֕מָת\rb*. \rb And Josiah was buried|וַיִּקָּבֵ֖ר\rb* \rb in the tomb|בְּקִבְר֣וֹת\rb* \rb of his fathers|אֲבֹתָ֑יו\rb*, \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb* \rb and Jerusalem|וִיר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb mourned|מִֽתְאַבְּלִ֖ים\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb him|יֹאשִׁיָּֽהוּ׃פ\rb*.
\s1 Laments over Josiah
\p \v 25 \rb Then Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָהוּ֮\rb* \rb lamented|וַיְקוֹנֵ֣ן\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Josiah|יֹאשִׁיָּהוּ֒\rb*, \rb and to|עַד־\rb* \rb this day|הַיּ֔וֹם\rb* \rb all|כָֽל־\rb* \rb the male|הַשָּׁרִ֣ים׀\rb* \rb and female singers|וְ֠הַשָּׁרוֹת\rb* \rb recite|וַיֹּאמְר֣וּ\rb* \rb laments|בְּקִינ֨וֹתֵיהֶ֤ם\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Josiah|יֹאשִׁיָּ֙הוּ֙\rb*. \rb They established them|וַיִּתְּנ֥וּם\rb* \rb as a statute|לְחֹ֖ק\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb and indeed|וְהִנָּ֥ם\rb* \rb they are written|כְּתוּבִ֖ים\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the Book of Laments|הַקִּינֽוֹת׃\rb*.
\p \v 26 \rb As for the rest|וְיֶ֛תֶר\rb* \rb of the acts|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Josiah|יֹאשִׁיָּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb and his deeds of loving devotion|וַחֲסָדָ֑יו\rb* \rb according to what is written|כַּכָּת֖וּב\rb* \rb in the Law|בְּתוֹרַ֥ת\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*— \v 27 \rb his acts|וּדְבָרָ֕יו\rb* \rb from beginning|הָרִאשֹׁנִ֖ים\rb* \rb to end|וְהָאַחֲרֹנִ֑ים\rb*— \rb they are indeed|הִנָּ֣ם\rb* \rb written|כְּתוּבִ֔ים\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the Book|סֵ֥פֶר\rb* \rb of the Kings|מַלְכֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb and Judah|וִיהוּדָֽה׃\rb*.
\c 36
\s1 Jehoahaz Succeeds Josiah
\r (2 Kings 23:31–35)
\p \v 1 \rb Then the people|עַם־\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקְחוּ֙\rb* \rb Jehoahaz|יְהוֹאָחָ֖ז\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Josiah|יֹאשִׁיָּ֑הוּ\rb* \rb and made him king|וַיַּמְלִיכֻ֥הוּ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb* \rb in place of|תַֽחַת־\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֖יו\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb Jehoahaz|יוֹאָחָ֣ז\rb*\f + \fr 36:2 \ft Hebrew \fqa Joahaz\ft , a variant of \fqa Jehoahaz\ft ; also in verse 4\f* \rb was twenty-three|שָׁל֧וֹשׁ\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִ֛ים\rb* \rb years old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֖ה\rb* \rb when he became king|בְּמָלְכ֑וֹ\rb*, \rb and he reigned|מָלַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb* \rb three|וּשְׁלֹשָׁ֣ה\rb* \rb months|חֳדָשִׁ֔ים\rb*. \v 3 \rb And the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb dethroned him|וַיְסִירֵ֥הוּ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּֽירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb and imposed|וַֽיַּעֲנֹשׁ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb on Judah a levy|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb of a hundred|מֵאָ֥ה\rb* \rb talents|כִכַּר־\rb* \rb of silver|כֶּ֖סֶף\rb*\f + \fr 36:3 \fqa 100 talents \ft is approximately 3.77 tons or 3.42 metric tons of silver.\f* \rb and a talent|וְכִכַּ֥ר\rb* \rb of gold|זָהָֽב׃\rb*.\f + \fr 36:3 \fqa A talent \ft is approximately 75.4 pounds or 34.2 kilograms of gold.\f*
\p \v 4 \rb Then Neco king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֜יִם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb made Eliakim|אֶלְיָקִ֣ים\rb* \rb brother of Jehoahaz|אָחִ֗יו\rb* \rb king|וַיַּמְלֵ֨ךְ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb* \rb and Jerusalem|וִיר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb*, \rb and he changed|וַיַּסֵּ֥ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Eliakim’s name|שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb to Jehoiakim|יְהוֹיָקִ֑ים\rb*.\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb But Neco|נְכ֔וֹ\rb* \rb took|לָקַ֣ח\rb* \rb Eliakim’s brother|אָחִיו֙\rb* \rb Jehoahaz|יוֹאָחָ֤ז\rb* \rb and carried him off|וַיְבִיאֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb to Egypt|מִצְרָֽיְמָה׃פ\rb*.
\s1 Jehoiakim Reigns in Judah
\r (2 Kings 23:36–37)
\p \v 5 \rb Jehoiakim|יְהוֹיָקִ֣ים\rb* \rb was twenty-five|עֶשְׂרִ֨ים\rb*\rb |וְחָמֵ֤שׁ\rb* \rb years old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָה֙\rb* \rb when he became king|בְּמָלְכ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and he reigned|מָלַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb eleven|וְאַחַ֤ת\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵה֙\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb*. \rb And he did|וַיַּ֣עַשׂ\rb* \rb evil|הָרַ֔ע\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb his God|אֱלֹהָֽיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb Then Nebuchadnezzar|נְבוּכַדְנֶאצַּ֖ר\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֑ל\rb* \rb came up|עָלָ֔ה\rb* \rb against Jehoiakim|עָלָ֣יו\rb* \rb and bound him|וַיַּֽאַסְרֵ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb with bronze shackles|בַּֽנְחֻשְׁתַּ֔יִם\rb* \rb to take him|לְהֹלִיכ֖וֹ\rb* \rb to Babylon|בָּבֶֽלָה׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb Nebuchadnezzar also|נְבוּכַדְנֶאצַּ֖ר\rb* \rb took|הֵבִ֥יא\rb* \rb to Babylon|לְבָבֶ֑ל\rb* \rb some of the articles|וּמִכְּלֵי֙\rb* \rb from the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and he put them|וַיִּתְּנֵ֥ם\rb* \rb in his temple|בְּהֵיכָל֖וֹ\rb*\f + \fr 36:7 \ft Or \fqa palace\f* \rb in Babylon|בְּבָבֶֽל׃\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb As for the rest|וְיֶתֶר֩\rb* \rb of the acts|דִּבְרֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Jehoiakim|יְהֽוֹיָקִ֜ים\rb*, \rb the abominations|וְתֹֽעֲבֹתָ֤יו\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he committed|עָשָׂה֙\rb*, \rb and all that was found|וְהַנִּמְצָ֣א\rb* \rb against him|עָלָ֔יו\rb*, \rb they are indeed|הִנָּ֣ם\rb* \rb written|כְּתוּבִ֗ים\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the Book|סֵ֛פֶר\rb* \rb of the Kings|מַלְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb and Judah|וִֽיהוּדָ֑ה\rb*. \rb And his son|בְּנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Jehoiachin|יְהוֹיָכִ֥ין\rb* \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֛ךְ\rb* \rb in his place|תַּחְתָּֽיו׃פ\rb*.
\s1 Jehoiachin Reigns in Judah
\r (2 Kings 24:6–9)
\p \v 9 \rb Jehoiachin|יְהוֹיָכִ֣ין\rb* \rb was eighteen|שְׁמוֹנֶ֤ה\rb*\f + \fr 36:9 \ft One Hebrew manuscript, some LXX manuscripts, and Syriac (see also 2 Kings 24:8); most Hebrew manuscripts \fqa eight\f* \rb years|שָׁנִים֙\rb* \rb old|בֶּן־\rb* \rb when he became king|בְּמָלְכ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and he reigned|מָלַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb three|וּשְׁלֹשָׁ֤ה\rb* \rb months|חֳדָשִׁים֙\rb* \rb and ten|וַעֲשֶׂ֣רֶת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֔ים\rb*. \rb And he did|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb evil|הָרַ֖ע\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb In the spring|וְלִתְשׁוּבַ֣ת\rb*\rb |הַשָּׁנָ֗ה\rb*,\f + \fr 36:10 \ft Literally \fqa At the turn of the year\f* \rb King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבֽוּכַדְנֶאצַּ֔ר\rb* \rb summoned Jehoiachin|שָׁלַח֙\rb* \rb and brought him|וַיְבִאֵ֣הוּ\rb* \rb to Babylon|בָבֶ֔לָה\rb*, \rb along with|עִם־\rb* \rb the articles|כְּלֵ֖י\rb* \rb of value|חֶמְדַּ֣ת\rb* \rb from the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*. \rb And he made Jehoiachin’s relative|אָחִ֔יו\rb*\f + \fr 36:10 \ft Or \fqa brother \ft or \fqa uncle\f* \rb Zedekiah|צִדְקִיָּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb king|וַיַּמְלֵךְ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb and Jerusalem|וִֽירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃פ\rb*.
\s1 Zedekiah Reigns in Judah
\r (2 Kings 24:18–20; Jeremiah 52:1–3)
\p \v 11 \rb Zedekiah|צִדְקִיָּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb was twenty-one|עֶשְׂרִ֧ים\rb*\rb |וְאַחַ֛ת\rb* \rb years old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֖ה\rb* \rb when he became king|בְמָלְכ֑וֹ\rb*, \rb and he reigned|מָלַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb* \rb eleven|וְאַחַ֤ת\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵה֙\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb*. \v 12 \rb And he did|וַיַּ֣עַשׂ\rb* \rb evil|הָרַ֔ע\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb his God|אֱלֹהָ֑יו\rb* \rb and did not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb humble himself|נִכְנַ֗ע\rb* \rb before|מִלִּפְנֵ֛י\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֥הוּ\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֖יא\rb*, \rb who spoke|מִפִּ֥י\rb* \rb for the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb He also|וְ֠גַם\rb* \rb rebelled|מָרָ֔ד\rb* \rb against King|בַּמֶּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבֽוּכַדְנֶאצַּר֙\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb had made him swear|הִשְׁבִּיע֖וֹ\rb* \rb by God|בֵּֽאלֹהִ֑ים\rb*. \rb But Zedekiah stiffened|וַיֶּ֤קֶשׁ\rb* \rb his neck|עָרְפּוֹ֙\rb* \rb and hardened|וַיְאַמֵּ֣ץ\rb*\f + \fr 36:13 \ft Or \fqa made strong \ft or \fqa made courageous\f* \rb his heart|לְבָב֔וֹ\rb* \rb against turning|מִשּׁ֕וּב\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb Furthermore|גַּ֠ם\rb*, \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the leaders|שָׂרֵ֨י\rb* \rb of the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֤ים\rb* \rb and the people|וְהָעָם֙\rb* \rb multiplied|הִרְבּ֣וּ\rb* \rb their unfaithful deeds|לִמְעָול־\rb*\rb |מַ֔עַל\rb*, \rb following all|כְּכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the abominations|תֹּעֲב֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֑ם\rb*, \rb and they defiled|וַֽיְטַמְּאוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb He had consecrated|הִקְדִּ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*.
\s1 The Fall of Jerusalem
\r (2 Kings 25:1–7)
\p \v 15 \rb Again and again|הַשְׁכֵּ֣ם\rb*\rb |וְשָׁל֑וֹחַ\rb*\f + \fr 36:15 \ft Literally \fqa Rising up early and sending (it),\f* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֩\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֨י\rb* \rb of their fathers|אֲבוֹתֵיהֶ֧ם\rb*, \rb sent word|וַיִּשְׁלַ֡ח\rb* \rb to His people|עֲלֵיהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb through|בְּיַ֥ד\rb* \rb His messengers|מַלְאָכָ֖יו\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb He had compassion|חָמַ֥ל\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb them|עַמּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb and on|וְעַל־\rb* \rb His dwelling place|מְעוֹנֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb But they|וַיִּֽהְי֤וּ\rb* \rb mocked|מַלְעִבִים֙\rb* \rb the messengers|בְּמַלְאֲכֵ֣י\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*, \rb despising|וּבוֹזִ֣ים\rb* \rb His words|דְּבָרָ֔יו\rb* \rb and scoffing|וּמִֽתַּעְתְּעִ֖ים\rb* \rb at His prophets|בִּנְבִאָ֑יו\rb*, \rb until|עַ֠ד\rb* \rb the wrath|חֲמַת־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb against His people|בְּעַמּ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb was stirred up|עֲל֧וֹת\rb* \rb beyond|לְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb remedy|מַרְפֵּֽא׃\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb So He brought up|וַיַּ֨עַל\rb* \rb against them|עֲלֵיהֶ֜ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of the Chaldeans|כַּשְׂדִּיִּים\rb*,\f + \fr 36:17 \ft That is, the Babylonians; also clarified in verse 19\f* \rb who put|וַיַּהֲרֹ֨ג\rb* \rb their young men|בַּחוּרֵיהֶ֤ם\rb* \rb to the sword|בַּחֶ֙רֶב֙\rb*\rb |בְּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb in the sanctuary|מִקְדָּשָׁ֔ם\rb*, \rb sparing|חָמַ֛ל\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb neither|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb young men|בָּח֥וּר\rb* \rb nor young women|וּבְתוּלָ֖ה\rb*, \rb neither elderly|זָקֵ֣ן\rb* \rb nor infirm|וְיָשֵׁ֑שׁ\rb*. \rb God gave them|נָתַ֥ן\rb* \rb all|הַכֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb into the hand of Nebuchadnezzar|בְּיָדֽוֹ׃\rb*, \v 18 \rb who carried off|הֵבִ֥יא\rb* \rb everything|הַכֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb to Babylon|בָבֶֽל׃\rb*— \rb all|וְ֠כֹל\rb* \rb the articles|כְּלֵ֞י\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּ֤ית\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִים֙\rb*, \rb both large|הַגְּדֹלִ֣ים\rb* \rb and small|וְהַקְּטַנִּ֔ים\rb*, \rb and the treasures|וְאֹֽצְרוֹת֙\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְאֹצְר֥וֹת\rb* \rb and of the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb and his officials|וְשָׂרָ֑יו\rb*. \v 19 \rb Then the Chaldeans set fire to|וַֽיִּשְׂרְפוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb and broke down|וַֽיְנַתְּצ֔וּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the wall|חוֹמַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb*. \rb They burned down|שָׂרְפ֣וּ\rb*\rb |בָאֵ֔שׁ\rb* \rb all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the palaces|אַרְמְנוֹתֶ֙יהָ֙\rb* \rb and destroyed|לְהַשְׁחִֽית׃ס\rb* \rb every|וְכָל־\rb* \rb article|כְּלֵ֥י\rb* \rb of value|מַחֲמַדֶּ֖יהָ\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb Those who escaped|הַשְּׁאֵרִ֥ית\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb the sword|הַחֶ֖רֶב\rb* \rb were carried by Nebuchadnezzar into exile|וַיֶּ֛גֶל\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb Babylon|בָּבֶ֑ל\rb*, \rb and they became|וַֽיִּהְיוּ־\rb* \rb servants|לַעֲבָדִ֔ים\rb* \rb to him|ל֤וֹ\rb* \rb and his sons|וּלְבָנָיו֙\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb the kingdom|מַלְכ֥וּת\rb* \rb of Persia|פָּרָֽס׃\rb* \rb came to power|מְלֹ֖ךְ\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb So the land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb enjoyed|רָצְתָ֥ה\rb* \rb its Sabbath|שַׁבְּתוֹתֶ֑יהָ\rb* \rb rest|שָׁבָ֔תָה\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the days|יְמֵ֤י\rb* \rb of the desolation|הָשַּׁמָּה֙\rb*, \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb seventy|שִׁבְעִ֥ים\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָֽה׃פ\rb* \rb were completed|לְמַלֹּ֖אות\rb*, \rb in fulfillment|לְמַלֹּ֤אות\rb* \rb of the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb spoken|בְּפִ֣י\rb* \rb through Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֔הוּ\rb*.\f + \fr 36:21 \ft See Jeremiah 25:12 and Jeremiah 29:10.\f*
\s1 The Proclamation of Cyrus
\r (Ezra 1:1–4; Isaiah 45:1–25)
\p \v 22 \rb In the first|אַחַ֗ת\rb* \rb year|וּבִשְׁנַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Cyrus|לְכ֙וֹרֶשׁ֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Persia|פָּרַ֔ס\rb*, \rb to fulfill|לִכְל֥וֹת\rb* \rb the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb spoken|בְּפִ֣י\rb* \rb through Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֑הוּ\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb stirred|הֵעִ֣יר\rb* \rb the spirit|ר֙וּחַ֙\rb* \rb of Cyrus|כּ֣וֹרֶשׁ\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Persia|פָּרַ֔ס\rb* \rb to send|וַיַּֽעֲבֶר־\rb* \rb a proclamation|קוֹל֙\rb* \rb throughout|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb his kingdom|מַלְכוּת֔וֹ\rb* \rb and|וְגַם־\rb* \rb to put it in writing|בְּמִכְתָּ֖ב\rb* \rb as follows|לֵאמֹֽר׃ס\rb*:
\pmo \v 23 “\rb This is what|כֹּה־\rb* \rb Cyrus|כּ֣וֹרֶשׁ׀\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Persia|פָּרַ֗ס\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֞ר\rb*:
\pmo ‘\rb The LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of heaven|הַשָּׁמַ֔יִם\rb*, \rb who|וְהֽוּא־\rb* \rb has given|נָ֣תַן\rb* \rb me|לִ֗י\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the kingdoms|מַמְלְכ֤וֹת\rb* \rb of the earth|הָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb*, \rb has appointed|פָקַ֤ד\rb* \rb me|עָלַי֙\rb* \rb to build|לִבְנֽוֹת־\rb* \rb a house|בַ֔יִת\rb* \rb for Him|ל֣וֹ\rb* \rb at Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in Judah|בִּֽיהוּדָ֑ה\rb*.
\pmo \rb Whoever|מִֽי־\rb* \rb among you|בָכֶ֣ם\rb* \rb belongs to|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb His people|עַמּ֗וֹ\rb*, \rb may the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb* \rb his God|אֱלֹהָ֛יו\rb* \rb be with him|עִמּ֖וֹ\rb*, \rb and may he go up|וְיָֽעַל׃\rb*.’”
